HZ.cmnem={"的":["of","The {Dentist} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Hut}, pulling a tooth from a *white dove*. She drops it into a *ladle* and labels it: tooth **of** dove. Soon the step is lined with ladles **of** everything: the beak **of** a duck, the honk **of** a goose, the hiccup **of** a frog."],"一":["one","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} café, balanced on **one** *plank* on **one** toe. A seagull lands and the plank wobbles. The yogi raises **one** finger, and the whole beach freezes, holding its breath, until a single grain of sand falls and he topples into the sea."],"是":["to be","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and stamps every bee with a giant *tick mark*. 'You **are** a bee. You **are** a bee.' One bee insists it wants **to be** a wasp; the sheriff slaps another tick on its back, and now it simply **is**, forever, officially, a bee."],"不":["not","The {Baker} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool}, waving a dripping *no sign* at everyone. Swimmers? **Not** allowed. Inflatable ducks? **Not** today. When the water tries to splash, he slaps the sign on it too, and the pool sits perfectly still, **not** moving, **not** even rippling."],"了":["done","The {Lifeguard} rocks a *swaddled baby* on the {Front Step} of the {Hut}, blowing her whistle as a lullaby. The baby burps, yawns and holds up a tiny sign: **done**. Feeding **done**, burping **done**, nap **done**. The lifeguard crosses off the whole day and goes home at eleven in the morning."],"在":["to be at","The {Zookeeper} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} lighthouse and lands on a huge map pinned down by a giant *left hand*. 'You **are at** this spot,' it booms, tapping a red dot. Every lost penguin waddles up, touches the hand and finally knows where it **is at**: right here."],"人":["person","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and builds a *person* out of candyfloss and hot-dog sticks. It sets the **person** walking on two stiff legs. The candyfloss **person** buys a ticket for the dodgems, and the robot, jealous, tries to become a **person** too by eating a toffee apple."],"有":["to have","The {Yogi} sits cross-legged in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, *holding meat*: a huge ham in each hand. Hungry ducks paddle in shouting 'I want to **have** it!' The yogi smiles, grows more arms, and soon he **has** twelve hams, sixty sausages and an angry goose. To **have** is easy."],"我":["I","The {Wizard} hides in the {Basement} of the {Fort} while a *spearman* stomps about asking who stole the cannon. The wizard leaps out, jabs a thumb at his own chest and shouts '**I** did! **I**, me, myself!' The spearman pokes him in the belly button, but the wizard keeps pointing at himself, glowing with pride."],"他":["he","The {Tailor} is measuring a *standing person* on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} when a *scorpion* scuttles out of the man's sleeve. 'Not me, **he** did it!' squeaks the scorpion. Everyone turns and points at the man: **he** ate the cucumber slices, **he** flooded the hot tub. The poor man just stands there being **he**."],"这":["this","The {Jockey} gallops a horse down a *road* and straight through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut}. He skids to a stop, rolls up his sleeve and shows off a fresh *tattoo*. '**This**! Look at **this**!' he yells, jabbing at it. The tattoo shows a tiny finger jabbing right back at him: **this** one, right here."],"个":["one (measure)","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} with a *pole* and a *person* to count. She counts them **one** by **one**: **one** person, **one** pole, **one** lost sock. Everything she touches gets a little numbered flag stuck on top, until the whole room bristles with flags, each item counted as **one**."],"们":["plural (-s)","The {Magician} taps his wand on the {Front Step} of the {Funfair} and a *standing person* walks out of the *gate*. Tap: two people. Tap: forty. Tap: a whole marching band of copies. 'One is boring,' he shouts, 'I want **plural**!' The step bulges with **plurals**, each one wearing a hat with an -s on it."],"中":["middle","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse firing arrows at a *bullseye* floating on the water. Every arrow thunks into the exact **middle**. Fish swim to the **middle** to watch, boats steer to the **middle**, and the whole lagoon slowly squeezes into the **middle** until the edges are completely empty."],"来":["to come","The {Lifeguard} blows her whistle at the top of the {Staircase} of the {Island} hotel: '**Come** here!' Up the stairs **come** sheaves of *barley*, marching on their stalks, hundreds of them, rustling and bumping. They **come** faster than she can count and bury her in a golden, sneezy pile on the landing."],"上":["up","The {Sheriff} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and stomps *upstairs*, swinging his lasso. Everything follows him **up**: aeroplanes float **up**, mechanics drift **up**, a toolbox rises like a balloon. By lunch the whole hangar is stuck to the ceiling, and the sheriff is shouting '**Up**!' through a megaphone."],"大":["big","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and lands on a *big man* soaking in the mud bath. He opens his mouth: it is **big**, so **big** that the dentist climbs inside with a torch and a ladder. Her echo booms out. The man stretches, yawns and knocks down both walls of the spa."],"为":["for","The {Wizard} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} pier into a canoe paddled by an *elephant handler*. 'Who is this canoe **for**?' asks the wizard. 'It is **for** the elephant!' The elephant climbs in, the canoe sinks, and the handler waves a ticket: the whole lake is booked **for** one elephant."],"和":["and","The {Hunter} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} with a *grain stalk* in one hand **and** a giant *mouth* in the other. He feeds the stalk to the mouth, **and** the mouth chews, **and** burps, **and** asks for another. Every step he climbs adds another **and**, until the stairs are piled with them."],"国":["country","The {Gardener} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} and builds a *fence* around a shining *jade gem* on the landing. She plants a flag and declares a new **country**. An anthem blares from a crate, and soon the tiny **country** has stamps, a parliament of mice and a border dispute with the broom cupboard."],"地":["ground","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} shack and hits the **ground** face first. She spits out *soil* and finds a *scorpion* tunnelling beside her. Together they drill into the **ground** with her dental drill, deeper and deeper, until the sand above sinks into a giant hole."],"到":["to arrive","The {Dentist} waits by the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} under a flashing *arrival* board. It clicks: her patient will **arrive** now! A hot-air balloon crashes through, then a horse, then a rowing boat, all shouting 'We have **arrived**!' The patient comes last, on a pogo stick, three hours late."],"以":["to use","The {Yogi} sits in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house with one enormous *tool*. He **uses** it to open coconuts, then to comb his beard, then to paddle out to sea. Neighbours queue down the steps, all desperate **to use** it, until the tool overheats, hums angrily and starts using them instead."],"说":["to speak","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} and tries **to speak**, but only a *small speech bubble* pops out, squeaking 'hi'. A *money changer* rushes over and swaps it for a huge one. Now when the sheriff **speaks**, bubbles as big as lorries float over the town, bumping chimneys and blocking the sun."],"时":["time","The {Sheriff} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} with the *sun* under one arm and a gigantic *thumb* for a clock hand. He jams the thumb into the sun and spins it: dawn, noon, sunset in three seconds. Bees check their wristwatches in panic. '**Time** is up!' he hollers, and **time** runs backwards to breakfast."],"要":["to want","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a *cabinet* stuffed with sweets. A *woman* is already inside, munching. 'I **want** that one,' says the yogi. 'I **want** them all,' says she. They yank out drawer after drawer until the cabinet tips over and rolls down the tower, still full of wanting."],"就":["then","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} into a cardboard *palace*. First he juggles a *wart* off his own nose, **then** the palace towers, **then** the guards, **then** the queen, who keeps shouting 'And **then**?' Every catch happens instantly, no waiting at all."],"出":["to go out","The {Chef} is on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building when a *double mountain* bursts up through the water, one peak stacked on another. Everything **goes out**: swimmers leap **out**, inflatables fly **out**, the chef's soufflé pops **out** of the oven. The mountain shoves itself **out** through the roof and keeps growing."],"会":["can","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} into a *meeting* of rabbits. Each rabbit stands and lists what it **can** do: juggle, yodel, knit a scarf with its ears. The hunter, embarrassed, shows that he **can** whistle. The rabbits vote that he **can** stay, if he makes the tea."],"可":["can","The {King} sits in the {Basement} of the {Hut} asking a *nodding head* in a jar for permission. '**Can** I eat cake for dinner?' Nod. 'Wear my crown in the bath?' Nod. '**Can** I ban Tuesdays?' The head nods so hard it rolls out of the jar and bounces up the stairs, still nodding yes."],"也":["also","The {Yogi} is stretching in the {Basement} of the {Hut} when a *scorpion* copies his pose. He lifts a leg; the scorpion lifts one **also**. He stands on his head; the scorpion does **also**. He sneezes, and the scorpion sneezes **also**, and so do the spiders, the mice and the boiler."],"你":["you","The {Ninja} creeps through the {Basement} of the {Beach} house and finds a mirror with *you* painted on it. Every time she moves, the mirror shouts '**You**!' and points. She hides in a bucket of sand: '**You**!' She disguises herself as a deckchair: '**You**, the deckchair!' There is no escaping **you**."],"对":["correct","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} between two *dance partners* doing a terrible tango. She grabs a clipboard: left foot **correct**, right foot wrong. She prods them with a dental mirror until every step is **correct**, and all the waiting patients stand up and cheer."],"生":["to grow","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse and plants a single *seedling* in his hat. It starts to **grow**: through the crown, past his nose, up into the clouds. Monkeys climb it, a parrot nests in it, and the sheriff clings to the brim as he **grows** too, stretched upward like toffee."],"能":["can","The {Ninja} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple behind a huge *bear*. The bear spins round and shows off everything it **can** do: backflips, karate chops, silent tiptoeing. The ninja tries every move and falls over. The bear pats her head: 'Practise, and one day you **can** too.'"],"而":["and yet","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Car Park} dragging an enormous *beard* that snags on every step. He is a ghost, **and yet** he trips. He is invisible, **and yet** the beard is bright orange. Drivers swerve and honk, **and yet** the ghost keeps climbing, tutting at his chin."],"子":["child","The {Zookeeper} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Beehive} rocking a *child* dressed as a bee. The **child** buzzes, the bees buzz back, and hundreds of them swarm out to babysit. The zookeeper sneaks off for a cup of tea while the **child** conducts the whole hive like an orchestra."],"那":["that","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, and a giant *pointing finger* swings round across the room. '**That**!' it booms. **That** towel. **That** cucumber. **That** man in the mud bath. The ninja rolls behind a potted plant, and the finger points at **that** too."],"得":["to get","The {Dentist} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} following *footsteps* painted in glitter. At the top a *found coin* glows on the carpet. She dives **to get** it, but a pigeon **gets** there first. She chases it round and round the banisters until she **gets** the coin back, plus a feather.","dé"],"于":["at","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} and hangs himself on a *coat stand* in the hall. Visitors stare **at** him: a yogi **at** the museum, labelled like an exhibit. He stays exactly **at** that spot for three days, upside down, while schoolchildren sketch him."],"着":["-ing (ongoing)","The {Jockey} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Hut} watching a *sheep* with one giant *eye*. The sheep is knitting, still knitting, knitting all night, needles clicking non-stop. The jockey keeps staring, staring, and the eye stares back. Nothing ever finishes: everything is **-ing**, **ongoing** forever."],"下":["down","The {Shepherd} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Piazza} and keeps going **down** the *downstairs*: past the cellar, past the sewers, past a snoring dragon. Her sheep tumble **down** after her, bleating, one bouncing step at a time, until they all land in a woolly heap at the very bottom."],"自":["self","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and lands *nose* to nose with her own reflection in a pool of honey. She taps her nose, the way people point to mean me, my **self**. The honey taps back. Delighted, she hugs her own **self**, then buys her **self** a jar."],"之":["of","The {Jockey} rides a *winding path* that curls up onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}. At every bend hangs a sign: Queen **of** the Bees, Honey **of** the Hive, Hat **of** the Jockey. The path coils round and round, linking everything to everything else in one long chain **of** ofs."],"年":["year","The {Ninja} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} in a *slanted cap*, and each step flips the calendar on by one **year**. A pair of *mirror feet* race behind her, copying every stride. By the top she has a long white beard, and the clerk hands her a cake: one hundred **years** of service."],"过":["to pass","The {Gardener} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} onto a *road* where a giant *thumb* is hitchhiking. Lorries **pass**, bikes **pass**, a marching band **passes**. Nobody stops. So the gardener gives the thumb a lift in her wheelbarrow, and they **pass** everyone, overtaking a snail with a roar."],"发":["to send out","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} beside a *launch pad*, loading bathrobes and rubber ducks into a cannon. Three, two, one! She **sends out** towels, flannels and cucumber slices, all whistling across the sky. Fluffy slippers rain on the town below as she keeps **sending** more **out**."],"后":["after","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and hides behind a *leaning cliff*. A *covered mouth* mumbles behind its hand: 'Wait until **after**.' **After** the boats leave, **after** the ducks sleep, **after** the moon sets. He waits so long he comes out a week **after** everyone forgot him."],"作":["to do","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse}, where a *standing person* is packing a *jack-in-the-box*. Every time the lid shuts, the jack springs out yelling 'Things **to do**!' and hands out chores. The zookeeper **does** them all: stacks crates, polishes forklifts, and finally sits on the lid."],"里":["inside","The {Lifeguard} jumps into the {Basement} of the {Beach} hotel and finds a whole tiny *village* **inside**: cottages, a church, a duck pond. She blows her whistle and the villagers scurry **inside** their houses. She peeks **inside** one cottage and sees an even smaller village **inside** that."],"用":["to use","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} jetty clutching a *bucket*, and finds a hundred jobs for it. He **uses** it as a hat, a drum, a boat, a bath for a crab. When a whale surfaces asking to borrow it, the yogi shows it how **to use** the bucket as a very small snorkel."],"道":["way","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} onto a *road* painted with arrows, where a giant *head* lies across it, blocking the **way**. 'Which **way** to the exit?' she asks. The head rolls its eyes left, then right, then rolls itself down the road to show her the **way**, flattening a hedge."],"行":["to walk","The {Shepherd} leads his flock up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where the canvas is painted as a *crossroads*. The sheep **walk** north, **walk** south, **walk** in circles, bumping into the referee. The boxers give up fighting and **walk** along behind them, and soon the whole crowd is marching round and round the ring."],"所":["place","The {Sailor} is down in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse}, where an *old door* stands alone in the middle of nowhere. She chops it open with an *axe*, and behind it is a secret **place**: a cosy room with a fire and slippers. She claims the **place**, hangs up her hammock and refuses ever to leave her new **place**."],"然":["so","The {Robot} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with *flames* shooting out of its toaster belly. The carpet catches, **so** the curtains catch, **so** the butler grabs a hose, **so** the robot fizzes and steams, **so** everyone goes outside to toast marshmallows. One thing leads to another, and it all turns out just **so**."],"家":["home","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} juggling a tiny *home*, a little house with smoke curling from its chimney. Pigeons fly down and move in. A cat follows, then a grandmother with soup. Soon the whole square wants to live in the flying **home**, and he can't stop juggling, because it's everyone's **home** now."],"种":["kind","The {Jockey} sorts seeds in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} aquarium, flinging each *grain stalk* at a *bullseye* chart on the wall. Every **kind** lands in its own ring: rice here, wheat there, corn dead centre. A curious fish swims up demanding to know what **kind** it is, and gets flung at the chart too."],"事":["matter","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and dangles a *fish hook* into the honey, fishing for clues. Up comes a soggy note marked serious **matter**. The bees crowd round: 'What's the **matter**?' Someone stole the queen's crown! The sheriff hooks the culprit, a sticky wasp, and the **matter** is closed."],"成":["to become","The {Chef} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple, grabs the golden *trophy* at the top and holds it high. At once she starts **to become** someone else: her hat **becomes** a crown, her apron a cape, her spatula a sceptre. Then a monkey snatches the trophy and **becomes** king of the jungle instead."],"方":["direction","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} on a giant compass painted as a *square*, one **direction** on each side. She sprays her hose north, then east, then south, then west. The planes below spin to face each **direction** she points, until they are dizzy and facing every **direction** at once."],"多":["many","The {Dentist} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} at night and sees *many moons* rising, stacked one on another. Two, then ten, then **many** more, so **many** that the sky gets crowded and they start bumping. She tries to count them with her little mirror, gives up, and writes **many** on her clipboard."],"经":["to pass through","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} threading a long *silk thread* through a needle the size of a canoe. The thread must **pass through** everything: the ropes, the referee's ear, both boxers' gloves, the popcorn machine. By sunset the whole arena is stitched together, the thread having **passed through** it all."],"么":["what?","The {Magician} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Hut} and pulls a *tiny thread* from his sleeve. It keeps coming: ten metres, a hundred, a kilometre. Neighbours gather, scratching their heads. '**What**?' says one. '**What**?!' says another. The thread finally ends in a small pink rabbit, which looks around and also says '**What**?'"],"去":["to go","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum}, waving pompoms at a glowing *exit* sign. 'Let's **go**! **Go**, **go**, **go**!' The dinosaur skeletons get up and clatter out the door. The mummies follow, then the paintings, then the guards, all chanting, until the museum is empty and everything has **gone**."],"法":["method","The {Firefighter} is stuck in the {Basement} of the {Spa} and needs a **method** to get out. Plan one, shouting, fails. Plan two: she cries so many *water drops* that the room floods and she floats up through the *exit* like a cork. She writes it down as the perfect **method** and teaches it to the goldfish."],"学":["to study","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} teaching a *child* to skate from a fat textbook. The child **studies** chapter one and falls over. **Studies** chapter two and spins into a wall. By chapter nine she is doing triple jumps while reading, and the shepherd is the one who needs **to study**."],"如":["if","The {Robot} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} diving board and shouts 'What **if** I jump?' The *echo* answers: '**If** I jump... **if** I jump...' The robot freezes. What **if** it rusts? What **if** it sinks? The echo keeps asking, and the robot stands there for an hour, metal toes curled over the edge."],"都":["all","The {Dentist} lands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} and sees a whole *capital city* floating down the river: palaces, trams, a parliament. She decides to check **all** its teeth. **All** the citizens queue up, **all** the statues open wide, even the trams. By midnight she has polished **all** of them until the city sparkles."],"同":["same","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} villa sewing outfits that are all the **same**. Everyone gets the **same** striped suit and drinks from *matching cups*. Even the flamingos wear them. When a crab turns up in a different hat, the tailor faints, wakes, and quickly makes it the **same** too."],"现":["now","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *king* and a *watcher* stare at a giant clock. 'When can we swap money?' asks the king. '**Now**!' shouts the watcher. 'Right **now**?' '**Now**!' The coins leap out of the tills that instant, and the shepherd is buried in yen before anyone can blink."],"当":["to act as","The {Dentist} is on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} when a plane's brakes fail. There is no barrier, so she leaps down **to act as** a *roadblock*. Next she has **to act as** the pilot, then the control tower, waving a torch. By nightfall she is **acting as** the entire airport, wearing six hats at once."],"没":["not have","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} lighthouse waving a *war club* like a wand. *Water drops* splash everywhere as his things vanish: hat gone, rabbit gone, trousers gone. He pats his pockets. He does **not have** a coin. He does **not have** a sock. He does **not have** anything at all, except the club."],"动":["to move","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} jetty onto a *cloud* that won't budge. A *strong arm* rises from the water and shoves it. Now everything starts **to move**: the cloud drifts, the island slides, the palm trees jog. Nothing stays still, and the dentist **moves** round the lagoon at fifty miles an hour."],"面":["face","The {Magician} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and pulls a giant rubber *face* out of his hat. He slaps it onto the cashier's window, and now the window has a **face** that winks at customers. He pulls out more and more, until every coin and banknote has a grinning little **face**."],"起":["to rise","The {Cheerleader} is in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house when a *runner* trips over a *coiled rope*. The rope springs alive and shoots straight up like a charmed snake. Everything starts **to rise**: the runner, the cheerleader, a sofa, a sleepy crab. They all **rise** through the ceiling and keep **rising** into the sky."],"看":["to look","The {King} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with a *shading hand* above one enormous *eye*. He **looks** left, he **looks** right, scanning the ballroom like a sailor at sea. '**Look**! Land ho!' he shouts, pointing at the buffet. All the guests **look** too, hands at their brows, squinting at the sandwiches."],"定":["to fix","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} onto a *roof* that keeps sliding about. She slams down a *foot stop* and the roof is **fixed**, stuck fast. Then she **fixes** the referee in place, **fixes** the bell, **fixes** both boxers mid-punch. Nothing can wobble now: the whole fight is frozen like a photo."],"天":["day","The {Tailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} sewing the *sky* like a big blue blanket. She stitches in the sun and it is **day**. She unpicks it and it is night. Stitch: **day**. Unpick: night. The clerks below keep opening and shutting the shop, and by lunch they have had forty **days**."],"分":["to divide","The {Firefighter} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} with a huge *cut cake* and an axe. Hungry children below scream for a slice. She **divides** it in half, then quarters, then hundreds of crumbs, flinging them down like confetti. Still they want more, so she starts **to divide** the crumbs as well."],"还":["still","The {Hunter} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Island} temple along a *road* with a *no sign* on every step. He is tired, he is soaked, and he is **still** climbing. A storm blows the signs over; he is **still** climbing. Hours later he reaches the top, and the last sign **still** says no."],"进":["to enter","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} into a *well* beside the *road*. A sign at the bottom says **Enter**. She **enters** a door in the wall, then another, each one smaller, until she squeezes in and **enters** a tiny room where the innkeeper is serving soup to mice."],"好":["good","The {Hunter} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where a *woman* hugs her *child* and hands out gold stars. Everything she touches turns **good**: mouldy bread goes fresh, bats sing in harmony, his muddy boots shine. '**Good**,' she nods at him. '**Good** boy.' He blushes and puts down his bow."],"小":["small","The {Shepherd} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} and scatters *crumbs* everywhere. Every cat that eats one shrinks: **small**, smaller, as tiny as a thimble. Soon he is herding a flock of **small** kittens with a toothpick. The owner hunts for her cats and finds them in a teacup, purring in very **small** voices."],"部":["part","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a *hillside* made of jelly. A *spitting mouth* at the top spits out **parts**: a wheel, a pedal, a bell, a saddle. The baker bolts each **part** to the next and builds a wobbly bicycle, then rides it straight down the hill and into the deep end."],"其":["its","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} tower tossing grain in a *winnowing basket*. Every grain flies home to **its** own spot, every shell to **its** own crab, every crab to **its** own rock. The basket hops back to **its** own hook, and she yells, 'Everything in **its** place!'"],"些":["some","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave}, on *this spot* laid across *two planks*, handing out snacks. 'Want **some**?' The yeti takes **some** biscuits. A goat takes **some** cheese. Then the planks creak, and **some** of the snacks slide off, landing on **some** very surprised skiers below."],"主":["master","The {Jockey} sits in the {Basement} of the {Pool} holding one tall *candle*, the only light. Whoever holds the candle is the **master**. The cleaners bow, the inflatable flamingos salute, the drain gurgles 'Yes, **master**.' Then a frog snatches the candle and becomes **master**, ordering everyone to croak."],"样":["appearance","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} into a fashion show where a *tree* and a *sheep* swap outfits. The tree in the woolly coat looks like a sheep; the sheep in leaves looks like a bush. The judges score only **appearance**, so the yogi changes his **appearance** too, dressing as a jet plane."],"理":["reason","The {Lifeguard} is called down to the {Basement} of the {Beach} hotel, where a *king* is about to sell his whole *village* for a lollipop. 'What's your **reason**?' she demands. He has no **reason**. She makes him write one **reason** after another on a whiteboard until he sighs and keeps the village."],"心":["heart","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} holding a giant *heart* that thumps like a drum. Every beat pulses through the building: beds bounce, soup sloshes, the guests' own **hearts** thump in time. The shepherd hands the **heart** to a lonely sheep, which falls instantly in love with the chimney."],"她":["she","The {Tailor} stitches a ballgown on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} for a *woman* with a pet *scorpion* on her shoulder. '**She** wants sequins,' the scorpion clicks. '**She** wants feathers. **She** wants a cape.' The woman just nods. The scorpion does all the talking, and it is always **she** this, **she** that."],"本":["root","The {Baker} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Funfair} and finds the whole place held up by *roots*. She tugs one **root** and the carousel above spins. She tugs another and the Ferris wheel wobbles. Everything grows from this one tangle, so she digs to the very **root** and finds a carrot running the fair."],"前":["front","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} straight to the *front* of the queue. Everyone else is behind her, grumbling. 'I'm in **front**!' she shouts, bouncing off a counter and landing in **front** of the manager. He hands her every coin just to get her out by the **front** door."],"开":["to open","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} castle and lifts a heavy *door bar*, and everything bursts **open**: windows, cupboards, treasure chests, clams on the beach, even the clouds. Coconuts **open** and squirt milk. The king laughs, and his mouth swings so wide **open** that a seagull flies in."],"但":["but","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} beside a *standing person* waiting for the *sunrise*. 'Here it comes!' **But** the curtains are shut. He opens them. **But** it's raining. The rain stops. **But** it's only a painting of a sunrise. The dentist yawns: 'Yes, **but** it's three in the morning.'"],"因":["cause","The {Yogi} unrolls a *sleeping mat* on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} and snores so loudly the tiles shake. That snore is the **cause** of everything: windows rattle, guests fall out of bed, cows stampede in the field. The innkeeper follows the chaos back up the stairs and finds the **cause**, still snoring."],"只":["only","The {Jockey} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Beehive} and finds a *lone bird* sitting on one egg. It is the **only** bird there, with the **only** egg, in the **only** nest, surrounded by a million buzzing bees. The jockey offers to babysit, but the bird shakes its head: **only** me."],"从":["from","The {Tsar} sweeps down the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} palace with a *follower* trotting behind, then another, then fifty. Where are they all coming **from**? **From** the sea, **from** the palm trees, **from** under the stair carpet. The tsar demands to know where they are **from**, and they all point back at him."],"想":["to think","The {Shepherd} sits in the {Basement} of the {Stadium} under a *lookout* tower, his *heart* thumping, trying hard **to think**. He **thinks** so hard that steam rises from his ears. The steam floats up to the lookout and forms a cloud shaped like an idea, and the crowd above gasps: they can all see what he **thinks**."],"实":["real","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} to inspect a bee with a towering *hairdo* that scrapes the *roof*. 'Is that hair **real**?' He tugs it and the bee yelps. It's **real**! The other bees gasp, then line the stairs combing their fuzz, desperate to grow **real** hair too."],"日":["sun","The {Robot} bursts up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} carrying the *sun* in its claws like a hot pizza. Honey melts, wax drips, bees put on tiny sunglasses. The **sun** is too hot to hold, so the robot juggles it, beeping in alarm, and finally hangs the **sun** back in the sky, slightly dented."],"军":["army","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} watchtower as an *army* of camels marches across the sand. She tosses up a ball, and the whole **army** stops to watch. She juggles ten, and the **army** cheers, drops its spears and joins in, until a thousand soldiers are juggling their way across the desert."],"者":["one who","The {Jockey} peeks into the {Basement} of the {Hut} and finds a *busy man* wearing a badge for every job: **one who** cooks, **one who** sweeps, **one who** sings to the potatoes. He dashes from task to task so fast he blurs. The jockey pins on a badge of her own: **one who** watches."],"意":["meaning","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} bar, where *music* plays straight into his *heart*. Every note carries a hidden **meaning**: the drum says hello, the flute says lunch, the trumpet says your trousers are on fire. The yogi leaps into the sea, finally understanding the true **meaning** of jazz."],"无":["without","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} slide behind a *vanishing man* who fades away bit by bit. First he is **without** his hat, then **without** his legs, then **without** his head. Only his swimming trunks whoosh down the slide, **without** anybody in them, and land in the water with a splash."],"力":["power","The {Lifeguard} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} tower flexing one *strong arm*. With pure **power** she lifts a capsized boat, tosses a whale back to sea and arm-wrestles the tide until the waves give up. The seagulls bow. Every swimmer feels the **power** and paddles very politely."],"它":["it","The {Tailor} is sewing on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} when a long *serpent* slithers up. Nobody knows what **it** is. **It** eats a towel. **It** wraps itself round the chimney. **It** steals her measuring tape and measures itself: forty metres. Everyone just calls **it** It, because no one dares to ask."],"与":["and","The {Yogi} finds a *gift* in the {Basement} of the {Museum} and unwraps it: a sock **and** a teapot **and** a goldfish **and** a trumpet. Every layer of paper reveals another **and**. He keeps unwrapping until the basement is knee deep in paper, **and** the curator comes down asking who ordered the camel."],"长":["long","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} trailing *long hair* behind her, so **long** it spills down every step, across the floor and out onto the runway. A plane taxis over it. Mechanics use it as a tow rope. She tries to plait it, but it keeps growing **longer**, all the way to the next airport.","cháng"],"把":["to hold","The {Baker} slips into the {Basement} of the {Spa}, where a *python* is stealing the cupcakes. A *helping hand* shoots out of the wall **to hold** the snake by its tail. Then it **holds** the cupcakes, **holds** the baker's hat, **holds** the door, until it is **holding** everything and nothing in the room can move."],"机":["machine","The {Juggler} builds a **machine** on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} café out of a *tree* and a *small table*. She pulls a lever: the tree shakes coconuts onto the table, which flips them into the air for her to catch. The **machine** speeds up, coconuts flying everywhere, until it starts juggling the juggler too."],"十":["ten","The {Sheriff} paints a big *cross* on each step of the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, counting aloud all the way to **ten**. On each cross a bee stands guard: **ten** steps, **ten** crosses, **ten** bees. An eleventh bee tries to squeeze in, and the sheriff sends it home with a ticket: only **ten** allowed."],"民":["people","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Inn} pulls a *commoner* out of his hat, then another, then two hundred. The **people** pour down the stairs into the bar, ordering soup, singing, demanding a vote. He tries to stuff the **people** back in, but they have already elected the innkeeper's dog as mayor."],"第":["number (ordinal)","The {Dentist} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} lifeguard tower with a *slingshot* made of *bamboo* and fires coconuts at a row of crabs. A scoreboard ranks every catch: **number** one, **number** two, **number** three. Each crab gets a rosette saying first, second or third, and the last one sulks in a shell."],"公":["public","The {Gardener} plants a whole *town square* on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hotel: fountain, benches, pigeons. A sign says **public**, everyone welcome. Dolphins leap up to sit on the benches, tourists picnic, a brass band moves in. The manager complains, but it's **public** now, and nobody is allowed to lock it."],"此":["this","The {Tsar} storms into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, stamps his boot down on *this spot* and declares, '**This**! Right here, **this**!' He builds a throne on it. The bees bring him honey, but only on **this** exact spot; one step to the left and they ignore him completely."],"已":["already","The {Yogi} rushes down to the {Basement} of the {Beach} house to start the party, but it has **already** happened. The cake is **already** eaten, the balloons **already** popped, the guests **already** asleep in hammocks. Even the washing-up is **already** done. The yogi sighs and lies down, **already** late for tomorrow."],"工":["work","The {Gardener} drags a *workbench* onto the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse and starts to **work**: sawing, hammering, gluing. In an hour she builds a boat, a bridge and a robot duck. The duck immediately gets to **work** too, and soon the roof is a clattering factory of ducks building more ducks."],"使":["to make","The {Sheriff} marches into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where a *clerk* is bossing around a *standing person*. 'I'll **make** you dance!' The person dances. 'I'll **make** you sing!' He sings. The sheriff grabs the clerk's pen, and now he **makes** the clerk dance instead while the bees hum along."],"情":["feeling","The {Cheerleader} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} hugging a *standing heart* covered in green *moss*. Every time it beats, a new **feeling** washes over the crowd: joy, gloom, a sudden urge for sandwiches. The boxers hug and sob. The referee writes poems. Nobody can fight with this much **feeling**."],"明":["bright","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} pulls the *sun and moon* from his hat and hangs them both above the ring. It is so **bright** that the boxers wear three pairs of sunglasses. The crowd glows, popcorn pops in the heat, and even the shadows flee, because everywhere is far too **bright**."],"性":["nature","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} and plants a *seedling* beside a *standing heart*. However hard the boxers punch it, the seedling just grows; that is its **nature**. The heart beats calmly; its **nature** is gentle. By the final bell a forest fills the ring, and the boxers are napping in it."],"知":["to know","The {Jockey} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} to visit a *sage* who **knows** everything. 'Which horse will win?' He **knows**. 'Where are my keys?' He **knows**. 'How many bees live here?' He **knows** that too, and counts them out loud, all fifty thousand, until the jockey falls asleep."],"全":["whole","The {Cheerleader} drags a *treasure chest* up the {Staircase} of the {Mint} and tips out every coin ever made. 'The **whole** lot!' she cheers, then balances a **whole** gold bar on her nose. The guards give chase, and she tumbles down the **whole** staircase inside the chest, clanking like a drum kit."],"三":["three","The {Sailor} nails *three planks* to the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} to build a raft. On it she loads **three** parrots, **three** barrels and **three** cannons. A storm floods the mansion, the raft floats free, and she sails round and round the garden to **three** loud cheers from the butler."],"又":["again","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, climbs out, and falls in **again**. His *right hand* waves from the water. He climbs out, slips on a fish, and splashes in **again**. By the tenth time the ducks are holding up score cards and quacking '**Again**! **Again**!'"],"关":["to close","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion guarding a tiny *mountain pass* made of flowerpots. When the swans try to march through, she slams the gate: **closed**! Then she **closes** the windows, **closes** the umbrellas and **closes** her eyes. The swans peck at the gate and waddle off to sulk."],"点":["dot","The {Dentist} visits a *fortune teller* in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, who flicks glowing *embers* onto a map. Each one lands as a tiny burning **dot**. 'Your future,' she whispers, joining the **dots** with a pencil: a picture of a toothbrush. The dentist sighs and adds one more **dot** for a smile."],"正":["straight","The {Jockey} gallops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} lodge towards a *goal line* painted between two trees. She rides **straight**: no bends, no zigzags, **straight** through vines, **straight** through a waterfall, past a baffled tiger. She crosses the line leaving a perfectly **straight** stripe of flattened leaves."],"业":["business","The {Yogi} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and builds a *scaffold* round it to open a **business**: yoga classes on every level. Customers climb up, stretch and pay in bananas. The **business** booms, the scaffold sways, and soon the yogi has an office, a tie and a hundred employees doing headstands."],"外":["outside","The {Wizard} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} cabin under a *dusk moon*, shaking a *fortune stick*. It jumps from the cup and points **outside**: the party is out there! Music and fireworks all happen **outside**, on the sand. He tries to go back in, but even the furniture has moved **outside**."],"将":["will","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} performs for a *general* who announces the future. 'You **will** drop that ball.' She drops it. 'You **will** sneeze.' She sneezes. 'The crowd **will** do the wave.' Ninety thousand people stand up. Whatever the general says **will** happen, happens."],"两":["two","The {Lifeguard} weighs everything on a *balance scale* in the {Basement} of the {Stadium}. Every time she puts something in one pan, a twin pops up in the other. **Two** footballs, **two** goalkeepers, **two** mascots in identical chicken suits. She blows her whistle in alarm and hears **two** whistles back."],"高":["tall","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} waters her sunflowers, and the whole *tower* grows with them. Each splash adds another floor. **Tall**, **taller**, so **tall** that clouds snag on her hat and geese stop to ask for directions. She waves to an aeroplane passing far beneath her boots."],"间":["between","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} juggles coins across the *gap* **between** two buildings. Each coin flies **between** her hands and the neighbour's window. One drops into the gap, so she wedges herself **between** the walls to fetch it, and gets stuck **between** two grumpy pigeons."],"由":["from","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} and finds a *sprouting field* growing on every step. Everything springs **from** it: carrots, rowing boats, a confused goose. 'Where did you come **from**?' he asks the goose. It points down at the soil: **from** here, like everything else."],"问":["to ask","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and finds a *gate* with a giant *mouth* in the middle. It won't open until it **asks** a riddle: 'What is a duck's favourite ride?' The wizard has no idea. The mouth keeps **asking**, so the wizard **asks** one back, and they're still at it at closing time."],"很":["very","The {Hunter} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Funfair} following muddy *footsteps*, and meets a *glare* so fierce it melts his torch. He is **very** scared. **Very**, **very** scared. The glare belongs to a goldfish in a plastic bag, who is **very** angry about losing at hoopla."],"最":["most","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *grabbing hand* snatches the *sun* off a poster: whoever grabs the **most** wins it. Everyone scrambles: the **most** magazines, the **most** chairs, the **most** biscuits. The zookeeper wins, holding the **most**, buried up to her chin in leaflets."],"重":["heavy","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} pier holding a *heavy weight*, so **heavy** that she sinks straight to the bottom. Fish try to lift it and fail. A whale tries and groans. So she rides it like a horse along the seabed, one **heavy** step at a time, until she bumps into a shipwreck."],"并":["and also","The {Baker} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} on a toy train running along *linked rails*. He delivers a loaf, **and also** a pie, **and also** a cake shaped like the referee. The boxers stop fighting to eat, **and also** to dance, **and also** to beg him for the recipe."],"物":["thing","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and casts a spell that turns every **thing** into a *cow*. Beach balls, flip-flops, the diving board: all cows, each waving a little *pennant* with its old name. One pennant just says THING, because nobody remembers what that **thing** used to be."],"手":["hand","The {Sheriff} climbs into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, and a giant *hand* rises out of the water to shake his. It squeezes so hard his hat flies off. The **hand** waves, gives a thumbs up, then plays rock, paper, scissors with him and wins every time. The sheriff raises his own **hand** in surrender."],"应":["should","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} in a little *shed* full of rules. Whenever a boxer looks up, he shouts through the window: 'You **should** stretch! You **should** breathe! You **should** hug, not punch!' The boxers feel guilty, do what they **should**, and the fight turns into a yoga class."],"战":["to fight","The {Jockey} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to find a *fortune teller* swinging a *halberd* at the butler. They **fight** over the last biscuit, crashing through vases and chandeliers. The jockey rides between them yelling 'No **fighting**!' but they keep **fighting** until the biscuit crumbles to dust."],"向":["towards","The {Shepherd} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} with a giant *weathervane* strapped to his hat. Wherever it spins, everything rushes **towards** it: sheep run **towards** it, footballs roll **towards** it, ninety thousand fans lean **towards** it. He spins round once, and the whole stadium tips sideways."],"头":["head","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} sews a giant *hairdo* onto a customer's **head**: braids, ribbons, a small rowing boat. It is so big that the **head** won't fit through the door. The customer has to crawl down the stairs **head** first while seagulls build a nest in the bun."],"文":["writing","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} with a new *tattoo* that keeps turning into **writing**: poems, shopping lists, a letter to his gran. Visitors queue to read it. The **writing** spreads off his arm onto the ride cars and the candyfloss, until the whole fair is one long, wiggling story."],"体":["body","The {Tailor} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house measures a *standing person* whose feet have grown *roots* into the floor. She measures his whole **body**: arms, legs, belly, ears. The **body** won't budge, so she sews the suit right onto him and leaves him standing there like a very well-dressed tree."],"政":["politics","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} parliament, where monkeys argue across a *goal line* painted on the floor. A tortoise bangs a *cane* for order. This is **politics**: shouting, voting, throwing bananas. The jockey is elected leader by accident and has to do **politics** all afternoon."],"美":["beautiful","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Lake} cabin waves his wand over a scruffy *sheep*, and it turns **beautiful**: silky wool, sparkly hooves, a tiara. A *big man* watching gasps and begs for a turn. One wave and he is **beautiful** too, in a ballgown, twirling so hard he knocks the magician into a laundry basket."],"相":["each other","The {Shepherd} climbs a *lookout* on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} and spots another shepherd on a lookout across the pitch. They wave at **each other**, then shout at **each other**, then throw sandwiches at **each other**. The fans swivel back and forth as if watching tennis, until the two shepherds blow kisses at **each other**."],"见":["to see","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into the arms of a *watcher* with eyes all over his coat. He can **see** everything: the coins in her pockets, the mouse under the counter, her breakfast. 'I **see** you,' all the eyes say together. She juggles faster, but he **sees** every ball."],"被":["by (passive)","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} pier and is swallowed **by** a giant fish. Inside, his *shirt* is nibbled **by** minnows and his hat is stolen **by** an eel. He wraps himself in an old cow *hide* as a disguise, but is spotted **by** a duck. Everything happens to him; he does nothing at all."],"利":["benefit","The {Lifeguard} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} tower swinging a *sickle* and harvests a field of ice lollies growing in the sand. The **benefit** is instant: free lollies for every swimmer. Kids cheer, seagulls cheer, and even the crabs get a **benefit**, a tiny lolly each, which they carry off sideways."],"什":["what","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} ghost train and meets a *standing person* holding a giant *cross* like a question mark. '**What** is this?' asks the sheriff. '**What**?' asks the person. '**What** what?' Ghosts lean out of the dark, all whispering **what**, until nobody knows **what** anybody means."],"二":["two","The {Ghost} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Car Park} carrying *two planks* and lays them across **two** parking spaces. On top he parks **two** bicycles, **two** prams and **two** wheelbarrows. A driver honks angrily. The ghost splits neatly in **two**, and both halves honk back even louder."],"等":["to wait","The {Dentist} sits in the {Basement} of the {Jungle} *temple* on a bench made of *bamboo*, holding ticket number nine million. She has **to wait**. She **waits** while the bamboo grows through the ceiling, **waits** while monkeys raise families, **waits** while her beard reaches the floor. At last a monk calls out: number two."],"产":["to produce","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} runs a strange kitchen where every oven **produces** a *newborn* animal: a lamb, a chick, a baby elephant. Ding! Another one. The basement fills with squeaking babies, and the ovens won't switch off; they keep **producing** more until the whole mansion is a zoo."],"或":["or","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into a *guard post*, where a guard blocks two doors. 'Left **or** right? Tea **or** coffee? Cake **or** tickling?' The hunter can't choose. He tries both doors at once and gets stuck in the middle, still muttering **or**, **or**, **or**."],"新":["new","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} chops a pile of *firewood*, and every log that splits pops out something **new**: a shiny kettle, a brand-**new** hat, a sheep still in its packaging. The guests stampede up the stairs to swap their old socks for **new** ones that still smell of the shop."],"己":["self","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house ties a *coiled rope* round her waist and starts to juggle her own **self**: she flings herself up, catches herself, flings again. Neighbours press their noses to the window. 'Who is helping you?' 'Nobody! Just my**self**!' she cries, upside down."],"制":["to control","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and grabs a *standing knife* like a joystick. Now she can **control** everything: tilt left and the bees fly left, tilt right and they swerve right. She makes them spell her name in the sky. The queen bee wants **control** back and bites her finger."],"身":["body","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} beside a giant inflatable *torso* that bounces in the wind. It is a whole **body** with no arms or head, and children trampoline on its belly. The sheriff lassoes it, but the **body** bounces off over the dodgems, dragging him behind it like a kite."],"果":["fruit","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} plants one seed, and *fruit* explodes from the ceiling: apples, mangoes, melons the size of cars. The **fruit** keeps falling, rolling, squishing. She surfs a wave of jam to the stairs while forklifts skid in the juice, and the whole place smells of **fruit** salad."],"加":["to add","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} juggles a giant *plus sign*. Every time she catches it, she has **to add** something: one ball, then a teapot, then a pigeon, then a scooter. The crowd keeps shouting '**Add** more!' until she is juggling the cathedral bell and the tower is leaning."],"西":["west","The {Shepherd} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} chalet as the sun sinks into the sea. A *bird nest* on the chimney empties as every bird takes off flying **west** into the sunset. His sheep follow, paddling **west** after the sun, bleating goodnight, until only their fluffy tails bob on the orange water."],"斯":["this","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, *tearing* pages out of her logbook and holding each one up. '**This**! And **this**!' she cries, waving maps of islands made of honey. The ripping noise sends the bees into a frenzy. Finally she tears out a page with one word on it, **this**, and everyone cheers."],"月":["moon","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} and lands on the *moon*, which has rolled down from the sky to go skating. The **moon** spins pirouettes, wobbles and crashes into the boards. In the end the yogi has to push the **moon** back up into the sky with a very long hockey stick."],"话":["speech","The {Hunter} shoots out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Water Park} on a slide shaped like a huge pink *tongue*. A *small speech bubble* floats over his head as he starts a **speech**: 'Friends, swimmers, inflatable bananas!' Every splash interrupts the **speech**, so he finishes it underwater, bubbles rising."],"合":["to join","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} with a pot and its *fitted lid*, which refuse **to join**. He pushes; they spring apart. He sits on it: click! They **join**, and suddenly everything wants **to join**: the stairs lock together, his boots glue together, and he hops away like a kangaroo."],"回":["to return","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a *fence* inside another *fence*, a box within a box. He walks round and round between them hunting for the exit, and always **returns** to the same plastic chair. He tries again: he **returns**. One last try, and he **returns** holding a sandwich."],"特":["special","The {Tailor} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} into a *temple*, where a *cow* is being dressed for a **special** day. She stitches it a golden suit with **special** buttons and a hat full of bells. The cow parades down the aisle while monks throw petals, feeling very **special** indeed."],"代":["generation","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} clinic and needs a *stand-in*. Her daughter takes over, then her granddaughter, then her great-granddaughter, each **generation** grabbing the drill as the last one retires. By sundown five **generations** of dentists stand in a row, all polishing the same tooth."],"内":["inside","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} cottage into an *inner room*, and **inside** it is another room, and **inside** that another, like nesting dolls. She crawls deeper and deeper **inside** until she reaches a room the size of a shoebox, where a frog is calmly drinking tea."],"信":["to believe","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} beside a *standing person* whose *speech bubble* says: your sheep can fly. The shepherd **believes** it. He tosses a sheep out of the window, and it flaps its ears and soars away. Now the whole inn **believes** every word, and starts **to believe** in flying cows."],"表":["to show","The {Baker} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} **to show** off her new outfit: a *robe hem* stitched with sequins and a *seedling top* sprouting from her collar. She strikes a pose. The cats **show** no interest. So she puts on a whole fashion **show**, and the cats fall asleep on the catwalk."],"化":["to change","The {Hunter} slides out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Water Park} chasing a *shape-shifter*. Every time he grabs it, it **changes**: into a dolphin, an inflatable ring, a lifeguard, a jelly. He splashes after it all day, and in the end the shape-shifter **changes** the hunter into a rubber duck."],"老":["old","The {Lifeguard} rescues an *old man* from the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where he has waited so long his beard wraps round the room three times. He is very **old**: he remembers when the tower was a pebble. She carries him up the stairs while he grumbles that stairs were better in the **old** days."],"给":["to give","The {Gardener} sits in the {Basement} of the {Lake} cottage wrapping presents in boxes with *fitted lids*, tied with *silk thread*. She **gives** one to a duck, one to a frog, one to a passing fish. Inside are more presents, which they **give** right back. They **give** and **give** until the basement is a mountain of bows."],"世":["world","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and lands on a spinning *globe*, the whole **world** in miniature. He rides it like a bucking bronco while bees zoom round it like satellites. Oceans slosh, mountains wobble, and the sheriff clings on, whooping that he is going round the **world**."],"位":["position","The {Wizard} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} pavilion beside a *podium*, where a *standing person* refuses to leave the top step. Everyone wants that **position**. So the wizard turns the podium into a seesaw, and the **positions** swap up and down every second while the crowd cheers and gets dizzy."],"次":["time (occurrence)","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and joins a *queue* of bees at the honey tap. The first **time**, he gets one drop. The second **time**, he gets stung. The third **time**, he wears a disguise. Each **time** he rejoins the back of the queue, and each **time** the bees recognise his moustache."],"度":["degree","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} clutching a giant *thermometer* and plunges it into the water. One **degree**, two **degrees**: the water heats up until the swimmers turn pink as prawns. Then she turns it down a **degree** at a time, until the pool freezes and everyone is skating."],"门":["door","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} haunted house, where a creaking *gate* blocks his way. He taps it with his wand and it becomes a **door**, then another **door** behind it, then a hundred. He opens **door** after **door**, and the very last one opens back onto the same staircase."],"任":["responsibility","The {Robot} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and becomes the *bearer* of every **responsibility**: it carries the Ferris wheel, the hot-dog stand and three lost toddlers on its back. Someone hands it the keys, the cash box and a goldfish. **Responsibility** piles up until its springs creak and it beeps for a holiday."],"常":["often","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} under a *hanging lamp* with a frilly *lampshade* that swings and bonks her head. It happens **often**. It happens on every step. She ducks, it bonks; she wears a helmet, it bonks the helmet. It happens so **often** that the mechanics set their watches by it."],"先":["first","The {Shepherd} races up to the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, but a *front runner* is already there, wearing a gold medal. '**First**!' she yells. The next day he runs faster: she is **first** again. He sleeps on the roof to beat her, and wakes to find her already standing on his chest, **first** as always."],"海":["sea","The {Hunter} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Island} cottage, where a *busy mother* fills buckets with *water drops* faster than he can blink. The buckets overflow, the floor floods, waves rise. Soon the basement is a whole **sea**, with ships and seagulls, and he is paddling a laundry basket across the **sea** to the stairs."],"通":["to go through","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hotel cuts a *tunnel* with her scissors, a *road* straight down through the building. Cars **go through** the bedrooms, a bus **goes through** the kitchen, a flock of flamingos **goes through** the lobby. Guests complain, but she insists it is much quicker to **go through**."],"教":["to teach","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} **to teach** her *dutiful son* to juggle, tapping a chalkboard with a *cane*. He drops everything. So the cats **teach** him instead, juggling balls of wool with their tails, and by dinner the son is **teaching** his mother a trick with nine kittens."],"儿":["child","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Car Park} chasing a pair of tiny running *legs*: a **child** playing hide and seek. The ghost has no legs of its own and is terribly jealous. The **child** zooms between the cars, giggling, and the ghost finally borrows a skateboard and gives up being spooky."],"原":["original","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} and finds a *cliff spring* gushing gold coins straight out of the wall. This is the **original** source: every coin in the world began here. He fills his turban to the brim, only to find the **original** coins are so ancient they have dinosaurs on them."],"东":["east","The {Dentist} wakes on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse as the sun bursts up in the *east*, blinding her. Every fish turns to face **east**, every palm tree bows **east**, and her dentist's chair swivels round until it points **east** as well. She brushes her teeth squinting into the sunrise."],"声":["sound","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse while a *scholar* listens for the strangest **sound** in the forest. He raises one *eyebrow* at every **sound**: a monkey burp, a parrot sneeze, a falling coconut. Then the sheriff's tummy rumbles, and the scholar's eyebrow flies clean off his face."],"提":["to lift","The {Tailor} struggles up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} chalet with a suitcase full of sand. A *helping hand* reaches down **to lift** it, then **lifts** her too, then **lifts** the whole chalet off the ground. A giant *tick mark* appears across the sky: job done, everything **lifted** and floating."],"立":["to stand","The {Lifeguard} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} on a *podium* and orders everyone **to stand** up straight. Sunbathers jump up and **stand**. Deckchairs **stand** on their hind legs. Even the sandcastles **stand** to attention. A wave rolls in, soaks them all, and nobody dares to sit down."],"及":["to reach","The {Juggler} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} pier with a *chaser* just behind her, arm outstretched. He can almost **reach** her. One more step and he **reaches** her hat, then her sleeve. At the top he finally **reaches** her, and she spins round and hands him three flaming torches to juggle."],"比":["to compare","The {Baker} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Beach} hotel to judge a pair of *twins* in a sandcastle contest. She **compares** their buckets, **compares** their spades, **compares** their freckles one by one through a magnifying glass. Everything is identical. She gives up trying **to compare** and awards both of them a cake."],"员":["member","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, where each *employee* wears a badge saying proud **member** of the coin club. The yogi wants to join too. He folds himself into the shape of a coin and rolls past security. They stamp his forehead, and now he is a shiny **member** as well."],"解":["to solve","The {Juggler} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, where the yeti sits weeping in a giant tangle of rope. She juggles the loops until every one is an *untied knot*, puzzle by puzzle. Problem **solved**! The yeti hands her a crossword next, and she **solves** that too, by juggling the letters into place."],"水":["water","The {Sheriff} sits in the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room} when *water* starts trickling under the door. Then gushing. Then roaring. The **water** rises past the magazines and the potted plant, and the patients float about on their chairs. The sheriff lassoes the water cooler, the source of all the **water**, and wrestles it shut."],"名":["name","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} and slaps a *name tag* on everything: the bell, the gloves, the referee's moustache. Each **name** is sillier than the last: Sir Dingdong, Punchy, Gerald. The boxers refuse to fight until he gives them a better **name**, so he calls them both Champion."],"真":["true","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} examines every prize through a *magnifying glass*. Is the gold teddy gold? Fake. Is the giant diamond real? Plastic. Is the fortune teller's crystal ball **true**? She peers closer, and it whispers one **true** thing: her horse is eating the candyfloss."],"论":["to discuss","The {Lifeguard} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} into a meeting where gamblers **discuss** a *neat stack* of chips. Each *small speech bubble* floats up and lands on the pile: 'Mine!' 'No, mine!' They **discuss** and **discuss** until the bubbles reach the ceiling and pop, raining chips on everyone."],"处":["place","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} on *trudging feet*, hunting for the right **place** to have her picnic. A *fortune stick* floats by and points to a **place** at the end of the diving board. She spreads her blanket there, the board bends, and she and her sandwiches are launched into the deep end."],"走":["to walk","The {Zookeeper} is in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} when a *runner* sprints past. 'No running! You must **walk**!' The runner slows to a **walk**. Then the ducks **walk**, the boats **walk** out on little wooden legs, and the whole boathouse parades round the basement at a very sensible speed."],"义":["meaning","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} gazebo, where a *judge* in a curly wig sits on a sandcastle. 'What is the **meaning** of this?' he thunders, pointing at a crab in sunglasses. The crab shrugs. The judge bangs his spade and rules that the **meaning** of life is ice cream."],"各":["each","The {Gardener} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut}, and a *visitor* climbs out, then another, then a hundred. She hands **each** one a flower, **each** a different colour. **Each** visitor sniffs it, sneezes and climbs back down, and the gardener starts all over again for **each** new arrival."],"入":["to enter","The {Robot} guards the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} changing room, beeping at every *person* who wants **to enter**. 'Password?' The swimmers guess: 'Splash?' 'Towel?' 'Verruca?' Wrong, wrong, wrong. Finally a toddler says 'Please', and the robot lets everyone **enter** at once, in a stampede of flip-flops."],"几":["how many","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house sets a *small table* for dinner, but she doesn't know **how many** guests are coming. Two? Twelve? She juggles plates, adding one every time the doorbell rings. '**How many** more?' she yells, as forty seagulls swoop in, all wanting chips."],"口":["mouth","The {King} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} and finds a giant *mouth* in the wall, wide open, eating rowing boats. The **mouth** crunches oars like crisps. To calm it, the king feeds it his royal sandwich and then his crown, and the **mouth** spits the crown back with a burp: too salty."],"认":["to recognize","The {Robot} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and scans every *person* in the queue. It **recognizes** nobody. Then a *small speech bubble* appears above an old lady: 'Hello, tin can!' The robot whirrs, beeps, and finally **recognizes** its inventor. It hugs her so hard she rattles."],"条":["strip","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} on *trudging feet*, dragging a *bare tree* behind her. She cuts its bark into long **strips** and hands one to every cat. The cats shred each **strip** into thinner **strips**, and soon the whole staircase is carpeted with curly ribbons."],"平":["flat","The {Pirate} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} with an enormous rolling pin and rolls everything *flat*: the ropes, the stools, both boxers, the referee. They lie there **flat** as pancakes, blinking. Then the pirate rolls the stairs **flat** too, and slides back down them like a playground slide."],"系":["system","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} lido onto a *slide* knotted with a *silk skein*. Each tug on the thread opens a gate, tips a bucket and sends a sheep whizzing down another slide. It is a whole **system**, all linked, and when one sheep sneezes the entire **system** goes off at once."],"气":["air","The {Cheerleader} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} sauna in a cloud of *steam*. She waves her pompoms and the **air** whooshes about, hot and sticky, inflating every lilo on the sand. Beach balls swell to the size of houses. She keeps pumping **air**, and the whole beach floats up like a balloon."],"题":["question","The {Tailor} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} lifeguard station with an exam *page* full of **questions**. Can a crab wear trousers? Do seagulls need hats? She answers each **question** and stitches a *tick mark* beside it in red thread. The last **question** asks her to sew a swimsuit for a whale."],"活":["to live","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} and splashes into a puddle of *living water* that giggles and wriggles. Wherever it flows, things start **to live**: crates sprout legs, a broom dances, boxes sing in harmony. The hunter puts down his bow; he would rather **live** here with the singing boxes."],"尔":["so","The {Ghost} haunts the {Basement} of the {Car Park} with a tinkling *wind chime*. One thing sets off the next: a car beeps, **so** the ghost jumps, **so** the chime rings, **so** a pigeon panics, **so** the alarm wails. The attendant just shrugs; it is always **so** down here."],"更":["more","The {Gardener} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} lodge and bangs a huge *gong*. Every bang makes the plants grow **more**: **more** leaves, **more** vines, **more** bananas. The monkeys beg for **more** bangs. By lunchtime the jungle is so thick that she has to gong her way out."],"别":["don't","The {Baker} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} with a *spare part* for the yeti's oven, past a sign on a *standing knife*: **Don't**! **Don't** touch. **Don't** knock. **Don't** sneeze. The baker sneezes. Avalanche! The yeti whizzes past on a tea tray, yelling '**Don't** say I didn't warn you!'"],"打":["to hit","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} is hammering a *nail* into the wall to hang a towel. She misses and **hits** her thumb. A *helping hand* grabs the hammer and **hits** the nail, then **hits** every pipe, the boiler and the gong, until the whole spa clangs like a drum kit."],"女":["woman","The {Ninja} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Museum} and finds a marble statue of a *woman*, which suddenly blinks. The stone **woman** steps off her plinth, dusts herself down and challenges the ninja to a race. She wins by a mile, and the guard on the cameras just sees a **woman** jogging past in a toga."],"变":["to change","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *sweating man* waves his *right hand* over a pile of coins **to change** them. Yen **change** to dollars, dollars to buttons, buttons to bread rolls. The baker grabs the rolls happily, and the man **changes** into a pigeon and flies off."],"四":["four","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a little *fence* pen, where one bee stands on **four** tiny *legs*. It has **four** wings, **four** eyes and **four** stripes. The sailor counts on her fingers, loses her place, and simply salutes it **four** times."],"神":["god","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} to a *small altar* where a tiny **god** in a golden hat sits. Offerings arrive on a *skewer*: kebabs, toffee apples, candyfloss. The **god** eats everything, grows enormous, and starts steering the dodgems with one finger while the sheriff hands him napkins."],"总":["overall","The {Zookeeper} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} aquarium keeps a *tally* on the wall of every creature: three hundred fish, forty crabs, one grumpy octopus. She adds it all up for the **overall** total, but the octopus keeps rubbing out marks. In the end the **overall** count is: lots, plus one octopus."],"何":["what","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} under a huge *lotus leaf* umbrella, though it isn't raining. A frog hops out of it: '**What** are you doing?' The hunter has no idea. '**What** is a staircase?' asks the frog. '**What** is a frog?' asks the hunter. They sit on the steps, puzzled, until dark."],"电":["electricity","The {Dentist} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} gripping a *lightning bolt* like a drill. **Electricity** crackles everywhere: the tills spin, coins stand on end, the cashier's hair puffs up like a dandelion. She plugs the bolt into the wall, and the whole building fizzes and glows with **electricity**."],"数":["number","The {Sheriff} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} beside a lifeguard with a *tall bun*, who taps each swimmer with a *cane* and shouts a **number**: one, two, three. The sheriff wants a **number** too. She taps his hat: four thousand and six, the biggest **number** of the day."],"安":["peaceful","The {Ghost} floats up onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, the one *safe home* left in a thunderstorm. Downstairs everything crashes and rattles. Up here it is **peaceful**: no wind, no thunder, just a mug of cocoa. The ghost lies back on the tiles, **peaceful** at last, and stops howling for the first time in three hundred years."],"少":["few","The {Sheriff} in the {Basement} of the {Tower} is cooking chilli for a hundred cowboys, but he has only a *pinch* of beans. A **few** beans: three, maybe four. He shares them out across a hundred plates, so **few** that each cowboy gets a sliver of bean, which they eat very slowly with tiny forks."],"报":["to report","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a newsroom where a *helping hand* writes and a *pressing hand* stamps every page. They **report** everything: the baker's arrival, his floury nose, the crumb on his lip. Within seconds the whole town is reading a front-page **report** about his breakfast."],"才":["only then","The {Tsar} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Island} palace, waiting for a *green shoot* to sprout before he eats his lunch. Day one: nothing. Day ten: nothing. On day forty a tiny leaf pops up, and **only then** does he unwrap his sandwich. **Only then**, and by now it is stale and curly."],"结":["knot","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} juggling a *lucky charm* tied to a *silk thread*. The thread twists and pulls itself into a giant **knot**. She tries to juggle her way free, but every throw ties another **knot**, until she and the yeti are trussed together in one big fluffy bow."],"反":["opposite","The {Firefighter} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, where a *rebel* does the **opposite** of everything. She says up; he goes down. She sprays water; he sprays lemonade. She shouts stop; he tangos. Finally she orders 'Do the **opposite**!' and the rebel freezes, his brain fizzing."],"受":["to receive","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} into the middle of a ceremony: the *handover* of a giant golden oar. He holds out his arms **to receive** it. It is so heavy that he sinks through the floorboards into the river, where he **receives** a second prize: a soggy, outraged duck."],"目":["eye","The {Magician} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and pulls an *eye* out of his hat, as big as a beach ball. The **eye** rolls down the steps into the water, blinking. It watches every swimmer, winks at the lifeguard and refuses to close. Everyone swims very carefully under that giant **eye**."],"太":["too","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} cottage onto a sleeping *giant*. She tries to sew him a shirt, but he is **too** big. The sleeves are **too** long, the buttons **too** small, the needle **too** short. He sneezes, the island tips over, and she declares the whole job **too** much."],"量":["quantity","The {Lifeguard} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} with a measuring jug and tries to measure the *sun*. What **quantity** of sunshine is there? She fills jug after jug with golden light, pouring it into buckets, then bathtubs. The **quantity** never runs out, and soon the whole pitch glows like a pancake."],"再":["again","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} cabin and builds a seesaw from a *plank* and a *tortoise shell*. She launches a tortoise into the sky. It lands and says '**Again**!' So she does it **again**, and **again**, until a queue of tortoises stretches all the way round the island."],"感":["to feel","The {Gardener} chops onions in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and *tears* stream down her face. She starts **to feel** everything at once: sad, happy, hungry, sleepy. The tears water her seedlings, and they **feel** it too: the roses weep, the tulips sniffle, and the cactus asks for a hug."],"建":["to build","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and helps a *builder* **build** a tower of coins. She tosses coins up, he catches them on top, stacking higher and higher. They **build** past the ceiling and past the clouds, until a passing aeroplane has to stop and buy some yen."],"务":["task","The {Wizard} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} with a list of every *chore*: scrub the tiles, fish out the plasters, polish the diving board. He waves his wand to do each **task** by magic, but the mop goes rogue and starts scrubbing the swimmers instead. That **task** did not go to plan."],"做":["to do","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse}, where a *storyteller* tells a *standing person* what **to do**. 'Now you lift a crate!' He **does**. 'Now you juggle three hedgehogs!' He **does**. The zookeeper joins in, and they **do** everything the story says, until it ends with a nap."],"接":["to receive","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} as the yeti hurls snowballs at her. A *handmaid* rushes up with a *helping hand* on a long pole, and together they **receive** every snowball, catching them neatly. Then they **receive** a fridge, a sledge, and the yeti himself, who only wanted a hug."],"必":["must","The {Baker} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} kiosk with a *pinned heart* badge listing her rules. She **must** bake a cake. She **must** ice it. She **must** deliver a slice to every crab before the tide comes in. She sprints across the sand, sweating, because the rules are pinned to her heart and she simply **must**."],"场":["field","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} shovels *soil* across the floor and switches on lamps that blaze *sun rays* everywhere. A whole **field** grows overnight: wheat, cows, a scarecrow. In the morning the pilots find their planes in the middle of a **field**, with sheep grazing under the wings."],"件":["item","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *standing person* is listing every **item** for sale: one hat, one teapot, one *cow*. Each **item** gets a price sticker, even the cow, who eats hers. The juggler buys the lot and juggles them, one **item** at a time."],"计":["to calculate","The {Juggler} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} ice-cream van and must **calculate** the change for a queue of crabs. She juggles numbers out loud, each sum floating up in a *small speech bubble* with a *cross* for every plus. Seven cones, three flakes... She **calculates** so fast that the bubbles pile up and blot out the sun."],"管":["to manage","The {Gardener} sits in the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion, where an *official* with a *bamboo* clipboard is trying **to manage** two hundred swans. He barks orders: swim left, honk quietly, no biting. The swans ignore him. The gardener tosses one crust of bread, and suddenly she **manages** them all perfectly."],"期":["period","The {Cheerleader} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} chalet timing the *moon* with a *winnowing basket* of sand that trickles like an hourglass. Every **period** the moon goes round, she flips the basket and cheers. New moon, full moon, new moon: each **period** ends with a pompom flourish and a neighbour yelling for quiet."],"市":["city","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a bustling *market*: bees selling honey, pollen and tiny umbrellas. Stalls spread, streets appear, traffic lights blink. By evening it is a whole **city**, with buses and skyscrapers made of wax, and the sheriff has been elected mayor of the **city**."],"直":["straight","The {Jockey} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} dangling a *plumb line* to check that everything is **straight**. The steps are crooked, so she bends them **straight**. The bees fly wonky, so she makes them fly **straight**. Even the queen's crown is adjusted, and the hive becomes one perfectly upright tower."],"德":["virtue","The {Dentist} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} following a saint's glowing *footsteps*, while a *watchful heart* on the wall judges her. Every kind act earns **virtue**: she rescues a spider, returns a lost sock, flosses a mouse. The heart glows brighter with each **virtue** until the whole place shines like a lantern."],"资":["capital","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} counting a pile of *shell* money, her **capital** for a new zoo. A *queue* of animals lines up to invest: a monkey brings bananas, a parrot brings buttons. The **capital** grows until she can afford a giraffe, which immediately starts eating the hive."],"命":["life","The {Magician} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} inside a little *tent* with a brass *door knocker*. He knocks once, and a dummy in the corner springs to **life**. He knocks again, and the gloves, the bell and the stools all come to **life** and start a boxing match of their own."],"山":["mountain","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} as a *mountain* pushes up through the chimney, rumbling. Tiles slide, the roof cracks, and he is lifted higher and higher. Soon the **mountain** has snow on top and goats on its slopes, and the sheriff has to ski down the **mountain** to get back to the front door."],"金":["gold","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggling bars of *gold* in the sunshine. Everything a bar touches turns to **gold**: her gloves, the chimney, a passing pigeon, which drops like a stone. The guests rush up to touch the bars, and soon the whole inn is solid **gold** and nobody can open the doors."],"指":["to point","The {Jockey} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where a *helping hand* unrolls an *edict scroll* and begins **to point**. It **points** at the honey: yours. It **points** at the wax: mine. It **points** at the jockey: guilty. Every bee **points** too, until she backs slowly up the stairs."],"克":["to overcome","The {King} is trapped under the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} by a huge *antique* wardrobe sitting on top. He braces his *legs*, pushes and grunts. He must **overcome** it. With one mighty royal heave he **overcomes** the wardrobe and bursts up through the floor in a shower of moth-eaten hats."],"许":["to allow","The {Shepherd} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Museum}, where a guard grinds a *pestle* under a *small speech bubble* that says: not **allowed**. The shepherd begs and begs. The guard grinds, thinking. At last the bubble flips: **allowed**! And the sheep pour in to graze on the dinosaur."],"统":["to unite","The {Tailor} sits in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} aquarium sewing every fish to a *balloon* with *silk thread*. Then she ties all the strings together **to unite** them, and the whole shoal floats up as one. Sharks and sardines, **united** at last, drift out of the window like a single giant kite."],"区":["area","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} waving a huge *district map*, cheering for each **area** as it lights up. 'Go, shopping **area**! Go, picnic **area**! Go, no-pigeon **area**!' The pigeons ignore the signs and land in every **area** at once, cooing smugly."],"保":["to protect","The {Baker} hides in the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where a fierce *nanny* stands guard over his birthday cake. She will **protect** it from everything: mice, flies, hungry uncles. She **protects** it with an umbrella and a frying pan, and when the baker himself reaches for a slice, she whacks his hand."],"至":["to arrive","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} just as an *arrow landing* thunks into the floor beside her, with a note: I **arrive** at noon. Another arrow: I **arrive** now! Then a third arrow wobbles in, carrying a tiny bee with a suitcase, who has finally **arrived**."],"队":["team","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and organizes her patients into a *team*. They wear matching bibs, pass a toothbrush like a relay baton and floss in perfect time. The **team** wins a trophy shaped like a molar, and the receptionist cheers so hard she joins the **team**."],"形":["shape","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} with a *door bar* covered in *bristles* like a giant brush. She sweeps it over the boxers, and each one changes **shape**: a triangle, a star, a squashed doughnut. The referee demands his old **shape** back, but she has already turned him into a square."],"社":["society","The {Sheriff} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and finds a tiny **society** of beetles living around a *small altar* in the *soil*. They have a mayor, a school and a dance on Fridays. The sheriff is invited to join the **society**, but first he has to shrink to the size of a crumb."],"便":["convenient","The {Baker} discovers a *shortcut* through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}: a slide straight from her oven to the till. How **convenient**! She whizzes down with loaves, swaps them for coins and pops back up in seconds. Soon the whole town uses her **convenient** chute, and the exchange smells of toast."],"空":["empty","The {King} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} castle and opens the door to an *empty room*. Nothing. Not a chair, not a crumb. He shouts, and his echo comes back **empty**. He opens his treasure chest: **empty**. Even the lagoon below has drained, leaving fish blinking on the sand."],"决":["to decide","The {Juggler} stands at the top of the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} juggling *icicles*, unable **to decide** whether to skate. She flips an *archer's ring*: heads, skate; tails, don't. It lands on its edge. She must **decide** right now, so she slides down the banister and crashes into a hockey match."],"治":["to govern","The {Jockey} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} onto a *stage* and tries **to govern** the bees. She passes laws: no stinging, buzz quietly. The bees boo and pelt her with *water drops*. She **governs** for exactly one minute, then the queen walks on stage and takes over with a single look."],"展":["to spread out","The {Jockey} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and finds a *lying man* stretched across the floor. He **spreads out** his arms, his legs, his newspaper, his picnic. He keeps **spreading out** until he fills every corner, and she has to tiptoe across his tummy to reach the stairs."],"马":["horse","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} pulls a *horse* out of a tiny bath towel. The **horse** shakes itself dry, puts on a fluffy robe and slides into the hot tub, neighing happily. The magician tries to make it vanish again, but the **horse** has booked a massage and refuses to leave."],"科":["branch of study","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} with a *grain stalk* and a *dipper*, measuring grain like a scientist. Each scoop starts a new **branch of study**: grainology, scoopology, the science of sneezing in dust. He writes a book for every **branch**, and soon the roof is stacked with encyclopaedias."],"司":["to manage","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} with a megaphone, helping a tiny *boss* bee in a suit **to manage** the hive. 'Faster! More honey! Fewer naps!' The sailor salutes and helps him **manage** the workers, until they both realise the queen has been in charge all along."],"五":["five","The {Wizard} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Pool} and unrolls a *spool* of thread with **five** knots. At each knot something pops out: a frog, a duck, a lilo, a mermaid and a very confused accountant. **Five** surprises! The wizard high-fives them all, with all **five** fingers."],"基":["base","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} lighthouse on a *winnowing basket* packed with *soil*, the **base** of her act. On that **base** she stacks a chair, a ladder, a cat and herself, juggling. The basket wobbles in the wind, but the **base** holds firm, and the crowd below gasps."],"眼":["eye","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} with one *eye* open, and that **eye** gives a *glare* so fierce the bats hide. The butler creeps down with tea: the **eye** glares. A mouse reaches for a biscuit: the **eye** glares. The yogi stays perfectly calm, but that **eye** never blinks."],"书":["book","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} reading a **book** when a *drop* of water lands on the page, then another. The pages swell, and the **book** grows bigger and bigger until it is the size of a raft. The sheriff floats off on it, down the waterslide, still reading."],"非":["not","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} lodge as a goose with *spread wings* lands beside her. 'Is this a fire?' she asks. **Not** a fire. 'Is this smoke?' **Not** smoke, just goose breath. Every question gets the same honk: **not**, **not**, **not**. She rolls up her hose and goes home."],"则":["rule","The {Zookeeper} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} reading a *rulebook* the size of a mattress. Every step has a **rule**: hop on step three, whistle on step four, never look a penguin in the eye. Then a penguin appears at the top, and the zookeeper breaks every **rule** at once."],"听":["to listen","The {Tailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} trying **to listen** to the fight below. A giant *mouth* keeps chattering in her ear, so she raises an *axe* and chops its words in half. Now she can **listen**: punches, cheers, the referee's hiccups. She **listens** so hard her ears grow as big as plates."],"白":["white","The {Baker} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} lighthouse covered in flour, and a *white dove* lands on his head. Everything they touch turns **white**: the stairs, the walls, the parrots, the sea. By the top the whole island is snowy **white**, and the baker can no longer find the dove anywhere."],"却":["but","The {Cheerleader} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} shouting 'Charge!' **But** her team sounds the *retreat*. She leaps forward; they skate backwards. She cheers louder, **but** they skate away faster, until she is cheering alone in an empty rink, **but** still waving her pompoms."],"界":["boundary","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} onto a *rice field* split in two by a painted **boundary**. The yeti glares from one side, a farmer from the other. A *go-between* scurries back and forth carrying insults, until the juggler starts tossing snowballs over the **boundary** and both sides join in."],"达":["to reach","The {Dentist} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa}, which stretches up like a *road* into the clouds. A *big man* in a bathrobe lies across it, snoring. She climbs over him, round him, under him, and finally **reaches** the top, where she **reaches** for a cucumber slice and collapses into the hot tub."],"光":["light","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swamp} shack with a lantern full of fireflies, and *light* spills over the black water. Frogs wake, crocodiles blink, lilies open. She shakes the lantern and the **light** floods everything, so bright the swamp becomes a disco and the frogs dance in the **light**."],"放":["to put","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and taps a chalk *square* on the floor with her *cane*. She **puts** everything in it: a plane, a bicycle, a cup of tea, the pilot. They squeeze in tight. She **puts** her own boot in last, and the whole pile topples over."],"强":["strong","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} as a giant *mosquito* blocks the way. She draws a *bow* and fires, but the mosquito is too **strong**: it catches the arrow and bends it like a straw. So she flexes, cheers, and hurls the mosquito clean out of the stadium. Now she is the **strong** one."],"即":["namely","The {Juggler} on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} pier meets a *kneeling man* proposing to his true love, **namely** a seagull. The seagull accepts, **namely** by stealing his chips. The guests gasp, **namely** three crabs and a lifeguard, and the juggler tosses the ring high in celebration."],"像":["to resemble","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} beside a *standing person* dressed as an *elephant*: grey suit, flappy ears, a trunk made from a hosepipe. He **resembles** an elephant so well that real elephants come over to say hello. The shepherd puts on ears too, and soon **resembles** one as well."],"难":["difficult","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} holding a *caught bird* that won't keep still. Sneaking is **difficult**: the bird tweets, flaps and pecks her nose, and every step creaks. It is **difficult**, then more **difficult**, and when the bird bursts into opera at the top, she gives up and lets it go."],"且":["moreover","The {Cheerleader} climbs a *stepladder* in the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, shouting one excuse per rung. She is late; **moreover**, she is cold. **Moreover**, she forgot her pompoms. **Moreover**, the yeti ate her lunch. At the top rung the yeti points out that, **moreover**, the ladder is his."],"权":["authority","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} and plants a *tree* that sprouts golden coins. She raises her *right hand* and announces that she has the **authority** to spend them. The guards salute. She orders cake for everyone, uses her **authority** to make Monday a holiday, and nobody dares argue."],"思":["to think","The {Sailor} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} staring at a *rice field* below, trying **to think**. Her brain whirs, her *heart* thumps, and thoughts buzz out of her ears like bees. The real bees join in, and soon everyone is **thinking** so loudly that the rice plants cover their ears."],"王":["king","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and finds a *king* using a jumbo jet as his throne. 'I am **king** of the skies!' he declares, ordering the pilots to wheel him in circles. The wizard taps his wand, and the plane takes off with the **king** still sitting on top, waving his sceptre."],"象":["elephant","The {Shepherd} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} and an *elephant* squeezes out and sits on the centre spot. The match can't start. The **elephant** won't budge for whistles, for buns or for the referee's red card. Finally the shepherd's sheep chase it round the pitch, and the **elephant** scores a goal."],"完":["to finish","The {Wizard} races down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} in a sack race against his own broom. At the bottom a *finish line* of glowing tape snaps across his beard and confetti pours from the chandeliers. The race is **finished**, the broom sulks, and the wizard declares the whole house **finished** too, so the walls politely fold themselves up like a deckchair."],"设":["to set up","The {Sheriff} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of a tiny {Hut} with a *war club* and a *small speech bubble* that shouts orders all by itself. Bonk, bonk: the club hammers in tent pegs, a table, a flagpole, a whole wedding marquee. In five minutes the bubble squeaks, Everything is **set up**! and the sheriff **sets up** a deckchair to admire it."],"式":["form","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Beehive} holding a giant *stencil* and a can of yellow spray paint. Every bee that buzzes past gets sprayed into exactly the same **form**: same stripes, same wings, same tiny moustache. The queen fills in a **form** to complain, but the form, of course, comes out the same shape too."],"色":["colour","The {Sailor} yanks open the {Trapdoor} of his {Hut} and a *rainbow* shoots out like a fire hose. It splashes **colour** over everything: the cat turns violet, the kettle goes tangerine, the sailor's beard turns electric green. He tries to mop it all up, but the mop just comes out in every **colour** at once."],"路":["road","The {Lifeguard} lifts a {Trapdoor} at the bottom of the {Pool} and a *pathway* of paving stones unrolls out of it like a carpet. It drains the water and keeps going, out the gate, across town, until it becomes a four-lane **road**. Cars honk past the diving board, and the lifeguard blows her whistle at a lorry for running on the **road**."],"记":["to record","The {Juggler} hauls a struggling *small speech bubble* up through a {Trapdoor} in the {Beach}. Before it can float off and forget what it said, he ties it down with a *coiled rope* and pins it into his notebook. Now every word it squeaks is **recorded**, and he plays the **recording** back to the seagulls each morning."],"南":["south","The {Ninja} slides down the banister of the {Mansion}'s {Staircase} clutching a compass whose needle has fainted and points only *south*. He follows it through a wall, a greenhouse and a flock of geese, all flying **south** for the winter. He lands in a hammock on a sunny beach, very far **south**, still in his black pyjamas."],"品":["product","The {Pirate} kicks open the door to the {Inn}'s {Basement} and finds it stacked to the ceiling with *goods*: boxes of rubber ducks, socks and tinned pineapple. He slaps a price tag on each crate and bellows, Finest **product** in the seven seas! By sunset the innkeeper is buying back his own **products** at triple the price."],"住":["to live","The {Jockey} opens a {Trapdoor} under the {Pool} and finds a *standing person* in slippers, reading by a *candle* in a dry little flat beneath the water. The person **lives** there, with a sofa, a fridge and a goldfish swimming in the ceiling. The jockey moves in too, because anywhere with a candle and a fridge is a fine place to **live**."],"告":["to tell","The {Gardener} drags an *announcer* out of the {Trapdoor} at the top of the {Tower} and hands him a megaphone. The announcer **tells** the whole city everything: who stole the gnome, who drowned the tulips, who snores. Neighbours run outside in their dressing gowns as he **tells** them secrets even the gardener didn't know."],"类":["kind","The {Lifeguard} opens a {Trapdoor} on a raft in the middle of the {Lake}, and a *big man* climbs out with a sack of *rice*. He tips it into a hundred bowls and sorts every grain by **kind**: long, short, sticky, brown, purple. Ducks queue up to choose their favourite **kind**, and one swan demands a kind that doesn't exist."],"求":["to seek","The {Cheerleader} stomps up and down the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} waving pom-poms and chanting, Who has seen my *fur coat*? She **seeks** it in every dorm, under bunks, inside backpacks, even in the toaster. At last she finds the fur coat walking about on the landing by itself, also **seeking** its owner."],"据":["according to","The {Juggler} climbs out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Museum} and a *helping hand* passes him a tiny model *house* with a map glued to its roof. **According to** the map, the treasure is under the dinosaur. He digs there and finds only a sock, but the hand taps the map again: **according to** this, the sock is the treasure."],"程":["process","The {Chef} wants to bake one loaf in the {Jungle}, but first a monkey makes her climb a vine {Staircase} with a *grain stalk* and a twelve-page *petition*. Step by step: stamp the petition, thresh the stalk, ask a parrot, sign again. The **process** takes three weeks, and by the end of the **process** the bread is a fossil."],"北":["north","The {Baker} sneaks into a {Basement} under the frozen {Lake} where the *north* wind lives in a jam jar. He unscrews the lid and a polar gale blasts him and his doughnuts straight **north**, past puffins, past icebergs, past a confused polar bear. He lands on the North Pole with his icing frozen solid, pointing **north** forever."],"边":["side","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} as a *road* winds right up the wall to meet him. A *strong arm* reaches out of the gutter and shoves every car to the **side** of the road, one by one, until they dangle off the edge. The baker sells them buns from the **side**, leaning over the drop."],"死":["to die","The {Sailor} digs in the {Basement} of the {Beehive} and finds a tiny *grave* with a bee-sized headstone. Here lies the drone who **died** of boredom, it reads. Suddenly the drone pops up, yawning, complains that being **dead** was even duller than being alive, and buzzes off to find something to do."],"张":["sheet (measure)","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} with a giant *stretched bow*, firing **sheets** of paper instead of arrows. Thwip! One **sheet** wraps a pilot, another a plane, a third the whole windsock. By evening the hangar is papered over like a birthday parcel, and the jockey counts every sheet: three thousand and one."],"该":["should","The {Gardener} is up on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse when a *wild boar* trots up carrying a *small speech bubble* in its tusks. The bubble nags: You **should** water the plants. You **should** wear a hat. You should not be on a roof. The gardener flings it into the sea, where it keeps advising the fish."],"交":["to hand over","The {Juggler} sits with *crossed legs* on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café}, and a long line of cats climbs up to **hand over** their toys: mice, balls, string, one stolen sausage. He juggles them all, then **hands over** each one to the next cat in the queue, so nobody ever gets their own toy back."],"规":["rule","The {Gardener} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} with a giant *compass* and scratches perfect circles on the tiles. Inside each circle he paints a **rule**: No humming. No sighing. No looking at the clock. Patients below hear the compass scraping and obey every **rule**, sitting perfectly round and perfectly still."],"万":["ten thousand","The {Wizard} pulls a lever and the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} drops open, releasing a *swarm* of glowing moths. He tries to count them: one, two, three, all the way to **ten thousand**! They cover the curtains, the piano, the butler's bald head. The butler sighs and starts dusting **ten thousand** tiny wings, one by one."],"取":["to take","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels into the {Museum}'s {Basement} and a *grabbing hand* shoots out of a crate. It **takes** her pom-poms, the guard's hat, a mummy's bandages and a dinosaur's toe. She chants, Give it back! but the hand just **takes** that too and stuffs the whole chant into its pocket."],"拉":["to pull","The {Lifeguard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} as a *pulling hand* grabs the plug chain of the hot tub. It **pulls** and **pulls**: out come the water, a rubber duck, three snoozing guests in towels, and finally a very surprised octopus. The lifeguard grabs its wrist and **pulls** it back before it drains the sky."],"格":["grid","The {Gardener} plants a *tree* by the {Staircase} of his {Hut}, and a *visitor* arrives carrying a ruler. The visitor saws the tree into straight planks and nails them into a giant **grid** of squares over the steps. Now every guest must hop from square to square, and the gardener plays noughts and crosses on the **grid** all summer."],"望":["to hope","The {Wizard} peers up from a {Trapdoor} in the {Hangar} at a *king* who takes a huge breath, his *diaphragm* swelling like a balloon. He blows at a paper plane, **hoping** it will fly. It flops. He breathes in again, bigger, full of **hope**, and this time the plane, the hangar doors and the wizard's hat all sail off together."],"觉":["to feel","The {Juggler} skates down an icy {Staircase} at the {Ice Rink} juggling an *alarm clock* that goes off in mid-air. RRRING! It wakes up his whole body: he **feels** the cold in his toes, the bump on his bottom, the wobble in his knees. He **feels** everything at once and sits on the ice, laughing."],"术":["technique","The {Sheriff} rises out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Pool} wearing a cape and performs a *magic trick*: he pulls a whole dolphin out of his hat. The crowd gasps. Asked for his secret, he says it is pure **technique**: wrist flick, wink, and a very patient dolphin. Children copy the **technique** all afternoon and pull out only wet socks."],"领":["to lead","Down in the {Basement} under the {Boxing Ring}, the {Lifeguard} follows a *herald* blowing a trumpet and a *page* carrying the gloves. The herald **leads** the march round and round the ring, and fighters fall in behind like ducklings. Soon a hundred boxers are being **led** in circles, and nobody remembers who was meant to fight."],"共":["common","The {Gardener} opens a {Trapdoor} on a floating dock in the {Lagoon}, and out come a hundred *joined hands* holding one enormous sandwich. Everyone takes a bite: fish, turtles, the gardener, a passing pelican. The sandwich is **common** property, so the lagoon shares one **common** lunch, and nobody can let go to wipe their mouth."],"确":["certain","The {Cheerleader} pops through a {Trapdoor} in the {Ice Rink} and tests the ice by dropping a *stone* on it, then whacking it with an *ox horn*. Not a crack. She stamps, jumps, invites a herd of oxen to tap dance. Now she is **certain**, absolutely **certain** the ice will hold. Then the ice machine rumbles in and she is slightly less sure."],"传":["to pass on","On the {Staircase} down to the {Swan Pond}, the {Chef} hands a *spindle* of thread to a *standing person* on the step below. They **pass it on** to the next person, and the next, all the way down to a swan, who knits it into a scarf. The scarf is then **passed on** back up the stairs, unravelling as it goes."],"师":["teacher","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} and finds a *teacher* with a tiny chalkboard giving lessons to the bees. Buzz is spelled with two Zs! the **teacher** cries, rapping the board. The bees take notes, the sheriff takes notes, and by sunset the **teacher** has taught the honey to sit up straight."],"观":["to watch","On the {Rooftop} of the pavilion at the {Swan Pond}, the {Gardener} shades her eyes with her *right hand* and sits beside a *watcher* with binoculars. Together they **watch** two swans fight over a bread roll. The swans notice, stop, turn round, and **watch** them right back, and nobody blinks for an hour."],"清":["clear","On the {Rooftop} above the {Boxing Ring}, the {Cheerleader} finds the skylight furred over with green *moss*. She shakes her pom-poms and a shower of *water drops* rinses it until the glass is perfectly **clear**. Now the boxers below can see the sky, the stars and her high kicks, all crystal **clear**."],"今":["now","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggling a giant *clock* that shouts **Now!** every second. Now! Now! Now! Guests lean out of the windows in their nightcaps, but the clock never says yesterday or tomorrow, only **now**. Finally the innkeeper yells, Bed, **now**! and everyone obeys."],"切":["to cut","The {Cheerleader} high-kicks across the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} with scissors taped to her shoes. Every kick makes a *cut*: icicles, the yeti's fringe, a snowman's scarf, the washing line. The yeti tries to stop her, but she **cuts** him off mid-roar, then **cuts** a perfect snowflake out of his fur.","qiē"],"院":["courtyard","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Mint}'s floor and finds a sunny **courtyard** dug into a *hillside*. Coins roll down the slope in a race and tumble across a *finish line* painted on the cobbles. The yogi sits cross-legged in the middle of the **courtyard** while pennies whizz round him like tiny racing cars."],"让":["to let","The {Robot} stands guard at the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} until a *small speech bubble* floats up and says, Please **let** me go *upstairs*. The robot beeps, thinks, and steps aside. It **lets** the bubble through, then a parrot, then a whole marching band, until upstairs is so crowded the roof politely lifts its hat."],"识":["to know","The {Sheriff} climbs the waxy {Staircase} of the {Beehive} and meets a *lone bird* holding a *small speech bubble* full of answers. Ask me anything, it chirps. The sheriff asks the capital of Peru, the queen's birthday, his own shoe size, and the bird **knows** every one. Now the bees won't do anything until the bird says it **knows** best."],"候":["time (when)","The {Hunter} crouches under the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, waiting for the right **time** to pounce on a giant pike. He checks his watch, the tide, the moon, his watch again. When the **time** finally comes, he leaps up, the trapdoor slams on his hat, and the pike paddles off in his canoe, laughing, right on **time**."],"带":["to bring","The {Dentist} pops through a {Trapdoor} on a tiny {Island} wearing a *belt* with a hundred pockets. He **brings** everything: toothbrushes, a coconut-sized drill, floss for a whale. Castaways rush over, and he pulls a sofa and a piano out of the belt too. Next time, they beg, **bring** a boat."],"导":["to lead","In the {Basement} of the {Tower}, the {Dentist} follows a *cobra* that sways ahead of him while a giant *thumb* points the way. Up the spiral stairs they go, the snake **leading** and hissing directions, the thumb jabbing left and right. They **lead** him to a room full of crocodiles with toothache, his biggest clients yet."],"争":["to strive","The {Jockey} stands on a treehouse {Rooftop} in the {Jungle}, refereeing a *tug of war* between a gorilla and an elephant. Both **strive** with all their might, grunting, sweating, digging in their heels, while the rope stretches across three valleys. Each one **strives** so hard that the treehouse is yanked off and lands in a river."],"运":["to transport","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Dunes} and a *road* unrolls across the sand. A fluffy *cloud* floats down and parks on it like a lorry. He loads it with camels, watermelons and a grand piano, and the cloud **transports** them all across the desert, raining on anyone who complains about the **transport**."],"笑":["to laugh","The {Shepherd} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Cat Café} just as a *dancer* starts tickling every cat with a stick of *bamboo*. The cats **laugh**, then the customers, then the coffee machine snorts froth. Soon the shepherd is **laughing** so hard he rolls under a table, and the dancer tickles him too."],"飞":["to fly","The {Firefighter} is stranded on the {Rooftop} of a cabin by the {Lake} when a giant *swan* lands beside her and offers its back. She hops on and they **fly** over the water, ladder and all. Ducks stare as she points the hose backwards like a jet pack and **flies** even faster, spraying rainbows."],"风":["wind","On the {Rooftop} of a hut in the {Jungle}, the {Firefighter} uncorks a bottle labelled *wind*. Whoosh! A howling **wind** blows the monkeys out of the trees, spins the parrots like pinwheels and puffs her helmet up like a balloon. She tries to hose it back into the bottle, but you cannot hose the **wind**."],"步":["step","The {Baker} descends through a {Trapdoor} at the bottom of the {Pool} onto a *step* made of baguettes. Each **step** he takes bakes another crusty step below. Crunch, crunch: ten thousand **steps** later he reaches the centre of the earth, which is, disappointingly, a bakery with a very long queue."],"改":["to change","In the {Basement} of the {Island} lighthouse, the {Gardener} whacks a *coiled rope* with a *cane*, and with every whack it **changes**: into a snake, a hosepipe, a necklace, a strand of spaghetti. He keeps tapping, delighted, until it **changes** into a second gardener, who grabs the cane and tries it on him."],"收":["to receive","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} with a *cane* tied to a long *twisted vine*, fishing for parcels in the river. Every cast **receives** something: a letter, a cake, a grumpy goose in a box. He signs for each one with a flourish, and soon the postman just throws everything at him, so he **receives** the whole town's mail."],"根":["root","On the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s haunted house, the {Gardener} spots a *tree* growing out of the chimney. She gives it a furious *glare*, and the tree is so scared it pulls up its **roots** and runs. The **roots** scuttle down the dodgems like spider legs, and the tree hides behind the candyfloss stall, shaking."],"干":["to do","The {Gardener} bursts up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with a *drying rack* on his back, ready to **do** every job at once. He hangs laundry, peels potatoes, polishes spoons and dries the cat, all on the rack's arms. The butler asks what else he can **do**, and the rack starts ironing the butler."],"造":["to build","The {Zookeeper} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of a half-finished {Tower} as an *announcer* bellows through a megaphone, Lay the *road*! Elephants stamp bricks into a road that spirals up the walls, and giraffes stack the top floors. They **build** all night, and by morning the zoo has **built** a skyscraper where the penguins live in the penthouse."],"言":["words","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} until a huge *speech bubble* floats out of his ear. It overflows with **words**, and they spill down the steps like marbles: banana, tremendous, hiccup, moustache. The maids sweep up **words** all afternoon, and the butler pockets the long ones to show off at dinner."],"联":["to unite","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} with a giant *ear* that hears traders yelling on both sides of a *mountain pass* made of paperwork. She blasts her whistle, and the traders shuffle across the pass to shake hands. The two sides **unite**, then hug, then **unite** so tightly they become one enormous, very confused banker."],"持":["to hold","Halfway up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, the {Chef} stops because a *helping hand* is **holding** up a tiny golden *temple* full of buzzing monks. Don't drop it! the bees beg. So the chef takes over and **holds** it, then sneezes, and the hand catches both chef and temple, balancing them on one finger."],"组":["to organize","In the {Basement} below the {Pool}, the {Zookeeper} climbs a *stepladder* and strings *silk thread* from wall to wall. He **organizes** the chaos: flippers on one thread, rubber rings on another, sleepy seals clipped on by their tails. By lunchtime the whole basement is **organized** like a washing line, and the seals are sorted by snore."],"每":["every","In a {Basement} under the {Lake}, the {Magician} watches a *busy mother* with eight arms make sandwiches. She makes one for **every** duck, **every** frog, every fish, every pebble. The magician waves his wand to help, and suddenly there are two of her, then four, until **every** creature in the lake has its own lunchbox."],"济":["to aid","The {Juggler} bursts from a {Trapdoor} in the {Beach} with a bucket of *water drops* for a *trimmed hedge* that is wilting in the sun. He juggles the drops onto its leaves, one by one, and it perks up. Soon every plant on the beach queues for **aid**, so he opens a first-**aid** tent with a sign: Hedges First."],"车":["car","The {Chef} pushes a wooden *cart* across the {Rooftop} of her {Hut}, steering with a saucepan. She bolts on an engine, a horn and four doughnuts for wheels, and the cart coughs into a roaring **car**. It leaps off the edge, and the chef zooms off to the shops in the world's tastiest **car**."],"亲":["parent","On the {Rooftop} of the {Inn}, the {Cheerleader} finds her *parents* sunbathing in matching swimsuits. They leap up with pom-poms and cheer her name louder than any stadium. Every guest leans out to see the most embarrassing **parents** in the world, and she hides behind the chimney while each **parent** waves a banner with her baby photo."],"极":["extremely","The {Juggler} sprints up a sandy {Staircase} on the {Beach}, followed by a *chaser* who is **extremely** fast. He climbs a palm *tree* to escape, but the chaser climbs it too, **extremely** quickly, and they reach the very tip at the same moment. The tree bends like a catapult and flings them both into the sea, extremely wet."],"林":["woods","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn}, and every step sprouts a tree until a whole *grove* fills the hallway. By the top floor the inn is thick **woods**: owls in the wardrobes, deer at the breakfast bar, a fox at reception. Guests check in with compasses and get lost in the **woods** on the way to the bathroom."],"服":["clothes","The {Firefighter} walks down the {Staircase} into the {Pool} at night, where a giant *pressing hand* is ironing **clothes** on the flat face of the *moon*. Shirts, socks and swimsuits come out crisp and silver. She hands up her soggy uniform, and the moon hands back the shiniest **clothes** in town."],"快":["quick","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Wine Cellar} wearing an *archer's ring*, and his *standing heart* starts pounding like a drum. He shoots arrows at runaway corks, **quick**, quicker, quickest, until the cellar is a blur. When the queen walks in, he hides every bottle at lightning speed, very **quick** indeed."],"办":["to handle","The {Baker} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to reveal a secret *workshop* full of hammers, ovens and spinning gadgets. Every problem in the house drops down to him: a leaking tap, a squeaky door, a duke stuck in a vase. He **handles** them all with a rolling pin and hangs up a sign: No job too odd to **handle**."],"议":["to discuss","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds a *judge* in a wig arguing with a *small speech bubble* about sandcastles. They **discuss** towers, moats, flags and the correct number of seashells. The tide comes in, the sandcastle melts, and they keep **discussing** it, up to their necks in the sea."],"往":["towards","In the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, the {Wizard} holds up a *candle* and sees glowing *footsteps* marching across the floor. They all head **towards** the far wall, then up it, then **towards** the roof, where a hatch opens onto a waiting jumbo jet. The wizard follows them in his slippers, clutching his candle."],"元":["yuan","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mint} as a giant *yuan coin* rolls down towards him, bump, bump, bump. It splits into ten, then a hundred smaller **yuan**, jingling over every step. The yogi stacks them into a wobbly tower and balances on top, paying one **yuan** a minute for the view."],"英":["British","On the {Rooftop} above the {Boxing Ring}, the {Yogi} meets a *hero* in a bowler hat holding a teacup. Instead of punching, the hero apologises, queues politely and offers the villain a biscuit. The crowd roars: how terribly **British**! Soon even the pigeons are saying sorry and sipping tea, very **British** indeed."],"士":["scholar","The {Sheriff} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds a *scholar* in spectacles, buried in books about honey. The **scholar** has measured every hexagon and written ten volumes on buzzing. The bees, deeply impressed, crown him with a wax mortarboard, and now the sheriff must bow and call him the Honourable **Scholar**."],"证":["proof","The {Jockey} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Jungle} just as a monkey kicks a coconut over a *goal line*. A *small speech bubble* snaps a photo: flash! Here is the **proof**, it squeaks, it was a goal! The gorilla goalkeeper demands more **proof**, so the bubble replays it in slow motion on a banana leaf."],"近":["near","The {Juggler} pops up through a {Trapdoor} in the {Inn}'s kitchen, where a lumberjack swings an *axe* to chop a long *road* shorter. Chop! Now the next town is **near**. Chop! Now it is right outside the door. Chop! Now it is so **near** that its church bell is ringing in the dining room."],"失":["to lose","The {Sheriff} fires a *lost arrow* from the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, and it immediately forgets where it is going. It wanders over hills, asks a cow for directions, and **loses** its feathers on the way. By sunset the sheriff has **lost** his arrow, his hat, and finally his temper."],"转":["to turn","In the {Basement} under the {Swan Pond}, the {Jockey} rides a *cart* bolted to a giant *spindle*. It starts to **turn**, slowly, then faster and faster, until the jockey is a blur and the swans upstairs spin on the water like ballerinas. Every time he tries to stop, the spindle **turns** the other way."],"夫":["husband","On the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, the {Firefighter} is getting married, and her *husband* climbs the ladder in a tuxedo and flippers. Her new **husband** slides down the fire pole to the reception and lands in the pool with the cake. She dives in after him, laughing, because a **husband** who brings cake is worth rescuing."],"令":["to order","The {Lifeguard} is refereeing in the {Boxing Ring} when a *herald* bursts up through the {Trapdoor}, unrolls a scroll and blasts a trumpet in her ear. By royal **order**, he reads, all boxers must wear tutus! The lifeguard blows her whistle and gives an **order** of her own: everyone into the pool, tutus and all."],"准":["accurate","In the {Casino}'s {Basement}, the {Jockey} bets on a *sparrow* that flicks *icicles* at a dartboard with its beak. Bullseye, bullseye, bullseye: perfectly **accurate** every time. The croupier tries to distract it with breadcrumbs, but the sparrow just spears each crumb in mid-air, still dead **accurate**, and the jockey wins the whole casino."],"布":["cloth","The {Baker} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Pool}'s floor and pulls out an endless roll of *linen*. He keeps pulling: metres of **cloth**, then kilometres, until the pool is draped like a giant tent. Swimmers splash about under a ceiling of **cloth**, and he uses one corner to wrap a loaf the size of a car."],"始":["to begin","In the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, the {Sheriff} sits in the front row as a *woman* steps onto a tiny *stage* and claps her hands. Let the show **begin**! Bees swirl, lights flash, the curtain rises. Then she claps again and it all **begins** again from the start, and the sheriff falls asleep during the third beginning."],"怎":["how","In the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, the {Zookeeper} winds a *jack-in-the-box* until it bursts open and out bounces a big red cartoon *heart*. **How**? he gasps. **How** does a heart fit in a toy box? The heart just shrugs, hops on the carousel and asks him how he fits in a basement."],"呢":["question particle","The {Ninja} sits on the {Front Step} of a {Hut} beside a *nun* whose *mouth* tacks a **question particle** onto every sentence. Nice weather, ne? A biscuit, ne? Each ne floats up like a bubble with a question mark on it. The ninja is so busy answering every **question** that he forgets he came to sneak, and stays for tea."],"存":["to deposit","The {Tsar} tiptoes down the {Staircase} of the {Casino} carrying a *piggy bank* the size of a pony. Instead of gambling, he **deposits** every chip, coin and jewel he finds into its slot, clink, clink. The pig grows fatter and fatter until it squeals, and the tsar makes one final **deposit**: his crown."],"未":["not yet","The {Wizard} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on an island in the {Lake} and taps a *sapling* with his wand. Are you a mighty oak yet? **Not yet**, squeaks the sapling. He waits a minute. Now? **Not yet**. He waits a hundred years, with a beard down to his toes, and the sapling still whispers, not yet."],"远":["far","In the {Basement} of the {Mint}, the {Yogi} rolls a *yuan coin* onto a *road* painted on the floor. It rolls and rolls, out of the door, across the country, over the sea. The yogi meditates while it travels **far**, **far** away, and three years later gets a postcard from it, from somewhere very far indeed."],"叫":["to call","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and finds a giant *mouth* tangled in a *twisted vine*, **calling** every cat in town. Here, kitty kitty! it booms. Hundreds of cats pour in through the windows. Then the mouth **calls** the juggler's name too, and he comes running on all fours, like a cat."],"台":["platform","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} lighthouse and sews a *stage* out of curtains and sailcloth. It stiffens into a solid **platform** jutting out over the sea. Whales gather to watch as he struts up and down the **platform**, showing off a new swimsuit for seagulls."],"单":["single","The {Dentist} plays tennis on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with one huge *racket* and one **single** ball. No partner, no net, no opponent, only him whacking the ball off the chimney. The butler brings out a second racket, but the dentist refuses: this is a **singles** match, a **single** dentist against a chimney."],"影":["image","In the {Basement} under the {Boxing Ring}, the {Yogi} dips a brush's *bristles* in paint and flicks a whole *landscape* onto the wall: hills, rivers, a sunset. The **image** comes alive, and a painted cow wanders out to drink from the water bucket. The boxers upstairs keep sneaking down to stare at the moving **image**."],"具":["tool","The {Juggler} drops through a {Trapdoor} into the {Museum} clutching a *toolbox* that won't stay shut. It snaps open and fires out every **tool** at once: hammers, spanners, a saw, a drill. He juggles them all above a priceless vase, and the guards hold their breath until the last **tool** lands safely in his pocket."],"罗":["to collect","The {Lifeguard} stands on the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse}, swinging a *gauze net* at everything that floats by. She **collects** loose buttons, lost socks, runaway kites and a confused bat. By the top step the net bulges, and she **collects** one last thing: the warehouse manager, who was only passing."],"字":["character","The {Zookeeper} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds a *child* sitting under a tiny *roof*, painting Chinese **characters** on the bees with a brush. Every bee buzzes off wearing a different word. Then the whole hive flies in formation and spells one enormous **character** across the sky: the word for honey."],"爱":["to love","The {Ghost} floats up through a {Trapdoor} on a lonely {Island} and meets a new *friend*: a coconut with a painted smile. He falls in **love** at once. He writes it poems, carves hearts in the sand and twirls it round in the moonlight. The coconut says nothing at all, but the ghost is sure it is **love**."],"击":["to strike","On the {Rooftop} of a hut on the {Beach}, the {Juggler} is juggling when a giant *punch* in a boxing glove drops out of the sky. Bam! It **strikes** a coconut, a sandcastle, a beach ball. He catches it and juggles it, and it **strikes** again, knocking his own ice cream into orbit."],"流":["to flow","The {Lifeguard} watches *water drops* begin to trickle down the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel}, then gush. A *tumbling baby* in a rubber ring rides the waves, giggling. The water **flows** past bunk beds, through the kitchen and out of the door, and the baby **flows** with it all the way to the sea, waving."],"备":["to prepare","The {Baker} opens a {Trapdoor} on the frozen {Lake}, and his *trudging feet* march him off to a *rice field* on the shore. He **prepares** for winter: harvests every grain, bakes a thousand rice cakes and stacks them in an igloo. The squirrels watch, impressed, and beg him to help them **prepare** too."],"兵":["soldier","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Baker} drills his *troops*: a line of gingerbread **soldiers** with icing helmets. Left, right, left! They march in perfect step, salute, and charge at a pigeon. The pigeon gobbles the front row, and the last brave **soldier** bites it on the toe."],"连":["to link","On the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange}, the {Lifeguard} blows her whistle and a *convoy* of tiny trucks drives up the steps. Each truck **links** onto the one in front with a hook, until the chain wraps round the building twice. She ties on a long rope and **links** the last truck to the moon."],"调":["to transfer","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} into a room humming with a giant electric *circuit*. A *small speech bubble* rides along the wires and announces: You are being **transferred**! Zap: the dentist is **transferred** to a cat basket, a cat lands in his dentist's chair, and nobody is happy about it."],"深":["deep","On the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s helter-skelter, the {Sheriff} drops a coin down a hole and hears *water drops* echoing from a *deep cave* far below. He jumps in after it. Down he slides, past the dodgems, past the rock, **deeper** and deeper, until he splashes into a lake so **deep** that the fish wear miners' helmets."],"商":["merchant","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} and finds a *skylight* propped open, with a **merchant** selling goods through it to the pilots below. Parachutes, peanuts, slightly used clouds! he cries. The sheriff tries to arrest him for blocking the light, but the **merchant** sells him a badge, a moustache and the skylight itself."],"算":["to calculate","The {Sailor} rises through a {Trapdoor} in the {Swan Pond} on a raft of *bamboo*, clacking a giant *abacus*. He **calculates** everything: how many swans, how many feathers, how many breadcrumbs per beak. The swans line up for their share, and one argues so hard that he has to **calculate** it all again, using its long neck as the abacus."],"质":["quality","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} as an inspector taps a golden *shell* with a *pair of axes*. Ting! Top **quality**. Next shell: clunk, poor **quality**, into the bin. The bees queue nervously with their honey shells, and the queen's shell rings so perfectly that the axes bow to her."],"团":["group","On the {Staircase} beside the {Swan Pond}, the {Tailor} builds a little *fence* around a single *green shoot*. Soon every swan, duck and frog crowds inside the fence to admire it, a whole **group** jostling and honking. The tailor measures them all and sews matching **group** uniforms, each with a hole for the shoot."],"集":["to gather","The {Juggler} sits on a driftwood {Staircase} on the {Beach} and whistles, and every *sparrow* for miles flies in to **gather** in one *tree*. Hundreds, then thousands, until the tree bends like a fishing rod. More birds **gather** on his head, his arms, his juggling clubs, until he has to juggle the sparrows instead."],"百":["hundred","In the {Basement} of a shack on the {Island}, the {Baker} finds a *banknote* poking out of the floorboards. He pulls it, and out comes another, and another: a **hundred** banknotes, tied in a line like a magician's hankies. He bakes them into a **hundred** loaves, and the coconuts queue up to buy one."],"需":["to need","The {Shepherd} is stuck on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum}, *waiting in rain* with forty soggy sheep. They **need** an umbrella. They **need** a towel. They need hot cocoa, a hairdryer and a ladder. At last a marble goddess leans out of her niche and hands them exactly what they **need**: one very large bath towel."],"价":["price","The {Juggler} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Piazza} to buy an ice cream, but the vendor refuses to talk to him. A *go-between* runs back and forth, and a *standing person* shouts the new **price** each time: one coin, two coins, a hat, a goat. By the time they agree, the **price** is the juggler's entire act."],"花":["flower","On the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park}, the {Hunter} chases a *shape-shifter* through a patch of *grass*. It turns into a frog, then a snail, then, just as he pounces, a huge pink **flower**. He cannot shoot a **flower**, so he tucks it in his hat, and it winks at him all the way down the slide."],"党":["party","In the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, the {Dentist} finds his *big brother* wearing a *lampshade* on his head and leading a political **party**. Vote for free dental floss! he shouts, and the mice cheer. By midnight the whole basement has joined the **party**, and the dentist is elected Minister of Teeth."],"华":["splendid","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Water Park}'s tallest slide, and *fireworks* burst out of every step he touches. Gold, crimson, emerald: the whole park lights up in a **splendid** display. He whooshes down in a shower of sparks, and the crowd agrees it is the most **splendid** exit anyone has ever made."],"城":["city","On a mossy {Staircase} in the {Jungle}, the {Chef} piles up *soil* into walls and towers and plants a golden *trophy* on top. Monkeys move in, then parrots, then tapirs with briefcases, until it is a bustling **city** with traffic lights. The trophy goes to the best **city** in the jungle, which is also the only one."],"石":["stone","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} and trips over a *stone*. He kicks it, and it kicks back. Suddenly every step turns to **stone**, the honey turns to **stone**, and the bees bounce about as tiny grey pebbles. The sheriff is the only soft thing left, and the stones roll him gently back down."],"级":["level","The {Juggler} races up a {Staircase} cut into the cliff at the {Beach}, towed by a *silk thread* while a *chaser* thunders behind. Every step is a new **level**, like a video game: crabs on the first, seagulls on the second, a sandcastle dragon on the third. At the top **level**, the chaser turns out to be his own shadow."],"整":["whole","In a {Basement} under the {Jungle}, the {Jockey} watches a *drill sergeant* march the **whole** jungle up to a *goal line*: every ant, every elephant, every vine. Nobody gets left out! he barks. When a single leaf drifts behind, he marches the **whole** jungle back to the start to begin again."],"府":["government","In the {Basement} of the {Pool}, the {Firefighter} discovers a tiny marble *mansion* where frogs in suits are running the **government**. They pass laws about splashing and put taxes on rubber ducks. When she tries to drain the pool, the entire **government** hops out to hold an emergency meeting on her helmet."],"离":["to leave","The {Lifeguard} spots a *goblin* sneaking down the {Staircase} to the {Beach} and blows her whistle: **leave**, now! The goblin packs one sandcastle, two towels and a crab into a tiny suitcase. It waves goodbye, climbs onto a seagull and **leaves**, then comes back three times to wave again."],"况":["situation","The {King} pops up through a {Trapdoor} in the {Swamp} to find his *big brother* frozen in a block of *icicles*, croaking for help. What is the **situation**? asks the king. The **situation**, his brother explains, is that the swamp froze, the frogs went skating, and he is stuck as a rather royal ice lolly."],"亚":["Asia","The {Yogi} rises from a {Trapdoor} in the {Spa} wearing a *silver medal* the size of a frying pan. He won it in a race across all of **Asia**, stretching from one end to the other in a single yoga pose. Steam paints a giant map of **Asia** above the hot tub, and he lies down on it for a nap."],"请":["to invite","In the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Cheerleader} **invites** the whole town to a party, writing each card on soft green *moss* and handing it to a *small speech bubble*. The bubbles float off and squeak at every door, You are **invited**! By nine the basement is packed with boxers, grannies and one bewildered moose."],"技":["skill","The {Juggler} emerges from a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and balances a *branch* on his nose while a *helping hand* tosses him coconuts. He catches them on the twigs, one, two, ten, without dropping any. Pure **skill**! cry the crabs. Then the hand throws in a jellyfish, and his **skill** gets very wobbly indeed."],"际":["between","The {Juggler} pops up through a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach}, wedged **between** a *hillside* and a stone *altar*. He cannot move left or right, so he juggles straight up. Gulls dart **between** his juggling pins, crabs scuttle between his toes, and he stays squashed between the two until the tide floats him free."],"约":["appointment","On the {Rooftop} of the {Ice Rink}, the {Yogi} ties a *promise knot* in his beard to remember an **appointment**. Then he forgets what the knot is for. He ties another, and another, until his beard is a tangle of knots and he has missed every **appointment** in town, including the one with his barber."],"示":["to show","The {Sheriff} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds the bees gathered round an *altar*, where the queen is **showing** off her new crown under a spotlight. Then every bee **shows** something: a dance, a drawing, a jar of jam. Put on the spot, the sheriff **shows** them his badge, and they faint with admiration."],"复":["to return","The {Firefighter} slides through a {Trapdoor} at the bottom of the {Pool} and pops out in Antarctica. She grabs a ticket for the *return trip* and **returns** at once, dripping and snowy. But the trapdoor flings her off again, so she spends all day **returning**, with a penguin who is starting to enjoy the commute."],"病":["illness","The {Baker} drops through a {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} and lands on a *sickbed* balanced on a wobbly *tripod*. He has caught a strange **illness**: every sneeze shoots out a bread roll. The boxers duck and dodge the rolls, and the referee declares the **illness** the winner by knockout."],"息":["to rest","On the {Rooftop} of a lifeguard tower on the {Beach}, the {Shepherd} lies down with his sheep for a **rest**. Every slow *breath* he takes puffs out a tiny cloud, and the sheep float up onto them, snoring. Soon the whole flock is **resting** on clouds above the sea, and nobody wants to come down."],"究":["to investigate","The {Juggler} prises open the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} with a *crowbar* and finds a *cave* hidden in the attic, full of muddy footprints. He **investigates** with a magnifying glass, sniffing, measuring, tasting. The trail leads to a backpacker eating everyone's yogurts, and the juggler **investigates** him so closely that he confesses."],"线":["line","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, unrolling a *silk thread* behind him. *Twin blades* snip it into neat pieces, and he lays them across the trading floor in one dead-straight **line**. Every banker must now stand on the **line**, and the sheep patrol to check that nobody wobbles."],"似":["to seem","The {Sailor} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and spots a *standing person* holding a *tool*. It **seems** to be a spoon. Then it **seems** to be a trumpet, then a toothbrush, then a small grumpy hedgehog. Nothing is what it seems, and the bees insist the person only **seems** to be a person: really, it is a very large bee."],"官":["official","On the {Rooftop} of the bandstand by the {Swan Pond}, the {Gardener} meets an *official* in a tall hat, stamping papers. Every swan needs a permit to paddle, the **official** announces, stamping each beak. Soon the gardener needs a permit to garden, a permit to sneeze, and a permit to complain to the **official**."],"火":["fire","In the {Basement} of the {Warehouse}, the {Hunter} lights a tiny *campfire* to toast one marshmallow. The **fire** gobbles the marshmallow, then the bag, then a crate of fireworks. Whoosh! Rockets zoom round the basement, and the hunter roasts sausages over the **fire** while sprinting in circles."],"断":["to break","The {Dentist} rises through a {Trapdoor} in the {Swan Pond} and swings an *axe* at a stuck rowing boat. Crack! The oar **breaks**. Crack! The jetty **breaks**. He swings once more and **breaks** the boat, a bread roll and the swans' concentration, and they all sulk in pieces."],"精":["essence","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Juggler} boils *rice* and *moss* in a giant kettle until only one glowing drop remains: pure **essence**. He takes a single sniff and juggles faster than ever. The boxers below catch the smell and start dancing ballet, because the **essence** of everything, it turns out, is ballet."],"满":["full","In the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, the {Magician} taps a teacup and *water drops* start pouring out of it, endlessly. The cup is **full**, the sink is full, the basement is **full**, and the butler is swimming laps. The magician pulls a rabbit out of the water, and even the rabbit is **full** of water drops."],"支":["to support","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, the {Jockey} wedges a forked *branch* under the sagging ceiling just in time. The branch **supports** the roof, the queen's throne and a very heavy jar of honey. Then all the bees pile on top to cheer, and the branch groans, but keeps **supporting** them all."],"视":["to look at","The {Sheriff} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds a *watcher* kneeling before a *small altar* with a telescope on it. The watcher **looks at** the sheriff. The sheriff **looks at** the watcher. Then both slowly turn to **look at** the telescope, which, it turns out, has been looking at them all along."],"消":["to subside","On the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café}, the {Shepherd} paints a *portrait* of a stormy sea, and real *water drops* splash out of the canvas, flooding the roof. He paints a sun, and the flood **subsides**. He paints a sleepy cat, and the waves **subside** to a purr, then to a puddle that the cats lick dry."],"越":["the more","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Ice Rink}, and a *runner* skates out waving a *ceremonial axe*. **The more** she twirls it, the faster she skates; **the more** she skates, the louder the crowd cheers; and the louder they cheer, the more she twirls. Soon she is a whirlwind, and the yogi is very dizzy."],"器":["device","The {Cheerleader} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} with a strange **device** strapped to a *dog*: four horns and a crank. When the dog wags, the horns sing like a *chorus*, in perfect harmony. Sunbathers dance along, and the cheerleader patents the **device** as the world's first barking orchestra."],"容":["to contain","The {Robot} clanks down a {Staircase} into the {Lagoon} carrying an empty *container*. It scoops in fish, coral, a shipwreck, a whale and finally the whole lagoon. Somehow the container **contains** it all and still has room. The robot peeks inside to see what else it can **contain**, and falls in."],"照":["to shine","The {Jockey} climbs through the {Trapdoor} at the top of the {Tower} and blows on a pile of *embers* until they glow. He feeds them into a giant *spotlight*, and it **shines** over the whole city: bats squint, owls put on sunglasses. He points it at the moon, which starts **shining** twice as bright to say thank you."],"须":["must","On the {Rooftop} of the {Museum}, the {Shepherd} finds a *page* of rules tied to a brush full of stiff *bristles*. Rule one: every sheep **must** be brushed. Rule two: every sheep **must** be brushed again. So he brushes all forty sheep into fluffy clouds, because rules are rules and sheep **must** sparkle."],"九":["nine","In the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel}, the {Juggler} prises open a crate with a *crowbar*, and out pop exactly **nine** cats, each wearing a little backpack. Each cat has **nine** lives, so he does the sum while juggling them all: eighty-one lives, purring at once, and not one of them has paid for a bed."],"增":["to increase","On the {Rooftop} of a treehouse in the {Jungle}, the {Zookeeper} pours *soil* into a bamboo *steamer* and pops the lid on. Puff! The soil doubles. Puff! It doubles again. Each burst of steam **increases** the pile until it buries the treehouse and the monkeys open a ski resort, and still it **increases**."],"研":["to research","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} grinding a *stone* with a heavy *door bar*, doing **research** into what is inside it. Dust, more dust, a fossil, a tiny surprised snail. He writes it all up in a notebook, and the butler, inspired, starts doing **research** into the inside of the teapot."],"写":["to write","In the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, the {Shepherd} finds a yeti hunched over a *writing desk*, **writing** a long letter with an icicle. The ink freezes, so every word **written** pops off the page like an ice cube. The shepherd scoops them into a bucket and drops them in his tea, one sentence at a time."],"称":["to name","On the {Rooftop} of a temple in the {Jungle}, the {Chef} hangs a *wind chime* made of *grain stalks*, and every time it tinkles it **names** a passing animal. Bob! it chimes at a tapir. Gertrude! at a tiger. Soon every creature in the jungle has a **name**, and the chef has to write them all on a menu."],"企":["enterprise","In a {Basement} dug under the {Beach}, the {Cheerleader} finds a *person* standing beside a *stop sign*, running a tiny **enterprise**: selling stop signs to crabs. Business is booming. Soon the **enterprise** has offices, a logo and a board of crab directors, and every crab on the beach stops politely before crossing."],"八":["eight","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and whips open a pair of *curtains*. Behind them sit **eight** octopuses in fluffy bathrobes, each waving **eight** arms, and each arm holding a cupcake. The baker counts on his fingers: eight times eight, sixty-four cupcakes, and he still has to make the tea."],"功":["achievement","On the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon}'s lighthouse, the {Gardener} slams a giant marrow onto a *workbench*, and a *strong arm* hammers a gold medal onto it. Biggest vegetable in history! What an **achievement**! Fish leap out of the water to applaud, and the marrow is so proud of its **achievement** that it demands a statue."],"吗":["yes-no question","On the {Front Step} of the {Spa}, the {Magician} meets a *horse* with a huge *mouth* that turns everything into a **yes-no question**. Is it sunny, ma? Am I a horse, ma? Is this a spa, ma? The magician can only nod or shake his head, and after the hundredth **yes-no question** his top hat falls off."],"包":["to wrap","On the {Rooftop} of the {Tower}, the {Baker} **wraps** a *parcel* in brown paper, then **wraps** the paper in more paper, then wraps the string, the scissors and the pigeon watching him. By sunset the whole tower is **wrapped** up like a birthday present, with the baker somewhere inside."],"片":["thin piece","The {Pirate} kicks open the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and starts shaving a log into *wood slices*, each one a **thin piece** you can see straight through. He hands them out as treasure maps. The bankers hold every **thin piece** up to the light, but each map only shows another pirate slicing wood."],"史":["history","In the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, the {Sheriff} finds a dusty *historian* reading out the hive's entire **history**: the Great Honey Flood, the War of the Wasps, the year the queen sneezed. He has been talking for nine hundred years. The sheriff dozes off and wakes up as a footnote in **history** himself."],"委":["to entrust","In a {Basement} under the {Lake}, the {Wizard} **entrusts** his last *wilting stalk* of magic wheat to a frog. Keep it safe, he whispers. The frog guards it day and night, watering it, singing to it, fending off herons with a twig. By spring the stalk is a golden field, and the wizard **entrusts** the frog with his wand too."],"乎":["at","On the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, the {Hunter} blows a *whistle* **at** everything: **at** the swimmers, **at** the clouds, at a passing helicopter. Each blast blows its target backwards, so swimmers shoot out of the water and clouds wobble. Finally he blows it at himself and tumbles off the roof into the deep end."],"查":["to check","The {Chef} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} at *sunrise* with a clipboard and **checks** every *tree* in the garden: leaves, branches, birds' nests. Then she **checks** the bathtubs, the towels and the eyebrows of every sleepy guest. The manager asks what she is looking for. She checks her clipboard: breakfast."],"轻":["light","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Cheerleader} loads a *cart* with feathers, bubbles and dandelion fluff. It is so **light** that it floats off the roof like a balloon, with her clinging to the handle. She sails over the city, **light** as air, waving her pom-poms at astonished pigeons."],"易":["easy","The {Yogi} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and watches a *lizard* do every impossible yoga pose: a handstand on one claw, a pretzel, a backflip into a coconut. It looks so **easy**! He tries. He ties himself into a sailor's knot, and the lizard yawns: **easy** for some."],"早":["early","In the {Basement} of the {Tower}, the {Zookeeper} is woken at four in the morning by an *early bird* tapping on his forehead. It is far too **early**! He hides under the pillow, but the bird fetches a trumpet, a rooster and a marching band. By dawn the whole tower is up very **early**, eating cornflakes in the dark."],"曾":["once","The {Tsar} climbs a vine {Staircase} in the {Jungle} and finds an old bamboo *steamer* with a note inside: Here **once** lived a dumpling. He lifts the lid, and a cloud of steam acts out the tale of the dumpling who **once** ruled the jungle, before a monkey ate it. The tsar takes off his hat in respect."],"除":["to remove","The {Chef} stomps down the {Staircase} into the {Pool} with a shovel, because a whole *hillside* of *leftovers* has slid into the water: cold noodles, soggy chips, one lonely sprout. She **removes** it scoop by scoop, flinging it over the fence. The swimmers cheer, until she **removes** them too, by mistake."],"农":["farming","The {Ninja} creeps down the {Staircase} into the {Lagoon} and finds an underwater *farm*: sea cows grazing, crabs ploughing, octopuses milking clams. He swaps his sword for a pitchfork and takes up **farming**. By autumn he is harvesting seaweed in perfect silence, the stealthiest **farming** the lagoon has ever seen."],"找":["to look for","In the {Basement} of the {Tower}, the {Jockey} **looks for** his lost horse with a *halberd*, poking behind barrels and under rugs. A *helping hand* joins in, then the guards, then the cook. Everybody **looks for** the horse for hours, while the horse sits upstairs on the throne, nibbling the crown."],"装":["to adorn","On the {Rooftop} of a shack in the {Swamp}, the {Jockey} watches a *strongman* **adorn** himself in a silky *robe* covered in sequins, frogs and fairy lights. Not enough! he roars, and **adorns** the robe with a chandelier and a live heron. He glitters so brightly that the swamp's fireflies go home in shame."],"广":["wide","In the {Basement} of an old *shed* in the {Swamp}, the {Gardener} pushes on a wall and it slides back, and back, and back. The shed grows **wider** and **wider** until it holds a football pitch, three ponds and a herd of puzzled cows. The gardener still cannot find his rake in a room so **wide**."],"显":["to reveal","In the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, the {Shepherd} whips a cloth off a glass *showcase* to **reveal** its treasure: a single golden sheep. Gasps! He whips off another cloth to **reveal** another, and another, until his whole flock is **revealed**, sparkling, and the bankers start bidding for them."],"吧":["suggestion particle","On the {Front Step} of the {Spa}, the {Baker} meets a *python* whose smiling *mouth* tacks a soft **suggestion particle** onto everything: Let's take a bath, ba. Let's share a bun, ba. The baker cannot refuse such polite **suggestions**, so soon they are both in a bubble bath, eating buns, ba."],"阿":["name prefix","On the {Rooftop} of the {Spa}, the {Ghost} meets an *auntie* who sticks a cosy **name prefix** onto everyone: A-Ghostie, A-Towel, A-Steamy. She puts the **name prefix** on the masseur, the sauna and even the moon. The ghost is so flattered to be A-Ghostie that he stays for tea and cucumber slices."],"李":["plum","In a {Basement} under the {Beach}, the {Lifeguard} finds a *child* who has grown a *tree* in a sand bucket. It drips with purple **plums** the size of beach balls. The child hurls them like dodgeballs, and the lifeguard blows her whistle, catches a **plum** and eats it in one juicy slurp."],"标":["mark","On the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café}, the {Baker} squeezes an icing bag to **mark** everything: an X on the *tree*, a star on the *altar*, a smiley face on each cat. The cats are furious and **mark** him back with muddy paw prints, until he looks like a spotty dog."],"谈":["to talk","On the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, the {Tailor} sits by a crackling *blaze* and **talks** with a *small speech bubble* that talks back. They **talk** about buttons, then hems, then the meaning of life. The talk gets so heated that the bubble catches fire, and they carry on chatting through the smoke."],"吃":["to eat","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, the {Chef} serves dinner to a *beggar* with an enormous *mouth*. He **eats** the soup, the bread, the table and the tablecloth. Still hungry, he **eats** the chef's hat and three honeycombs, then politely asks what is for pudding."],"图":["picture","On the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, the {Tailor} paints a **picture** of a *winter coat* on a garden *fence*. It looks so real that the shivering swimmers try to put it on. He adds a scarf, then a mug of cocoa, until the fence is one huge **picture** of a cosy ski lodge, and everyone climbs inside."],"念":["to read aloud","The {Ninja} creeps up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and, instead of stealing anything, **reads aloud** a love poem to the giant *clock* with all his *heart*. The traders stop shouting to listen. He **reads aloud** a second poem, even louder, and the clock blushes and chimes thirteen."],"六":["six","The {Lifeguard} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Youth Hostel}, and a pair of giant *dice* tumbles out. Every throw lands on **six**. Six! Six! Six! The backpackers bet their socks, their snacks, their bunks. By midnight the lifeguard owns **six** beds, **six** sandwiches and six very smelly socks."],"引":["to pull","In the {Basement} of the {Inn}, the {Yogi} hooks a giant *bow* onto a *pole* and **pulls** back the string, slowly, breathing deeply. He **pulls** so far that the pole bends, the barrels roll and the innkeeper is dragged in by his apron. Then he lets go, and the whole cellar is fired into the garden."],"历":["to experience","The {Lifeguard} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach}, and a *strong arm* hauls her up a *cliff* for the **experience** of a lifetime: bungee jumping, eagle wrestling, a ride on a cloud. She comes back down with frizzy hair and a sunburnt nose, having **experienced** everything except a quiet afternoon."],"首":["head","In the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, the {Sheriff} finds a giant stone *head* wearing a captain's hat. The **head** opens its eyes and starts barking orders: row left, row right, polish my nose. The sheriff salutes, and the head, being the **head** of the boathouse, promotes him to chief oar."],"医":["medicine","On the {Rooftop} of a pier café on the {Beach}, the {Yogi} finds an *open crate* full of **medicine** and an *arrow* pointing at a sunburnt walrus. He spoons the **medicine** into its mouth. The walrus turns from lobster red back to grey, sings a little opera, and asks for a second spoonful."],"局":["office","On the {Staircase} of the {Museum}, the {Juggler} trips over a *lying man* who has set up his **office** right there: desk, phone and filing cabinet balanced on his tummy. People queue on the steps to get forms stamped. The juggler joins the queue, and by lunch he has a job in the **office**, juggling paperwork."],"突":["sudden","On the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, the {Tailor} is sewing quietly when a *dog* bursts out of a *cave* in the chimney with a **sudden** bark. He jumps so high that his needle shoots into the clouds. Then, all of a **sudden**, the dog sneezes, and the tailor tumbles into the deep end."],"专":["special","On the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond}'s tearoom, the {Jockey} turns a magic *spindle* that spins a **special** thread, softer than swan feathers. He weaves a **special** saddle for one very **special** swan, and the next morning that swan wins every race on the pond, with the jockey bouncing on its back."],"费":["to cost","The {Firefighter} opens a {Trapdoor} on a jetty in the {Lake}, and a crab with a *dollar sign* painted on its *shell* scuttles out with a bill. Rescuing a cat **costs** ten shells, it snaps. Sitting on the jetty **costs** five. Breathing costs one. By the time she leaves, the crab owns her helmet."],"号":["number","The {Hunter} pops through the {Trapdoor} at the top of the {Tower}, and a giant *mouth* blows out a *puff of breath* shaped like a **number**: seven. Then thirty-two. Then a million. The **numbers** drift over the city like clouds, and everyone below jumps up and shouts bingo."],"尽":["to the utmost","In the {Basement} of the {Inn}, the {Juggler} balances a *ruler* on his nose and juggles *two sparks* on top, pushing himself **to the utmost**. Sweat drips, the sparks fizz, the innkeeper holds his breath. Then he adds a teapot, straining **to the utmost**, and everything stays up until he sneezes."],"另":["another","The {Lifeguard} drops through a {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} with a bag of *spare parts*. Every time a boxer is knocked down, she bolts on **another** arm, **another** glove, another nose. By the last round one boxer has eight arms and wins by tickling, and the loser demands **another** match."],"周":["week","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse}, the {Jockey} rides a toy horse round a tiny *circuit*, one lap per day. Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday: after seven laps a whole **week** has gone by and his beard has grown. He keeps going, lap after lap, and the rowers mark each **week** with a chalk tally on his back."],"较":["to compare","The {Juggler} pops through a {Trapdoor} in the {Cat Café} and finds two cats sitting with *crossed legs* on a *cart*, **comparing** whiskers with a ruler. Then they **compare** tails, purrs and the number of naps they took today. The juggler measures himself too, and the cats agree he **compares** poorly: no whiskers at all."],"注":["to focus","The {Jockey} rises through a {Trapdoor} in the middle of the {Pool}, balancing a lit *candle* on his helmet while *water drops* splash all around him. He must **focus**. A beach ball bounces off his nose. He keeps his **focus**. A whale surfaces right beside him. He does not blink, and the flame never flickers."],"语":["language","In the {Basement} of the {Museum}, the {Yogi} finds a *speaker* blasting out a *small speech bubble* in a new **language** every second: Welsh, Swahili, dolphin, toaster. The mummies sit up and start chatting in a **language** nobody has spoken for four thousand years, mostly complaining about the dust."],"仅":["only","In the {Basement} of the {Inn}, the {Juggler} meets a *standing person* who juggles with **only** a *right hand*. Just one hand, and yet twelve plates, a cat and a bowling ball stay in the air. The juggler tries it with **only** his right hand and is promptly buried under a heap of plates."],"考":["to test","In the {Basement} of the {Tower}, the {King} sits at a tiny desk, sweating over an *exam*. The jester **tests** him on everything: crown polishing, banquet maths, how to wave. The king fails, so the jester **tests** the throne instead, which passes with top marks and gets to wear the crown."],"落":["to fall","The {Lifeguard} steps on a {Trapdoor} in the {Warehouse} and **falls**, straight through the floor, past the *grass* roots, past the worms, landing with a splash on an underground *riverbank*. Boxes **fall** after her, then a forklift, then a very surprised warehouse manager."],"青":["green","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Cheerleader} rolls across a carpet of fuzzy *moss* and stands up completely **green**. Her pom-poms are green, her teeth are green, even her cheers sound **green**. The boxers think she is a cheering cabbage and offer her salad dressing."],"随":["to follow","The {Sailor} stumbles down the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room}, and a *pilgrim* starts to **follow** him, step for step, out of the door and up a *hillside*. Then the patients **follow** the pilgrim, then the doctor, then a goat. At the top the sailor turns round to find the whole town behind him, and nobody knows where they are going."],"选":["to choose","In the {Basement} of the {Mint}, the {Shepherd} lines up his sheep at the start of a *road* painted on the floor. They race, and he must **choose** a *front runner* to win a golden coin. It is an eleven-way tie. He **chooses** all eleven, and the mint has to stamp eleven coins in a hurry."],"列":["to line up","The {Lifeguard} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Yeti Cave} and blows her whistle: everyone **line up**! Yetis shuffle into a *lineup*, tallest to shortest, then hairiest to baldest. One keeps sneaking to the front, so she makes them **line up** again by shoe size, and that takes all winter."],"武":["martial","In the {Basement} of the {Pool}, the {Wizard} trains a *warrior* in **martial** arts: kicks, chops, a flying somersault over the boiler. She is so good she can split a stack of floats with one finger. The wizard, deeply impressed, swaps his wand for a pair of nunchucks and signs up for **martial** arts classes."],"红":["red","On the {Staircase} down to the {Lagoon}, the {Hunter} sets up a *workbench* and dyes a reel of *silk thread* bright **red**. He wraps it round everything: the rocks, the boats, a startled flamingo. Soon the whole lagoon glows **red**, and even the fish start blushing."],"响":["sound","In the {Basement} of the {Stadium}, the {Shepherd} finds a *weathervane* with a huge *mouth* that makes a **sound** every time it spins: moo, honk, foghorn, opera. The crowd upstairs goes silent to listen. Then the wind picks up, and the **sound** gets so loud that the goalposts start dancing."],"虽":["although","On the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, the {Sailor} is cornered by a *mosquito* the size of a seagull. **Although** it is huge, it is very polite and asks permission before every bite. **Although** he says no, it waits patiently in the queue downstairs with everyone else, reading old magazines."],"推":["to push","On the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, the {Tailor} watches a *sparrow* try to **push** a sofa off the edge with its beak. A *helping hand* joins in, and together they **push** the sofa, a piano and a sleeping patient over the gutter, where they all land neatly on a trampoline."],"势":["power","The {Sheriff} kicks open the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and slaps *handcuffs* on a wasp, but its *strong arm* snaps them like spaghetti. Such **power**! The wasp flexes, lifts the hive and juggles three bears. The sheriff hands over his badge, because the wasp clearly has more **power** than he does."],"参":["to take part","On the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, the {Tsar} stumbles on a race between knobbly *ginseng* roots with tiny legs. Everybody **takes part**: the butler, the cook, the dog, a passing pigeon. The tsar cannot resist, hitches up his royal robe and **takes part** too, coming last behind a root."],"希":["to hope","On the {Rooftop} of a beach bar on the {Beach}, the {Shepherd} knits a giant net out of *lace*, **hoping** to catch a shooting star. He waits all night, **hoping** and hoping. At dawn a star finally drops in, tangled in the lace, and asks very politely to be put back."],"古":["ancient","In the {Basement} of the {Pool}, the {Gardener} digs up an *antique* rubber duck, cracked and furry with moss. It is **ancient**: carvings show pharaohs bathing with it. The duck opens one eye and quacks in an **ancient** language, demanding its bath at once."],"众":["crowd","The {Jockey} opens a {Trapdoor} on a raft in the {Lagoon}, and out climbs a *person*, then another *person*, then a third *person*, then hundreds more. Soon a whole **crowd** is squeezed onto the raft, cheering, waving flags and eating hot dogs. The raft sinks lower and lower, and the **crowd** goes for a swim."],"构":["to construct","The {Gardener} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, chops down a *tree* and uses a giant *hook* to swing the logs into place. He **constructs** a boat, then a bigger boat, then a floating castle with turrets. The ducks watch him **construct** a moat round it and ask where the drawbridge is."],"房":["house","On the {Staircase} of the {Hangar}, the {Firefighter} finds a single *door* standing in a chalk *square*. She opens it, and behind it unfolds a whole **house**: kitchen, bedrooms, a cat in the window. She steps in, the door clicks shut, and now the **house** lives inside the hangar, with planes parking in its garden."],"半":["half","The {Baker} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with a giant bread knife and saws every guest's dinner in *half*. Then he cuts the table in **half**, the piano, the chandelier. When the duchess complains, he slices her hat in **half** too, and she storms off looking like a boiled egg."],"节":["festival","On the icy {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave}, the {Juggler} plants a single blade of *grass*, and the yetis declare a **festival**. They hang lanterns, play icicle flutes and dance round the grass in party hats. It is the Grass **Festival**, the biggest night of the yeti year, and the juggler is crowned its king."],"土":["earth","In the {Basement} of the {Pool}, the {Tailor} measures a mountain of *soil* for a suit. He sews pockets of **earth**, buttons of pebbles and a worm for a tie. The suit stands up and strolls off, leaving a trail of **earth** across the tiles, and the cleaners chase it with a vacuum."],"投":["to throw","The {Tailor} stands on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse}, and a *helping hand* passes him a *war club*. He **throws** it like a boomerang: it knocks over three oars and a pigeon's hat, then whizzes back. He **throws** it again, harder, and this time it comes back holding a fish."],"某":["a certain","In the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, the {Magician} pulls a *plum* out of his hat and says it belongs to **a certain** someone. Who? He won't say. **A certain** someone with a beard. A certain someone who rows. Every rower in the boathouse blushes and claims the plum."],"案":["case","The {Ghost} floats up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with a magnifying glass to solve a **case**: who stole the *tree* from the garden? The clues lead to the attic, where the tree is hiding in a *safe home* with a teddy bear. **Case** closed, says the ghost, and tucks the tree in with a hot-water bottle."],"黑":["black","On the {Rooftop} of the {Lake}'s old pump house, the {Hunter} pokes the chimney, and a cloud of *soot* explodes all over him. He is **black** from boots to hat. The swans scream, thinking he is a giant **black** swan, and he spends the whole afternoon trying to explain."],"维":["to maintain","On the {Staircase} down to the {Lake}, the {Wizard} watches a *sparrow* **maintain** an old wooden bridge with nothing but *silk thread*: stitching cracks, tying loose planks, darning holes. Every morning it **maintains** the bridge again, and every evening the wizard trips over it anyway."],"革":["leather","On the {Staircase} of his {Hut}, the {Gardener} beats a strip of *rawhide* until it turns into soft **leather**. He makes **leather** boots, a leather hat and tiny leather jackets for his carrots. The carrots complain that they are too hot, so he gives them leather sunglasses as well."],"划":["to plan","The {Hunter} rises through a {Trapdoor} in the {Water Park} with a *halberd* and a *standing knife*, and scratches a **plan** onto the slide: here the ambush, there the escape. The ducks gather to admire his **plan**, then switch on the wave machine, and the plan floats away."],"敌":["enemy","On the {Staircase} down to the {Beach}, the {Dentist} meets his greatest **enemy**: a giant toffee with a sticky *tongue*. It licks his *cane* and glues it to the steps. He tugs, it pulls, and they wrestle all the way down to the sand. His **enemy** wins, and the dentist limps off with one boot stuck in toffee."],"致":["to cause","The {Jockey} taps the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} with his *cane*, and an *arrow landing* on the lid **causes** a chain reaction: the lid flips, honey splashes, a bear sneezes, a tree falls, and a cow ends up on the moon. The bees ask what **caused** it, and everybody points at the jockey."],"陈":["to display","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} up a grassy *hillside* facing *east*, and **displays** every cake she has ever baked on its steps. As the sun rises in the east, the icing gleams. Visitors gasp at the **display**, and a seagull swoops off with the top tier."],"律":["law","The {Lifeguard} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Museum} and follows muddy *footsteps* to a statue writing a new **law** with a giant *writing brush*: No running in the museum! She blows her whistle and adds a **law** of her own: no diving off the dinosaurs."],"足":["foot","On the {Staircase} into the {Pool}, the {Zookeeper} treads on a giant *foot*. It wiggles its toes. The **foot** belongs to an elephant trying to dip one **foot** into the water, very slowly, because it is cold. The zookeeper gives it a gentle push, and the whole pool sloshes out into the street."],"态":["attitude","The {Tailor} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Island}, and a *giant* with a tiny *heart* stomps out, sulking and kicking coconuts. What an **attitude**! The tailor sews him a waistcoat with a heart-shaped pocket. The giant admires himself in a puddle, and his whole **attitude** changes: he starts handing out coconuts."],"护":["to protect","The {Hunter} stands guard at the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} with a *door* for a shield, while a *helping hand* **protects** a nervous goldfish in a jar. Seagulls dive-bomb, pelicans swoop. The hunter swings the door, **protecting** the fish from every beak, and the goldfish sleeps through it all."],"七":["seven","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beach}'s ice-cream kiosk, the {Cheerleader} twists her body into a *bent cross* and shouts **seven**! Seven seagulls land on her arms. She twists again: seven crabs, seven kites, seven ice creams. In the end she is holding **seven** of everything and cannot move."],"兴":["interest","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} into a surprise *party* for his sheep. The boxers lose all **interest** in fighting and join in: musical chairs, pin the tail on the ram. Even the referee loses **interest** in the rules and dances the conga with a lamb."],"派":["group","The {Pirate} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Island}, and *water drops* gush out and split into streams that run off in different directions. Each stream is a **group** with its own idea: one heads for the sea, one for the cave, one for the pirate's boots. He tries to herd every **group** into his hat and ends up soaked."],"孩":["child","On the stone {Staircase} of the {Island} temple, the {Hunter} meets a *child* riding a *wild boar* like a pony. The **child** shrieks with joy, bounces down the steps and snatches his hat. The hunter chases them round the island, then gives up, because nobody can catch a **child** on a boar."],"验":["to test","The {Yogi} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a grand *assembly* of scientists **testing** a *horse*. Can it count? Can it knit? Can it do the splits? The horse passes every **test**, then turns round and **tests** the yogi, who falls over in his own pose."],"责":["duty","On the {Staircase} of his {Hut}, the {Zookeeper} is ambushed by a *debt collector* waving a clipboard. It is your **duty** to feed the penguins! he shouts. It is your **duty** to brush the lions! The zookeeper, guilty, sprints off to do every duty at once, with the collector ticking boxes behind him."],"营":["camp","On the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring}, the {Yogi} rolls out a carpet of *grass* and pitches a tent. Soon every boxer is setting up **camp**: sleeping bags in the corners, sausages on the ring posts, campfire songs at midnight. The referee joins the **camp** too, in pyjamas and a bow tie."],"星":["star","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Shepherd} catches a falling *star* in his crook. It is hot, so he juggles it, and it sprinkles glitter over his sheep. They glow all night, the crowd below thinks they are **stars**, and the shepherd's flock becomes the brightest **star** act in town."],"够":["enough","The {Gardener} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and finds a *quotation* written in moonlight above the water, under *many moons* hanging so low the boats glow. He picks one moon, then another, then another, then shouts **enough**! One moon is **enough** for anyone, and the rest float politely away."],"章":["chapter","On the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, the {Jockey} pins a shiny *badge* on each finished **chapter** of his memoir: The Horse Who Flew, The Saddle Disaster. Every **chapter** is folded into a paper plane, and he launches them one by one, until the whole city is reading his life story off their windscreens."],"音":["sound","On the {Rooftop} of the {Inn}, the {Yogi} hums, and *music* pours out of his ears like smoke. Every **sound** turns into a colour: a blue cello, a pink trumpet, a lime-green kazoo. Guests lean out of their windows to catch the **sounds** in jam jars and sell them at breakfast."],"跟":["to follow","On the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s ghost train, the {Gardener} finds a *kicking foot* that **follows** her everywhere. She gives it a fierce *glare*, but it keeps **following**, hopping behind her down the ladder, through the dodgems and onto the carousel, nipping at her heels the whole way."],"志":["ambition","The {Jockey} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds a tiny *scholar* bee with a huge *heart* and an even bigger **ambition**: to fly to the moon. It builds a rocket out of honeycomb. Everyone laughs, but the bee's **ambition** carries it up, up, past the clouds, waving a tiny flag."],"底":["bottom","In the {Basement} of a *shed* on the {Beach}, the {Dentist} digs through the *foundation*, looking for a lost tooth. Down, down, past crabs and pirate gold, to the **bottom** of the world, where an upside-down sea sloshes. At the very **bottom** he finds his tooth, resting on a velvet cushion."],"站":["to stand","The {Jockey} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} onto a *podium*, where a *fortune teller* tells him he must **stand** perfectly still for a hundred years to win a prize. He **stands**. Guests hang coats on him, pigeons nest in his cap. He keeps standing, and the prize turns out to be a chair."],"严":["stern","On the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, the {Yogi} meets a **stern** judge with a frown as steep as a *cliff*, who only ever hands out a *silver medal*, never gold. You blinked, she says. You breathed. Even the yogi's beard gets a **stern** look, and the medal seems to glare at him too."],"巴":["to long for","On the {Rooftop} of the {Spa}, the {Baker} watches a *python* gaze down at the hot tubs, **longing for** a warm soak. It sighs, it drools, it writes poems about bubbles. At last the baker lowers it in on a rope, and the moment it is wet, it **longs for** a towel."],"例":["example","The {Lifeguard} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and pulls a *standing person* out of the *lineup* of swimmers. Here is an **example** of how not to swim! she announces, as he flaps like a chicken. Then she shows a good **example**: a seal, who swims beautifully and gets a medal."],"防":["to defend","The {Firefighter} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and builds a fort on a *hillside*: a perfect *square* of sandbags. She **defends** it against water balloons, flying custard and a squadron of pigeons. She **defends** it so well that the pigeons surrender and ask to join her side."],"族":["nationality","On the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, the {Zookeeper} meets a *clan* of penguins, each holding a passport that shows its **nationality**: Emperor, King, Rockhopper. They squabble over which **nationality** gets the best diving board, and the zookeeper settles it by throwing a fish into the deep end."],"供":["to supply","On the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon}'s snack bar, the {Gardener} and a *standing person* form a chain of *joined hands* down to the water. Bucket by bucket, they **supply** the fish with lemonade and the turtles with crisps. Soon every creature wants more, and the **supply** runs dry by teatime."],"效":["effect","The {Shepherd} rises through a {Trapdoor} in the {Cat Café}, sits with *crossed legs* and taps a sleeping cat with a magic *cane*. The **effect** is instant: the cat sprouts wings and circles the lampshade. He taps another, and the **effect** spreads, until every cat in the café is hovering and purring like a little helicopter."],"续":["to continue","The {Shepherd} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Museum} and finds a *market stall* selling one endless *silk thread*. He pulls, and it **continues**: through the Egyptian room, past the dinosaurs, out of the door. Closing time comes, but the thread **continues**, so he keeps pulling all night and by morning has knitted a sock the size of a tent."],"施":["to carry out","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, the {Sheriff} gives a *snake* orders to **carry out**: slither round the *square*, salute, catch the wasp. The snake **carries out** every order perfectly, then carries out one of its own: it swallows the sheriff's hat whole and wears it as a lump."],"留":["to stay","The {Lifeguard} tries to leave down the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel}, but every backpacker presses a *keepsake* into her hands: a shell, a badge, a slightly chewed postcard. Please **stay**! they beg. Her arms are so full she cannot open the door, so she **stays** another week, then another year."],"讲":["to explain","In the {Basement} of the {Stadium}, the {Juggler} peers into a deep *well*, where a *small speech bubble* **explains** the offside rule. It **explains** it again, more slowly. It draws diagrams on the walls with chalk. By midnight the juggler finally understands, but the bubble has talked itself into a deep sleep."],"型":["type","On the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Shepherd} sits each sheep in a pair of wooden *stocks*, like a photo booth, and presses its face into wet *soil* to make a mould. Each mould is a **type**: curly, fluffy, grumpy, sleepy. He labels them all, and the boxers queue to find out which **type** of sheep they are."],"料":["material","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} with a giant *dipper* and scoops *rice* into a heap on the floor. It is building **material**: she glues the grains into bricks and builds a cat castle. The cats bring more **material**, yarn, feathers and a tin of tuna, and the castle grows a fishy tower."],"终":["end","On the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon}'s ferry office, the {Jockey} knits a *winter coat* from one *silk thread*, row after row, until at last he reaches the **end**. He ties it off. The coat is a hundred metres long and wraps round the whole lagoon. That is the **end** of the thread, and the end of the jockey's patience."],"答":["to answer","On the {Staircase} of the {Spa}, the {Dentist} finds a *bamboo* basket with a *fitted lid* that **answers** any question. Is flossing fun? Yes. Will it rain? Maybe. What is for dinner? Dumplings. Then he asks how to open it, and the basket **answers** by blowing a loud raspberry."],"紧":["tight","In the {Basement} of the {Inn}, the {Juggler} winds a *silk skein* round a barrel, round and round, pulling it **tight**. Then **tighter**. The barrel squeaks, the hoops creak, and the cork pops out like a cannonball. By now he has wound himself in so **tight** that he can only hop back upstairs."],"黄":["yellow","On a rickety {Staircase} in the {Swamp}, the {Hunter} trips and smashes a giant egg, and a flood of *yolk* pours down the steps. Everything turns **yellow**: frogs, lily pads, a startled crocodile. He climbs out **yellow** from head to toe, and a line of ducklings decides he is their mother."],"绝":["to cut off","On the {Staircase} into the {Ice Rink}, the {Juggler} finds a *rainbow* dangling by a single *silk thread*. Snip! He **cuts off** the thread, and the rainbow falls, shattering into coloured ice cubes. The skaters slide about on them, and the furious rink manager **cuts off** the juggler's free skating for life."],"奇":["strange","On the {Staircase} down to the {Beach}, the {Cheerleader} meets an *oddball* in a tuxedo made of seaweed, walking a lobster on a lead. How **strange**! He bows, offers her a sand sandwich and sings a love song to a jellyfish. Then it gets even **stranger**: the jellyfish sings back."],"察":["to examine","On the {Staircase} of the {Spa}, the {Chef} is stopped by a *detective* who **examines** her soup with a magnifying glass. He sniffs it, **examines** a noodle under a microscope, and interviews a carrot. Verdict: too much salt. The chef throws a cucumber slice at him, which he also examines, very carefully."],"母":["mother","In the {Basement} of the {Pool}, the {Magician} finds his *mother* knitting swimsuits for everyone. Wear a vest! she shouts, stuffing him into one. Like every **mother**, she has a towel, a snack and a plaster ready. When he pulls a rabbit from his hat, she knits it a jumper too, because she is everybody's **mother**."],"京":["capital","On the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, the {Juggler} builds a *palace* out of juggling pins and declares it the **capital** of Juggleland. Pigeons queue for passports, and clowns open embassies. Before long the boxers below demand that the **capital** move into the ring, and start fighting over it."],"段":["section","The {Dentist} opens a {Trapdoor} beside the {Swan Pond}, and a *blacksmith* climbs out and hammers a long iron bar into neat **sections**. Clang! One **section** for the bridge, one for the fence, one for the swans' new railings. The dentist takes the last section home as a giant toothpick."],"依":["to depend on","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beach}'s surf school, the {Yogi} balances on one toe, **depending on** a *standing person* to hold the hem of his *robe*. If the person lets go, he falls. The person sneezes, the yogi wobbles, and the surfers below realise they all **depend on** that sneeze never happening again."],"批":["to approve","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beach}'s pier, the {Pirate} sits with a giant rubber stamp while *twins* bring him plans: a sandcastle, a tunnel to the other side of the world. A *helping hand* stamps every one. He **approves** the castle, **approves** the tunnel, and accidentally **approves** the twins' plan to make him walk the plank."],"群":["crowd","On a sandy {Staircase} in the {Dunes}, the {Cheerleader} sees a *lord* in a velvet cape leading a huge **crowd** of *sheep* to a picnic. Thousands of them, baaing in chorus. She leads them in a cheer, and the whole **crowd** spells LORD with their woolly bodies, then wanders over to eat his cape."],"项":["item","The {Shepherd} pops through a {Trapdoor} in the {Stadium} with a *workbench* and a *page* listing every **item** he needs for the match: a whistle, a flag, ten thousand hot dogs. He ticks off each **item** as a sheep trots up with it, until the final item, the trophy, arrives in the mouth of a very proud lamb."],"故":["reason","The {Gardener} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Pool}, and a dripping *storyteller* climbs out to explain the **reason** the water is green: a frog prince, a lost slipper, a broken spell. Every time someone asks why, he invents another **reason**, until the swimmers forget the question and just float there, listening."],"按":["to press","The {Ghost} hovers over the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} as a *helping hand* **presses** a big red button marked *safe home*. Ding! The whole mansion folds itself up like a tent. The ghost **presses** it again, and the mansion springs back up, but upside down, with the butler standing on the ceiling."],"河":["river","On the {Staircase} of his {Hut}, the {Hunter} spills a cup, and the *water drops* will not stop: they trickle, gush and become a roaring **river** down the steps. A fisherman floats past on a log, his *nodding head* bobbing hello. The hunter grabs a paddle and rows his whole hut down the **river** to the sea."],"米":["rice","In a {Basement} under the {Beach}, the {Magician} waves his wand at a single grain of *rice*, and it multiplies: ten, a thousand, a million. Soon the basement is packed with **rice**, spraying out onto the sand like a fountain. Seagulls open a sushi bar, and the magician sits on a dune of **rice**, eating with chopsticks."],"围":["to surround","On the {Staircase} down to the {Lake}, the {Wizard} builds a *fence* and buckles each post with a *leather strap*. It grows and grows until it **surrounds** the whole lake. The ducks are **surrounded**, the fish are surrounded, and a swan files a formal complaint about being fenced in."],"江":["river","On the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium}, the {Juggler} bangs on a *workbench*, and *water drops* start running along the gutter, then pour into a great **river** that wraps round the stadium like a moat. The crowd paddles home in rubber dinghies, and the juggler juggles fish above the **river** for tips."],"织":["to weave","On the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, the {Jockey} watches a *lone bird* **weave** a nest from *silk thread*, in and out, faster than a sewing machine. It **weaves** a nest, then a hammock, then a tiny saddle for the jockey's horse. The bees grow jealous and start weaving tiny scarves of their own."],"害":["to harm","The {Hunter} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Island}, and a *pest* scurries out: a tiny beetle that **harms** everything it touches. It nibbles the palm trees, chews the hammock and bites holes in the boat. The hunter chases it with a net, but it **harms** the net too, and he ends up stranded while the beetle sunbathes in his hat."],"斗":["to fight","The {Dentist} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} waving a *dipper*, ready to **fight** a rower armed with a soup ladle. Clang! Bonk! They duel across the boats, splashing soup everywhere. The ducks place bets, and the **fight** ends only when both slip into the river and share what is left of the soup."],"双":["pair","On the {Rooftop} of the sheriff's office in the {Swamp}, the {Sheriff} holds up *both hands*: in each is a boot, a perfect **pair**. A frog steals one. So he grabs a **pair** of frogs instead, then a pair of crocodiles, and soon he is juggling pairs of everything, with both hands full."],"境":["surroundings","The {Juggler} pops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} for his grand *finale*, but the **surroundings** have changed overnight: *soil* everywhere, sunflowers tied to the ropes, cows in the front row. He juggles anyway, and his new **surroundings** cheer him on with a chorus of moos."],"客":["guest","The {King} opens the {Trapdoor} of a humble {Hut}, and a *guest* climbs in, then another, then a hundred **guests**, all expecting dinner. He gives up his throne, his crown and his slippers. The last **guest** takes his bed, and the king spends the night curled up in the bath."],"纪":["era","The {Juggler} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and hauls up a *coiled rope* with a *silk thread* tied to every knot. Each knot is an **era**: dinosaurs, pyramids, knights, the invention of ice cream. He unwinds it along the sand, and each **era** comes to life, until a dinosaur is queuing at the ice-cream van."],"采":["to pick","In the {Basement} of the {Island}'s palace, the {Tsar} meets a *fruit picker* who **picks** everything in sight: mangoes off the ceiling, coconuts off the walls, buttons off the tsar's coat. She **picks** his pocket too, finds a banana, and pops it in her basket with a satisfied nod."],"举":["to lift","In the {Basement} of the {Museum}, the {Juggler} is at a *party* for the statues when he decides to **lift** the heaviest guest, a marble lion. He bends, heaves, and **lifts** it high over his head. The statues cheer, and the lion, delighted, **lifts** the juggler in return and parades him round the room."],"杀":["to kill","On the {Rooftop} of the {Spa}, the {Sheriff} catches an *assassin* in a dressing gown, armed with a fly swatter. His secret mission: to **kill** every mosquito in the spa. Swat! Swat! He **kills** them all, and the guests sleep soundly for the first time in years, so the sheriff gives him a medal instead of handcuffs."],"攻":["to attack","On the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon}'s lifeboat shed, the {Gardener} is **attacked** by a seagull. She grabs her *cane*, leaps onto a *workbench* and **attacks** back, swinging wildly. The seagull calls its friends, and soon five hundred birds are on the attack, until she surrenders her sandwich."],"父":["father","The {Firefighter} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Pool}, and her *father* bursts out in a stripy swimsuit, doing a cannonball. Like any **father**, he tells terrible jokes, soaks the lifeguard and asks if anyone wants a sandwich. Everybody groans, but every other **father** in the pool joins him for one more cannonball."],"苏":["basil","On the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, the {Sailor} builds a *workshop* among the *grass* and grows giant **basil**. The leaves are as big as surfboards and smell so strong that swimmers float up the ladder, sniffing. He blends a pesto pool, and everyone swims in **basil**."],"密":["secret","The {Magician} slips through a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} into a *hideout* under a straw *roof*, where he keeps his **secret**: how the rabbit gets into the hat. He tells no one. A crab peeks in, sees the **secret**, and faints. Ever since, every crab on the beach walks sideways, too stunned to walk straight."],"低":["low","On the {Rooftop} of a changing hut on the {Beach}, the {Dentist} meets a *standing person* who keeps sinking into the sand, down past the *foundation*, **lower** and lower, until only his hat shows, very **low** indeed. The dentist lies flat on his tummy to check his teeth, the **lowest** check-up he has ever done."],"朝":["court","On the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, the {Chef} carries a cake up to the *royal court*, where lords bow and trumpets blare. The whole **court** falls silent as she lifts the lid. Inside is a tiny dancing king, and the **court** bows to the cake instead of the throne."],"友":["friend","In the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, the {Yogi} meets his new best *friend*: a walrus who also does yoga. They stretch together, meditate together, and get stuck in the same pretzel pose. Rowers try to untangle them, but a **friend** in a knot is still a **friend**, so they stay that way all summer."],"诉":["to tell","The {Sailor} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Pool}, and a *small speech bubble* floats up carrying a *chipped axe*. It **tells** the axe's story: it chopped an iceberg as big as a whale, lost a chip, and swore revenge. The sailor listens, then **tells** his own story back, and they both weep into the water."],"止":["to stop","In the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, the {Jockey} holds up a *stop sign*, and every bee **stops** dead in mid-air, buzzing on the spot like a little helicopter. The honey **stops** dripping and the clock **stops** ticking. Then he flips the sign, and they all zoom off at once, straight into his face."],"细":["thin","The {Shepherd} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and leads his sheep along a *silk thread* stretched over a flooded *rice field*. The thread is so **thin** that only skinny sheep can balance on it. The fluffy ones wobble and splash, so he shears them all, until the flock is as **thin** as noodles."],"愿":["wish","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Mint} and finds a *cliff spring* bubbling with coins. He throws one in, hand on his *heart*, and makes a **wish**: more coins. The spring gushes, and coins spray all over the mint. Now everybody wants a **wish**, and the queue goes round the block."],"千":["thousand","On the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, the {Cheerleader} coaches a squad of a *thousand ants*, waving pom-poms the size of crumbs. One **thousand** tiny voices chant, and they climb into an ant pyramid that spells out a **thousand** in the air. The bankers below gasp and drop a thousand pens."],"值":["worth","On the waxy {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, the {Jockey} meets a *standing person* dangling a *plumb line* over every honeycomb to see what it is **worth**. Straight comb: a gold coin. Wonky comb: a button. Then he dangles it over the jockey, frowns, and declares him **worth** exactly three jars of honey."],"仍":["still","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle}, where a *standing person* has been waiting for a hundred years with a pink *ribbon* tied round her nose. Monkeys tug it, parrots peck it, a hurricane blows through, and the *ribbon* is **still** there. The Robot checks again next century: she is **still** standing, **still** beribboned, and **still** annoyed."],"男":["male","The {Ninja} somersaults down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and lands in a ballroom packed with bearded *man* after bearded *man*. Every guest is **male**: the cook, the maid, the baby in the pram, even the cat has a moustache. A sign on the door reads **male** guests only, and the Ninja sticks on a fake beard to blend in."],"钱":["money","The {Cheerleader} high-kicks up the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} waving *twin blades* instead of pom-poms. Every kick slices a bar of metal into shiny *gold coins* that rain down the steps. The clerks scramble on their knees stuffing **money** into their socks, and the Cheerleader chants: give me an M, give me **money**!"],"破":["broken","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} riding a giant *stone* like a sledge. He lands right on the army drum, and its stretched *hide* splits with a boom. Now the drum is **broken**, the floor is **broken**, the Pirate's wooden leg is **broken**, and the general's afternoon nap is very much over."],"网":["net","The {Wizard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} and waves his wand at an old stone *archway*. Silver cords shoot out and knot themselves into a huge *lattice*, a fishing **net** stretched across the arch. A runaway jet plane rolls straight into it and bounces back, wriggling like a trout in the **net**."],"热":["hot","The {Robot} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lands, wrists locked in *handcuffs*, on a bed of glowing *embers*. The cuffs turn red, its metal bottom starts to sizzle, and steam pours from its ears. It's **hot**, so **hot** that the Robot cooks a fried egg on its own head while it waits for the key."],"助":["to help","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and is about to sink, horse and all. A *strong arm* bursts out of the water and props a *stepladder* against the side. The Jockey climbs out, then the horse climbs out, then a soggy duck. Everybody shouts thanks to the arm, which waves back, happy **to help**, always ready **to help**."],"倒":["upside down","The {Dentist} pops out of the {Trapdoor} at the top of the {Tower} feet first. A *standing person* waiting at the *arrival* gate grabs his ankles and holds him **upside down**, so all his drills and mirrors clatter out of his pockets. Soon the whole tower flips **upside down** too, and the visitors have to walk on the ceiling."],"育":["to raise","The {Yogi} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} clutching a tiny baby *moon* in a nappy. He feeds it moonbeams from a bottle, sings it lullabies and measures it on the wall each night. Slowly he helps **to raise** it until it is a full moon, so heavy he needs a crane **to raise** it up into the sky."],"属":["to belong to","The {Sheriff} wades into the {Basement} of the {Pool} where all his *kinfolk* are splashing about. Every one of them wears a rubber ring stamped with his family name. A lost inflatable flamingo floats by and he stamps it too: now it seems **to belong to** the clan. By sunset even the pool seems **to belong to** them."],"坐":["to sit","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} onto a crate where a *sitting pair* of gorillas are lounging. There is no room left, so he has **to sit** on their laps. A forklift beeps by and its driver also tries **to sit** down, and soon fourteen people are stacked on one crate, all perfectly comfortable."],"帝":["emperor","The {Dentist} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds a *sky god* sunbathing on a golden deckchair. The god wears a crown and a robe of clouds: he is the **emperor** of everything. He opens wide for a check-up and the Dentist finds every tooth is a tiny palace, because even the **emperor**'s teeth need somewhere grand to live."],"限":["to limit","The {Shepherd} herds sheep through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and up a steep *hillside* of banknotes. At the top an owl fixes him with a terrible *glare*: no further, this is the edge. Every time a sheep crosses the line the *glare* zaps its wool off. The owl's job is **to limit** spending, and also **to limit** sheep."],"船":["boat","The {Chef} sails down the {Staircase} of the {Swan Pond} in a *boat* made from a giant soup pot, stirring with an oar. The swans hop aboard demanding dinner, the **boat** tips, and spaghetti spills into the pond. The Chef just keeps rowing and calls it a cruise **boat**, buffet included."],"脸":["face","The {Lifeguard} dives into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} where an *assembly* of bankers stares up at a glowing *moon*. Its round pale **face** opens its eyes and winks. Every banker gasps, their mouths drop, and suddenly every **face** in the room turns the same silver colour, like a coin."],"职":["duty","The {Jockey} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, where a *lone bird* sits with one enormous *ear* pressed to the honeycomb. Its **duty** is to listen for the queen's orders and pass them on. The Jockey offers it a holiday, but the bird refuses with a salute: **duty** first, and anyway the bees bring snacks."],"速":["fast","The {Sailor} shoots out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands on a slippery *road*. Someone has tied a *bundle* of rockets to his back and he zooms off, **fast**, faster, waterskiing on the tarmac. Cars spin in his wake, and a snail at the roadside holds up a sign: too **fast**!"],"刻":["moment","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and comes face to face with a *wild boar* holding a *standing knife* like a clock hand. The boar carves a notch in the wall every **moment**, tick, tick, tick. The King stays perfectly still, because if he blinks he'll miss the exact **moment** the boar notices him."],"乐":["happy","The {Lifeguard} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lands in a nest of *joy bells*. They ring, jingle, clang, and everyone within a mile starts dancing. The grumpy farmer next door is suddenly **happy**, his cows are **happy**, and the Lifeguard swims laps across the floor out of pure delight."],"否":["to deny","The {Firefighter} storms into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} and asks the boats if they started the fire. A huge *mouth* on the wall opens and spits out a red *no sign*. Every boat holds one up. They all want **to deny** it, they **deny** everything, while smoke curls from the canoe's pocket."],"刚":["just","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} slicing the roof *ridge* with a *standing knife* to plant tulips in the crack. A plane lands right where the ridge **just** was. The Gardener shrugs, it's **just** a flower bed, then plants a tulip on the plane's nose."],"威":["power","The {Wizard} hovers over the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house, but a *woman* is already up there swinging an enormous *battle axe*. With one swing she splits the lake in two and the fish line up to salute. The Wizard drops his wand: her **power** beats his magic. Thunder rumbles, impressed by her **power**."],"毛":["hair","The {Magician} glides down the {Staircase} of the {Tower} and pulls a ball of *fur* out of his top hat. It keeps coming: metres of **hair**, then kilometres, a river of **hair** pouring down every step. At the bottom a bald man gratefully sticks a handful on his head."],"状":["shape","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swamp} onto a *split log* where a *dog* is chewing a branch. The dog carves the log into any **shape** you shout: a horse, a teapot, a crocodile. The crocodile carving comes to life and swims off, and the Jockey asks for something in the **shape** of a boat."],"率":["rate","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and casts a *dragnet* across the dinosaur hall. She counts what she catches every minute: three mummies an hour, five fossils a minute. A scoreboard flashes the catch **rate**, and the curator complains her **rate** of stealing is too high."],"甚":["even","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into an *overflowing bowl* of candyfloss that keeps on swelling. It covers the rides, the ticket booth, **even** the Ferris wheel. Then it covers the Sheriff, **even** his hat, **even** the tip of his moustache, until only his badge sticks out."],"独":["alone","The {Dentist} wanders up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} where a *prowling dog* guards a single tiny *bug* floating on a lilo. Everyone else has fled the water. The bug sunbathes **alone** in the whole pool, sipping a cocktail, and the Dentist decides to leave it **alone** too."],"球":["ball","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel}, where a *king* in a *fur coat* is rolled up into a perfect **ball**. She kicks him down the hall like a football, the hostel backpackers pass him around, and his crown pings off. He bounces happily, he's always wanted to be a **ball**."],"般":["kind","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} selling loaves to a *boatman* who rows by in the gutter. He wants every **kind**: rye, sourdough, rolls, buns, croissants. The Baker throws him one of each **kind**, and the boat sinks under the weight of the bread."],"普":["general","The {Pirate} kicks open the {Basement} of the {Pool} and floods it with *broad daylight* from his lantern. Suddenly everything is visible to everyone: the lost goggles, the socks, the shark. This is a **general** announcement, he roars, as the light spreads to every corner, the **general** public cheers."],"怕":["to fear","The {Pirate} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and lands in the mud bath, face to face with a *white dove*. His *standing heart* thumps so hard it rises out of his chest. He's always been terrified of birds. He has a hook and a sword, yet he dares not move, so great is his **fear**. Pirates aren't supposed **to fear** anything."],"弹":["bullet","The {Dentist} blasts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with a *bow* in one hand and a tennis *racket* in the other. He fires a **bullet** with the bow, then smacks it back with the racket, ping, pong, through every chandelier. The butler catches the last **bullet** on a silver tray."],"校":["school","The {Shepherd} crawls out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and finds a class in session under a *tree* growing through the floor. The cats sit with *crossed legs* on cushions, chalk on their whiskers, learning their sums. It's a **school**, and the Shepherd is the oldest pupil at the **school**."],"苦":["bitter","The {King} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Pool} and drinks tea from an *antique* cup filled with pond *grass*. His face crumples, his crown spins: it is so **bitter**! He spits it into the pool, which turns green and **bitter** too, and the frogs complain."],"创":["to create","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swamp} into a *barn* full of junk. He grabs a *standing knife* and carves, glues and hammers until he has made a robot alligator that cooks soup. He loves **to create** things nobody has ever seen, and tomorrow he plans **to create** a soup that cooks alligators."],"假":["fake","The {Juggler} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Piazza}, where a *standing person* is handing out a *borrowed tool*: a plastic hammer. Everything here is **fake**: the gold is chocolate, the statues are cardboard, the pigeons run on batteries. Even the Juggler's balls turn out to be **fake**, they're painted grapes."],"久":["long","The {Juggler} curls up in the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel} under a *blanket* and falls asleep for a **long** time. The cleaner comes every year to *sweep* round him, then decades pass and a beard grows over the floor. He wakes up, yawns, and asks how **long** he slept."],"错":["wrong","The {Tsar} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and starts paying the workers in *sun-dried meat* and bacon. Then he feeds the dogs *gold coins*. Everything is **wrong**, totally **wrong**: the workers chew the coins and the dogs buy a sofa."],"承":["to bear","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} with *three planks* balanced on his head. Two *lifting hands* reach out of the ferns to help him **bear** the weight, but then they pile on a gorilla, a hippo and a wedding cake. He has **to bear** it all the way to the top."],"印":["to print","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} and lands on a *kneeling man* who has been dipped in ink. Every time the man bows, he stamps himself on the floor. The Yogi uses him **to print** posters of himself all over the walls, until even the guests have a little **print** on their foreheads."],"晚":["evening","The {Wizard} hides in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} while a sly *dodger* sneaks off with the *sun* in a sack. Without it, it's suddenly **evening**: the lamps flicker on, the bats wake up. The Wizard chases the dodger round the boiler room, but it stays **evening** forever."],"兰":["orchid","The {Lifeguard} slides down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} into a jungle of *orchids*. Each **orchid** sniffs, coughs and demands a glass of water. She rushes around with her whistle, saving drowning flowers in the vase, and finally pins the prettiest **orchid** to her red swimsuit."],"试":["to try","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and holds a *stencil* of a bee. A *small speech bubble* pops out: wanna buzz? He paints himself yellow and black **to try** flying, flapping his arms. The bees giggle, but he'll **try** again tomorrow."],"股":["stock (share)","The {Gardener} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Pool} and smashes a *war club* on a slice of the *moon*. It shatters into a hundred little pieces, each a **stock** certificate, a share of the moon. Bankers dive into the pool to grab them, shouting: buy **stock** now, sell later!"],"拿":["to hold","The {Ninja} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and a giant *hand* bursts from a jar under a *fitted lid*. It grabs his sword, the towels and a bucket of mud. The hand will not let go: it loves **to hold** things, and wants **to hold** the Ninja next."],"脑":["brain","The {Ninja} slips into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and finds a glowing *moon* sitting in a jar with wires sticking out. It's a giant **brain**, thinking out loud, solving puzzles and writing poems. The Ninja tries to steal it, but the **brain** guesses his plan and locks the door first."],"预":["in advance","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} with an *offering* of fruit and a *page* from tomorrow's newspaper. He knows everything **in advance**: the vase will fall at noon, the guard will sneeze at one. He puts cushions under the vase **in advance**, and hands the guard a tissue."],"谁":["who","The {Sheriff} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house, where a *sparrow* is shouting a *small speech bubble* at every passer-by: **who**? **Who** are you? **Who** stole my worm? The Sheriff shows his badge, the sparrow points a wing at the duck."],"益":["benefit","The {Yogi} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} carrying a *spilling dish* of vitamins. Everything they splash on gets better: a starfish grows an extra arm, a sandcastle turns into a real castle. It is all **benefit**, pure **benefit**, and the seagulls line up for a sip."],"阳":["sun","The {Yogi} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar}, to the top of a *hillside* where a *sun* is stuck in the mud. He heaves and pulls until the **sun** pops out like a cork and rises. Planes take off wearing sunglasses, the **sun** shines into every hangar."],"若":["to seem","The {Robot} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and meets its *lookalike*: another robot, exactly the same, except it's made of cardboard. It **seems** real, it **seems** to beep, it **seems** to think, and nobody can tell them apart. The boss gives the cardboard one the promotion."],"哪":["which","The {Ninja} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Spa} where a huge *mouth* floats over three identical hot tubs. A *pointing finger* swings between them like a compass: **which** one? This one? That one? The Ninja jumps into the wrong tub, it fizzes like lemonade, and the mouth keeps asking **which**, **which**, **which**."],"微":["tiny","The {Wizard} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house and follows a trail of *footsteps* no bigger than rice grains. They lead to a **tiny** army of ants carrying a **tiny** cake. He shrinks himself to join the party and gets lost inside a crumb."],"尼":["nun","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} and bumps into a *nun* surfing down the steps on an ironing board. The **nun** does a backflip, lands in a sandcastle and starts praying for bigger waves. The Ninja bows: this **nun** is stealthier than any ninja."],"继":["to continue","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} spinning a *silk thread* that never ends. He knits a scarf, then a jumper, then a blanket for the whole beach, and he can't stop. Night falls and he has **to continue**, the crabs bring him tea so he can **continue** till dawn."],"送":["to deliver","The {Sailor} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} with a pizza box and races along a winding *road* over a snowy *mountain pass*. Wolves chase him, avalanches tumble, but he must **deliver** it hot. He knocks on the door of an igloo **to deliver** it, and the penguin inside refuses to tip."],"急":["urgent","The {Juggler} scrambles up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} with a *racing heart* banging out of his chest like a drum. The tide is coming, his juggling balls are rolling into the sea, the ice cream van is leaving: it's all **urgent**! He sprints in circles yelling **urgent**, **urgent**, and drops everything."],"血":["blood","The {Shepherd} skates through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} carrying a *dish* and a single red *drop*. It's a vampire's dinner: one *drop* of **blood** on a fancy plate. The vampire on skates sips it with a straw, says it needs salt, and the Shepherd blushes **blood**-red."],"惊":["to startle","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} when a whole *palace* pops up out of nowhere in the ring below. His *standing heart* leaps so high it bonks him on the chin. Fireworks bang, he drops his clubs, and the boxers are **startled** too: nothing can **startle** a crowd like a surprise palace."],"伤":["injury","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} as a *standing person* topples off a plane wing and lands on him. Ouch, an **injury**! Now both have bandaged ankles, bruised elbows and a broken pride. The ambulance arrives, sees one more **injury** on the roof, and calls for a second ambulance."],"素":["plain","The {Sailor} sinks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a *seedling top* sprouting from a ball of white *silk skein*. Nothing else: no colours, no pattern, no flavour. The whole pool is **plain**, the water, the tiles, even his sandwich is **plain** bread."],"药":["medicine","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a garden of magic *grass* tied in a *promise knot*. He boils the knot into green soup, swallows it and his sneeze vanishes. It's **medicine**, and the knights queue up for a spoonful of **medicine**."],"适":["to fit","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} onto a *road* made of a giant sticky *tongue*. Every shoe that steps on it gets licked into the right size. His old boots finally **fit**, his hat **fits**, and even the bees' tiny shoes now **fit**."],"波":["wave","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} throwing dough into the sea, and a huge *wave* comes back made of custard. The **wave** sweeps the soldiers off the wall and into the moat, and the next **wave** brings sprinkles."],"夜":["night","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and the lights go out: it is pitch black *night*. Owls hoot, the moon peeks through the chimney, he lights a candle and meditates all **night**. In the morning the hut is still dark, because the **night** liked it there."],"省":["to save","The {Sheriff} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Jungle} with one beady *eye* on every penny. He takes a tiny *pinch* of rice for dinner, a pinch of water, a pinch of light. He wants **to save** everything, and he does **save** so much that the jungle gives him a medal."],"初":["at first","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} with a *knife* and a brand-new *shirt*. Before any cooking, before any swimming, **at first**, he cuts out a pattern. Everyone asks why. **At first** you sew the apron, he says, and then you can fry the pool."],"喜":["to like","The {Shepherd} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Beach} and starts banging on a *joy drum*. The sheep start to dance, the crabs clap, the shells hum: they all **like** it. The Shepherd decides he must **like** drumming too, and plays all night."],"卫":["to guard","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and stands a *plank* upright in front of the door. He casts a spell and the plank comes alive, salutes, and begins **to guard** the house with a little wooden sword. Ducks try to sneak in, but the **guard** sends them off."],"源":["source","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, following *water drops* upward. At the top a *cliff spring* gushes coins instead of water. That's the **source** of all money, he realises, and the bankers fill their buckets at the **source**."],"食":["food","The {Sheriff} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} and finds *food* everywhere: honey pies, pollen pizzas, waxy sandwiches. The bees have built a restaurant. He eats so much **food** that he gets stuck in the door, and the bees bring more **food** to cheer him up."],"险":["danger","The {Shepherd} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, down a slippery *hillside* of coins. At the bottom an *assembly* of snarling wolves in suits waits. **Danger**! He tiptoes, holding his breath, every step a **danger**, until the sheep pull him back with a rope."],"待":["to wait","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} into a *temple* where a line of *footsteps* stops at a bench. He has **to wait**, and he waits for a year, two, a decade, until a palm tree grows from his head. A sign reads: please **wait**, the dentist will see you soon."],"述":["to tell","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a *road* where a performer is doing a *magic trick*. The magician won't stop talking: he loves **to tell** how the trick works, every single detail. The Sheriff begs him to stop, but he has more **to tell**."],"陆":["land","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and swims for hours until she reaches a *hillside*. She gives the sand a *punch*: it is solid! **Land**! She plants a flag and declares the pool's bottom a new **land**, and the ducks apply for citizenship."],"习":["to practise","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} flapping a *single wing* he found in the sand. He flaps, falls, flaps, falls, for hours, every day. He must **practise**, the seagulls laugh, but he goes on **to practise** until he hovers one inch in the air."],"置":["to place","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} holding a *fishing net* and a *plumb line*. Using the line he works out exactly where **to place** each honeycomb, then he scoops them up with the net and **places** them straight, in perfect rows."],"居":["residence","The {Juggler} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} and builds a tiny *house* out of his juggling clubs. It is his new **residence**, with a doorbell made of a juggling ball. The curator writes it down as the museum's smallest **residence**, and charges him rent."],"劳":["to toil","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, where a sweaty *labourer* is carrying the building up stone by stone. He does not stop **to toil**, he toils all day and all night. The Lifeguard brings him a lemonade, and even that he carries **to toil**."],"财":["wealth","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} and finds a *shell* with a *green shoot* growing out. Every leaf on the shoot is a banknote! He waters it with champagne and soon the whole island is covered in **wealth**, and he's the richest man in the sea, with **wealth** sprouting from his ears."],"环":["ring","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Swan Pond} and finds a *king* holding a *no sign*. The king pulls off his crown and flings it onto the pond, where it turns into a golden **ring** floating on the water. Swans swim through the **ring** like circus lions."],"排":["to line up","The {Pirate} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Island} and a *helping hand* shoves all the parrots into a row, their *spread wings* touching. The Pirate barks orders and everyone must **line up**: crabs, coconuts, even the treasure chests **line up** neatly."],"福":["good fortune","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a *small altar* with a *full jar* of golden coins. She bows to it, and luck rains down: she finds keys, socks, a winning ticket. It's **good fortune**, and the pool turns into a fountain of **good fortune**."],"纳":["to accept","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} into an *inner room* tied up with *silk thread*. Guests hand him their gifts, and he must **accept** every one: a teapot, a towel, a wet frog. He nods politely to **accept** each one until the room is full."],"欢":["joyous","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} and lifts his *right hand* as the swans give an enormous *yawn* that turns into a laugh. The whole pond is **joyous**, swans dancing, frogs singing. The Hunter puts down his bow and joins in, **joyous** as a child."],"雷":["thunder","The {Lifeguard} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house as *rain* pours onto the *rice field* behind it. **Thunder** booms so loud the rice jumps out of the mud, and the Lifeguard blows her whistle at the clouds. The **thunder** answers with a burp."],"警":["police","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} until a *speech bubble* bursts through the ceiling: STOP! A crisp *salute* follows. The **police** have arrived, an officer in each corner of the ring, and they arrest the Juggler for juggling **police** hats."],"获":["to obtain","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into *grass* where two dogs are having a *dog fight* over a bone. He reaches in, grabs it, and wins: he manages **to obtain** the bone! Both dogs turn and chase him, so now he will have **to obtain** a bigger bone."],"模":["model","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort}, where a *tree* glows against a dramatic *sunset*. He snaps his fingers and the tree poses, chin up, like a fashion **model**. The soldiers paint it, sculpt it and build a tiny **model** of it in clay."],"充":["to fill","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hut pumping air into a *balloon*. He wants **to fill** it with soup, then air, then more soup. It swells, bigger and bigger, filling the sky, until the lagoon floats away. He begs it **to fill** no more."],"负":["to bear","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} wearing a huge *backpack* stuffed with hoses, fire engines and three grandmothers. She must **bear** it all, and she does, swimming laps with it. Nobody else can **bear** such a load."],"云":["cloud","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Dunes} and sits on a fluffy *cloud* parked there like a taxi. The **cloud** lifts off, raining on the hot sand and growing cacti on its way. He waves down to the camels from his **cloud**."],"停":["to stop","The {Tailor} races up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} where a *standing person* is sheltering under a *pavilion*. He's shouting **stop**! at the boxers, who all freeze mid-punch. The Tailor measures them while they **stop**, and sews them matching shorts."],"木":["tree","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and pulls a *tree* out of his hat. Then another **tree**, and another, until the pool is a forest and the swimmers are in the branches. The lifeguard asks for one more **tree** to hang his whistle on."],"游":["to tour","The {Yogi} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} on a stream of *water drops*, waving a long *streamer* like a tour guide. He wants **to tour** every boat, and the tourists follow his streamer from canoe to yacht. Next he plans **to tour** the duck pond."],"龙":["dragon","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut and finds a *dragon* doing laps in the water. The **dragon** breathes fire and boils the lagoon into a hot tub. The Lifeguard blows her whistle, so the **dragon** puts on armbands and swims slower."],"树":["tree","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a *tree* waltzing with its *dance partners*, two other trees. They twirl their branches, drop their leaves, and splash. He arrests the most reckless **tree** for dancing in a pool, but the **tree** just keeps dancing in jail."],"疑":["to doubt","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} making a *puzzled face* at the sea. Is it real? Is the sand real? Is he real? He starts **to doubt** everything, then he begins **to doubt** his doubts, and the crabs give up waiting for an answer."],"层":["layer","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} and finds a *lying man* sleeping on a *cloud*. On top of him sleeps another man on a cloud, and another: **layer** after **layer** of sleepers stacked up to the treetops like a cake."],"冷":["cold","The {Lifeguard} dives into the {Basement} of the {Jungle} where *icicles* hang from the vines. A shivering *herald* blows a trumpet and announces: it's **cold**! So **cold** that the monkeys wear scarves and the parrots freeze mid-squawk. The herald's trumpet note itself freezes and drops to the floor with a clink."],"洲":["continent","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} while *water drops* fall onto a map and form *islands*. They join up, grow and spread, until a whole **continent** appears and his horse can gallop from one coast to the other of a new **continent**."],"冲":["to rush","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hut, slides down a chute of *icicles* and aims at a *bullseye* painted on the water. He has **to rush**, faster and faster, ladle first, and hits it dead centre with a mighty splash. The fish **rush** off to tell their friends."],"射":["to shoot","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut}, where an *archer* is aiming at his hat. The archer lets go and the arrow zips past, so the Sheriff draws his pistol **to shoot** back. They **shoot** at each other all afternoon, but only ever hit the teapot."],"略":["outline","The {Lifeguard} skates through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} and finds a *visitor* drawing a map of a *rice field* on the ice. He only scratches the **outline**: four lines, no details, no rice. The Lifeguard adds a duck, and the visitor yells that it's just an **outline**!"],"范":["model","The {Firefighter} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} as a *flood* pours in and lays *grass* in a perfect pattern across the ballroom. Everyone gasps: it's the **model** of a perfect garden. The Firefighter sprays her hose to copy it, and now every guest wants a **model** lawn."],"竟":["unexpectedly","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} right during the *finale*. Everyone thinks the champion will win, but **unexpectedly** the Juggler knocks him out with a juggling ball. The crowd gasps, and **unexpectedly** the referee gives the belt to a pigeon."],"句":["sentence","The {Juggler} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and catches a *quotation* flying out of an old book. Each word is a ball, and he juggles them into a **sentence**: the cat sat on the king. The king, in a nearby portrait, objects to the **sentence**."],"室":["room","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and sees an *arrow landing* under a *roof* of wax. Where it lands, a **room** appears with walls, a bed and a little lamp. The bees fire more arrows, building a **room** for every guest."],"异":["different","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} and finds a *cobra* sitting in the *grass* wearing a tutu. Everything here is **different**: the sea is purple, the sand tastes of mint, the crabs walk forwards. The Yogi meditates upside down, just to be **different** too."],"激":["to arouse","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut juggling *water drops* that throw off a *sparkle* each time they fall. The sparkles **arouse** the sleepy seagulls, who start dancing. Each drop is sure **to arouse** more excitement, until the whole beach is awake and cheering."],"汉":["Han","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and splashes into *water drops* pouring from a *right hand* painted on the ceiling. They spell out the river name **Han** in shiny letters. He writes **Han** on his hat and rows down the hallway."],"村":["village","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} and balances a whole *tree* on his *thumb*. A tiny **village** sprouts in its branches: huts, a well, a market, chickens clucking. The gamblers stop playing cards and bet on which **village** chicken will lay the first egg, and the Tsar wobbles to keep everyone from falling out."],"哈":["ha","The {Hunter} climbs on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and lifts the *fitted lid* off a hot tub. A giant *mouth* inside lets out a booming laugh: **ha**! **Ha**! The bubbles laugh too, the towels giggle, and the Hunter falls off the roof laughing."],"策":["plan","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lays out a battle **plan** using *bamboo* sticks and a sharp *thorn* as pointer. Sticks are soldiers, the thorn is the general. The mouse at his feet suggests a better **plan**."],"演":["to perform","The {Yogi} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and finds a stage lit by a *temple arrow* and dripping *water drops*. He must **perform** a play, so he bends into a pretzel, sings opera and juggles cucumbers. The rats throw roses: they love **to perform** too."],"简":["simple","The {Juggler} climbs into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} where the bankers are lost in complicated spreadsheets. He strings a *bamboo* curtain across a *gap* in the wall and draws one line on it: buy cheap, sell dear. It's **simple**, so **simple** that the bankers cry and frame it."],"卡":["card","The {King} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Spa}, where a *fortune stick* points *upstairs*. He climbs and finds a **card** stuck between the floors: his own credit **card**, wedged there for years. He prises it out and buys a mud bath."],"罪":["crime","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a parrot with *spread wings* caught in a *fishing net*. The parrot has stolen all the magazines, a terrible **crime**! The Zookeeper reads out the list of each **crime**, and the parrot pleads innocent in three languages."],"判":["to judge","The {Pirate} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and sees two lords fighting over a cake. He draws a *standing knife* and cuts it exactly in *half*. Both are pleased. Everyone asks him **to judge** every quarrel in the house, and he must **judge** fairly or walk the plank."],"担":["to carry","The {Dentist} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} while a *helping hand* lifts a glowing *sunrise* onto his shoulders. He must **carry** it across the roof without dropping it. It's heavy and hot, but he manages **to carry** it all the way to the chimney, and morning begins."],"州":["state","The {Jockey} gallops along the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse}, jumping from one of the *islands* to the next in a river. Each one is a **state** with a flag and a mayor. The Jockey is crowned governor of every **state** and gives his horse a seat in parliament."],"静":["calm","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} into a soft bed of *moss*, where two boxers are frozen in a *tug of war*. Nobody moves. Everything is **calm**, perfectly still, not a whisper. The Juggler drops a ball and the crowd glares, so **calm** is the room."],"退":["to retreat","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, sees a queue of four hundred grumpy people, and makes an instant *u-turn*. He must **retreat**, walking backwards with needles blazing. One by one everyone in the room begins **to retreat** too, shuffling backwards out of the door, until the receptionist sits alone with the magazines."],"既":["already","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} with a hamper, but all he finds is a *finished meal*: empty plates, chicken bones, one sad crumb. The seagulls have **already** eaten everything, sandwiches, cake and the napkins. He's **already** too late, and the fattest gull burps politely and asks what's for pudding."],"衣":["clothes","The {Yogi} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut wearing a giant *robe*. He pulls out more **clothes**: a scarf, socks, a ball gown. He dresses the seagulls, the crabs and the sun, and soon the beach is full of **clothes**."],"您":["you (polite)","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Inn}, bowing to every guest with his *heart* in his hand. To each *you* he says a polite **you**: after **you**, sir; thank you, madam. Even the mice get bows, and they bow back."],"宗":["sect","The {Zookeeper} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hut and finds an *ancestral hall* full of monkeys in robes chanting. They are a **sect** that worships bananas. The Zookeeper joins the **sect** and soon chants with a banana on his head."],"积":["to accumulate","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut as a *lone bird* drops one *grain stalk* after another onto his head. He doesn't move. Year after year the grain starts **to accumulate**, into a haystack, then a mountain. He wears a hat of **accumulated** grain."],"余":["surplus","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} carrying a tray of *leftovers* from the great feast. There is too much: **surplus** pies, spare sausages, extra cake. He hands the **surplus** to the statues, who are delighted to eat for the first time in centuries."],"痛":["pain","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} hut onto a *sickbed* inside a dark *tunnel*. Ow, ow, ow! He's sat on his own pins. The **pain** shoots up, and he rolls over onto more pins. **Pain**, pain, pain, until the doctor arrives with tweezers."],"检":["to check","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} as an *assembly* of inspectors marches in, each holding a magnifying glass. They climb every *tree* of coins **to check** each one for fakes. They **check** the Juggler's balls too, and find a fake grape."],"差":["short of","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and finds a *sheep* at a *workbench*, trying to bake a cake. It's **short of** sugar, **short of** eggs, short of time. The Chef gives it his last egg, and now he's **short of** dinner."],"富":["rich","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a house where the *roof* shelters a *full jar* of gold. She sprays it with water and it overflows, gold everywhere! Now she's **rich**, so **rich** that she buys a golden fire engine."],"灵":["quick","The {Lifeguard} bounds up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} with a *comb* that she runs through the flames of a *campfire*. The fire turns **quick** and nimble, darting and dancing like a boxer. The Lifeguard herself becomes **quick**, dodging punches with a wink."],"协":["to cooperate","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} and finds a *cross* carved on the door of a *workshop*. Inside, yetis must **cooperate**: one saws, one hammers, one paints. They **cooperate** so well they build a sleigh in five minutes."],"角":["corner","The {Juggler} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} and finds an *ox horn* poking out of every **corner**. The cats each sit in a **corner**, fighting over the horns. The Juggler juggles them, and the cats sulk in their corners."],"占":["to occupy","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and a *fortune teller* is sitting in every chair, every bath, every bed. She moved in uninvited and plans **to occupy** the whole house. She even manages **to occupy** the Jockey's saddle."],"配":["to match","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house with a *wine jug* and a *coiled rope*. He tries **to match** them: jug and rope, cup and saucer, boot and sock, shark and teeth. Everything finds its partner, and he's left without a **match**."],"征":["to recruit","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple and blows a horn to start a *march*. Monkeys, tigers and parrots come running. He wants **to recruit** them all for his army, and they **recruit** each other in a long parade."],"修":["to repair","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} with a hammer, a needle and a roll of tape. Everything is broken: the chimney, the satellite dish, the backpackers' socks. He sets out **to repair** them all, sewing, nailing, taping, until he must **repair** the hammer too."],"皮":["skin","The {Pirate} hops up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} with a crocodile *hide* slung over his shoulder. He unzips it and steps in, wearing the **skin** like a onesie. The crocodile pops out of the sea and demands its **skin** back."],"挥":["to wave","The {Hunter} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, and a *helping hand* gives him a flag to signal an *army* below. He starts **to wave**, and the soldiers march left, then right. He **waves** too fast, and the army ends up dancing the conga."],"胜":["victory","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} under a full *moon* and sees a *seedling* racing a tree. The **victory** goes to the seedling, which grows a mile in a night! The Sheriff pins a medal on it for its **victory**."],"降":["to fall","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} and slides down a *hillside* of seats, *descending feet* first. He begins **to fall**, faster and faster, juggling as he goes. The crowd watches him **fall** onto the pitch and score a goal."],"阶":["stairs","The {Juggler} wobbles on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} while a *go-between* runs up and down the snowy *hillside* carrying love letters. To save his legs, the yeti carves **stairs** into the slope, step after step, then a thousand more. Soon the **stairs** reach the clouds and the go-between takes a lift instead."],"审":["to examine","The {Sheriff} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where a *courtroom* has been built inside the ghost train. He must **examine** each witness: a clown, a candyfloss, a carousel horse. He **examines** them one by one with a magnifying glass."],"沉":["to sink","The {Chef} drops down the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} into a pond of *water drops*, carrying a pile of *clutter*. He begins **to sink**, pots, pans and all. The ducks watch him **sink** to the bottom, where he starts a restaurant for the fish."],"坚":["solid","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} and stamps on a pile of *soil*. It's **solid**: harder than steel, harder than diamonds. He juggles bricks on it and they bounce off. Even the pigeons can't peck the **solid** floor."],"善":["kind","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion}, and a huge *mouth* on the wall says only nice things to him. It's so **kind** that it compliments his boots, offers him tea, and sings him a lullaby. The Sheriff hands out hugs, being **kind** too."],"妈":["mom","The {Magician} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and pulls a *woman* riding a *horse* out of his hat. It's his **mom**, who gallops around the roof telling him to put on a coat. He tries to make his **mom** disappear, but she just takes the hat away."],"刘":["to kill","The {Lifeguard} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} holding a *tattooed blade* covered in pictures of skulls and dragons. She is hunting the mosquito that kept everyone awake all night. She swings, misses, swings again, and finally manages **to kill** it with a mighty whack. The backpackers cheer, then realise the whack was strong enough **to kill** the bunk bed too."],"读":["to read","The {Dentist} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} past a *market stall* selling books by the kilo. Every page lets out a *small speech bubble* that chatters its words aloud. He buys a whole cartload and sits on the diving board **to read**, but the books talk so fast he must **read** with earplugs in."],"啊":["ah","The {Ghost} floats onto the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and taps a dozing *auntie* in a face mask on the shoulder. Her enormous *mouth* opens wide: **ah**! **Ahhh**! The scream blows the cucumber slices off her eyes, and every guest in the spa yells **ah** in reply, a full choir of fright."],"超":["to overtake","The {Chef} sprints across the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a soufflé, chased by a *runner* and a *town crier* ringing his bell. The crier yells that the Chef is losing, so the Chef straps rockets to his clogs **to overtake** them both. He zooms past the runner, past the crier, and even manages **to overtake** a passing pigeon."],"免":["to exempt","The {Magician} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a sly *dodger* is ducking under the tax collector's desk. The Magician waves his wand and the dodger's bill vanishes with a puff: he is **exempt**! Everyone in the queue wants **to exempt** themselves too, and starts crawling under the desk."],"压":["to press","The {Yogi} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} under a towering *cliff*, holding a single *clod* of earth in his palm. A boulder rolls off the cliff and he catches it, then **presses** it flat like a pancake. He uses it **to press** the guests' towels, and soon the whole spa smells of hot stone."],"银":["silver","The {Yogi} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} carrying a tray of *gold coins*. The innkeeper gives them such a frosty *glare* that the gold turns pale, chilly and shiny: they are now **silver**. Even the Yogi's beard turns **silver**, and the guests pay with icicles."],"买":["to buy","The {Magician} digs his way into the {Basement} of the {Island} with an enormous *shopping basket*. He wants **to buy** everything: coconuts, crabs, the volcano, the sea. He pays with rabbits pulled from his hat, and the shopkeeper parrot squawks: **buy** more, buy more, until the basket floats off the island."],"皇":["emperor","The {Hunter} wades up the {Staircase} of the {Swamp} and finds a frog sitting in a *golden crown* bigger than itself. Every alligator bows. This frog is the **emperor** of the swamp, and he croaks orders through a reed. The Hunter kneels in the mud, and the **emperor** knights him with a dragonfly."],"养":["to raise","The {Yogi} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} and finds a lamb, a goat and a baby jet plane all crying for milk. He decides **to raise** them all. He bottle-feeds the plane jet fuel, sings to the lamb, and when they're grown he has **raised** a goat that can fly."],"伊":["you (literary)","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut when a *standing person* in a long robe climbs up beside him: a *magistrate*. The magistrate bows and recites an ancient poem to him: O **you**, O thou, who sits so still. The Yogi bows back and replies with the same old-fashioned **you**, and the seagulls clap."],"怀":["bosom","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Wine Cellar} cradling a baby barrel in his **bosom**. His *standing heart* thumps with love. A *no sign* swings in front of him: no barrels upstairs! He just hugs it tighter to his **bosom** and refuses to let go."],"执":["to grasp","The {Jockey} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, and a bee clamps a pair of *handcuffs* onto his wrist. They chain him to a honeycomb, so he must **grasp** it with both hands, sticky and dripping. Every jockey who visits must **grasp** the comb, and nobody can let go."],"副":["secondary","The {Firefighter} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a *full jar* of jam being sliced by a *standing knife*. The first piece goes to the chief: the **secondary** slice goes to her, the deputy. She gets the **secondary** helmet, the **secondary** boots, and the slightly smaller pool float."],"乱":["in disorder","The {Lifeguard} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond} on a single *ski*, and a giant *tongue* licks her off course. She crashes into the swans, the swans crash into the boats, feathers fly, paddles spin: everything is **in disorder**. The pond is **in disorder** and the swans file a complaint."],"抗":["to resist","The {King} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar}, and a *helping hand* tries to strip off his *high collar*. He wriggles, kicks, and fights **to resist**. Everyone in the hangar pulls, but he holds on with his teeth. The collar stays on: he can **resist** anything except a tickle."],"犯":["to offend","The {Firefighter} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} as a *prowling dog* steals the lord's sausage. A *bowing man*, the butler, is horrified: this is bound **to offend** his lordship. The dog barks rudely. Everything it does seems designed **to offend**, and it ends up chewing the lord's wig."],"追":["to chase","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} as a runaway taxi speeds down the *road* below. He leaps on his horse **to chase** it, galloping over the *sandbags* the builders have left. The taxi skids, the horse jumps, the passengers wave, and the Jockey keeps **chasing** it all around town."],"帮":["to help","The {Baker} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} as a whole *country* floods with flour. He grabs a *towel* and begins wiping the mountains and rivers clean. He works night and day **to help**. The pilots join in **to help**, and soon the country shines like a freshly baked loaf."],"宣":["to announce","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} with a gigantic *megaphone*. He wants **to announce** that every new coin will have a sheep on it. His voice booms so loud that coins jump out of their bags, and every coin begins **to announce** it too, rattling: baa!"],"佛":["Buddha","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort} and finds a *standing person* who sits down crossed-legged and becomes a smiling golden **Buddha**. A *dollar sign* rains down from his halo. The soldiers try to grab the money, but the **Buddha** just smiles, and the money turns into lotus flowers.","fó"],"岁":["year of age","The {Sailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and waits by a window showing a *mountain*. A *dusk moon* rises over it, sets, rises again. Each time a candle appears on his cake: another **year of age**. By the time his name is called, he has a white beard and a cake on fire with years: ninety-one **years of age**."],"航":["to sail","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and finds a *boat* parked among the planes, wearing a captain's *high collar*. It wants **to sail**, so it raises its sails, and the wind blows it right out of the hangar door. The planes taxi behind it, and they all **sail** across the airfield."],"优":["excellent","The {Yogi} relaxes on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} next to a *standing person* with a *wart* on his nose. The wart sings opera so beautifully that the boats stop rocking. It's **excellent**, the best voice on the river! The judges give it ten out of ten and a medal saying **excellent**."],"怪":["strange","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Wine Cellar}, where a *saint* with a halo is juggling wine bottles. The Gardener's *standing heart* jumps. Then the bottles start singing, the barrels tap-dance, the corks fly in a circle. Everything is **strange**, very **strange**, and the saint winks."],"香":["fragrant","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} lighting a giant stick of *incense*. Smoke curls over the pitch and everyone sniffs: roses, cinnamon, fresh bread. The whole stadium is **fragrant**, the players stop to sniff the **fragrant** air, and even the referee's socks smell of lavender."],"著":["famous","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a lawn of *grass* where a *busy man* is signing autographs. He is **famous**: crowds scream, cameras flash. The Jockey asks why, and learns he's the man who mows the grass. Everyone wants to be as **famous** as him.","zhù"],"田":["field","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and finds a *rice field* growing on the trading floor. The bankers wade through it in their suits. He stitches a quilt of green squares, each one a **field**, and sells each little **field** for a fortune."],"铁":["iron","The {Tailor} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a *lost arrow* has hit a pile of *gold coins* and turned them grey. They're no longer gold but heavy **iron**! The yeti uses them to make an **iron** pan, and the Tailor uses the leftovers as buttons."],"控":["to control","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} hut into an *empty room* where a *helping hand* holds a remote. He grabs it **to control** the lagoon: waves up, waves down, fish go left. He tries **to control** the moon next, and the tide falls over."],"税":["tax","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} as a *money changer* counts out the farmers' grain. He takes a *grain stalk* from every bag: that's the **tax**. The farmers grumble, so the Sheriff takes a **tax** on grumbling too."],"左":["left","The {Zookeeper} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse}, where every arrow, crate and sign points *left*. He tries to walk straight but the floor turns **left**, the forklifts drive **left**, even his hat slides off to the left. He walks in circles for an hour and ends up exactly where he started."],"右":["right","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} where a *feeding hand* is feeding the ducks, but only on the **right**. The left ducks quack with jealousy. The Yogi raises his **right** hand too, and all the ducks swim to the right side, so the boathouse tips over."],"份":["portion","The {Firefighter} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and finds a *standing person* cutting a giant cake. Each child gets one **portion**, the clown gets one, the elephant gets one. The Firefighter asks for her **portion** and gets a slice the size of a fire engine."],"穿":["to wear","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} and pokes a *fang* through the wall of a *cave*, making a neat hole. Now he can thread his clothes through it **to wear**: a sock, a sleeve, a whole coat. The swans also want something **to wear**, so he dresses them in tutus."],"艺":["art","The {Yogi} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} and finds a *swan* painting with its beak on a canvas of *grass*. It makes masterpieces: sunsets, portraits, spaghetti. It's **art**, real **art**, and the crabs pay a seashell each to see the gallery."],"背":["back","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and carries the *moon* on his **back** while facing *north*. He walks so far that the moon gets heavy, bending his **back** like a croissant. He turns around and the moon sets."],"阵":["troop formation","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair}, and soldiers on a *hillside* push a *cart* into place. They arrange themselves into a **troop formation**: a triangle, a square, a dragon. The Jockey shouts orders, and the bumper cars line up in **troop formation** too."],"草":["grass","The {Tsar} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where *grass* grows up through the floor. An *early bird* pecks at it every morning. The **grass** grows faster than the bird can eat, up the stairs and out the windows, until the tower wears a wig of **grass**."],"脚":["foot","The {Juggler} slides into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} under the *moon* and steps on a cat's tail. He has to *retreat* fast, hopping on one **foot**. The cats chase him, nibbling his toes, so he juggles with his **foot** to distract them."],"概":["general","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} and finds a *tree* standing over a *finished meal*. He can't tell what was eaten, but he knows in **general**: coconuts. He gives a **general** report to the gulls: it was coconuts, more or less."],"恶":["evil","The {Ghost} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and finds a villain with a black *heart* polishing a *silver medal* he stole. He's **evil**, cackling, twirling his moustache. The Ghost spooks him so hard his **evil** laugh comes out as a hiccup."],"块":["chunk","The {King} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Wine Cellar} into a heap of *soil* and pulls out an *archer's ring*. It's stuck to a **chunk** of rock. He bites off a **chunk** of chocolate to celebrate, then drops it into the wine."],"顿":["to pause","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} into a *camp* of gamblers reading a *page* of rules. Everyone has **to pause** while he reads it out loud. He **pauses** between every word, and the roulette wheel falls asleep."],"敢":["to dare","The {Gardener} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} with nothing but a walking *cane*. A bear is sleeping there. Who would **dare** to poke it? The Gardener does, he **dares** to tickle its nose, and the bear sneezes him out of the window."],"守":["to guard","The {Sheriff} sits in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} under a leaky *roof*, keeping his *thumb* in a hole. He must **guard** the boats from sinking. All night he stays there **to guard** them, until his thumb turns into a prune."],"酒":["wine","The {Juggler} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel} and finds *water drops* leaking from a giant *wine jug*. He tastes one: it's **wine**! He juggles cups of **wine**, the backpackers cheer, and the hostel smells like a vineyard."],"岛":["island","The {Dentist} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and finds a tiny *island* floating in a bathtub, palm trees and all. A pirate the size of a thumb waves from the **island**. The Dentist checks the pirate's teeth and leaves him a toothbrush on his **island**."],"托":["to entrust","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} and a *helping hand* gives him a single *grass blade* to hold. It's precious, and he has **to entrust** it to someone. He hands it to a pigeon, who gives it back. Nobody wants to be **entrusted** with grass."],"央":["centre","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} with a wooden *yoke* across his shoulders, a bucket hanging from each end. He must stay in the exact **centre** or the buckets spill. He wobbles left, right, and finally finds the **centre**, perfectly balanced, as planes land on both sides."],"户":["household","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and knocks on a *door* floating on the water. Behind it lives a whole **household**: grandma on a lilo, dad on a duck, three kids and a goldfish. They invite him in for dinner, and the Hunter becomes the seventh member of the **household**."],"烈":["intense","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} and finds a *lineup* of yetis warming their feet on glowing *embers*. The fire roars **intense**, so hot their fur starts to curl. The heat is so **intense** that the icicles melt into a hot bath, and the yetis put on sunglasses."],"洋":["ocean","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} as *water drops* rain from a leaky plane. A *sheep* is caught in the flood and starts to swim. The drops become a sea, then a whole **ocean**, and the sheep sails off across the **ocean** on a floating suitcase, waving goodbye."],"哥":["elder brother","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} watching his *elder brother* climb up with a ladder. His **elder brother** steals the gardener's watering can and waters the clouds. It rains, and the **elder brother** laughs, as big brothers do."],"索":["to search","The {Sailor} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} following a *silk skein* that leads into the dark. He has **to search** every crate for the end of the thread. He finds a sock, a parrot, a lost grandma, and keeps on **searching** till dawn."],"胡":["reckless","The {Hunter} skids down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} on a tea tray, his long *whiskers* flying. He's **reckless**: he cannonballs off the diving board, juggles flaming torches, and rides a duck backwards. The lifeguard shouts that he's **reckless**, and he waves his whiskers."],"款":["funds","The {King} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} and lets out a great *yawn*. Out tumble coins, banknotes and gold bars: the royal **funds**, saved for a rainy day. The swans paddle up, scoop the **funds** into their wings and sail off to buy a speedboat, while the King yawns again and finds his purse empty."],"靠":["to lean on","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a room where a *cow head* sips a cup of *coffee*. Too tired to stand, he tries **to lean on** the cow. The cow leans back, so they **lean on** each other and fall asleep."],"评":["to comment","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} and lies *flat* on the mat. A *small speech bubble* pops out of his mouth **to comment** on every punch: too slow, too fast, nice hat. The boxers stop fighting and **comment** on his comments."],"版":["edition","The {Baker} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and catches a *rebel* carving letters into a *wood slice* to print a secret newspaper. The Baker joins in and prints the next **edition** on slices of toast. The lord upstairs eats the news with butter, and every morning he demands a fresh **edition** with more jam."],"宝":["treasure","The {Baker} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and finds a *jade gem* hidden under the *roof* beam. It's **treasure**! He bakes it into a loaf to hide it, then forgets which loaf has the **treasure**, and has to eat a hundred."],"座":["seat","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into a *shed* where a *sitting pair* of elephants hog the only **seat**. He waits an hour, then perches on their trunks. Soon every worker wants a **seat**, so the elephants sell tickets and the forklift turns into a sofa with seatbelts."],"释":["to explain","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and finds *animal tracks* all over the honey. He needs **to explain** who's been stealing it. He follows the tracks, stops, turns to the bees, and points his finger to **explain**: it was the bear, wearing slippers."],"景":["scenery","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} and finds a painted *landscape* on the wall: mountains, rivers, cows. He steps into it and the **scenery** comes to life, the cows moo, the rivers flow. The boxers come down to admire the **scenery**."],"顾":["to look after","The {Gardener} slips through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a *trapped man* under a *page* of instructions. The page says: please **look after** him. The Gardener feeds him, waters him like a plant, and promises **to look after** him forever."],"弟":["younger brother","The {Dentist} pops out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and his *little brother* bursts out after him, waving a spade. His **younger brother** buries him in the sand, draws a moustache on him, and steals his ice cream. The Dentist sighs: that's what a **younger brother** does."],"登":["to climb","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple as a *climber* scrambles up the vines toward him. The climber wants **to climb** higher still, onto the Dentist's head, then onto a passing parrot. He loves **to climb** anything, even the Dentist's ladder of teeth."],"货":["goods","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and finds a *shape-shifter* turning into anything you want: a vase, a bike, a sofa. It pays with a *shell*. The Hunter fills his trolley with **goods**, and the shape-shifter turns into more **goods** to sell."],"互":["mutual","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a floating *plank*, beside a *pig snout* that sniffs him. He sniffs back. They sniff each other, it's **mutual**. They trade hats, they trade sandwiches: everything is **mutual**, and they become best friends."],"付":["to pay","The {Firefighter} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and splashes down beside a *cashier* sitting on a lilo. The cashier hands her a bill: one hose, one helmet, one pool. She has **to pay**, so she sprays the cashier with gold coins. Now everyone wants **to pay** in water."],"伯":["uncle","The {Baker} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort} and meets a *standing person* with a *white dove* on his head: it's his **uncle**. His **uncle** does magic tricks with the dove, pulls coins from the Baker's ears, and eats all the bread."],"慢":["slow","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} wearing a *long veil* that trails behind him. His *standing heart* beats very **slow**, so he walks very **slow**, one step every minute. The guests fall asleep waiting for his trick."],"欧":["Europe","The {Ghost} floats onto the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse}, unrolls a *district map* and gives a huge *yawn*. Out pours all of **Europe**: the Eiffel Tower, a Venetian gondola, a cuckoo clock, a wheel of cheese. The rowing boats bump into windmills, and the Ghost sails off on the gondola to tour **Europe** by moonlight."],"换":["to exchange","The {Hunter} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond}, and a *helping hand* grabs him for a *makeover*: pink wig, glitter boots, a feather boa. Horrified, he wants **to exchange** them for his old muddy coat. But the swans have put on his coat, and they refuse **to exchange** it back, strutting off looking very rugged."],"闻":["to hear","The {Wizard} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and presses his *ear* to the creaky *gate* of the haunted house. He can **hear** the ghosts inside gossiping about him. Desperate **to hear** more, he grows his ear the size of an umbrella, and now he catches every whisper, every giggle, and every rollercoaster scream for miles."],"危":["danger","The {Wizard} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house and sees a *teetering man* balancing on the chimney. **Danger**! The man wobbles, the roof cracks, the lake bubbles. The Wizard yells **danger**, and casts a spell that gives the man wings."],"忙":["busy","The {Magician} races up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} with his *standing heart* pounding. A *tombstone* stands at the top, carved: too **busy** to rest. He's so **busy**, pulling rabbits from hats, sawing ladies in half, that he forgets to have lunch."],"核":["pit","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and finds a *wild boar* chewing a peach under a *tree*. The boar spits out the **pit**, which shoots across the room and hits the Hunter on the nose. He plants the **pit**, and a tree grows instantly."],"暗":["dark","The {Ghost} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and plays a sad *music* that makes the *sun* hide. The rooms go **dark**, the candles go out, and the guests bump into each other. The Ghost glows a little in the **dark**."],"姐":["older sister","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave} until a *woman* on a *stepladder* climbs down: his **older sister**. She takes his juggling balls, she takes his snacks, and she bosses the yeti too, because she's the **older sister**."],"介":["to introduce","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} and a *go-between* appears in a tuxedo. He loves **to introduce** people: Juggler, meet Yeti; Yeti, meet Juggler. He goes on **to introduce** the icicles, the snow and the yeti's mum."],"坏":["bad","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Wine Cellar} onto a pile of *soil* where someone has planted a *no sign*. The wine has gone **bad**, the cheese is **bad**, the mice have **bad** manners. He holds his nose and runs."],"讨":["to discuss","The {Tailor} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Tower} where a group raises a *thumb* every time a *small speech bubble* floats up. They want **to discuss** the dress code: top hats or not? They **discuss** for three days and decide on socks."],"丽":["beautiful","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} onto a rotten old *plank*. She paints it with shells, sunsets and glitter until it shimmers and becomes a **beautiful** surfboard. She rides it on the biggest wave of the year, and everyone on the sand drops their ice creams, it looks so **beautiful**."],"良":["good","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} carrying a *good meal* for the hungry football team. The soup is **good**, the bread is **good**, the dumplings are perfect. One bite and the players start playing **good** football, scoring ten goals, and the goalkeeper asks for second helpings in the middle of the match."],"序":["order","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a *shed* full of statues, each with an *offering* bowl. He lines them up in **order**: smallest to tallest, oldest to youngest. The curator nods: the statues are in perfect **order**."],"升":["to rise","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple and pours *grass* seed onto a *slide*. The grass grows upward, the slide tilts, and everyone begins **to rise**: monkeys, parrots, the Sheriff. He keeps **rising**, waving to the clouds."],"监":["to supervise","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} and an *inspector* with a clipboard watches every coin he juggles. The **inspector** is there **to supervise**, scribbling notes. The Juggler drops a coin, and the inspector frowns: he'll **supervise** even more closely."],"临":["to face","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} and at the top meets a monster. She must **face** it, so she turns and stares it right in the eyes. The monster blinks first, embarrassed, and runs. Next time she has **to face** the bill."],"亮":["bright","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} onto a *small table* with a lamp on it. She flicks it on, and the light is so **bright** it floods the whole pitch. The players put on sunglasses, the ball glows, the night is **bright** as day."],"露":["to reveal","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} as heavy *rain* washes away the tiles of a garden *pathway*, **revealing** glinting gold coins underneath. She digs with her whistle and her bare hands **to reveal** more, and finally uncovers a secret door with a pirate behind it, who is very embarrassed to be found."],"永":["forever","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut beside a *stream* that never stops flowing. He sits there **forever**: years pass, then centuries, and his beard grows down the stream to the sea. Fish build nests in it. The stream will run **forever**, and the Yogi has no plans to get up for lunch."],"呼":["to call","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} hut with a silver *whistle* in his *mouth*. He blows **to call** the swimmers in, and everyone leaps out of the water. Then the ducks waddle over, then the frogs, then a confused submarine. He keeps **calling** until half the town is standing around the pool, dripping."],"味":["taste","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house into the garden, where a huge *mouth* is chewing a *sapling*. Every leaf has a different **taste**: lemon, then chocolate, then soap. The Wizard nibbles one, and the **taste** is so strong his hat spins off and his beard turns the colour of mint ice cream."],"野":["wild field","The {Yogi} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Hut} and finds a whole *wilderness* inside: wolves, cacti, a waterfall. It's a **wild field** hidden under the hut. He meditates in the middle of the **wild field** while the wolves howl."],"架":["frame","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Piazza} and nails a *plus sign* onto a *tree*. It becomes a **frame**, and he hangs pictures on it: a cat, a pizza, his mum. The pigeons perch on the **frame** to pose."],"域":["region","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a patch of *soil* with a *guard post* at each corner. It's his own **region**: he plants a flag and declares it a country. The guards block anyone from entering his **region** without a ticket."],"沙":["sand","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} as *sand* pours down from the sky. It fills the hot tubs, the saunas, the massage rooms. **Sand** in his boots, **sand** in his hat, and the guests build sandcastles in the pool."],"掉":["to drop","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café}, and a *helping hand* passes him a lit *beacon*. It's hot! He has **to drop** it, and it rolls under a sleeping cat. The cat wakes, and **drops** its milk."],"括":["to include","The {King} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and a *helping hand* lays out a giant *tongue* like a carpet. He wants **to include** everything on it: crates, boxes, workers. The tongue wraps around them all, and **includes** the King too."],"舰":["warship","The {Juggler} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and lands on the deck of a grey *boat* bristling with cannons. A *watcher* in the crow's nest shouts: enemy bankers ahead! It's a **warship**, steaming through the trading floor, firing paper money from its guns. The Juggler is promoted to admiral of the **warship** and salutes a calculator."],"鱼":["fish","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} and finds a *fish* in a glass case, holding a sign: please do not tap. He taps. The **fish** leaps out, flops up the steps, and swims through the air past the dinosaurs. The visitors chase it with butterfly nets, and the Yogi teaches the **fish** to meditate on a marble pillar."],"杂":["mixed","The {Zookeeper} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and finds a *bare tree* hung with everything imaginable. A *crowbar* pries open a cupboard and out falls more: towels, ducks, a trumpet, spaghetti. It's all **mixed** up, mud with bubbles, cucumbers with socks. The guests soak in a **mixed** bath of everything, and the trumpet plays itself."],"误":["mistake","The {Wizard} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, where a *loudmouth* is shouting a *small speech bubble* full of wrong directions. Following them, the Wizard dives into the snack bar instead of the water. **Mistake**! He casts a drying spell and turns the pool into jelly. Another **mistake**. The loudmouth gives him a thumbs-up."],"湾":["bay","The {Wizard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a *bent bow* and fires *water drops* into the garden. Each arrow digs a curve in the lawn until the sea rushes in and fills it. Now the mansion has its own **bay**, with sailing boats and a lighthouse. The butler serves tea on a raft in the middle of the **bay**."],"吉":["lucky","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} juggling a *lucky charm*: a golden four-leaf clover. Every time he catches it, something wonderful happens: he finds a coin, a seagull returns his hat, the sun comes out. It's his **lucky** day! He throws the charm to a crab, and the crab wins the lottery, looking very **lucky** indeed."],"减":["to decrease","The {Juggler} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, where *icicles* drip on piles of gold. He throws *salt* on them and they shrink, and so does the gold, coin by coin. The bankers watch their money **decrease**, and the Juggler keeps salting until even the price of bread starts **to decrease**."],"编":["to weave","The {Baker} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} with a long *silk thread* and an old *nameboard*. He begins **to weave** the thread around the board, over and under, until the bankers' names are stitched into a tapestry. He can't stop: he goes on **to weave** a hat, a jumper and a hammock for the pigeons."],"楚":["clear","The {Chef} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a tangled *grove* blocks the view. He rolls out a white *bolt of cloth* and wipes every leaf until the water sparkles. Now everything is **clear**: the bottom of the pool, a lost ring, a sleeping eel. The eel wakes, annoyed, but the view is perfectly **clear**."],"肯":["to be willing","The {King} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where a *stop sign* blocks the ghost train. Under a full *moon* the sign suddenly flips: go! He's finally **willing**, he jumps into the carriage and screams all the way through. The ghosts are **willing** to give him a second ride, and even a free candyfloss."],"测":["to measure","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} into a puddle of *water drops* with a fat *rulebook* tucked under his arm. He has **to measure** everything: the drops, the hut, the cat's whiskers. He even tries **to measure** his own shadow, but it keeps running away whenever the ruler comes near."],"败":["to defeat","The {Baker} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} swinging a *cane* at an army of crabs, each armoured in a *shell*. Smack, smack, smack! He means **to defeat** them all and save his bread. One by one the crabs fall on their backs, legs waving, **defeated**, and surrender their claws as rolling pins."],"屋":["house","The {Wizard} lands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} hut and finds a whole *cottage* built on top of it. With a flick of his wand, the **house** grows a chimney, a doorbell and a garden gnome. Swimmers queue at its front door for towels. The Wizard moves in, and the **house** floats when it rains."],"跑":["to run","The {Pirate} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and finds a *parcel* that suddenly sprouts a *kicking foot*. It kicks him in the shin and starts **to run**, leaping up the stairs. The Pirate chases it round and round the tower, and they both **run** until the parcel bursts open: it's full of trainers."],"梦":["dream","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} into a misty *grove* under a *dusk moon*. He falls asleep and has a **dream**: the trees play violins, the monkeys float like balloons, his hat swallows the moon. He wakes up and the monkeys are still floating. Was it a **dream**, or is the jungle dreaming him?"],"散":["to scatter","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} clutching a sack of *scattered seeds*, and the sack bursts. Seeds bounce across the ballroom, under the piano, into the soup. A flock of pigeons swoops in and the guests **scatter**, screaming. The pigeons **scatter** too, and so does the orchestra, still playing."],"温":["warm","The {Wizard} lands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} holding a *warm bowl* of soup that steams into the cold night. *Water drops* condense on the roller coaster, which sighs happily. Everything turns **warm**: the dodgems, the candyfloss, the frozen clown. The Wizard ladles soup to the riders, and the whole funfair glows **warm** and cosy."],"困":["trapped","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} and lands next to a *trapped tree* growing in a box. It can't get out, and neither can he: the box closes around them both. They're **trapped**! The King bets his crown, loses, and is still **trapped** with the tree, who's better at poker."],"剑":["sword","The {Juggler} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into an *assembly* of bankers, each brandishing a *standing knife*. He snatches the longest one: it's a **sword**! He juggles three swords at once, and the bankers flee. With a flourish of his **sword** he slices the stock prices in half."],"渐":["gradually","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} next to a *chopping block*, where *water drops* fall one at a time. Drip, drip, drip, and **gradually** the block wears away. Year by year it gets smaller, and the bankers watch **gradually** turn into eventually, until only a splinter is left."],"封":["to seal","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple holding a *jade tablet* and presses her *thumb* onto a pot of red wax. She must **seal** the temple's secret scroll. She stamps it so hard the wax fuses shut. The monkeys try to open it, but it stays **sealed** forever."],"救":["to save","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} and hooks a drowning cat out of the bath with his *cane*. He wraps it in a *fur coat* and rubs it dry. He has managed **to save** it! The cat purrs, then calls its friends, and the Juggler has **to save** forty more."],"贵":["expensive","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a cup of coffee with a giant *price tag*: one million dollars. It's **expensive**! The magazines are **expensive**, the chairs are **expensive**, even the air is charged by the breath. He holds his breath and runs out."],"枪":["gun","The {Cheerleader} high-kicks on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} and accidentally knocks a *tree* through the roof of a *barn*. Out falls an old **gun** filled with confetti. She fires it at the crowd: bang! Glitter everywhere. The referee grabs the **gun** and fires it at the ceiling, starting the match."],"缺":["to lack","The {Cheerleader} spins across the {Rooftop} of the {Ice Rink} with a *clay jar* that's missing a chunk, and an *archer's ring* that doesn't fit any finger. The team **lacks** a captain, the jar **lacks** a lid, and she **lacks** a skate. She keeps cheering anyway: what do we **lack**? Everything!"],"楼":["building","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} and finds a *tree* wearing a *tall bun* of hair. The bun keeps growing, storey after storey, until it becomes a **building** with windows and lifts. Ducks rent the top floor, and the **building** sways in the breeze."],"县":["county","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, and a *stepladder* unfolds under his *elbow*. From the top he can see the whole **county**: farms, sheep, towns. He declares himself mayor, and the bankers give him the **county** keys."],"尚":["still","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and climbs into the dusty *attic*. Everything there is **still** there: his old cowboy boots, his first hat, a jar of sweets. Even his childhood horse is **still** waiting, and it neighs hello."],"毫":["tiny bit","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} carrying one single hair of *fur* as a trophy. It weighs a **tiny bit**, smaller than an eyelash. He displays it on a velvet cushion. The guests peer at it with a magnifying glass, seeing only a **tiny bit** of fluff."],"移":["to move","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} carrying a *grain stalk*, and over *many moons* he begins **to move** the whole beach. Grain by grain, shell by shell, he shifts it to the next bay. The crabs help him **move** the sea too."],"娘":["mother","The {Ninja} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} and finds a *woman* serving a *good meal* to the whole football team. She's everyone's **mother**: she wipes their noses, ties their shoelaces, and scolds the referee. The Ninja gets a hug from the **mother** too."],"朋":["friend","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} arm in arm with his two *buddies*, a monkey and a parrot. They share bananas, sing sea shanties and swing through the vines together. A tiger joins, and the Pirate has a new **friend**. Even the snakes want to be his **friend**."],"画":["to draw","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Water Park} with a *plank* as his easel. He loves **to draw**: he draws a slide, and it becomes real; he draws a wave, and it splashes. He decides **to draw** a shark, then rubs it out quickly."],"班":["class","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} and teaches a **class** of bread rolls with *twin jades* as their teachers. The rolls raise their crusts to answer questions. The jades give gold stars, and the whole **class** graduates as croissants."],"智":["wisdom","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and meets a *sage* polishing the *sun* with his beard. The bees bring him questions, and he answers each one with great **wisdom**: buzz less, make more honey. The Jockey asks how to win the race, and the sage's **wisdom** says: ride faster."],"亦":["also","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} and lands beside a *sweating man* copying everything he does. The Yogi bends; the man **also** bends. The Yogi stands on his head; the man **also** stands on his head. Soon the crabs, the seagulls and the setting sun are **also** doing yoga, all dripping with sweat."],"耳":["ear","The {Ghost} floats into the {Basement} of the {Car Park} and finds a giant *ear* lying across three parking spaces. It hears every engine, every honk, every whisper. The Ghost whispers boo into the **ear**, and the **ear** jumps so high it hits the ceiling."],"恩":["kindness","The {Ghost} floats onto the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} and gives the shivering clown a *warm hug*. The clown is so touched by such **kindness** that he hands out free balloons to every child. The **kindness** spreads, and the carousel horses hug each other."],"短":["short","The {Dentist} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} with an *arrow* and a *bean* to measure the swans. The arrow is **short**, the bean is even **shorter**, and he's pretty **short** himself. The swans stretch their long necks and laugh. In the end the tape measure shrinks in shame and becomes **short** too."],"掌":["palm","The {Jockey} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, where a giant *palm* sticks up out of the floor. He sits in the **palm**, and it lifts him up like a lift. It waves him around, then high-fives a plane with its **palm**."],"恐":["afraid","The {King} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut, where a metal *brace* is clamped round a trembling *heart*. He's **afraid**: of the dark, of the crabs, of the sound of water. The heart shakes so much the brace pops off, and the King is too **afraid** to pick it up."],"遗":["to leave behind","The {Yogi} strolls up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} and drops a *price tag* on the sandy *road*. Then he forgets his sandals, his towel, his snacks and finally his own shadow, **leaving behind** a trail all the way to the sea. The seagulls collect everything he has **left behind** and open a second-hand shop."],"固":["solid","The {Gardener} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and builds a *fence* around an *antique* vase. The fence is **solid**, unbreakable, made of iron and glue. The swimmers bounce off it, the sharks bump it, but it's **solid**, and the vase stays perfectly safe."],"席":["seat","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} and lays down his *towel* on the hot sand to save a **seat**. The sheep do the same, a hundred towels, a hundred seats. No space left for the crabs, who must take a **seat** on the Shepherd's head."],"松":["loose","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hut looking down at a *tree* in the *town square*. Its roots are **loose**, its leaves **loose**, its trousers **loose**. It wobbles and wanders off down the street. The Sailor ties it up again, but the knot is **loose** too."],"秘":["secret","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach}, where a *pinned heart* hangs on a *grain stalk*, whispering a **secret**. He listens carefully, but it won't tell. He does a trick and the **secret** pops out: the sea is actually lemonade."],"谢":["to thank","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} and an *archer* saves him from a yeti. A *small speech bubble* pops out of his mouth **to thank** him: thank you, thanks, cheers! He doesn't stop **thanking** him, even after the archer goes home."],"鲁":["crass","The {Lifeguard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a *fish* is eating a slice of the *sun*. It burps, slurps, and wipes its fins on the curtains. It's so **crass**: it spits, it yells, it wears socks in the pool. The Lifeguard blows her whistle at the **crass** fish."],"遇":["to meet","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and walks down a *road*, when he happens **to meet** a *monkey* in a top hat. They bow, shake hands, and go for tea. He goes on **to meet** a mummy, a dinosaur, and the museum's ghost."],"康":["healthy","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} eating a bowl of *rice husk*. It's so **healthy**: he flexes his muscles, he does push-ups, he lifts a plane. All the pilots eat husks too and become **healthy** enough to fly without engines."],"虑":["to consider","The {Lifeguard} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and freezes: a stuffed *tiger* has come alive and is licking its lips. Her *heart* drums so loudly the exhibits rattle. She sits on a bench, chin in hand, to **consider** her options, and the tiger sits beside her to **consider** its lunch."],"幸":["lucky","The {Shepherd} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} and lands on a heap of soft *soil*, right beside an upturned *pitchfork* that missed him by a whisker. The crowd gasps. He finds a four-leaf clover in the soil, a coin in his boot, and bows: the **luckiest**, most **lucky** man alive."],"均":["even","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} hotel dividing *soil* into perfectly *even shares* for a hundred flowerpots. A gust tips one pot higher than the rest, and she shrieks, scoops, and levels it with a ruler until every pot is dead **even**. Even the sand dunes below rearrange themselves to be **even**."],"销":["to sell off","The {Shepherd} runs a clearance sale on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café}, flinging *gold coins* of change while a grumpy *portrait* of the owner yells \"Everything must go!\" Cats carry off teapots, cushions, the counter itself. By sunset he has **sold off** the entire café, then **sells off** the roof he's standing on."],"钟":["clock","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse and pins a giant *bullseye* to the wall. Archers shoot *gold coins* at it, and every hit makes it BONG the hour. It is now a **clock**: the whole lagoon checks the time by the jockey's **clock**, which strikes thirteen whenever someone misses."],"诗":["poem","The {Sheriff} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, which is shaped like a tiny *temple*, and recites to the bees. A *small speech bubble* drifts from his mouth with each line, rhyming \"honey\" with \"money\". The bees hum along, buzz the chorus, and by dawn the whole hive is buzzing his **poem**, a sticky **poem** about sheriffs."],"藏":["to hide","The {Tsar} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar}, crown wobbling, and dives into a pot of tall *grass* to **hide**. Guards run past. Then he crawls into a steel *vault* and slams the door, whispering \"you'll never find me.\" He **hides** so well that the planes take off without him."],"赶":["to hurry","The {Gardener} sprints down into the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, late for the tulips, wheelbarrow squeaking. A *runner* in a tracksuit vaults a *drying rack* of socks beside him, yelling \"**Hurry**!\" They race each other round the furnace, scattering laundry, and the gardener **hurries** so fast he arrives yesterday."],"剧":["play","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the stage of the {Museum} mid-show, knives flying. A *house* made of cardboard collapses, a *standing knife* wobbles upright on the floorboards, and the audience roars, sure it's part of the **play**. The juggler bows, takes a curtain call, and stars in the **play** for forty years."],"票":["ticket","The {Pirate} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café}, parrot squawking, and demands entry. A cat at the door punches a tiny hole in a paper *ticket* and holds out its paw. No **ticket**, no catnip latte. The pirate hands over a treasure map instead, and the cat stamps it as a **ticket**."],"损":["to harm","The {Sailor} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Casino}, where a rogue *employee* in a waistcoat is smashing slot machines. A *helping hand* reaches from the shadows to stop him, but too late: dice cracked, cards torn, roulette wheel dented. Everything the sailor touches gets **harmed**, and the manager screams about the **harm**."],"忽":["suddenly","The {Hunter} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, aiming at nothing, when **suddenly** a *pennant* flaps loose and smacks him in the face. His *heart* leaps out of his chest and dives into the pool below. **Suddenly** everyone is swimming after a beating heart, and the hunter is hunting for himself."],"巨":["huge","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} clutching a *set square*, and starts measuring the new exhibit: a dinosaur egg. It's **huge**. It's bigger than the museum. Every time she measures, it grows again, until the set square is the size of a church and the egg is even more **huge**."],"炮":["cannon","The {Pirate} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower}, lights a *campfire* under a mysterious brown *parcel*, and runs. KABOOM! The parcel was a **cannon**. It fires the pirate's hat, his boots and his parrot over three counties, and the tower is now officially a **cannon** that points at the moon."],"旧":["old","The {Juggler} climbs up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} into an attic where a dusty *pole* props up a tired, faded *sun* made of cardboard. Everything is **old**: socks from 1902, a grandpa backpacker, biscuits fossilised in their tin. She juggles three **old** teapots and they crumble into dust mid-air."],"端":["end","The {Dentist} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} boathouse, on a wobbly *podium* at the very **end** of the gutter. A green *sprout tip* pokes from a crack beside him. Swans queue for checkups along the gutter, but the dentist only treats whoever reaches the **end**, so they shove each other into the pond."],"探":["to explore","The {Tailor} slips through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and finds a *deep cave* under the floor. A *helping hand* holding a torch pokes out of the wall and points the way. She **explores** with a tape measure, measuring stalactites and bats, and **explores** so far she pops out in somebody's bathtub in Peru."],"湖":["lake","The {Hunter} bounds down the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, and huge *water drops* splash from his hat. A walrus with enormous *whiskers* sneezes, and the pool overflows, flooding the street, the park, the whole town. By morning there's a **lake** where the town was, and the walrus is mayor of the **lake**."],"录":["to record","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} with a soggy *logbook* and a whistle. She **records** everything: each splash, each cannonball, each duck that sneaks a swim. When a swimmer sneezes she writes it down in ink. When the pool drains, she **records** that too, then writes \"lifeguard drowned in paperwork\"."],"叶":["leaf","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lands in a lotus pose on a giant **leaf**. A huge *mouth* in the wall blows, and the leaf takes off like a magic carpet, its veins forming a *cross*. The yogi meditates as they surf over rooftops, carried by one enormous green **leaf**."],"春":["spring","The {Chef} throws open the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} and serves a cake labelled *springtime*. One bite and flowers burst from the roulette wheels, birds nest in the slot machines and the croupiers sneeze pollen. It is **spring**, and gamblers bet on which tulip opens first, because **spring** has come early."],"乡":["countryside","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} and draws one long *slash* of green paint across the city. Wherever the paint touches, buildings sink and fields pop up: cows, haystacks, a muddy lane. The football fans find themselves in the **countryside**, mooing at the referee, deep in the **countryside**."],"附":["to attach","The {Firefighter} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Pool}, slips on a *hillside* of wet towels, and crashes into the *cashier*'s booth. When she stands up, the cashier is **attached** to her helmet by a hose, the till **attached** to the cashier, and a chain of swimmers glued behind. Now they all go to fires together."],"吸":["to breathe in","The {Shepherd} stretches on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut, opens his *mouth* wide and starts to **breathe in**. A *chaser* in a speedboat races round the bay trying to escape the suction, but the shepherd keeps **breathing in**: sand, seagulls, sunscreen, the whole sea, until the beach is just a puddle."],"予":["to give","The {Yogi} sits cross-legged in the {Basement} of the {Museum}, an *offering* bowl in her lap. Visitors line up and she **gives** each one something: a mummy's sock, a dinosaur tooth, the Mona Lisa's eyebrow. The curators weep. She smiles and **gives** them the museum's front door too."],"礼":["gift","The {Lifeguard} shoots down a snow ramp on a single *ski* into the {Basement} of the {Beach} club, where a *small altar* glows with candles. She leaves a **gift** wrapped in seaweed on it, and the altar opens its own **gift** in return: a rubber duck that sings opera."],"港":["harbour","The {Gardener} wheels a barrow of *water drops* down the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, through a narrow *alley* of crates, and pours them out. The floor floods, tugboats chug in, cranes sprout like sunflowers, and fishermen yell. The hangar is now a **harbour**, and the gardener plants seaweed along the **harbour** wall."],"雨":["rain","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Museum}, so calm that clouds form on the ceiling. Then the *rain* starts indoors: drops on the dinosaurs, puddles under the pharaohs. The yogi chants louder, the **rain** falls harder, and the curators hand out umbrellas while the paintings drip in the **rain**."],"呀":["ah","The {Yogi} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Spa}, eyes shut, when a vampire with one shiny *fang* pops out of a bush. Her *mouth* drops open: \"**Ah**!\" The vampire screams back, \"**Ah**!\" and they both sit there going \"ah, ah, ah\" like a broken car alarm until the spa staff bring cucumbers."],"板":["board","The {Baker} saws away in the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, slicing a whole *tree* into a single flat **board**. A tiny *rebel* with a red bandana keeps leaping onto the board and shouting slogans. The baker ignores him, rolls dough on the **board**, and bakes the rebel into a pizza by accident."],"庭":["courtyard","The {Tailor} strolls down the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, past a rickety *shed*, into a sunny **courtyard** where two boxers are fighting over a fountain. She measures the *courtyard*, pins the paving stones with chalk and sews a lawn into the **courtyard**, so the boxers have to fight in socks."],"妇":["woman","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} to save a *woman* who is stuck with a giant *comb* tangled in her hair. Splashing, hosing, combing, the firefighter frees her. The grateful **woman** combs the firefighter's moustache in return, and a queue of every **woman** in town forms for a turn."],"归":["to return","The {Gardener} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, using a *comb* to brush the clouds into neat rows, waiting for his pigeons to **return**. One by one they **return**, each carrying a lost thing: a sock, a key, the gardener's wife, who'd been missing since Tuesday."],"睛":["eyeball","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} juggles glass **eyeballs** under the stars. One *eye* slips, rolls through the *moss* in the gutter and gets covered in green fluff. It blinks at her. Now every **eyeball** in the pile wants a moss coat, and they all stare at the juggler, very fashionably."],"饭":["meal","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} pole straight into a dining room, hose blazing, and accidentally washes a *side dish* off the table. A small furious *rebel* in a napkin leaps up and declares war. They sign a truce over a **meal**, and the firefighter cooks the whole **meal** with her hose."],"额":["forehead","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and bumps its **forehead** on the ceiling: BONK. A *guest* in pyjamas hands it a cold *page* from a newspaper to press on the bump. The ghost sticks the page to its **forehead** and reads the news upside down all night."],"含":["to keep in the mouth","The {Hunter} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with a whole gobstopper in his *mouth*, cheeks bulging. A grandfather *clock* booms each minute he survives. Rules: **keep it in the mouth**, no chewing, no swallowing. The butler bets against him, but the hunter **keeps it in the mouth** for a week and wins the house."],"顺":["to follow","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} into an underground *river*, clutching a single *page* of the rulebook. He can't swim against it, so he **follows** the current past roulette tables and floating poker chips. The page reads \"**follow** the river,\" so he does, all the way to the sea."],"输":["to lose","The {Sheriff} rides a *cart* across the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, racing a cowboy in a *dugout canoe*. The canoe slides down the slide, splashes into the pool and zooms ahead. The sheriff's cart crashes into a chimney. He **loses**, loses his hat, his boots, his badge: he **loses** everything except his moustache."],"摇":["to shake","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} stops mid-pose because a giant *helping hand* reaches through the window and **shakes** the whole building like a snow globe. Stairs wobble, bricks rattle, the yogi bounces from floor to floor, calmly chanting, until the hand **shakes** her out of the window like a crumb."],"招":["to recruit","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} beside a *town crier* ringing a bell and bellowing \"Wanted! Riders! Brave ones!\" A *helping hand* swoops down and plucks volunteers off the street. The jockey **recruits** grannies, toddlers and a confused horse, and keeps **recruiting** until the tower is full of jockeys."],"婚":["marriage","The {Hunter} kneels on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} at *twilight* before a *woman* in a sequinned dress, holding out a ring he won at blackjack. She says yes, the slot machines all hit jackpot at once and fireworks burst. It's a **marriage**, and every gambler in the casino throws chips at the **marriage** like confetti."],"脱":["to take off","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} under a full *moon*, while a shifty *money changer* offers coins for her clothes. She **takes off** her hat, then her scarf, then her jacket, haggling for each one. The moon blushes. By dawn she's **taken off** her shoes and sold them too."],"补":["to patch","The {Baker} sits in the {Basement} of the {Pool} trying to **patch** a torn *shirt* with dough. A *fortune stick* pokes out of the hole, reading \"more dough\". He **patches** the shirt with pastry, the shirt with croissants, and soon the shirt is a loaf, which he wears proudly to the pool."],"谓":["to say","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house, opens his mouth and a *small speech bubble* floats out. A hungry *stomach* growls back at him. \"What do you **say**?\" he asks it. The stomach **says** \"pancakes\", and the wizard spends three days trying to translate the gurgles into a spell."],"督":["to supervise","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} with one giant *eye* glued to a telescope, **supervising** the swimmers. Her fat *uncle* sits beside her with a whistle. Every time a swimmer forgets to floss, the eye blinks red and the uncle blows. She **supervises** so strictly that the ducks floss too."],"毒":["poison","The {Dentist} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, holding a green *seedling top* that smokes and fizzles. A furious *mother* snatches it from him and shrieks \"**Poison**!\" The leaf drips on the stairs and dissolves them. The mother chases the dentist round the pool waving a sign saying **POISON** in big letters."],"油":["oil","The {Yogi} slips on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse}, which drips with black *water drops* from a *sprouting field* of oil wells growing on the roof. She slides down the stairs, out the door, across the pier and into the river, leaving a rainbow slick of **oil**, still in perfect lotus pose, gleaming with **oil**."],"疗":["to cure","The {Lifeguard} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} with a *swaddled baby* that has a terrible fever. She lays it on a *sickbed* of kittens, and the kittens purr until the fever melts away. The baby is **cured**, and the café now **cures** sniffles for the price of a latte."],"旅":["to travel","The {Lifeguard} climbs down into the {Basement} of the {Museum}, finds a dusty *square* of carpet and sits on it. It shoots off like a magic rug. She **travels** through Egypt, the Ice Age, a medieval castle and back to the gift shop, still in her swimsuit, and asks to **travel** again."],"泽":["pond","The {Zookeeper} waddles down the {Staircase} of the {Hut} carrying buckets of *water drops* for a thirsty hippo. She trips, the buckets fly, and the floor floods into a muddy **pond** full of frogs and lilies. The hippo sighs happily and sinks in, and the zookeeper has to row across the **pond** to reach the kettle."],"材":["material","The {Tsar} storms down the {Staircase} of the {Island} palace with an axe, chopping every *tree* into planks of building **material**. A cheeky *green shoot* springs back up behind him each time. He stacks wood, bamboo and coconut shells into a mountain of **material**, then builds himself a throne that sprouts leaves."],"灭":["to put out","The {Magician} vanishes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a yeti is roasting marshmallows over a roaring *campfire*. With a flourish, she slams a wooden *plank* down on the flames: whump. Fire **put out**. The yeti weeps a snowy tear, and she **puts out** his candles too, just to be thorough."],"逐":["to chase","The {Jockey} gallops down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} on horseback, **chasing** a greased *pig* that squeals across the tiles. They thunder along the *road* outside, through a market, round a roundabout. The pig dives into the deep end, the horse follows, and the jockey keeps **chasing** it underwater."],"莫":["do not","The {Magician} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} at *sunset* waving a big sign that says **DO NOT**. Do not touch the cannon. Do not feed the guards. Do not open the trapdoor. A soldier opens it anyway and a hundred rabbits pour out, all holding tiny signs saying \"**do not**\"."],"笔":["writing brush","The {Baker} sits in the {Basement} of the {Beach} shack, dipping a long *bamboo* stick tipped with *fur* into a pot of chocolate. It's a **writing brush**! He paints love letters on the cakes, poems on the baguettes, and when a cat walks by, he uses the cat as a spare **writing brush**."],"亡":["to die","The {Wizard} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} with a wobbly *tombstone* strapped to his back. \"Not yet,\" he tells it. The tombstone sighs, \"everyone has **to die** sometime.\" They argue all the way up, until the wizard sneezes, the tombstone falls on a plane, and the plane pretends **to die** dramatically."],"鲜":["fresh","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} trades coins for a flapping *fish* and a freshly shorn *sheep*. Both are so **fresh** they sparkle: the fish winks, the sheep smells of daisies. Bankers queue to sniff them, and the shepherd puts up a sign: \"**Fresh** air, one yen a breath.\""],"词":["word","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, where a bossy *boss* bee pops a *small speech bubble* over each worker. Every bubble holds a single **word**: \"buzz\", \"honey\", \"faster\". The tsar collects them in a jar, and when he opens it at dinner, each **word** flies out and stings a guest."],"圣":["sage","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} temple and lands at the feet of a glowing *saint* sitting under a palm. The **sage** strokes his beard and answers every question before it's asked. The sheriff tries to arrest him for being too wise, and the **sage** gently arrests the sheriff instead."],"择":["to choose","The {Zookeeper} on the {Staircase} of the {Hut} faces a hundred animals all begging for one banana. A giant *helping hand* lowers from the ceiling and lets her **choose**: monkey? giraffe? ant? She dithers for hours, and finally **chooses** to eat the banana herself while the animals boo."],"寻":["to search","The {Shepherd} crawls down the {Staircase} of the {Dunes} palace, combing the sand with a huge *comb*, **searching** for a lost sheep. He licks his *thumb* to test the wind. He finds a teapot, a camel, a buried car and a pharaoh's sock, and keeps **searching** while the sheep snores on the roof."],"厂":["factory","The {Chef} marches into the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, which is carved into a *cliff*, and flips a giant switch. Conveyor belts roar, robots whisk eggs, pancakes fly from chimneys by the thousand. The hangar is now a pancake **factory**, and the chef is its only worker, running the whole **factory** in a hairnet."],"睡":["to sleep","The {Sheriff} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a *weeping willow* growing among the chairs. He lies beneath it, closes one *eye*, then the other, and falls **asleep**. The willow snores. The patients snore. By lunchtime the whole waiting room is **sleeping**, and the doctor is too."],"博":["extensive","The {Baker} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Fort} holding a royal *proclamation* sealed with a *cross*, announcing an **extensive** bake-off. It lists every bread in history, from Roman rolls to moon bagels. The list is so **extensive** it unrolls down the stairs, out the gate and across three kingdoms."],"勒":["to rein in","The {Lifeguard} swings through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} on a runaway horse, gripping a strip of *rawhide*. With one *strong arm* she hauls back hard to **rein in** the beast, and it skids to a stop on its bottom. Then she **reins in** a runaway cow, a goat and a startled grandpa on a bicycle."],"烟":["smoke","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} on a straw *sleeping mat*, right next to a crackling *campfire*. **Smoke** curls up and forms shapes: a dragon, a teapot, a giant nose. The yogi doesn't open her eyes, but the neighbours call the fire brigade, who find only **smoke** doing yoga."],"授":["to teach","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} to **teach** rowing. A *helping hand* passes oars down the line in a tidy *handover*, rower to rower. The sheriff **teaches** them to row backwards, sideways and in circles, and by sunset the boat is spinning like a top."],"诺":["to promise","The {Ninja} drops silently through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and meets his own *lookalike*. A *small speech bubble* pops up between them: \"I **promise** I'm the real one.\" They both **promise**, pinky-swear, and shake hands, then can't remember which one made the first promise."],"伦":["human relations","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Casino}, where a *standing person* sorts gamblers into a *neat stack* by family: cousins here, grandmas there, in-laws in a sulky pile. She whistles at anyone arguing. It's a lesson in **human relations**, and the casino now charges entry for **human relations** therapy."],"岸":["shore","The {Ghost} slides down the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a hidden sea. It paddles toward a *mountain* rising from the waves and finally reaches the *shore*. Sandcastles, shells, a lifeguard chair. The ghost builds a sandghost on the **shore** and sunbathes, invisible, on the **shore** all afternoon."],"奥":["mysterious","The {Ghost} drifts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a *maze* of twisting corridors that rearrange themselves when nobody looks. Even the ghost gets lost. Strange music plays, doors open onto clouds. It's deeply **mysterious**, and the ghost leaves a note: \"this tower is too **mysterious** even for me.\""],"唐":["Tang dynasty","The {Tailor} skips up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} carrying a sack of *sugar* and sprinkles it over a jumbo jet. The plane turns into a silk-sailed ship from the **Tang dynasty**, with poets, horses and emperors waving from the windows. She tailors them all new robes, very **Tang dynasty**, with sugar sequins."],"卖":["to sell","The {Magician} springs up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} beach and sets up a *market stall*. He **sells** coconuts that turn into rabbits, sunglasses that see tomorrow, and bottles of sea air. Tourists stampede. By lunch he has **sold** the whole island, including the beach he is standing on."],"俄":["Russia","The {Ghost} glides up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and finds a *standing person* in a fur hat sharing tea with a fierce *spearman*. Snow piles at the window, a samovar bubbles and balalaika music plays. The hut has teleported to **Russia**, and the ghost learns Cossack dancing in **Russia** till morning."],"炸":["to explode","The {Jockey} gallops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and knocks a *jack-in-the-box* into a *campfire*. It hisses, it fizzes, it **explodes**: BOING-BOOM! Bubble bath sprays the ceiling, cucumber slices rain down, and the jockey's horse is blown into a mud bath. Even the towels **explode** into fluff."],"载":["to carry","The {Zookeeper} drives a wooden *cart* up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} zoo, a knight's *lance* strapped on top. The cart **carries** a giraffe, three penguins and an angry tortoise. It's so overloaded that the wheels squeal, but she **carries** on, the lance poking every coconut off the trees."],"洛":["Luo River","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and finds a whole river rushing between the shelves: the **Luo River**. She sits on the *riverbank* with her whistle, and boxes float past like boats. She yells \"no running beside the **Luo River**!\" at a crate that ignores her completely."],"健":["healthy","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a gym where a *builder* is lifting a *standing person* over his head like a dumbbell. They do push-ups on coins and sprints round the vault. Everyone's cheeks glow; they're horribly **healthy**. Even the coins become **healthy** and start jogging."],"堂":["hall","The {Tailor} sweeps up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} into a *main hall* with a ceiling so high clouds float under it. She unrolls a carpet the length of a runway and the echo repeats her every sneeze nine times. A thousand guests dine in the **hall**, and the tailor sews curtains for the whole **hall**."],"旁":["side","The {Pirate} thumps up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and parks his ship on the *roadside* outside. He refuses to stand in the middle of anything, ever; he always shuffles to the **side**. The planes pass him on one **side**, the parrot on the other, and the pirate tiptoes sideways like a crab."],"宫":["palace","The {Gardener} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} villa and stacks a golden *roof* on top of it, then another, held up by a huge stone *spine*. Fountains, peacocks and crowns sprout everywhere. It becomes a **palace**, and the gardener rules the **palace** with a hose instead of a sceptre."],"喝":["to drink","The {Hunter} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} with a giant jug of lemonade. A *question mark* floats from his *mouth*: thirsty? He **drinks** it all, then the rain barrel, then the pond, then the rain as it falls. The clouds dry up, and the hunter keeps **drinking** with a hiccup."],"借":["to borrow","The {Juggler} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave}. A *standing person* is drying *sun-dried meat* on a washing line. \"Can I **borrow** some?\" she asks, juggling it before he answers. She **borrows** the meat, the line, his hat and the yeti, promising to bring them back next Tuesday."],"君":["monarch","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} palace, crowning a stern *lord* with a sand-castle crown. Instantly he becomes **monarch** of the desert. Camels bow, scorpions salute, and the wind spells his name. The juggler juggles the royal jewels, and the **monarch** demands she juggle him too."],"禁":["to forbid","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} into a *forbidden grove* where every tree wears a red sign: **forbidden**. No juggling, no singing, no laughing. She juggles anyway. The trees gasp, the signs flash, and a strict owl **forbids** her from ever coming back, while secretly clapping its wings."],"阴":["overcast","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} meditating in the *shade* of one enormous grey cloud. The sky is **overcast**, gloomy and drizzly, but the yogi refuses to move. More clouds pile up, the whole town goes dim, and the guests eat breakfast by candlelight, complaining it's **overcast** indoors too."],"园":["garden","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, drops a *yuan coin* into the soil and a whole **garden** springs up overnight: roses, tomatoes, money trees. She builds a little white *fence* around it, but coins keep sprouting through the fence, and bank robbers sneak into the **garden** to pick them."],"谋":["to plan","The {Magician} sneaks down the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} with a basket of *plum* fruit and a *small speech bubble* whispering secrets. They **plan** a heist: swap every boat for a plum. Maps, diagrams, codes. The **plan** is perfect until the magician eats all the plums before midnight."],"宋":["Song dynasty","The {Sailor} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} hut into a scroll painting: a tiled *roof*, a gnarled pine *tree*, and scholars sipping tea in the **Song dynasty**. They hand him a brush and teach him to paint mist. He stays so long he gets a job in the **Song dynasty** navy."],"避":["to avoid","The {Baker} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} café and spots a *pioneer* in a coonskin cap stomping down the *road* to sell him wagon wheels. The baker **avoids** him: ducks behind a sandcastle, rolls under a towel, hides in a croissant. The pioneer looks everywhere, and the baker **avoids** him for a decade."],"抓":["to grab","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} reaches out a *helping hand* while a giant eagle swoops with one *talon* outstretched. They both **grab** the last rubber ring. Tug-of-war! The eagle wins, so the jockey **grabs** the eagle, and they fly down the slides together."],"荣":["glory","The {Robot} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon}, where crowds throw *grass* garlands at him like confetti. He has just won the world's toaster championship. Trumpets blare and medals clank on his chest. He basks in the **glory**, beeping proudly, and his batteries glow gold with **glory**."],"姑":["aunt","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} with his **aunt**, a fierce *woman* who collects *antique* swimsuits. She models one from 1890 with frills and a bonnet and cannonballs off the roof. Splash! Everyone claps for his **aunt**, who climbs out and changes into an even older antique."],"孙":["grandson","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} rocking a tiny *grandson* in his arms. The baby grabs the dice and rolls a double six every time. The casino panics. Gamblers line up to touch his little toes for luck, and the sailor's **grandson** wins the casino before he can say \"**grandson**\"."],"逃":["to escape","The {Tailor} sprints down the {Staircase} of the {Tower} with a *cracked shell* of an egg on her head and a dragon hatchling behind her. She bursts out onto the *road* and **escapes** on a bicycle, the baby dragon chasing. They both **escape** into the forest, and the tower guards don't even notice."],"牙":["tooth","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and finds a vampire lying in a mud bath, one *fang* aching. She ties a string to the **tooth** and the other end to the door. SLAM! The **tooth** flies across the spa and lands in someone's cucumber water, and the vampire whimpers happily."],"束":["to bind","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands on a *bundle* of floating pool noodles. She lassos them, ties them with rope and **binds** them tight into one huge raft. Then she **binds** the swimmers to it too, so nobody can drift away, and they all bob around grumbling."],"跳":["to jump","The {Tailor} bounces through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} on a pogo stick, *kicking foot* first, and lands on an egg. A *cracked shell* pops open and out leaps a kitten that **jumps** onto her head. Cats everywhere start **jumping**: off tables, out of cups, onto the chandelier."],"顶":["top","The {Dentist} climbs out of the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} with a hammer and a giant *nail*, pinning a single *page* to the very **top** of the corner post. It reads: \"Floss!\" Boxers climb after her to read it, stacking on each other's shoulders, and the dentist bows from the **top** of the pile."],"玉":["jade","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} balancing a glowing green *jade gem* on her nose. Guards chase her, but every time they touch the **jade** they turn calm and start stretching. Soon the whole museum is doing yoga around the stone, and the director swaps the Mona Lisa for more **jade**."],"镇":["to calm","The {Jockey} crashes through the {Trapdoor} into the {Funfair}, where riders are screaming on a runaway rollercoaster. She tosses *gold coins* to the crowd and holds up a huge *magnifying glass* that makes everything look tiny and silly. Everyone giggles and **calms** down. Even the rollercoaster sighs, **calmed**, and parks itself."],"雪":["snow","The {Shepherd} wanders into the {Basement} of the {Ice Rink}, where the *rain* is freezing mid-air. He drags a giant *comb* through the clouds and flakes tumble out: **snow**! It piles up to the ceiling, and the sheep bounce in it, building a snowman wearing his hat, then a whole **snow** family."],"午":["noon","The {Wizard} sits in the {Basement} of the {Pool} grinding a *pestle* in a mortar, waiting for exactly **noon**. The moment the clock strikes twelve, the pestle sings, sunlight shoots through a pipe and every swimmer's shadow disappears. At **noon** sharp the wizard eats lunch, his only spell of the day."],"练":["to practise","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} with a spool of *silk thread* and **practises** knots. Reef knot, bowline, granny knot, a thousand times. She ties the bankers to their chairs by accident. \"Sorry, still **practising**!\" she shouts, and ties the vault door to the moon."],"迫":["to force","The {Pirate} springs up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} and **forces** a terrified *white dove* down the *road* at cutlass-point. \"Deliver my ransom note!\" The dove refuses, so he **forces** it into a cannon and fires it over the walls. It lands on the king's breakfast, note and all."],"爷":["grandpa","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut}, where her **grandpa** sits in a rocking chair telling stories about her *father* as a baby. He does a headstand to prove he's still flexible, then a cartwheel, then a backflip. **Grandpa** lands in the soup and declares it a perfect landing."],"篇":["piece of writing","The {Pirate} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, scribbling on strips of *bamboo* and nailing them under a *nameboard* with his title. It's a **piece of writing** about buried coins, so thrilling that bankers climb ladders to read it. The wind steals one strip, and the whole city chases the **piece of writing** down the street."],"肉":["meat","The {Robot} clanks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} carrying a giant slab of *meat* on his shoulder, dripping and wobbling. He tries to use it as a paddle. The **meat** floats! He rows across the lake on a raft of sausages, and seagulls dive at him, screaming for **meat**."],"嘴":["mouth","The {Zookeeper} opens the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room}, where a pelican with a gigantic *beak* sits next to a toddler's wide open *mouth*. Who can open the biggest **mouth**? The pelican swallows a chair. The toddler swallows a sandwich whole. The zookeeper gasps, and her own **mouth** is the biggest of all."],"馆":["building","The {Gardener} wheels a cart into the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion, where a stern *official* in a top hat guards a tiny *side dish* of peas. He declares the pea a national treasure and builds a whole **building** around it: columns, staircases, ticket desk. Swans queue to visit the **building**."],"遍":["time (round)","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and runs a lap of the *road* round the bank, reading the *nameboard* on every door aloud. Then another **time**. And another. Each **time** round he adds a loaf to the pile, and by the hundredth **time** the bank is buried in bread."],"凡":["ordinary","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} expecting dragons and gold, but finds only a plain white *sail* draped over a chair. It's totally **ordinary**: no ghosts, no treasure, just dust. She is so bored she hoses the sail into a boat, but even that floats in an **ordinary** way."],"础":["foundation","The {Chef} digs into the {Basement} of the {Pool} and pushes a giant *stone* under a *double mountain* of whipped cream. The pool, the diving boards and the snack bar all wobble on top. Without that **foundation** everything would slide away. He calls it a cake with a solid **foundation** and serves it."],"洞":["hole","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} jetty and finds a **hole** in the sea. *Water drops* trickle into it like a drain. She tries to plug it with a *matching cup*, but the cup falls through too. Now there's a cup-shaped **hole**, and fish swim down it waving goodbye."],"卷":["to roll up","The {Juggler} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Mint}, where freshly printed money is drying on a giant *scroll* of paper. She starts to **roll up** the scroll, faster and faster, and rolls up the printer, the guards and herself inside. The mint finds a huge paper burrito and **rolls it up** further."],"坦":["flat","The {Tailor} kneels in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} at *sunrise*, ironing the *soil* with a giant iron until the lumpy floor is perfectly **flat**. Then she irons the stairs, the cat and the butler, all **flat** as pancakes. They slide under the door and go to work like paper dolls."],"牛":["ox","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} and meets a huge *cow* wearing a backpack. Not a cow: an **ox**, with horns, booking a bunk bed. The ninja tries to sneak past, but the **ox** moos and sits on him, and the backpackers take selfies."],"宁":["peaceful","The {Ninja} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, climbs a ladder under the *roof* and hammers one *nail* through a boxing glove. Now nobody can punch. The crowd stops yelling, the boxers have tea, birds sing. It's so **peaceful** that the ninja naps in the ring, very **peaceful**."],"纸":["paper","The {Jockey} rides into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where bees spin *silk thread* into thin sheets and write their *family tree* on each one. Stacks of **paper** rise to the ceiling. The jockey's horse eats one, sneezes, and the whole basement explodes in a snowstorm of **paper**."],"诸":["all","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} doing a *headcount* of the swimmers below. **All** of them? She counts again, and again, and the number grows each time, until **all** the fish in the sea, all the ducks and all the clouds are in the pool, waving to be counted."],"训":["to train","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes} oasis, where a *river* runs between the sand hills. A *small speech bubble* hovers over his head shouting orders to his camels: sit, swim, roll over. He **trains** them until they can paddle down the river in formation, the best **trained** camels in the desert."],"私":["private","The {Sailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} hugging a single golden *grain stalk*, elbowing bees away with one sharp *elbow*. \"**Private**!\" he yells. \"My grain!\" The bees buzz a protest. He puts up a sign, \"**PRIVATE**: no buzzing\", and the bees build a hive on the sign."],"庄":["village","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Swamp} cabin, and a whole *farmstead* sprouts from the mud: barns, ducks, haystacks, a church bell. Soon it's a **village**, with frogs as postmen and alligators running the bakery. The jockey becomes mayor of the **village** because she's the only one with boots."],"祖":["ancestor","The {Zookeeper} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, props a *stepladder* against a *small altar*, and climbs up to light candles for her **ancestor**, a famous hippo tamer. The candles flicker and a ghostly hippo rises, splashing. Every **ancestor** joins in, until the pool is full of ghost hippos doing laps."],"丝":["silk","The {Sailor} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} across a narrow *plank*, while the bees spin shiny threads of **silk** around him. They wrap him from head to toe like a gift. He wobbles, falls, and dangles from the roof on a single strand of **silk**, swinging like a happy pendulum."],"翻":["to turn over","The {Firefighter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} slips on a pile of *feathers* and tumbles across a *footprint field* of muddy tracks. She keeps **turning over**, somersault after somersault, flipping roof tiles, chimneys, the weathervane. By the bottom the whole mansion has **turned over** and sits upside down."],"暴":["violent","The {Baker} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} during a scorching *heatwave*. Ovens explode, bread pops like popcorn, and a **violent** wind slams doors and rips the curtains. The baker wrestles a rogue baguette in a **violent** brawl, and they tumble down the tower together, crumbs everywhere."],"森":["forest","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} ferris wheel and plants a *tree*. Then another *tree*. Then a third *tree*. They multiply like popcorn until the dodgems are under ferns and owls run the ticket booth. The funfair has vanished into a **forest**, and the sailor sails a rowboat through the **forest**."],"塔":["pagoda","The {Tailor} scoops *soil* into the {Basement} of the {Spa} and stacks it higher and higher, each level with a tiny *thatch* roof. It pokes through the ceiling, then the clouds. It's a **pagoda**! Monks climb it, spa guests climb it, and the tailor sews bells to every floor of the **pagoda**."],"默":["silent","The {Magician} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort}, covered in *soot*, with a *dog* who has swallowed his whistle. Not a sound. The soldiers stop shouting, the cannons stop booming. The magician waves his wand and the whole fort turns **silent**, even the birds, even the dog's wagging tail, perfectly **silent**."],"握":["to grasp","The {Wizard} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort}, and a giant *helping hand* reaches out of a tiny *cottage* to **grasp** him. It squeezes him like a lemon. He wriggles loose, but it **grasps** his wand, his beard, his hat, and won't let go until he shakes it politely."],"戏":["drama","The {Shepherd} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto a stage on the {Beach}, where a hero raises a *halberd* in his *right hand* and roars. The sheep play the villains, the seagulls play the orchestra. It's pure **drama**: tears, betrayals, a sheep wedding. The shepherd sobs through every act of the **drama**."],"隐":["hidden","The {Yogi} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Inn} and slips into a crack in the *hillside* behind the wine barrels. Her *racing heart* thumps so loud it might give her away. She stays **hidden** for a week, and the innkeeper stays **hidden** from his taxes in the same crack."],"熟":["ripe","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Pool} roasting peaches over glowing *embers* like a *roast*. They swell, soften and smell divine: perfectly **ripe**. The swimmers climb out dripping and line up. Every bite is so **ripe** that juice squirts across the pool and sticks to the ceiling."],"骨":["bone","The {Gardener} digs in the {Basement} of the {Pool} and unearths a giant *bone*. Then another. A whole dinosaur skeleton rises from the drain and climbs the ladder. The gardener feeds it a **bone**-shaped biscuit and it wags its tail, rattling every **bone**, and dives into the deep end."],"访":["to visit","The {Firefighter} climbs down to the {Basement} of the {Hangar} to **visit** her old friend, who lives in a chalk *square* on the floor. A *small speech bubble* pops up: \"Come in!\" She steps in, has tea, and **visits** every square in the hangar, one after another, until dawn."],"弱":["weak","The {Robot} clanks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and tries to lift a feather. He can't. His arms are **weak** as wet noodles and his batteries flicker. A mouse carries him home on its back, and the robot sighs, feeling so **weak** that even his beeps come out as tiny squeaks."],"蒙":["to cover","The {Magician} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple and pulls out a giant *blindfold*. He uses it to **cover** a monkey's eyes, then a tiger's, then the sun. Darkness falls. He **covers** the whole jungle like a birdcage at night, and the parrots finally stop squawking."],"歌":["song","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} with his *elder brother*, who lets out a huge *yawn* that turns into a tune. They sing a **song** about turnips so loudly the clouds dance. The neighbours join in with pots and pans, and the **song** goes on until the turnips sing too."],"店":["shop","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a rickety *shed* where a *fortune teller* sells crystal balls. They open a **shop** together: toothpaste and prophecies. \"Your future: fewer cavities.\" Customers flood the **shop**, and the dentist predicts every filling."],"鬼":["ghost","The {Gardener} sweeps the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a *ghost* waiting for an appointment that ended in 1850. The **ghost** sighs, rattles a chain and asks for a magazine. The gardener plants a geranium in its lap. The **ghost** is so pleased it haunts the flowerbeds instead."],"软":["soft","The {Robot} rolls a *cart* into the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion, piled with feather pillows. He gives a huge *yawn* and flops onto them. Everything is **soft**: soft pillows, soft swans, soft marshmallow walls. His metal body melts into jelly, and he's too **soft** to stand up."],"典":["canon","The {Dentist} sits in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} behind velvet *curtains*, reading aloud from the great **canon** of tooth law. Each rule is a *song*, and bankers sing along: \"floss before dawn\". The **canon** is so long the dentist reads it to the vault, which hums every verse."],"欲":["desire","The {Yogi} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a painted *valley* full of chocolate rivers. She gives a huge hungry *yawn*: **desire** sweeps over her. She wants everything: the cake, the fountain, the moon. Her **desire** grows so big that the museum guards hide the exhibits."],"萨":["Bodhisattva","The {Sailor} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and finds a serene **Bodhisattva** sitting on a mat of fresh *grass*, glowing gold. Spa guests float around in bliss. The sailor offers him a cucumber slice, and the **Bodhisattva** smiles, blessing the bubble bath, which turns into lotus flowers."],"伙":["companion","The {Hunter} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} beside a *campfire*, alone, until a *standing person* steps out of the shadows with sausages. Instant friends! They sing, swap stories and toast marshmallows. Now he has a **companion**, and the **companion** follows him everywhere, even into the bath."],"遭":["to suffer","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} when a feeding *trough* of mud tips over and slides down the *road* straight at her. Splat! She **suffers** a bath of mud, then a flock of pigeons, then a hailstorm. She **suffers** it all with a smile, and the pigs cheer."],"盘":["plate","The {Pirate} clomps up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with a little *boat* balanced on a big *dish*. He serves it at dinner: a **plate** with a ship sailing on gravy. Guests poke the sails with forks. Then he spins the **plate** like a frisbee, and it sails out the window."],"爸":["dad","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and finds a giant *python* wearing a *father*'s tie and slippers, reading the paper in a mud bath. \"**Dad**?\" The python nods, hisses a dad joke and wraps the baker in a hug. **Dad** always gives the longest hugs."],"扩":["to enlarge","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and grumbles that his garden *shed* is too small for his crowns. A giant *helping hand* grabs the walls and stretches them like chewing gum. The shed swells to the size of a stadium. The king keeps shouting \"**enlarge**!\", so the hand **enlarges** it until it swallows the warehouse."],"盖":["lid","The {Gardener} pops up through the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} with a *sheep* that won't stop eating. She drops a huge silver *dish* over it like a **lid**: clang! The sheep bleats from inside, so she stacks a pot **lid**, a bin lid and a manhole cover on top, and the whole pile baas."],"弄":["to do","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} and finds a lazy *king* lying in the *grass*, waving a list of chores. \"What should I **do**?\" the king asks. The ninja **does** everything at once: mows, sweeps, juggles fish, paints the lagoon, in a blur of black pyjamas."],"雄":["male","The {Shepherd} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Club} beside a *sparrow* flexing a huge *upper arm*. The sparrow puffs its chest, shows off its muscles and crows like a rooster. It's the most **male** bird in the world, and every **male** in the club tries to arm-wrestle it and loses."],"稳":["steady","The {Wizard} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, his *racing heart* pounding, balancing a single *grain stalk* on his nose. The rollercoaster thunders overhead and the floor shakes, but he stays **steady**. Not a wobble. Children stack teacups on the grain, and he keeps it **steady** all night."],"忘":["to forget","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and trips over a *tombstone* engraved with his own name. His *heart* skips. Who buried him? He can't remember. He **forgets** his spells, his hat, his way out. Then he **forgets** that he forgot, and happily flies off on a broom he thinks is a plane."],"亿":["hundred million","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} and counts swans. A *standing person* points: another *swan*, and another. They multiply until there are a **hundred million** swans honking, covering the sand, the sea and the sky. The yogi keeps counting calmly, all **hundred million** of them, one breath per swan."],"刺":["thorn","The {Tsar} plummets through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and sits on a huge *thorn*. OUCH! A *standing knife* next to it can't cut it free. The **thorn** sticks to his royal bottom while the bees laugh. He waddles back to the throne, and the throne now has a **thorn** on it too."],"拥":["to embrace","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} spreads her arms wide and **embraces** everyone who climbs up: tourists, crabs, the postman. A giant *helping hand* carries a *bucket* of fish and she hugs that too. She **embraces** the whole lagoon until the water wraps its waves around her."],"徒":["disciple","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, followed by a puffing *runner* who copies her *footsteps* exactly. Every stitch she sews, he sews. Every dive, he dives. He is her devoted **disciple**, and soon a hundred **disciples** march behind her, all wearing tape measures."],"姆":["nanny","The {Magician} clatters into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a stern *woman* with an umbrella is babysitting a hundred toddlers. She's the **nanny**, and a better *mother* than anyone. She pulls rubber ducks from her handbag. The magician tries a trick, but the **nanny** out-tricks him with a floating pram."],"杨":["poplar","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar}, where a tall skinny *tree* has sprouted through the roof, its leaves glittering in the *sun rays*. It's a **poplar**, shaking and whispering in the wind. Planes park in its shade, and the yogi does a tree pose beside the **poplar**, much shorter."],"齐":["neat","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} club with giant scissors and trims everything into a perfect *trimmed hedge*: palm trees, sandcastles, the lifeguard's hair. Everything is **neat**, square and level. She even trims the waves until the sea is **neat** as a carpet."],"赛":["competition","The {Sailor} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} with a starter pistol. Bang! A **competition** begins: crabs race across the *roof* of the beach hut, coconuts roll downhill and seagulls sprint. The sailor commentates, gets too excited and joins the **competition** himself, in flippers."],"趣":["interesting","The {Cheerleader} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} chasing a *runner* who snatched a vase with one *grabbing hand*. Pom-poms flying, she follows him past mummies and suits of armour. It's the most **interesting** tour ever, and the visitors follow, cheering, finding everything suddenly **interesting**."],"曲":["crooked","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} sings a *song* so wobbly that everything around her bends. The flagpole kinks, the chimney twists and the statues lean over. The whole skyline goes **crooked**, and the museum curator straightens his **crooked** glasses in despair."],"刀":["knife","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} sharpening a giant *knife* that flashes in the sun. Pigeons gasp. She uses the **knife** to slice clouds into neat cubes, to cut the wind and to trim the moon. The tower dwellers duck as the **knife** spins back like a boomerang."],"床":["bed","The {Chef} squelches up the {Staircase} of the {Swamp} cabin and finds a *tree* growing out of a *shed*. He chops it, carves it and builds a giant **bed**, then cooks breakfast in it. Frogs leap into the blanket, alligators fluff the pillows, and the chef snores in the **bed** with a frying pan."],"迎":["to welcome","The {Yogi} stands on the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, lifting her *upward gaze* to the sky as a hot-air balloon drifts down the *road*. She throws petals and bangs a gong to **welcome** the passengers: astronauts, grannies, a goat. Boxers line up to **welcome** them with soft punches."],"冰":["ice","The {Baker} slips across the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}, where *water* poured from a hose has frozen into dangling *icicles*. Everything is **ice**: ice gloves, ice ropes, ice bell. The baker skates round the ring juggling frozen buns, and the boxers fight in skates on the **ice**."],"虚":["empty","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Museum}, which looks out over old *ruins*. He opens the exhibit cases: **empty**. The frames: empty. The ticket booth: empty. Even the gift shop is just echoes. He shouts \"hello?\" and his echo replies \"**empty**!\" from every corner."],"玩":["to play","The {Wizard} skips up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with a *king* who flips a *yuan coin* to see who's \"it\". Heads! They **play** hide and seek, tag and hopscotch through every hallway. The wizard cheats with spells, and the king **plays** by hiding inside a chandelier."],"析":["to analyze","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut with a *woodcutter*, who splits a log into tiny pieces. They **analyze** every splinter under a magnifying glass, sorting grain, knots and beetle tunnels into charts. The seagulls want to **analyze** the sandwiches, so the woodcutter splits those too."],"窗":["window","The {Chef} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Swamp} hut, where steam pours from a *chimney* built into a *cave*. He knocks a hole in the wall to let the smoke out. Now it's a **window**! Frogs peer in, mosquitoes peer in, and the chef hangs curtains on the **window** made of spaghetti."],"醒":["to wake up","The {Shepherd} snores in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring}, hugging a *wine jug*. Then a falling *star* crashes through the roof and bonks him on the nose. He **wakes up**! Bells ring, boxers shout, sheep bleat, and everyone else in the stadium **wakes up** too, in their pyjamas."],"妻":["wife","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} villa, waving pom-poms at a bride in flip-flops. It's her new *wife*, who parachutes in wearing a veil. They throw a beach party on the roof, and the **wife** wins the sandcastle contest while the cheerleader cheers her **wife** louder than the sea."],"透":["to seep through","The {Tailor} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} as water begins to **seep through** the floorboards. A pink *blossom* drifts in on the trickle, then another, from a *road* outside. The leak grows; flowers, fish and frogs **seep through** every crack, and the boathouse becomes a soggy garden."],"购":["to purchase","The {Gardener} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} with a fishing *hook* and dangles it into a pile of *shell* money. He **purchases** a canoe, a lifebuoy and a pet seal, paying with seashells. The shopkeeper accepts, so he **purchases** the boathouse too, and the lake."],"替":["to substitute","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} volleyball court, where the star player has twisted an ankle. The coach sends in a *substitute*: a walrus. Then another **substitute**: a beach umbrella. Finally the tailor herself **substitutes**, and wins with a needle serve."],"塞":["to stuff in","The {Sailor} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut and **stuffs in** everything he owns through a hole in the *roof*: hammocks, coconuts, a canoe, three parrots. The hut bulges. He **stuffs in** one more banana, and the walls burst, scattering his belongings over the whole island."],"努":["to strive","The {Ninja} sweats in the {Basement} of the {Pool}, a tired *drudge* pushing an enormous boulder up the ladder with one *strong arm*. Push, slip, push again. He **strives** all night, grunting. At dawn the boulder plops into the pool, and the ninja **strives** to fish it out again."],"休":["to rest","The {Shepherd} flops onto the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} beside a *standing person* leaning against a shady *tree*. They both sigh and **rest**. The sheep **rest** too, then the clouds stop drifting, the backpackers stop talking, and the whole city takes a nap under one tree."],"虎":["tiger","The {Hunter} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, rifle shaking, and finds a *crouching tiger* in a swimming cap. The **tiger** stretches, roars, and does a perfect backstroke. The hunter drops his gun and applauds. He buys the **tiger** a towel and they share the hot tub."],"扬":["to raise","The {Yogi} bounds up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and lifts a giant *helping hand* toward the *sun rays*. She **raises** a plane over her head, then a flag, then the roof. Everyone cheers and **raises** their arms, and the hangar floats upward like a balloon."],"途":["route","The {Tailor} hurries down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and follows a *road* paved with *leftovers*: half a sandwich, a banana peel, cold noodles. Seagulls swoop. She marks the **route** on a map with thread. The **route** leads to a picnic where a bear is eating the rest."],"侵":["to invade","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} spots a *standing person* sneaking over the wall with a ladder, then a hundred more. They **invade** the inn: they steal the pillows, eat the porridge and occupy the bathtubs. The cheerleader chants \"No **invading**!\" and they all cheer back."],"刑":["punishment","The {Shepherd} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a referee has locked a cheating boxer in wooden *stocks*. His **punishment**: the crowd throws custard pies. Splat, splat, splat! The shepherd's sheep lick the custard off his face, which is the worst **punishment** of all."],"绿":["green","The {Lifeguard} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum}, tugging a spool of *silk thread* dyed a shocking **green**. She ties it to the *logbook* and swings it round; everything it touches turns green: statues, paintings, the guards' noses. By lunchtime the museum is completely **green**."],"兄":["elder brother","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Club} beside his *big brother*, who is ten feet tall and wears a cape. His **elder brother** lifts him up, carries the sheep, fixes the chimney and wins every game. The shepherd sulks, but his **elder brother** gives him a piggyback to the moon."],"迅":["rapid","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes} house onto a *road* where a *swift* bird zips past faster than sound. He chases it on a camel. Whoosh! The camel is so **rapid** it skids across the dunes, leaving rapid dust clouds, and the swift waves from far ahead, even more **rapid**."],"套":["to cover","The {Tailor} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a giant sock, ready to **cover** a *big man* with wild *flowing locks*. She yanks it over his head. His hair still escapes, so she adds a tent, a duvet and a tarp. The tower is now **covered** too."],"贸":["trade","The {Magician} vanishes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a busy market, where traders bang a wooden *mortise* together and swap a *shell* for a sheep. Shouting, haggling, juggling. The magician joins the **trade**, swapping rabbits for teapots, and the tower becomes a world **trade** fair."],"毕":["to finish","The {Baker} pops out of the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} where *twins* are racing to the *cross* marked in the sand. They sprint, dive, tumble. Both **finish** at the same moment, panting. The baker hands them cupcakes and **finishes** the race himself an hour later, crawling."],"唯":["only","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house and finds a *sparrow* with a big *mouth* singing alone. The **only** bird left; the others flew south. The wizard turns the stairs into a choir stand, but the sparrow refuses to share. It's the **only** singer and it knows it."],"谷":["valley","The {Gardener} descends into the {Basement} of the {Pool} and finds a hidden *valley*: mountains on both sides, a river down the middle and sheep grazing. She plants carrots on the slopes. Swimmers wander in and get lost in the **valley**, and the pool becomes the deepest **valley** in town."],"轮":["wheel","The {Lifeguard} rolls down the {Staircase} of the {Casino} on a *cart* with one giant **wheel**. It bumps over a *neat stack* of poker chips and they scatter. The roulette wheel joins in, then every wheel in town rolls inside, and the casino becomes a racetrack of **wheels**."],"库":["warehouse","The {King} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a secret *warehouse* under the deep end. Inside are rows of rubber ducks, inflatable flamingos and old swimsuits, stacked to the ceiling. He declares it the royal **warehouse** and hires a duck to guard the **warehouse** door."],"迹":["trace","The {Juggler} pops up through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and follows a *road* of sweaty footprints left by a *sweating man*. Every **trace** shows him jogging, crying, buying ice cream. She follows every **trace** until she finds him asleep under a towel, still sweating."],"尤":["especially","The {Yogi} clambers up the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} and discovers she has a magical *wart* on her nose that glows. Everything is beautiful, **especially** the wart. Boats, waves, seagulls, all lovely, but **especially** the wart, which she paints gold and shows off to everyone."],"竞":["to compete","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} and leaps onto a *podium*, where a *big brother* in a cape challenges her to **compete**. Who can juggle more knives? They **compete** for hours, adding swords, eggs and kittens, until both stand on the podium tied."],"街":["street","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} and paints a *crossroads* onto the snow, then props up a *jade tablet* as a street sign. Instantly a **street** appears: lamp posts, cafés, a bus full of yetis. She juggles traffic cones at the junction while yetis honk up and down the **street**."],"促":["to hurry","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and stomps one huge *foot*. \"**Hurry**!\" A *standing person* in a dressing gown jumps in, swims ten laps in three seconds and climbs out. The tsar stamps again, and every swimmer **hurries** so fast that the water sloshes out over the town."],"延":["to extend","The {Yogi} walks down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} onto a *stretching road* that keeps getting longer. Every step she takes, it grows another mile. She stretches too, arms reaching across rivers, legs crossing valleys. She **extends** the road around the world, and then **extends** her lunch break to match."],"震":["to shake","The {Jockey} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair}, and a giant *clam* in the ghost train slams shut under the *rain*. BOOM! The ground starts to **shake**. The ferris wheel wobbles, candy floss trembles, the dodgems bounce. Everything **shakes** like jelly, and the jockey's horse dances to the rhythm."],"弃":["to abandon","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} with a pram full of tall *grass*. She waves her pom-poms, gets bored, and **abandons** the pram by a sandcastle. Then she **abandons** her shoes, her whistle and her team, and wanders off to start a new career as a crab."],"甲":["first","The {Juggler} clanks into the {Basement} of the {Piazza} wearing shiny *armour* and wins every contest down there: arm-wrestling, pizza eating, spaghetti juggling. **First** in everything! She wears a gold medal on her helmet, and the pigeons bow to the **first** knight of the square."],"伟":["great","The {Wizard} rummages in the {Basement} of the {Lake} house and finds a tiny *standing person* tied with a *leather strap*. Untied, he grows and grows, until he's a giant who builds bridges with one hand. A **great** man! The wizard is too short to hug him, so he hugs his **great** toe."],"麻":["hemp","The {Magician} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} carrying a bundle of scratchy *hemp*. He weaves it into towels, robes and slippers. Guests itch and squirm. \"Natural **hemp**!\" he cries, and pulls a rope of **hemp** from his sleeve that never ends, until the spa is knee-deep in it."],"川":["river","The {Chef} stirs a pot on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion, and soup overflows into a roaring *river*. It rushes down the roof, across the lawn and out to sea. Swans paddle on it. The chef keeps stirring, and the **river** of broth grows wider, a delicious **river** that smells of noodles."],"申":["to state","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} ticket booth and holds up a long *skewer* stacked with kebabs. Megaphone on, she **states** the rules: no cutting queues, no feeding seagulls, no laughing at the clowns. She **states** them so firmly that the skewer stands to attention and so does the rollercoaster."],"缓":["slow","The {Hunter} dangles into the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion on a *rescue rope* made of *silk thread*. It lowers him **slow**, slower, slowest. A snail overtakes him. The swans fall asleep watching. By the time he lands it's next week, and everything in the pavilion has gone **slow** too."],"潜":["hidden","The {Cheerleader} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange}, dripping *water drops*, because she's a secret agent. A *substitute* teller takes her place at the desk. She stays **hidden** inside a vault, a periscope poking out of a coin purse. Nobody knows she's there; she's **hidden** for twelve years."],"闪":["to dodge","The {Sheriff} bursts into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} through a creaky *gate*, and a *person* flings pies at her. She **dodges**: left, right, backflip. Custard misses her by inches. She **dodges** so fast she leaves a blur, and the pies hit the butler instead."],"售":["to sell","The {Sheriff} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and sets up a stall with a *sparrow* that shouts through its big *mouth*: \"Boats for **sale**!\" It **sells** rowing boats, canoes, a submarine and a duck. Everything goes. The sparrow even tries to **sell** the sheriff."],"灯":["lamp","The {Dentist} hammers a *nail* into the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse and hangs a jar with a tiny *campfire* in it. It's a **lamp**! Moths, monkeys and fireflies gather round to read, and the dentist checks their teeth by the light of the **lamp**."],"针":["needle","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} threads a giant **needle** with a string of *gold coins* and stitches the sky into a *cross* pattern. Clouds get sewn into quilts. A kite tangles in the thread. She sews the moon on tight with her **needle**, so it never wanders off."],"哲":["wise","The {Jockey} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} to see a **wise** old owl holding a *snapped stick* and opening its *mouth* to speak. Every word is a riddle that solves itself. The jockey asks \"Why?\" and the owl answers \"Because.\" It's the most **wise** thing she has ever heard, and she writes it on her saddle."],"络":["network","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and finds a giant spider weaving *silk thread* between every shelf. A lost *visitor* is tangled in the middle. The threads link every box, every forklift, every phone. It's a **network**, and every tug sends news across the **network** in seconds."],"抵":["to resist","The {Dentist} digs into the {Basement} of the {Beach} house as a huge wave crashes in. She plants a *helping hand* against the *foundation* and pushes back. She **resists** the wave, the tide and a passing whale. Soaked but standing, she keeps **resisting** until the sea gives up and goes home."],"朱":["vermilion","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} spilling a pot of *red lacquer* everywhere. The tiles turn **vermilion**, the slide turns vermilion, the swimmers come out glowing like lobsters. She paints her horse **vermilion** too, and it shines like a fire engine."],"埃":["dust","The {Ghost} floats up to the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse and sneezes on a pile of *soil*. A huge cloud of **dust** puffs out, swirling into a tiny *full stop* that hangs in the air. Everyone coughs. The ghost sneezes again, more **dust**, until the island looks like a giant snow globe of grime."],"抱":["to hold","The {Baker} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a giant *parcel* that won't stop wriggling. A *helping hand* tries to take it, but the baker **holds** it tight. Inside: a puppy. He **holds** it all night, singing lullabies, and it falls asleep in his apron."],"鼓":["drum","The {Gardener} bangs a fat *branch* on a giant *drum* in the {Basement} of the {Pool}. BOOM! The water jumps out of the pool. BOOM! The tiles rattle. She plays the **drum** faster and the swimmers dance underwater, while the **drum** booms like thunder through every pipe in town."],"植":["to plant","The {Jockey} skips down the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, dangling a *plumb line* to check that every hole is straight, then **plants** a *tree* in each one. Saplings sprout everywhere: in the honey, in the queen's bed, on the stairs. She **plants** so many that the beehive becomes a forest."],"纯":["pure","The {Chef} glides down the {Staircase} of the {Casino} in a white apron spun from *silk thread*, carrying a pot of snow-white soup from his mountain *camp*. Everything he touches turns **pure**: dice turn white, cards go blank, money glows. The gamblers sip the soup and feel **pure** for the first time."],"夏":["summer","The {Shepherd} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Piazza} and the sun blazes: it's high *summer*. Fountains sizzle, ice creams melt, and his sheep shed their wool in a fluffy blizzard. The shepherd spreads a towel on the cobbles and declares **summer** officially open, with sheep in sunglasses enjoying **summer**."],"忍":["to endure","The {Robot} sits in the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where a *blade edge* tickles his metal *heart*. It's itchy and annoying, but he must **endure** it: clowns honk at him, children poke him, a goat chews his antenna. He **endures** everything with a polite beep and a twitching eyebrow."],"页":["page","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and finds one giant *page* on the floor. She reads the **page**, turns it over, and it turns into a flying carpet. Words tumble off as she flies, and villagers catch them in buckets, each word taking a whole **page** to itself."],"杰":["hero","The {Juggler} bounds up the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a fallen *tree* is burning down to glowing *embers*. Trapped yetis whimper. She juggles the embers out the window, carries a yeti on each shoulder and saves the day. A **hero**! The yetis chant \"**hero**\" and give her a medal made of ice."],"筑":["to build","The {Jockey} rides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} hauling poles of *bamboo* and a wooden *brace*. She **builds** a tower in the deep end: a diving board, then a castle, then a whole skyscraper. Swimmers climb it, and she keeps **building** until it pokes the moon."],"折":["to break","The {Jockey} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} with a twig and a *snapped stick* in her hand, and everything she touches **breaks**: snap goes the banister, crack goes the chair, crunch goes the teapot. Her horse sneezes and **breaks** the window, and now the hut is mostly kindling."],"郑":["Zheng","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle} carrying a *pitcher* of lemonade for Mr **Zheng**, a famous explorer who lives in a tree. He drinks it all, burps loudly, and carves his name into a banana: **Zheng**. Monkeys copy it everywhere."],"贝":["shell","The {Baker} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house into the water, and an enormous *shell* snaps shut on his hat. He prises it open with a baguette: inside is a pearl the size of a melon. He keeps the **shell** as a bath, and floats across the lake in the **shell**."],"尊":["to respect","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} and raises a glass in a *toast* to the oldest tortoise in the world. Everyone bows. Gamblers take off their hats to **respect** him, the dice fall silent, and the tortoise blinks slowly, accepting all that **respect**."],"吴":["Wu","The {Wizard} clatters up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} chasing a *loudmouth* named Mr **Wu**, who shouts his own name on every step. \"**Wu**! Wu! Wu!\" The swimmers chant along like an owl choir. The wizard shrinks him with a spell, but tiny Mr Wu is even louder."],"秀":["graceful","The {Shepherd} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} balancing a single pink *blossom* on his crook. He twirls, he pirouettes, he leaps over bunk beds. He is **graceful**, impossibly graceful, and the backpackers sigh. Even his sheep tiptoe behind him in a **graceful** line."],"混":["to mix","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} into a huge bowl and starts to **mix**: *water drops*, poker chips, playing cards and a swarm of *insect* gamblers. He stirs and stirs with a rifle. Everything gets **mixed** up, and the insects start playing poker with soggy cards."],"臣":["official","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} helter-skelter, where a *minister* in robes is checking tickets. He's a royal **official**, stamping papers, inspecting candy floss and fining the dodgems. The chef serves him a hot dog, and the **official** stamps it \"approved\"."],"雅":["elegant","The {Yogi} glides into the {Basement} of the {Spa}, where a *sparrow* with a single silver *fang* sips tea from a thimble. It's terribly **elegant**: tiny pearls, a silk shawl, a pinky raised. The yogi tries to copy it, and spills tea on her nose, much less **elegant**."],"振":["to shake","The {Jockey} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and a *helping hand* grabs a giant *clam* and **shakes** it like a maraca. Pearls rattle out, the carousel spins faster, and the ferris wheel jiggles. The jockey's teeth chatter; the hand keeps **shaking** until the funfair hums."],"染":["to dye","The {Robot} clanks into the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, where a *mountain spring* bubbles purple. He dips a whole *tree* into it, then the curtains, then the butler. Everything gets **dyed**: purple sheep, purple walls, purple soup. The robot **dyes** himself last and shines like a giant grape."],"盛":["flourishing","The {Sheriff} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} temple holding a golden *trophy* and a *dish* piled with mangoes. Wherever she sets them down, fruit trees sprout, flowers bloom and villages grow. Everything is **flourishing**; the jungle is so **flourishing** that the vines start building houses."],"怒":["anger","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a poor *drudge* scrubbing tiles. The drudge's *heart* swells with **anger**. He goes red, steam pours from his ears and the pool boils. His **anger** blows the diving board into orbit, and the ninja apologises in a hurry."],"舞":["to dance","The {Wizard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, waves his wand, and his slippers grow *dancing feet*. He starts to **dance**: tango, twist, moonwalk. The mop joins in, then the lifeguard, then the water itself, which **dances** in waves up and down the walls."],"圆":["round","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, where an *employee* is building a *fence* around a giant coin. Everything is **round**: round fence, round coins, round guards. She rolls up into a round ball and bounces down the stairs, followed by a hundred **round** coins."],"搞":["to do","The {Gardener} trudges into the {Basement} of the {Tower} with a mile-long to-do list. A *helping hand* pops out of the wall and asks \"What shall I **do**?\" It does everything: polishes the *tower*, waters the cellar, weeds the stairs. Then it **does** the gardener's hair."],"狂":["mad","The {King} squelches up the {Staircase} of the {Swamp} castle, chased by a *mad dog* wearing a crown. It barks at frogs, bites logs and howls at teapots. The king catches the madness and goes **mad** too, dancing in the mud, sending royal decrees to the mosquitoes, utterly **mad**."],"措":["to handle","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} where a mountain of *sun-dried meat* has toppled. A *helping hand* swoops in to **handle** it: stacks, wraps, labels. The tsar barks orders, and the hand **handles** him too, folding him neatly into a crate."],"姓":["surname","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a *woman* holds a little *seedling* and announces it needs a **surname**. The crowd shouts suggestions: Punch, Mudge, Sprout. The shepherd yells \"Wool!\" and the seedling sprouts a fluffy **surname** tag."],"残":["to destroy","The {Tsar} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, followed by a clattering *skeleton* waving *twin blades*. They **destroy** everything: vases shattered, curtains shredded, the piano chopped into toothpicks. The skeleton is having so much fun it **destroys** its own leg and hops."],"秋":["autumn","The {Cheerleader} leaps onto the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} and shakes her pom-poms, and red and gold leaves come pouring out. It's suddenly *autumn*. Backpackers rake leaves off their bunks, squirrels hoard their socks and a pumpkin rolls down the stairs. She cheers \"Go **autumn**!\" and the trees drop every leaf for **autumn**."],"培":["to cultivate","The {Pirate} kneels on the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house, heaping *soil* around a sad little seed. A *spitting mouth* carved in the wall sprays water on it every hour. He **cultivates** it with sea shanties and rum-scented compost. It grows into a palm tree, and he **cultivates** coconuts on the stairs."],"迷":["to be lost","The {Magician} wanders down the {Staircase} of the {Beach} hotel with a *lost traveller* clutching a map upside down. They try left, then right, then a secret door. Every exit leads back to the stairs. They are both **lost**, and the magician makes the map vanish, so now they are truly **lost**."],"诚":["sincere","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} lodge holding a golden *trophy* and a *small speech bubble* that says \"I really mean it.\" He is **sincere**: he hands the trophy to the monkey who stole his bananas. The monkey weeps. Even the parrots feel how **sincere** he is and stop swearing."],"宽":["wide","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion and pulls the *roof* wider and wider, like dough. Purple *amaranth* flowers spill over the edges. The roof becomes so **wide** that it covers the pond, the park and the city. Swans skate on it, and the king rolls across the **wide** tiles like a bowling ball."],"宇":["universe","The {Yogi} floats into the {Basement} of the {Museum}, where a dusty *coat stand* is propping up a crumbling *roof*. She lifts the roof off and finds the whole **universe** hidden underneath: planets, comets, a galaxy shaped like a teapot. She hangs Saturn on the coat stand and naps in the middle of the **universe**."],"猛":["fierce","The {Magician} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Jungle} hut, where a *prowling dog* guards a sleeping *firstborn* tiger cub. The dog snarls, foam flying, **fierce** as a dragon. The magician pulls out a rabbit, the dog eats the hat, and the cub wakes up even more **fierce**, roaring a tiny roar."],"摆":["to arrange","The {Baker} kneels in the {Basement} of the {Island} hut, where a *dropped net* has scattered shells and starfish everywhere. A *helping hand* helps him **arrange** them in rows: big shells, small shells, rainbow shells. He **arranges** them into a perfect cake shape, then eats the one made of sugar."],"梅":["plum","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house to a *tree* heavy with purple **plum** fruit. A *busy mother* rushes past with baskets, picking, pitting, jamming. The magician pulls a plum from her ear, then a dozen, and soon every stair is sticky with **plum** jam."],"毁":["to destroy","The {Hunter} swings a huge *war club* in the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room}. Crash! The magazines fly. Bang! The chairs explode. He **destroys** the clock, the vending machine, the potted fern. The receptionist calmly takes his name, and he **destroys** the pen too."],"伸":["to stretch","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}, where a *standing person* skewered on a giant *skewer* begins to **stretch**. His arms stretch to the rollercoaster, his neck to the ferris wheel. He **stretches** so far he can tickle the clouds and ring the bell on the high striker."],"摩":["to rub","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort} with a scratchy bundle of *hemp* in one *hand*. He **rubs** a cannon with it until it shines and a genie pops out. The genie **rubs** its eyes, grumbles, and grants him a wish: a fort-sized bubble bath."],"盟":["alliance","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} treehouse to a *dish* glowing with the *sun and moon* side by side. Every animal crowds round: lions, monkeys, ants. They shake paws over the dish and form an **alliance** against mosquitoes. The magician seals the **alliance** with a fizzing firework."],"末":["end","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} and climbs to the very *treetop* of the tallest pine. He keeps climbing until there's no tree left: the **end**. He waves a flag at the very **end** of the world, where the sky is held up by string."],"乃":["to be","The {Ninja} slides into the {Basement} of the {Island} cave and finds a ribbon spelling out a riddle: \"Who are you **to be**?\" The *ribbon* wraps around him and ties him into a parcel labelled \"ninja\". So that's what he is **to be**: a present, delivered to the island's crab king."],"悲":["sad","The {Baker} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house, so **sad** that his *heart* droops like a wet sock. A bird with *spread wings* lands beside him and sobs too. Their tears fill the gutters and the lake rises. Even the bread is **sad**, sagging and soggy."],"拍":["to clap","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} fort and starts to *clap*. His parrot joins in, then the crabs, then the coconuts thumping on the sand. The whole island begins **clapping**, the palm trees too. They **clap** so hard that a passing ship turns round to take a bow."],"丁":["man","The {Dentist} hops onto the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} and hammers a giant *nail* into the beam. It wobbles, sprouts arms and legs and becomes a skinny little **man**. He spars with the boxers, bending but never falling. Everyone cheers for the **man** made from a nail."],"赵":["to surpass","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} on a racing *runner* holding a pair of *scissors*. He snips the finish ribbon early and **surpasses** every rival. Then he **surpasses** the clouds, the moon, and finally himself, overtaking his own shadow in a cloud of sparks."],"硬":["hard","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} and lands head-first on a *stone*. BONG! It rings like a *gong*. Her head is **hard**, the stone is **hard**, and the boxers' gloves bounce off them both. She meditates on the stone, which gradually turns into a cushion out of politeness."],"麦":["wheat","The {Magician} pops up through the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} with a pile of *seedling top* sprouts and *trudging feet* covered in mud. Wherever he walks, **wheat** springs up: golden, waving, rustling. By sunset the island is an ocean of **wheat**, and the coconuts are confused."],"蒋":["Jiang","The {Juggler} skids into the {Basement} of the {Stadium}, where a stern *general* named **Jiang** lies hidden in tall *grass*, planning a parade. She juggles his medals. He's furious, then delighted, and General **Jiang** promotes her to Chief Juggler of the army."],"操":["to grasp","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} as a flock of birds flies past in a riot of *birdsong*. A giant *helping hand* reaches out and **grasps** one tune right out of the air. The tsar **grasps** it too and keeps it in his crown, so he hums all day."],"耶":["ye (sound)","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} on a tiny *hillside* of pillows, cupping one *ear* to the wind. Every echo comes back \"**ye**!\" She shouts \"ye!\", the mountains shout \"**ye**!\", and the whole valley goes \"ye, ye, ye\" like an excited choir of goats."],"阻":["to block","The {Zookeeper} wedges a *stepladder* across the {Basement} of the {Pool}, then piles a *hillside* of sandbags behind it. She **blocks** the drain, the door and the escaping penguins. A walrus tries to squeeze through, and she **blocks** him with her own belly."],"订":["to book","The {Dentist} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boxing Ring} with a *small speech bubble* saying \"Reserved\". She hammers a *nail* through it into the best seat. She **books** the front row, then the ring, then the boxers, and **books** an appointment to check their teeth."],"彩":["colour","The {Tsar} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Island} cave, where a *fruit picker* paints the walls with *bristles* of a giant brush. Red, gold, turquoise! **Colour** splashes everywhere: on the bats, the stalactites, the tsar's beard. He sneezes and a rainbow of **colour** shoots out of his nose."],"抽":["to pull out","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse}, where a *sprouting field* of carrots grows in the gutters. A giant *helping hand* reaches down and **pulls out** a carrot, then another, then a pirate, then a whole boat. The chef keeps **pulling out** things until the boathouse is empty."],"赞":["to praise","The {Zookeeper} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to watch *two racers* sprint for a golden *shell*. They tie! She **praises** them both so loudly that the chandelier rattles. The butler **praises** them too, the dogs bark praise, and the racers blush like tomatoes."],"魔":["devil","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort} and finds a *ghost* wrapped in a cloak of *hemp*, horns poking out. It's a **devil**, grinning, juggling fireballs. The magician tries a disappearing trick, but the **devil** makes the magician disappear first, and laughs from the battlements."],"纷":["numerous","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} slicing a giant *cut cake* while a spool of *silk thread* streams ribbons into the wind. Confetti, balloons, cake crumbs, flags: **numerous** things whirl everywhere. She tries to count them, but they're too **numerous**, so she hoses them into a rainbow."],"沿":["along","The {Yogi} walks down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, following a trail of *water drops* **along** the hallway, **along** the kitchen and out the door. They lead along the river to a duck dripping in a dressing gown. She walks along with it, meditating at every puddle."],"喊":["to shout","The {Hunter} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, gets a mouthful of *salt* by mistake and opens his *mouth* to **shout**. \"AAARGH!\" The windows shatter, the wine bottles pop and the butler's wig blows off. He **shouts** so loud that the whole mansion jumps three feet."],"违":["to disobey","The {Wizard} bounds up the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house, wearing a *leather strap* of rules: no spells, no running on the *road*, no frogs in the kitchen. He **disobeys** them all at once: spells, sprinting, frogs everywhere. He even **disobeys** the stairs and walks up the banister."],"妹":["younger sister","The {Magician} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house with his **younger sister**, a tiny *woman* holding a *sapling*. She plants it in his hat. It grows! His **younger sister** giggles, climbs the tree and pulls rabbits out of his hair."],"浪":["wave","The {Lifeguard} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} with a *good meal* on a tray, as *water drops* turn into a roaring **wave**. It crashes through the hangar, lifting jets like toy boats. She surfs the **wave** on her tray, never spilling a single noodle."],"汇":["to converge","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where *water drops* drip from every tap into one *open crate*. Rivers of patients, magazines and rubber ducks all **converge** on the crate. The streams **converge** so fast the crate fills, floats, and sails into the doctor's office."],"币":["coin","The {Baker} slides down a giant *slide* through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, landing on a *towel* covered in golden **coins**. He flips one: heads, he gets a cake; tails, a seagull steals his hat. Every **coin** lands on its edge, spinning forever."],"丰":["abundant","The {Firefighter} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} lodge and plants a single stalk of *wheat*. Boom! Crops burst out everywhere: mangoes, rice, pumpkins, a mountain of bread. The harvest is **abundant**, so **abundant** that monkeys sell snacks to tourists and the lodge sinks under the fruit."],"蓝":["blue","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, where an *inspector* in a trench coat is painting the *grass* bright **blue**. She blows her whistle, but he paints her blue too, then the stairs, then the sky. The mansion is now completely **blue**, and so is the inspector's tongue."],"殊":["special","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, where a *skeleton* coated in shiny *red lacquer* is diving in. It's a **special** guest: it does a triple somersault and lands as a pile of bones that rebuild themselves. The judges hold up a **special** score: eleven out of ten."],"献":["to offer","The {Shepherd} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} with a *dog* wearing a hat that points *south*. He kneels before the bankers to **offer** them the dog. They refuse. He **offers** the sheep, the hat and a sandwich, and finally they accept a single wagging tail."],"桌":["table","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} saws a fallen *tree* in half and nails four legs on. It's a **table**! She serves a feast on it: pies, tea, a whole roast turkey. Pigeons sit round the **table** in tiny chairs, and the horse lies under it."],"啦":["la (particle)","The {Lifeguard} lounges on the {Front Step} of the {Spa}, humming \"**la**, la, la\". A *pulling hand* tugs her *mouth* into a big grin and the song goes louder. Every guest joins in, \"**la** la la!\", until the steam rooms sing along."],"瓦":["tile","The {Wizard} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Spa} and lifts a loose *tile* from the floor. Underneath is another **tile**, and another, a stack a mile deep. He builds a tile staircase out of them and climbs out through the roof, stacking each **tile** with a magic click."],"莱":["goosefoot","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} hut, where a goat munches *grass* and *barley*. In the middle grows a scruffy weed: **goosefoot**, with leaves shaped like little webbed feet. Geese waddle in to compare. The lifeguard blows her whistle, and the **goosefoot** waddles off on its own."],"援":["to help","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, when a banker falls into the coin vault. She throws a *rescue rope* and a *helping hand* to **help** him out. Then she **helps** the coins, a lost cat and a confused printing press, pulling them all to safety in perfect lotus pose."],"译":["to translate","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut where a crab and a seagull are arguing, each word popping out in a *small speech bubble*. She **translates**: \"He says your feet smell.\" The seagull squawks; she **translates** that too. Soon she's translating the waves and the sand."],"夺":["to seize","The {Dentist} storms up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} to **seize** a giant toothbrush from a *big man* who's been hogging it. She pins him down with one *thumb*, grabs the brush, and **seizes** his candy stash too, waving it in triumph."],"汽":["steam","The {Cheerleader} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} sauna, where *water drops* sizzle on hot stones and hissing *steam* billows out. She can't see her pom-poms. **Steam** fogs the sea, the gulls, the lighthouse. A train chugs out of the cloud, powered entirely by **steam** and cheering."],"烧":["burn","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} and finds a tiny *emperor* roasting marshmallows over a roaring *campfire*. \"Put it out!\" yells the Sheriff, but the emperor just fans the flames with his crown. Shingles start to **burn**, the flagpole starts to **burn**, and the Sheriff's hat goes up like a birthday candle."],"距":["distance","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and lands on a giant *kicking foot* that boots a wooden *set square* clean across the gallery. It sails past mummies and dinosaurs. The Juggler sprints after it with a tape measure, unrolling it yard after yard, shouting out the **distance**: what a **distance**, all the way to the gift shop."],"裁":["cut out","The {Tsar} storms up the {Staircase} of the {Island} palace, waving a jousting *lance* like a pair of scissors. A huge velvet *robe* hangs at the top, and he slashes at it until he has **cut out** a perfect gingerbread-man shape. His tailor weeps, then asks him to **cut out** the sleeves too."],"偏":["lean","The {Pirate} swings onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *standing person* is hanging up a heavy *nameboard* that says BANK. The Pirate lands on one end of it. Everything begins to **lean**: the board, the person, the chimney, the whole building. Bankers inside **lean** sideways at their desks and their coins slide into the sea."],"符":["sign","The {Firefighter} hauls a hose up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and meets a *cashier* sitting at a till made of *bamboo*. \"No entry without a ticket,\" she says, and paints a strange **sign** on the Firefighter's helmet. Instantly every lifeguard salutes. That painted **sign** opens every door, even the one to the diving board."],"勇":["brave","The {Yogi} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut, where a sea monster is snoring. A little *man* with a silver *hairpin* steps forward, pulls out the pin and jabs it, like a sword, at the monster's nose. The monster flees, squeaking. \"So **brave**,\" gasps the Yogi, and from then on the **brave** little man wears the hairpin as a medal."],"触":["touch","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool} carrying an *ox horn*, and a shiny green *bug* lands on its tip. The Chef reaches out to **touch** it. Zap! The bug sparks like a doorbell and every swimmer leaps out of the water. Now nobody dares **touch** anything, not even the rubber duck."],"课":["lesson","The {King} slides down the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} into a tiny classroom. A *small speech bubble* floats above the blackboard, drawing pictures of *fruit*: apple, pear, banana. The King has to sit at a desk and copy them all, because today's **lesson** is fruit. The bubble rings a bell and starts the next **lesson**: more fruit."],"敬":["respect","The {Juggler} pops up through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring}, still juggling, and the whole crowd rises in a giant *salute*. The champion bows. The referee bows. Even the bell bows. The Juggler is so shocked by all this **respect** that he drops every ball, and the crowd salutes again out of pure **respect**."],"哭":["cry","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building next to a *dog* whose loud *chatter* has turned into howling. The dog starts to **cry**, and its tears pour down the drainpipe and fill the swimming pool. The King starts to **cry** too, and soon the water spills over the diving boards."],"懂":["understand","The {Dentist} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse and finds a film *director* shouting at a *standing heart* wearing sunglasses. \"Feel it! Beat louder!\" The heart thumps once, twice, then suddenly nods. At last it **understands** the scene. The Dentist claps, because now he too can **understand** why the heart was crying."],"墙":["wall","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} and finds a *miser* building a **wall** out of *soil*, one mean spoonful at a time, so nobody can see the game for free. She kicks it, but the mud just grows taller. By halftime the **wall** reaches the scoreboard and the miser charges a coin to peek over it."],"袭":["raid","The {Shepherd} is counting sheep on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house when a *dragon* in a silk *robe* swoops down. It snatches every towel, every bucket, every ice cream. It's a **raid**! The Shepherd chases it with his crook, but the dragon is already planning its next **raid** on the sandcastles."],"召":["summon","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and lands beside a *town crier* ringing an enormous bell. \"Oyez! I **summon** the horses!\" he bellows. At once, three hundred horses gallop up the tower stairs and squeeze into the room. The Jockey begs him to stop, but he keeps ringing to **summon** more."],"罚":["punish","The {Firefighter} trips on the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and gets tangled in a giant *fishing net* hanging there. The manager scoops her up and dangles her over the hot tub to **punish** her for running indoors. Every time she wriggles, the net dips her in again. That is how they **punish** you at the spa."],"侠":["hero","The {Shepherd} waits on the {Staircase} of the {Piazza} when a *standing person* bursts through the crowd holding a pair of blacksmith's *tongs*. She snatches a burning pie off a stall and saves a lost lamb from a pigeon gang. Everyone cheers the masked **hero**. The Shepherd gets her autograph, which just says \"**hero**\"."],"厅":["hall","The {Tailor} stitches on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} and drops his sewing *nail*. It falls into a vast stone *cliff*-sided **hall** where a thousand fans are waiting. The nail pings, echoes, and rattles round the walls for ten minutes. The whole **hall** cheers, thinking it is the starting bell."],"拜":["bow","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Island} and finds a crowd of crabs raising one *shading hand* each, peering at him. Then they **bow**, all together, claws to the sand. The Baker nervously bows back. The crabs **bow** lower, the Baker bows lower, until everyone is face down in the sand."],"巧":["skilful","The {Cheerleader} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café}, where a *workbench* is covered in tiny wooden mice. With one *puff of breath* she blows sawdust off a mouse that can dance, juggle and spin. The cats go wild. \"So **skilful**!\" they purr, and they order her to make a **skilful** robot ball of yarn too."],"侧":["side","The {Tsar} topples through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hut}, where a *standing person* reads a huge *rulebook* aloud: \"Rule one: always walk on the left **side**.\" The Tsar shuffles to the left. \"Rule two: now the other **side**.\" He shuffles right. By rule ninety he is spinning like a top on his own **side**."],"韩":["Korea","The {Hunter} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} at *dawn*, holding a *leather strap* like a lasso. At the top, a window opens onto **Korea**: mountains, kimchi jars and a pop band waving. The Hunter lassoes the band's microphone and sings along. Every morning at dawn, the strap pulls him to **Korea** again."],"冒":["emit","The {Magician} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} wearing a tall *brimmed hat*. The hat starts to **emit** smoke, then bubbles, then pigeons, then a brass band. Rabbits pour out of it like toothpaste. The Magician presses down on the brim, but the hat just keeps on going to **emit** more and more."],"债":["debt","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut and lands on a *standing person*, who is being chased by a *debt collector* waving a giant bill. \"Pay your **debt**!\" The Jockey lends him a horseshoe. Now the debt collector chases the Jockey instead, because the **debt** has jumped over to him."],"曼":["graceful","The {Magician} floats down through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} wrapped in a *long veil* that ripples like smoke. She drifts across the ballroom, so **graceful** that the chandeliers sway in time. The butler tries to copy her, trips on the veil, and pirouettes into the punch bowl, almost **graceful**."],"融":["melt","The {Robot} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut carrying a *cauldron*, and a little *bug* in it starts to stir. Steam rises. The robot's metal knees begin to **melt**, then its elbows, then its bolts, until it is a silver puddle. The bug sips the puddle and says, \"Watching robots **melt** is my favourite soup.\""],"惯":["used to","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond} and lands among swans, each wearing a *string of coins*. His *standing heart* jumps in fright at first, but now he visits every day and he is **used to** it. The swans jingle, the coins clink, he naps through it all. He is so **used to** the noise."],"享":["enjoy","The {Shepherd} wanders into the {Basement} of the {Stadium} and finds a huge *feast* laid out on the locker benches: roast chickens, jellies, towers of dumplings. He tucks in with both hands, and the sheep join him. Upstairs the match goes on, but down here everyone **enjoys** themselves, slurping, burping, and learning to **enjoy** every crumb."],"戴":["wear","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut, where a *lance* is propped against the wall with a *strange mask* hanging on its tip. He pulls it on. It fits perfectly. He decides to **wear** it for every patient, and now they all **wear** masks too, so nobody knows who is pulling out whose teeth."],"童":["child","The {Tailor} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut with a tape measure, chased by a *schoolkid* who won't stand still. The **child** wriggles, giggles, and leaps into the lagoon in a half-sewn suit. The Tailor dives after the **child** and ends up measuring a dolphin instead."],"犹":["as if","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} when a *prowling dog* sniffs at the *wart* on his nose. The Yogi doesn't move: **as if** he were a statue. The dog licks the wart. The Yogi keeps still, **as if** made of stone, until the dog gives up and paddles away."],"乘":["ride","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} treehouse with a soup pot and meets a *rider* sitting on an elephant. \"Hop on!\" The Chef jumps up and they **ride** through the vines, soup sloshing everywhere. Monkeys leap aboard to **ride** too, and soon the elephant is carrying a whole kitchen."],"挂":["hang","The {Gardener} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Water Park} clutching a green *jade tablet*. A *helping hand* shoots out of the water slide and snatches it, then tries to **hang** it on a slippery tube. It slides off. The hand tries again and again, until finally the gardener himself is left to **hang** from the slide."],"奖":["prize","The {Juggler} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Stadium} and finds a *big man* guarding a golden trophy taller than himself. \"Juggle twenty eggs and win the **prize**!\" The Juggler juggles twenty-one. The big man bursts into tears, hands over the **prize**, and is buried under falling egg yolk."],"绍":["introduce","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a party where a *town crier* runs around tying *silk thread* from guest to guest. \"May I **introduce** the Sheriff!\" he shouts, and ties her to a duchess. Then he ties the duchess to a goat. He has to **introduce** everyone, so soon all of them are knotted together."],"厚":["thick","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} into a pile of blankets, where a small *child* is wrapping herself in one more quilt, then another, then another. She is now so **thick** she cannot fit through the door. The Hunter pushes, she bounces back like a mattress, wrapped in **thick**, thicker, thickest wool."],"纵":["vertical","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} hut holding a spool of *silk thread*, and a *follower* grabs the loose end and climbs straight up it. The thread goes **vertical**, stiff as a flagpole. More followers climb up after her. Soon there is a **vertical** line of people reaching from the lagoon to the clouds."],"障":["block","The {Jockey} gallops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and his horse skids into a *hillside* that has slid inside overnight. A guard with a shiny *badge* stands on it, arms crossed, to **block** the way. The Jockey jumps; the guard jumps higher to **block** him. The planes have to take off through the roof."],"讯":["news","The {Shepherd} topples through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes} hut and a *swift* bird zooms in after him, carrying a *small speech bubble* in its beak. It drops the bubble on his head: \"Breaking **news**! The sheep have learned to surf!\" Another swift arrives with more **news**, then another, until the sand is covered in headlines."],"涉":["wade","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} into knee-deep *water drops* that have flooded the floor. She has to take one careful *step* at a time to **wade** across the room to the coffee pot. Fish nibble her boots. By the time she **wades** back, the coffee is also full of fish."],"彻":["thorough","The {Chef} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and leaves muddy *footsteps* everywhere. In a frenzy he scrubs them all off, then makes one last *cut* through every cobweb and onion. The cleaning is so **thorough** that the hut squeaks. Even the mice have been sliced, washed and labelled, which is a bit too **thorough**."],"刊":["publish","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} beside a *drying rack* hung with wet newspapers. With a *standing knife* he trims each page and flings them to the crowd below. \"We **publish** today!\" Pigeons carry copies across the city, and the King decides to **publish** a new paper every hour."],"丈":["ten feet","The {Jockey} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and lands next to an old man's *walking staff* that keeps growing. It shoots up **ten feet** tall and lifts the old man to the ceiling. The Jockey measures it with his whip: exactly **ten feet**, not an inch more, and the old man waves from the rafters."],"爆":["explode","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a tray of popcorn kernels and sets it on a *campfire* during a fierce *heatwave*. Pop! Pop! The kernels **explode**, then the oven, then the Baker's hat. The whole tower shakes. Finally the roof itself starts to **explode** into a fountain of buttered popcorn."],"乌":["crow","The {Wizard} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building when a black *crow* lands on his pointed hat and caws so loudly that the pool water ripples. He tries a spell to turn the **crow** white. It turns into ten black crows. Soon the whole roof is a cawing mat of **crows**."],"役":["labour","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and is handed a *war club* by a sergeant. Muddy *footsteps* lead to a mountain of sand to be moved. \"Hard **labour**!\" Bash, dig, haul. The Yogi does every bit of **labour** in a perfect lotus position, which annoys the sergeant greatly."],"描":["trace","The {Magician} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} with tracing paper. A *helping hand* lays the paper over a tray of *young crop* seedlings and begins to **trace** every little leaf with a pencil. The cats lean in, curious, so the hand starts to **trace** the cats as well, whiskers and all."],"洗":["wash","The {Shepherd} dashes into the {Basement} of the {Beach} house where a muddy *front runner* from the marathon is standing in a bathtub. *Water drops* rain from the ceiling and the Shepherd scrubs him with a sheep. \"Must **wash** before the finish line!\" They **wash** until the runner gleams, then he sprints off, dripping."],"玛":["agate","The {Magician} slips into the {Basement} of the {Spa}, where a *king* sits on a *horse* in a mud bath. The horse spits out a striped stone: a polished **agate**. The king gasps. The horse spits out another **agate**, then a hundred, until the mud bath is full of glossy striped pebbles."],"患":["suffer","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swan Pond} carrying a *kebab* skewered right through a pink *heart*. The swans hiss. The heart moans, \"Oh, I **suffer**!\" The Hunter pulls out the skewer, but now the kebab moans too. Everyone at the pond has to **suffer** their wailing until sunset."],"妙":["wonderful","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and a *woman* hands her a *pinch* of glittery powder. She sprinkles it on the cats, and they start to tap-dance in perfect rows. \"**Wonderful**!\" shrieks the woman. Another pinch, and the teapots join in. Everything is **wonderful** until the sugar bowl tap-dances off the table."],"镜":["mirror","The {Juggler} bursts through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} for the grand *finale* and juggles a shower of *gold coins*. Each coin is polished like a **mirror**, so a thousand tiny Jugglers flash around the ring. The boxer punches the wrong one and hits a giant **mirror** hanging over the ropes, which only makes more Jugglers."],"唱":["sing","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} holding a frying pan with a *double sun* sizzling in it like two eggs. Each sun opens a little *mouth* and starts to **sing** opera. The pilots stop work. The Chef flips the suns and they **sing** even louder, in harmony, until the planes hum along."],"烦":["annoyed","The {Firefighter} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} to put out a *campfire* someone lit on the landing. Every time she sprays it, a *page* of homework flutters out and lands on her face. Spray, page, spray, page. She is so **annoyed** she starts to growl, and the fire looks **annoyed** too."],"签":["sign","The {Cheerleader} flips onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a whole *assembly* of bankers waits with *bamboo* pens. \"Everyone **sign** here!\" she shouts, and they scribble their names on her pompoms. Then they **sign** her shoes, her megaphone and the chimney, until every brick has a signature."],"仙":["immortal","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} and sees a *standing person* floating over the *mountain* behind it, robes fluttering, eating clouds like candyfloss. \"I am **immortal**,\" she says, \"I've been here for three thousand years.\" The Shepherd offers her a sheep. She makes it **immortal** too, and it floats off grazing on stars."],"彼":["that","The {Baker} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Beach} house following sandy *footsteps* to a pile of buckets. Under one is a crab trying to *hide*. \"Not this one,\" says the Baker, \"**that** one!\" He points at the next bucket. Under it, another crab. \"No, **that** one!\" He points and points at things over there, never here."],"弗":["not","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and a giant *dollar sign* blocks her path. She tries to pay to swim. The dollar sign shakes its head: **not** today. She offers more money. **Not** enough. In the end she hoses it down, and it shrinks to a cent and rolls into the drain."],"症":["illness","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} hospital and lands on a *sickbed* parked right on a football *goal line*. A monkey doctor checks him: \"This **illness** is serious, you scored an own goal.\" Nurses in jerseys carry the bed up and down the pitch, but the **illness** only gets worse each time the crowd cheers."],"仿":["imitate","The {Firefighter} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} as a *standing person* sneaks in carrying a cardboard *square*. Every move the Firefighter makes, the person copies: hose up, helmet off, sneeze. They **imitate** her so well that the pilots salute the wrong one. Even the cardboard square starts to **imitate** her fire engine."],"倾":["tilt","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels onto the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} where a *standing person* with a *tilted head* is peering at the crowd. The Cheerleader copies the pose, then the referee, then the audience. The whole arena starts to **tilt**. The ring itself slides to one side, and boxers keep falling out because everything **tilts** a little more."],"牌":["sign board","The {Pirate} drags a *wood slice* up the {Staircase} of the {Island} and paints it with skulls, then fans it dry with a giant paper *fan*. Now it is a **sign board** reading \"NO PARROTS\". A parrot lands on it at once. The Pirate paints a bigger **sign board**, and ten parrots land on that."],"陷":["trap","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and, at the bottom of a grassy *hillside*, falls into a hidden *trap pit* full of coins. The bank set this **trap** for thieves. The Shepherd shouts for help; a banker peeks over the edge, laughs, and sets another **trap** right beside him."],"鸟":["bird","The {Ninja} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café}, silent as a shadow, carrying a cage with one tiny **bird** inside. The cats spot it. Total chaos: cats leap, cups fly, and the *bird* escapes, perching on the Ninja's head. Now every cat in the café is staring at the Ninja, who freezes, pretending to be a **bird** too."],"轰":["bang","The {Hunter} is on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse when a runaway *cart* comes rolling up. He grabs it with *both hands*, but it is packed with fireworks. **Bang**! The cart explodes, flinging him into the water. **Bang**, bang! Rockets whizz over the lagoon and every fish leaps out to watch."],"咱":["we","The {Zookeeper} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and finds every animal sitting at one giant table with a *mouth* and a *nose* drawn on a big group photo. \"That's **we**, all of us together!\" says the giraffe. The zookeeper squeezes into the frame, and the elephant trumpets, \"**We** are family!\""],"菜":["vegetable","The {Tsar} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Island}, where a *fruit picker* is wading through tall *grass* plucking giant cabbages. She throws one at the Tsar. It lands on his crown. \"Eat your **vegetable**!\" she says. He refuses, so she throws carrots, leeks and pumpkins, until he is buried in every **vegetable** on the island."],"闭":["close","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut, where a tiny *green shoot* is growing in the middle of an iron *gate*. It sneezes, and the gate slams shut. The Baker shoves; it won't open. The shoot giggles and makes every door **close**, then every window, then the Baker's eyes, which **close** for a nap."],"奋":["strive","The {Firefighter} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into a muddy *rice field* behind the rides, where a *big man* is pushing a stuck bumper car. He grunts, sweats and pushes with all his might. \"**Strive**!\" yells the Firefighter, spraying him for encouragement. He keeps on, **striving** until the car shoots forward and loops the rollercoaster."],"庆":["celebrate","The {Cheerleader} bursts through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} and finds a *big man* dancing on the roof of a garden *shed* that someone has put in the middle of the ring. Confetti cannons fire. \"Let's **celebrate**!\" he roars. The crowd throws streamers, the boxers do the conga, and the shed itself starts to **celebrate** by playing music."],"撤":["withdraw","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hut} kitchen and burns the soup. A *helping hand* waves a white napkin: \"**Withdraw**! **Withdraw**!\" Every pan, spoon and potato marches backwards out of the door in perfect order. The Chef is left alone with the burnt pot, which also tiptoes away."],"泪":["tears","The {Lifeguard} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Lake} and finds one huge *eye* floating there, chopping onions. *Water drops* spill down its lid. The **tears** fall so fast that the lake rises. The Lifeguard blows her whistle, but it only cries harder, until she is swimming in **tears** up to her nose."],"茶":["tea","The {Chef} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and stuffs a kettle with fresh *grass* from the lawn. He pours boiling water and serves it to the guests: green **tea**. They sip politely. The goats in the garden smell it and storm the spa, demanding **tea** too, with biscuits."],"疾":["disease","The {Juggler} sneezes on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house and gets a blazing *fever*. Thermometers pop out of his mouth like party blowers. This **disease** makes everything he juggles get hot too: the balls glow red and the sand turns to glass. The doctor arrives and catches the **disease** at once."],"缘":["fate","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mint} when a *hog* trots up trailing a red *silk thread* tied to its tail. The other end is tied to the Yogi's toe. \"It's **fate**,\" sighs the hog. They try to untie it; the knot only tightens. They are bound by **fate** forever, and the hog moves in."],"播":["sow","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} with a sack of seeds. A giant *helping hand* swings over a *footprint field* below and scatters them, one into every footprint. The Baker joins in to **sow** too. Seconds later, sunflowers burst up from every footprint and the soldiers' boots start sprouting as they **sow**."],"朗":["bright","The {Lifeguard} climbs into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} at night with a mirror and catches the full *moon* in it. She aims it around: the hangar goes **bright** as noon. Planes squint. Bats flee. Pilots put on sunglasses. It is so **bright** that the moon itself blinks and asks her to turn it down."],"杜":["stop","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a small *tree* growing out of a mound of *soil* on the bottom. Its roots plug the drain and the water stops dead. \"**Stop**!\" cries the Dentist to the leaking water, and it obeys. The tree waves a branch: \"**Stop** the swimming too.\" Everyone freezes mid-stroke."],"奶":["milk","The {Ninja} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Island} hut, where a *woman* is milking a coconut tied with a pink *ribbon*. Fresh **milk** squirts out, into a bucket, onto the Ninja's mask. He tries to escape silently, but slips in the puddle of **milk** and slides straight into the sea."],"季":["season","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut juggling a *grain stalk*, an ice cream, a snowball and an autumn leaf. A *child* catches each one in turn. Every catch changes the **season**: spring, summer, autumn, winter. The child grins and throws them back faster, until a new **season** passes every second."],"丹":["red","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} painting a stone *archway* bright **red**, then slaps a **red** *lid* on top like a cherry. The paint drips down every window. The owners open their curtains and find everything red: the cat, the toast, the tea. The Dentist just keeps on painting."],"狗":["dog","The {Gardener} hides in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} as a *prowling dog* sniffs between the boats. It sits up and speaks in a giant *quotation* mark: \"Woof!\" The Gardener writes it down. The **dog** says another quote, then a poem. Soon the Gardener has a whole book by a **dog**."],"尾":["tail","The {Wizard} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Lake} cottage, where a *lying man* is snoring with a long bushy *fur* thing poking out of his trousers. The Wizard tugs it. It's a **tail**! The man wakes up, wags the **tail**, and knocks the Wizard's hat into the lake."],"仪":["ceremony","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house for a grand **ceremony**. A *standing person* in a wig, the *judge*, bangs a seashell gavel and announces the winner of the sandcastle contest. Trumpets blow. Crabs throw petals. The Yogi falls asleep halfway through and the whole **ceremony** has to start again."],"偷":["steal","The {Tailor} creeps across the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} and watches a *standing person* lower a *dugout canoe* from the roof on ropes, piled with buttons. \"You **steal** my buttons!\" shouts the Tailor. The thief paddles off through the air. The Tailor leaps into another canoe to **steal** them back."],"奔":["rush","The {Baker} is on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s big wheel when a *big man* crashes out of the *shrubbery* below and starts to **rush** across the park, dragging candyfloss and balloons. The Baker leaps down to follow. They **rush** past the carousel, through the ghost train and out into traffic, still not knowing why."],"珠":["pearl","The {Jockey} gallops onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building and finds a *king* polishing a tray of *red lacquer*. On it sits one giant **pearl**. The king flicks it and it rolls off the roof, bouncing into the pool. The Jockey dives after it, while the king throws in another **pearl** for fun."],"虫":["bug","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut with a salad and finds a *bug* sitting on the lettuce, wearing a tiny chef's hat. The **bug** seizes a fork and starts to cook. Soon a thousand more bugs march up the stairs. The Chef is fired, and the **bug** runs the kitchen."],"驻":["station","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} on his *horse*, which plants its hooves on the bottom and refuses to move. He lights a *candle* and stays the night. Guards come to **station** themselves around him. Morning comes; the horse has taken root. They must **station** a lifeguard on its back."],"孔":["hole","The {King} falls into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut through a round *hole* in the floor. He peeks through another **hole** in the wall and sees a fish peeking back through a third. Soon the whole room is full of holes, and the King is wearing a **hole**-shaped crown."],"宜":["suitable","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house into a *cozy room* with cushions and lamps. She tries the bed: too soft. The hammock: too swingy. Finally the floor mat: exactly **suitable**. She sits in perfect lotus. The crabs agree it is **suitable** too and queue for yoga."],"艾":["mugwort","The {Ghost} slides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut and drifts into a jungle of *mugwort*, the grey-green herb. It sniffs it, sneezes, and turns green itself. Villagers burn **mugwort** to chase it away, but the Ghost loves the smell and dances in the smoke, wearing a crown of **mugwort**."],"桥":["bridge","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels down the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} onto a *tree* trunk balanced across a stream on two wobbly *stilts*. It is the only **bridge**. The cats refuse to cross, so she forms a human pyramid to make a second **bridge**, and three hundred cats march over her back."],"淡":["bland","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} kitchen, where a soup is boiling over a *blaze*. He keeps adding *water drops*, more and more, until it is ten buckets of soup. He tastes it: so **bland** it tastes like a wet sock. The guests sip and fall asleep from the **bland** soup."],"翼":["wing","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and finds a pile of *feathers* and a *strange mask* shaped like a seagull. She puts on the mask, glues feathers to her arms, and flaps. Each arm becomes a **wing**. She takes off over the waves, but one **wing** is lopsided, so she flies in circles round the ice-cream van."],"恨":["hate","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into the hall of mirrors, where a *standing heart* gives him a furious *glare*. It stomps, puffs smoke, and kicks the candyfloss stand. \"I **hate** clowns!\" it shrieks. A clown walks in. The heart's **hate** boils over and it chases him round the dodgems."],"繁":["numerous","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and meets an *acrobat* juggling a *silk skein* that keeps unravelling into more and more threads. Threads everywhere, **numerous** as spaghetti. The Firefighter tries to count them and gives up at a million. The acrobat sneezes, and the threads become even more **numerous**, tangling the chandelier."],"寒":["cold","The {Hunter} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} in shorts, and someone pulls the *roof* off above him like a lid. A blizzard pours in. It is so **cold** that his moustache freezes into icicles and the portraits grow scarves. He hides under the stairs, but even there it is **cold** enough to freeze his sneezes into snowballs."],"伴":["companion","The {Baker} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and finds a *standing person* sawn in *half*. \"Don't worry,\" says one half, \"I'm just waiting for my **companion**.\" The other half waddles in from the kitchen. They join up, and the Baker becomes their third **companion**, sharing a loaf three ways."],"叹":["sigh","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion}, where a sad statue has a huge open *mouth*. A *right hand* pats it on the back and the statue lets out a giant **sigh** that blows the curtains off the windows. The Tailor sews new curtains, and the statue gives another **sigh** that blows those away too."],"旦":["dawn","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} cellar at midnight and waits with his drill. Suddenly a *sunrise* bursts up through the floorboards, a blazing ball of orange. **Dawn**! The roosters scream, the butler drops his tray, and the Dentist has to wear sunglasses to work through the **dawn** shift."],"愈":["recover","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a *dugout canoe* lying on a pile of cushions, carrying a sad, cracked *heart*. She rows it gently round the dinosaurs. With every stroke the heart grows healthier, the cracks sealing up. By the gift shop it has started to **recover**, and by closing time it has fully **recovered**."],"潮":["tide","The {Chef} carries a soup tureen up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} into a *royal court* where the queen is sitting with her feet in *water drops*. Every time she sneezes, the water rushes in and out: the **tide**. The Chef's soup goes out with the **tide** and comes back with a crab in it."],"粮":["grain","The {Lifeguard} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} carrying a sack of *rice* to a *good meal* laid out for the team. The sack bursts and **grain** rains down on the pitch. Pigeons flood in from every direction. The match is cancelled and the whole crowd eats **grain** porridge in the stands."],"缩":["shrink","The {Sailor} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} and finds a tiny *inn* tied up with *silk thread*. He pulls the thread and the inn starts to **shrink**, smaller and smaller, until it fits in his pocket. Guests wave from the tiny windows. Then the Sailor's hat begins to **shrink** too."],"罢":["stop","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Spa}, and a *dropped net* falls on everyone in the steam room. Nobody can move. \"**Stop**!\" shouts the manager, and the massage, the music and the bubbles all **stop** together. The Baker sells bread rolls through the holes in the net."],"聚":["gather","The {Juggler} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Museum} where a *gathering* of statues has come to life. They all **gather** round him in a circle: knights, mummies, a stone horse. He juggles three vases. More statues shuffle in to **gather**, until the room is so packed that the T-rex has to watch from the doorway."],"径":["path","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} and finds a trail of glowing *footsteps* painted on the canvas. He follows the **path**, round the corner post, under the ropes, through the referee's legs. The crowd cheers each step. The **path** finally leads to a door marked EXIT, which is locked."],"恰":["exactly","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Piazza} with a cooking pot and a *fitted lid*. Her *standing heart* thumps as she drops the lid on, and it fits **exactly**, with a perfect click. The crowd gasps. She tries the lid on a fountain, a bell and a pigeon: it fits each one **exactly**."],"挑":["choose","The {Tailor} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} where a *helping hand* sorts a basket of eggs, each with a *cracked shell*. \"**Choose** the best one,\" says the cat owner. The hand picks one, and out pops a duckling. It picks another: a dragon. The Tailor must **choose** which to sew a tiny jacket for."],"袋":["bag","The {Dentist} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut, where a *stand-in* dentist is stuffing a huge *robe* with seashells to make a **bag**. She ties the sleeves together and hoists it on her back. It rattles like a drum kit. The real Dentist grabs his own **bag**, and they race to fill teeth with shells."],"灰":["ash","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} and accidentally knocks over the chimney pot. A cloud of *ash* blasts out, covering the patients inside. Everyone is grey as a pigeon. They sneeze **ash**, sit in **ash**, and the receptionist calls their names through a mouthful of soot."],"捕":["catch","The {Baker} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Pool} building, where a *helping hand* leaps out of a *seedbed* and tries to **catch** a runaway rubber duck. It misses. It grabs again and gets the Baker's apron. Finally it manages to **catch** the duck, the Baker and three lifeguards in one fist."],"徐":["slowly","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} so **slowly** that a snail overtakes him. His *footsteps* go thud... thud... thud. He is carrying a tray of *leftovers* from the café and mustn't spill a crumb. By the top the museum has closed, and he walks back down just as **slowly**."],"珍":["treasure","The {Jockey} rides onto the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s ghost train, where a *king* is combing his long, *thick hair*. Out tumbles a glittering **treasure**: rubies, coins and a golden toothbrush. Children scramble for it. The king just keeps combing, and more **treasure** pours out with every stroke."],"幕":["curtain","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} stage and lands behind a thick *grass* **curtain** strung across the diving boards. He pulls it open: the audience cheers, but a hippo is in his spot. He yanks the **curtain** shut, then open again: now the hippo is doing his card trick."],"映":["reflect","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring} carrying a wooden *yoke* hung with two polished pans. The *sun* bounces off them and the light **reflects** into the boxers' eyes. They swing blindly and punch the ropes. The Yogi bows, and the pans **reflect** a sunbeam that pops a balloon in the back row."],"裂":["crack","The {Lifeguard} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave} and finds a *lineup* of yetis trying on one tiny *robe*. The first yeti pulls it on, flexes and... rip! A huge **crack** splits it from neck to knee. The next yeti tries; another **crack**. Soon the cave walls split too, from all the flexing."],"泰":["peaceful","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Island} and finds a *spring planter* gently *splashing water* over flowers. A turtle sleeps beside it, smiling. The waves hum. Even the Tailor's needle stops jabbing. Everything is so **peaceful** that a coconut falls slowly, like a feather, and lands without a sound: the most **peaceful** island ever."],"隔":["separate","The {Gardener} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} carrying a giant *cauldron* and plants it on the *hillside* between two arguing goats. It sits there like a wall, to **separate** them. They butt it. Bong! The Gardener adds a second cauldron to **separate** the chickens, then a third for the arguing cabbages."],"启":["open","The {Cheerleader} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Beach} house in front of a locked *door* with a huge *mouth* painted on it. She yells, \"**Open**!\" The mouth yawns wide and the door swings **open**, letting in a tidal wave of sand, crabs and a lost surfer."],"尖":["sharp","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} as a *big man* below sharpens a pencil, scattering *crumbs* of wood. The pencil grows so **sharp** it pokes holes in the clouds. Rain pours through. The Juggler juggles it carefully, but it is so **sharp** it slices his juggling balls into neat halves."],"忠":["loyal","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse, aiming arrows at a *bullseye* painted on a giant *heart*. Every arrow hits dead centre. The heart doesn't flinch: it is **loyal** to him, whatever happens. Even when he misses and hits a pelican, the heart stays **loyal** and pretends it was the bullseye."],"累":["tired","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Lake} and lands on a towering *yarn pile*. She must knit it all into towels before sunset. Click, click, click. By the last ball she is so **tired** that she falls asleep on the needles. The fish are **tired** of waiting and go knit their own.","lèi"],"炎":["inflammation","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and her knee touches a *blaze* on the banister. It swells up red, hot and puffy: a nasty **inflammation**. She sits in an ice bucket. The butler's ankle catches the **inflammation** too, then the dog's tail, until the whole mansion glows like a toaster."],"暂":["temporary","The {Zookeeper} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} kitchen onto a *chopping block* with a tiny *sun* sitting on it. \"I'm only here as a **temporary** cook,\" says the sun, frying eggs on its own face. By evening it sets out the window, and the moon arrives as the next **temporary** chef."],"估":["estimate","The {Gardener} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building with a *standing person* holding a dusty *antique* vase. \"**Estimate** its price!\" The Gardener sniffs it, weighs it, licks it. \"Five pence.\" The vase cracks with shame. The standing person holds up a teapot: \"Now **estimate** this one.\""],"泛":["float","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a flooded ballroom full of *water drops*, sitting on a *flat tyre*. It starts to **float**, round and round, past the chandeliers. Butlers paddle by on trays. Even the grand piano begins to **float**, playing a waltz all by itself."],"荒":["barren","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swamp} lodge looking out over a *wasteland*. No trees, no frogs, not even mud: just one dry tumbleweed. It's **barren**. He plants a seed; a crow eats it. He plants a tree; a goat eats it. The land stays stubbornly **barren** and the goat looks pleased."],"偿":["repay","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} where a *standing person* is giving a *taste test* to his soup. \"Disgusting! You must **repay** me for my tongue!\" So the Chef **repays** him: a thousand more spoonfuls, each worse than the last, until the man flies off in the nearest plane."],"横":["horizontal","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} treehouse and finds a fallen *tree* lying flat across the steps, an egg *yolk* dripping off it. He tries to climb over it, but it stays **horizontal**. He tries under it. Everything around him turns **horizontal**: the monkeys, the snakes, even the waterfall now flows sideways."],"拒":["refuse","The {Juggler} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Museum} where a *helping hand* holds up a wooden *set square* like a stop sign. \"Ticket?\" He offers a juggling ball. The hand **refuses**. He offers a pie. It **refuses** again, and pokes him back up the trapdoor with the set square."],"瑞":["lucky","The {Robot} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *king* is waiting to see the doctor holding a pot with a single *sprout tip*. The sprout blooms into a four-leaf clover. \"How **lucky**!\" Everyone's name is called at once. The Robot touches the clover and wins the raffle: a **lucky** day for metal."],"忆":["recall","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut where a *swan* rests its head on a *standing heart*. \"I **recall** the day we met,\" says the heart dreamily, and pictures float above them: sandcastles, sunburn, ice cream. The swan honks. Now the Yogi starts to **recall** everything too, including where she buried her car keys."],"孤":["lonely","The {Gardener} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building beside a *child* who is alone with one giant *melon*. No friends, no ball, nobody to talk to. It's so **lonely**. The child draws a face on the melon and they chat. The Gardener, now feeling **lonely** himself, draws a face on a cucumber."],"鼻":["nose","The {Baker} is on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house when a giant *nose* on a wooden *serving stand* sniffs his fresh bread. It sniffs so hard that the loaves shoot up its nostrils. \"Give them back!\" yells the Baker. The **nose** sneezes them out across the beach. Every gull now has a **nose** for bread."],"闹":["noisy","The {Ninja} sneaks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a *market* squeezed behind an iron *gate*. Vendors shout, chickens squawk, drums bang, a tuba plays. So **noisy**! The Ninja tries to tiptoe, but a goat bleats right in his ear. He covers his ears, but the market only gets more **noisy**."],"羊":["sheep","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and finds a *sheep* doing a perfect headstand on a jet's wing. Then twenty more **sheep** arrive and copy the pose. The Yogi joins them, and the pilot comes back to a plane covered in upside-down wool. He sighs and counts every **sheep** before take-off."],"呆":["dull","The {Dentist} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut beside a patient who gives him a *blank stare*. He tells a joke; the stare stays blank. He juggles coconuts; still **dull**. A parrot does a backflip; the stare doesn't blink. The Dentist falls asleep from how **dull** it all is."],"厉":["strict","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and finds a granite *whetstone* where she sharpens her whistle. Now it shrieks at every tiny mistake. A toe in the wrong lane: whistle! A splash: whistle! She is so **strict** that the waves stand still. Even the sharks swim in neat rows for the **strict** Lifeguard."],"衡":["weigh","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} treehouse and arrives at a *crossroads* where an elephant is standing on a balance scale. He has to **weigh** it against a mountain of bananas. One banana too many: crash. He pulls one off and tries to **weigh** it again, while monkeys steal bananas from the other side."],"胞":["womb","The {Baker} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} under the *moon*, which is wrapped in a little brown *parcel* tied with string. Inside, curled up warm, sleeps a baby star. \"It was safe in the **womb**,\" whispers the Baker. He rocks the parcel gently, like a **womb** made of paper."],"零":["zero","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} as a *herald* in a feathered cap reads the score in the *rain*. \"Champion: nine. Challenger: **zero**!\" The challenger slumps. Raindrops form a giant 0 on the canvas. Everyone stares at it. The herald adds another **zero** to the challenger's prize money."],"穷":["poor","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Youth Club} into a damp *cave*, where a *strong arm* sticks out of the wall holding out an empty bowl. Not a penny, not a crumb: it's so **poor**. She shakes her pompoms and coins fall out. The arm pockets them, then pretends to be **poor** again."],"舍":["give up","The {Sheriff} kicks open the {Basement} door of the {Hut}, but the *hut* itself sighs and starts walking away on chicken legs. \"I **give up**,\" it groans, \"too many sheriffs.\" She tries to lasso it, but it hops over the fence. Finally she sits down too and decides to **give up**."],"码":["number","The {Magician} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Spa} where a *horse* is stamping a *stone* tablet with its hoof. Each stamp leaves a **number**: 1, 7, 42. The guests' lockers open whenever the horse hits the right **number**. The Magician guesses 13 and gets a bucket of mud."],"赫":["impressive","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lands in front of a giant warrior with glowing *red cheeks*, two shining suns on his face. He flexes, and the whole hut lights up. \"**Impressive**!\" says the Hunter, shielding his eyes. The warrior blushes even redder, which is even more **impressive**."],"婆":["granny","The {Pirate} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Fort}, but an old *woman* on a surfboard rides a giant *wave* straight up the steps behind him. \"Out of my way, young man!\" She knocks him into a cannon. The **granny** fires the cannon herself. The Pirate decides never to race a **granny** again."],"魂":["soul","The {Hunter} tiptoes down the {Staircase} of the {Casino} when a wispy *ghost* drifts out of a slot machine, riding a little *cloud*. It is the **soul** of a gambler who never won. The Hunter feeds it a coin. Jackpot! The **soul** whoops, spins three times, and floats away on its cloud."],"灾":["disaster","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut when a monkey lights a *campfire* right beneath the *roof*. Sparks fly, the thatch catches, parrots scream. **Disaster**! The Zookeeper pours a bucket of water, which turns out to be lemonade. Now the island is sticky as well as smoking: double **disaster**."],"洪":["flood","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut as *joined hands* of a hundred villagers try to hold back the *water drops*. Too late: a **flood** pours over them. Boats float through the kitchen, fish swim through the bedroom. The Hunter surfs down the stairs on a door, riding the **flood**."],"腿":["leg","The {Tailor} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room}, where a patient's **leg** is so long it pokes out of the window towards the *moon*. The Tailor measures it, but the **leg** suddenly does a *u-turn*, swings back in, and kicks the receptionist's coffee into the fish tank."],"胆":["courage","The {Dentist} hides in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} at midnight, too scared to come out. Then the *moon* outside turns into a *sunrise*, and a warm glow fills his chest with **courage**. He marches upstairs, drill raised, and pulls out the vampire's fangs. Never has a dentist shown such **courage** before breakfast."],"津":["saliva","The {Juggler} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggling lemons, and every guest's mouth fills with **saliva**. *Water drops* drip from their chins onto the tiles. An artist catches them with a *writing brush* and paints a portrait of a lemon using pure **saliva**. The Juggler slips on it and falls into the chimney."],"俗":["custom","The {Sailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and sees a *standing person* in the deep *valley* of the diving pit, about to throw a fish into the water before swimming. \"It's the local **custom**,\" he says. So the Sailor throws a fish. Everyone throws a fish. Soon the **custom** fills the pool with mackerel."],"辩":["debate","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a loud *quarrel* between two bankers, each with a *small speech bubble* jammed with numbers. They **debate** whether a doughnut is money. The bubbles bump and pop. The Baker eats the doughnut, so they start a new **debate** about the Baker."],"胸":["chest","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Club} under the *moon* and puffs out his **chest** like a pigeon. A tiny treasure *chest* pops out of his shirt, full of sheep stickers. The teenagers cheer. He puffs again, and his **chest** grows so big it blocks out the moonlight."],"晓":["dawn","The {Shepherd} sleeps in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} until an *emperor* bursts in carrying the *sun* on a golden tray. \"Wake up! It's **dawn**!\" Light floods every corner. The cats yowl, the coffee boils, and the Shepherd realises the emperor brings **dawn** to the basement every single morning, whether you like it or not."],"劲":["strength","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} and lands on a table where a *strong arm* is challenging everyone to arm-wrestle. The Juggler grips it. With incredible **strength** the arm slams him through the table, the floor, and into the cellar. He crawls back up with new **strength**, juggling the splinters."],"贫":["poor","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} with one *cut cake* and one *shell* coin to his name. He is so **poor** that he slices the cake into a hundred crumbs to feed the whole crew. The innkeeper takes the shell as rent. The Pirate, still **poor**, sleeps in the hat stand."],"仁":["kind","The {Robot} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and finds a *standing person* laying *two planks* across a puddle so a duckling can cross. The Robot is moved: so **kind**! It lays down two more planks for a snail, a frog and a grandmother. Soon the whole fair is a maze of **kind** little bridges."],"偶":["by chance","The {Ghost} drifts into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} and finds a *standing person* and a *monkey* who have bumped into each other **by chance**. They are wearing the same hat. They stare. Then they discover they share a birthday and a favourite banana. All **by chance**, and the Ghost faints with surprise."],"辑":["compile","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house pushing a *cart* piled with seashells, while each shell lets out a *whisper* of gossip. He must **compile** them all into one book. He sorts, stacks and staples. The crabs keep whispering more, and the book he **compiles** grows into a ten-volume encyclopedia of crab scandal."],"邦":["nation","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, waves a flag and declares the roof a new *country*. He paints borders round the skylights. The pigeons apply for passports. By lunchtime the tiny **nation** has its own bread money and anthem, and the planes must ask the **nation** permission to land."],"恢":["restore","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} as a *standing heart* rises out of a pile of *ash*, beating faster and faster. Its colour comes back, red and shiny. The patients below are cured one by one. The Hunter cheers: the heart can **restore** anything. It even **restores** his burned toast."],"赖":["rely on","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut and finds a lazy *freeloader* in her deckchair, eating her snacks and wearing her whistle. He **relies on** her to rescue him, fetch drinks and fan him. She sighs, because he'll always **rely on** her, even when he floats away on a lilo."],"圈":["circle","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} and unrolls a long *scroll* in a perfect **circle** round the chimney. A wooden *fence* pops up along it. Coins roll out of the mint and race round and round inside the **circle**, unable to stop."],"摸":["touch","The {Magician} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} at *sunset*, blindfolded. A *helping hand* guides her fingers to **touch** a cannon, a soldier's moustache and a sleeping cat. She guesses each one by feel. Then she reaches out to **touch** the sun itself, and it sizzles like a pancake."],"仰":["look up","The {Yogi} lies in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} next to a *standing person* with an *upward gaze*, staring at the ceiling. \"What's up there?\" The Yogi has to **look up** too. A plane is parked on the ceiling, upside down, its pilot waving. Everyone who walks in has to **look up** and wave back."],"润":["moist","The {Robot} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino}, where a calendar shows a strange *leap month*: thirteen weeks of rain. *Water drops* trickle down the roulette wheels. The Robot's metal goes soft and **moist**, the cards turn soggy, and the croupier's moustache curls. Everything stays **moist** until the extra month runs out."],"堆":["pile","The {Dentist} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} as a *sparrow* drops one clump of *soil* after another next to him. Soon there's a **pile** as tall as the chimney. The sparrow builds a nest on top. The Dentist adds a **pile** of old teeth to it and calls it art."],"碰":["bump","The {Pirate} crashes through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle} and lands *side by side* with a big round *stone*. They **bump** foreheads. Bonk! The stone rolls into a tree, which **bumps** a monkey, which bumps a parrot, until the whole jungle is bouncing like pinballs."],"艇":["boat","The {Tailor} paddles a little **boat** into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring}, through a flooded *courtyard*. The *boat* is small enough to fit in a bathtub. The boxers climb aboard, one by one, until it sinks. The Tailor stitches a bigger **boat** out of their gloves."],"稍":["slightly","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} hanging a *portrait* next to a *grain stalk*. It's crooked. She nudges it **slightly** left. Now it's crooked the other way. She nudges it **slightly** right. A pigeon lands on it and the whole tower tilts, just a little."],"迟":["late","The {Chef} hurries up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} with a birthday cake, but there's a giant *ruler* blocking the *road* to the queen's chamber. He measures his way round it. Two hours pass. He arrives **late**: the party is over, the bees are asleep, and the cake is buzzing. **Late** again!"],"辆":["counter for vehicles","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} onto a *balance scale* where a *cart* sits on one side. One car, two buses, three tractors: she has to count each vehicle with the **counter for vehicles**, 辆. The scale tips. Every **counter for vehicles** clicks like a turnstile as more trucks roll in."],"废":["abolish","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and finds a rusty *shed* with a rocket *launch pad* on top. \"I **abolish** this!\" she yells, and sprays it with foam. The launch pad sinks into the lake. Then she decides to **abolish** the shed, the ducks' rules, and Mondays too."],"净":["clean","The {Juggler} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring}, where two teams play *tug of war* with a rope made of *icicles*. The icicles melt, washing the canvas sparkling **clean**. Every boxer slips over. The referee holds up a mirror-bright ring: it has never been so **clean**."],"凶":["fierce","The {Shepherd} crawls across the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Club} and steps on a *booby trap*. Snap! Out leaps a **fierce** guinea pig with teeth like nails, growling. It chases him round the chimney. The teenagers below cheer for the **fierce** little beast as it tears the Shepherd's woolly jumper to ribbons."],"署":["office","The {Sheriff} kicks open the {Basement} of the {Pool} building and finds a *busy man* at a desk tangled in a *fishing net* of paperwork. It's the town's tax **office**. Stamps fly, phones ring, forms flap like fish. The Sheriff tries to arrest him, but she leaves the **office** with three forms to fill in."],"壁":["wall","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and meets a *pioneer* building a **wall** out of wet *soil* and sand. Brick after brick, it grows higher than the waves. The sea crashes against it and stops. The Baker leans on the **wall** to eat a sandwich, and the whole thing collapses."],"御":["defend","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Museum} as muddy *footsteps* charge towards the crown jewels. A *porter* grabs a suitcase and holds it up like a shield to **defend** them. Thieves bounce off. The Yogi joins in, using a meditation mat to **defend** the dinosaurs."],"奉":["offer","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} temple and a line of monkeys carry a golden *tribute* basket towards her. Bananas, mangoes, a tiny crown. They kneel and **offer** it. She politely accepts. The monkeys look delighted and **offer** her their grandmother too."],"旋":["spin","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} on a giant *spinning top*. It starts to **spin** faster and faster, and coins fly off in every direction like sparks. Sheep whirl around him. When it finally stops, he keeps on **spinning** for three more minutes."],"冬":["winter","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} lighthouse in a fluffy *winter coat* as snow starts to fall. The lagoon freezes, seals skate, and icicles hang from his nose. It's **winter** already! He pulls teeth from a penguin who sits patiently in the long **winter** queue."],"矿":["mine","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swamp} hut into a dark **mine** full of glowing *stone*. Miners wheel carts out of a little *shed* at the bottom. He swings a pickaxe and strikes gold, then mud, then a frog. The frog declares itself owner of the **mine**."],"抬":["lift","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} to a wooden *stage* where a *helping hand* is trying to **lift** a giant coconut. It strains, it wobbles. The Tailor helps. They **lift** it high above their heads to great applause, and it bonks the Tailor on the nose."],"蛋":["egg","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and lands on a *bolt of cloth* wrapped round a huge **egg**. A *bug* knocks on it from inside. Crack! Out hops a baby chicken wearing the bug as a hat. The Dentist wraps up another **egg** to see what comes out."],"晨":["morning","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} carousel just as the *sun* rises. A giant *clam* opens on the top step, yawning, with a fried egg inside. \"Good **morning**!\" says the clam. The Chef serves breakfast on the merry-go-round, and every **morning** after that the clam wants toast."],"伏":["lie low","The {Firefighter} creeps down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} where a *standing person* and a *dog* lie low behind the diving board, flat as pancakes. \"**Lie low**!\" they whisper; the lifeguard is coming. The Firefighter flattens herself too. They **lie low** for an hour, until the dog sneezes."],"吹":["blow","The {Chef} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} as a huge *mouth* opens in a *yawn*. Then it starts to **blow**. Hats fly off, patients spin like weathervanes, the clock blows away. The Chef holds onto his pot, but the mouth **blows** the soup out and across the town."],"鸡":["chicken","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut and catches a *bird* in his *right hand*. It's a **chicken** that won't stop laying eggs. He juggles the eggs, the **chicken** clucks along, and the whole roof fills with omelettes when the sun comes out."],"倍":["times","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and meets a *standing person* with a *spitting mouth* that copies everything twice. One cherry stone becomes two, then four, then eight. The Baker's buns double, then grow ten **times** bigger. Soon there are a hundred **times** as many buns as fish in the lake."],"糊":["paste","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} with a bowl of sticky *rice* and mashes it into a gluey **paste**. A cat's *whiskers* get stuck in it. Then the cat. Then the Hunter. He tries to peel himself off the wall, but the **paste** holds everyone like a giant wallpaper."],"秦":["Qin","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} with a *spring planter* full of tall *grain stalk* shoots. At the top, a terracotta warrior stamps it with a seal: \"**Qin**, first empire!\" Clay soldiers march out of the planter. The innkeeper serves them tea, and the whole **Qin** army refuses to leave."],"盾":["shield","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} holding a giant drill, and the gamblers raise a *shield* of poker tables against him. He drills; the **shield** holds. They fling chips at him. He raises his own **shield**, a gold tray, and the chips bounce back into the slot machines."],"杯":["cup","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house where a little *tree* grows a single teacup on every branch. A *no sign* says DO NOT PICK. He picks one anyway, fills the **cup** with lake water, and the tree cries. It grows another **cup** to hold its tears."],"租":["rent","The {Zookeeper} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building with a *stepladder* made of *grain stalk* bundles. A landlord pops out. \"That ladder costs **rent**!\" The zookeeper pays with a banana. The next day, the landlord wants **rent** for the clouds, the wind, and the view."],"骑":["ride","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house onto a *horse* that is clearly an *oddball*: it wears flippers and sunglasses. She tries to **ride** it, but it walks backwards. She stands on its back doing pom-pom routines, and the horse decides to **ride** on her instead."],"乏":["tired","The {Firefighter} drags herself up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} carrying a *flat tyre* that has lost all its air. She is so **tired** she could sleep on the steam room bench. The tyre sighs and flops on her lap, just as **tired**, and they snore together in the jacuzzi."],"隆":["grand","The {Lifeguard} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} palace, which is carved into a whole *hillside*. Trumpets blare, banners unroll, fireworks shoot from the cliffs. It's a **grand** opening for a swimming pool the size of a sea. She cuts the ribbon with her teeth, the **grand** fountain erupts, and she is washed back down the hill."],"诊":["diagnose","The {Jockey} lies in the {Basement} of the {Funfair}'s first-aid tent while a doctor peers at his *thick hair*. A *small speech bubble* pops up: \"Hmm, candyfloss in the scalp.\" The doctor tries to **diagnose** him with a stethoscope, a magnifying glass and a hair dryer. Finally she **diagnoses** him: a severe case of rollercoaster."],"奴":["slave","The {Ninja} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a weary *drudge* carrying every towel, float and inflatable crocodile for a lazy king. He's treated like a **slave**. The Ninja cuts his ropes and hands the towels back to the king. Now the king huffs up the stairs, no longer anyone's **slave**-driver."],"摄":["take in","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and catches an *eavesdropper* with his ear pressed to the wall. A *helping hand* grabs the words floating out and stuffs them in a jar. Every secret it can **take in**, it swallows. The jar burps. It wants to **take in** the Sheriff's secrets too."],"丧":["lose","The {Sailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar}, waving his arms about, and everything starts to fall out of his pockets: his map, his compass, his parrot. He spins to grab them and **loses** his hat, then his boots. By the time he reaches the plane he has managed to **lose** the plane as well."],"污":["dirty","The {Wizard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building holding a *leaky pot* of swamp potion. *Water drops* of green sludge drip into the pool below. Everyone climbs out **dirty**, covered in slime, with frogs in their hair. The Wizard tries a cleaning spell and makes the pool even more **dirty**."],"渡":["cross","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool} and must **cross** to the other side. He balances on a giant *thermometer* floating on the *water drops*, paddling with his drill. Halfway there, the thermometer heats up and boils the water. He makes it **across** just as the pool turns to soup."],"旗":["flag","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house holding a giant *square* of cloth on a pole. She plants it in the sand: a **flag** with her face on it. The crabs salute. Then a seagull plants its own **flag** next to hers, with a chip on it."],"甘":["sweet","The {Gardener} plants *candy* on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, and lollipop trees burst out of the tiles. Everything turns **sweet**: the rain tastes of syrup, the bricks are fudge, the weather vane is a candy cane. Ants climb up from miles around, and the Gardener has to guard his **sweet** roof with a spoon."],"耐":["endure","The {Ninja} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Island} and must stand still while a crab pulls his *beard* hair by hair. He clenches his *thumb* and doesn't flinch. He can **endure** anything. The crab calls its friends. The Ninja continues to **endure**, now with a hundred crabs dangling from his chin."],"凭":["rely on","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} where a *bearer* carries a *small table* for him to lean on. He'll **rely on** it to stand up after every punch. He swings, misses and leans. Swings, misses, leans. When the bearer walks away, the Pirate has nothing to **rely on** and topples flat."],"扎":["prick","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} in a pair of *ski* boots, as a *helping hand* holds out a cactus. It gives him a tiny **prick** on the nose. \"Ow!\" He jumps, slides off the roof on his skis, and lands in the hot tub, where another cactus waits to **prick** him."],"抢":["grab","The {Cheerleader} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Stadium} and finds a tiny *barn* with the last hot dog in the world in it. A *helping hand* shoots out to **grab** it. She leaps. They wrestle over the bun. A goat runs out of the barn and **grabs** the sausage while they're fighting."],"绪":["thread","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and finds a *busy man* winding a tangle of *silk thread* round his fingers. Every **thread** is the start of a story: a knight, a mummy, a lost sock. The Shepherd pulls one loose **thread**, and the whole tangle unravels across the dinosaur gallery."],"粗":["thick","The {Tsar} climbs a *stepladder* onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building with a sack of *rice* and a rope to tie it down. But the rope is **thick** as a tree trunk, too **thick** to knot. The Tsar wraps it round the chimney instead and the whole pool building is tied up like a parcel."],"肩":["shoulder","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} with a whole *door* on one **shoulder** and the *moon* on the other. The bankers come out to watch. He shrugs; the door swings open, and coins pour out of the moon onto his other **shoulder**."],"梁":["beam","The {Lifeguard} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} with a whole *tree* trunk across her back to hold up the falling roof. She shoves it into place: a giant wooden **beam**. Just in time. The roof creaks and rests on it. The crowd cheers, and birds start nesting on the **beam**."],"幻":["illusion","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swan Pond} and sees a silky *cocoon* hanging inside a giant *bracket* on a tree. It opens and out flies a swan made of rainbows. He reaches out, but his hand goes straight through. It's an **illusion**. The pond, the trees, even the Hunter's own boots turn out to be an **illusion**."],"菲":["fragrant","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house surrounded by *grass* so sweet it smells of roses. A cloud of butterflies with *spread wings* fans the scent towards her. The air is so **fragrant** that she forgets the fire. The smoke itself turns **fragrant**, like lavender candles."],"皆":["all","The {Juggler} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} and all the yetis come out *all together*. \"**All** of you, catch!\" He throws snowballs to every yeti at once, and **all** of them catch, and all of them throw them back, and the Juggler disappears under a mountain of snow."],"碎":["smash","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} where a chess *pawn* is trying to crack a *stone* with its tiny head. Bonk, bonk, crack! The stone splits. The pawn gets carried away and starts to **smash** the chairs, the vending machine and the clock. The Sailor shields himself as it **smashes** the fish tank."],"宙":["universe","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and lands under a glass *roof* over a *sprouting field*, where tiny planets are growing like turnips. He plucks one: it's Jupiter. The whole **universe** is sprouting here. He rides off on a comet, pockets full of stars, the **universe** spilling behind him."],"叔":["uncle","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building and finds her *uncle* sunbathing on the chimney in striped trunks. \"Come down, **Uncle**!\" He waves and does a cannonball off the roof into the pool, splashing the whole town. Every **uncle** in the area climbs up to copy him."],"岩":["rock","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} until a *mountain* rolls down the steps, shedding a *stone* at every step. Boulders bounce past her nose. She doesn't flinch. A huge **rock** stops right in front of her and starts meditating too. They sit there all day, two **rocks** in the stairwell."],"荡":["sway","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} into a giant bowl of *soup* hanging from the ceiling on ropes of *grass*. It starts to **sway**, left, right, left. Soup sloshes out over the planes. The pilots below **sway** too, seasick, and the Dentist hands out mints."],"综":["combine","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} temple, an *ancestral hall*, and ties a *silk thread* to every animal: zebra, parrot, crocodile. She pulls them all together and they **combine** into one creature with stripes, feathers and big teeth. It roars and squawks. She tries to **combine** it with a teapot next."],"爬":["climb","The {Pirate} struggles up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} as a huge *python* with eagle *talon* feet slithers past him. It starts to **climb** the walls, the steam pipes, the towel rack. The Pirate tries to **climb** after it with his hook, but slips on a bath bomb and lands in the plunge pool."],"荷":["lotus","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} by the pond, where *grass* gives way to one giant *lotus leaf*. He steps on it and floats off like a raft. A pink **lotus** flower opens beside him, as big as an umbrella. He takes a nap in the **lotus** and drifts out to sea."],"悉":["know","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} house studying *animal tracks* in the sand below. His *heart* thumps: he **knows** every one. Crab, dog, sheep, octopus. \"I **know** who stole my sandwich!\" he shouts, and points at a seagull with mustard on its beak."],"蒂":["stem","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where a *sky god* rises out of the *grass* holding a huge cherry by its **stem**. He swings it like a lasso and lets go. The cherry flies off, leaving the god holding only the **stem**, which he uses as a toothpick."],"返":["return","The {Firefighter} hides in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} as a *rebel* runs off down the *road* with her fire engine. A mile later he **returns**, because he forgot the hose. Then he **returns** again for the helmet. On the third trip he just parks it back and goes home."],"井":["well","The {Juggler} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} and finds a deep stone *well* in the middle of the floor. He drops a juggling ball down; it takes ten seconds to splash. A voice from the bottom shouts \"Thanks!\" and throws back a boxing glove. Every night the **well** sends up more gloves, and the boxers queue at the **well**."],"壮":["strong","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swamp} hut and lands on the shoulders of a *strongman* lifting an alligator in each hand. He is so **strong** that he lifts the Jockey's horse too, then the whole hut. Frogs cheer. The strongman flexes, and the swamp mud trembles: the **strongest** man in the bog."],"薄":["thin","The {Baker} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Fort} and rolls out a pancake so **thin** that he can see through it. He spreads it over the *grass* of the *floodplain* below like a sheet of glass. A cow steps on it and it tears like tissue. He makes another, even **thinner**."],"悄":["quietly","The {Cheerleader} tiptoes across the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} so **quietly** that the cats don't wake. Her *standing heart* thumps in her chest. She reaches the *portrait* of the head cat and draws a moustache on it. Then she creeps back **quietly**, and the portrait winks at her."],"扫":["sweep","The {Sailor} sweeps the {Basement} of the {Tower} with a giant *comb* held in a *helping hand*. The comb catches dust, spiders, lost socks and a sleeping bat. He has to **sweep** it all up the stairs. The bat wakes up, grabs the comb and starts to **sweep** him out."],"敏":["quick","The {Magician} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Inn} and an *acrobat* flips past so **quick** she leaves a trail of sparkles. She steals the Magician's hat and returns it before he blinks. He pulls a rabbit from it; the acrobat is so **quick** she has already put the rabbit back."],"碍":["hinder","The {Ghost} drifts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} hut and finds a *found coin* glued to a huge *stone* blocking every door. It tries to float through, but the stone **hinders** it, wobbling side to side. Crabs try to roll it away, but the coin keeps **hindering** them with its shine."],"殖":["breed","The {Jockey} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} and finds a *skeleton* holding a *plumb line*, measuring honeycombs. Every cell he checks pops out a new bee. The bees **breed** so fast that the hive grows another storey every minute. The skeleton keeps measuring, and the bees keep on **breeding**."],"详":["detailed","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} and a *sheep* blocks his path with a *small speech bubble* describing the match. Every pass, every blade of grass, every sneeze. It's so **detailed** that halftime comes and goes. The Shepherd falls asleep, and the sheep starts a **detailed** account of his snoring."],"迪":["enlighten","The {Dentist} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house with a lantern, following a *road* through a *sprouting field* of ideas. Each sprout pops a lightbulb. He is suddenly **enlightened**: brush the teeth in circles! The crabs crowd round, eager for him to **enlighten** them too."],"矛":["spear","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} with a long *spear* and pulls a rabbit out of its tip. Then a pigeon. Then a scarf a mile long. The **spear** keeps going. The audience gasps. At the top, he hurls the **spear** into the sky and it turns into a shooting star."],"霍":["suddenly","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into a dry room, and **suddenly** a *rain* cloud opens. A thousand *sparrow* chicks pour out with the drops, chirping. He opens his umbrella. **Suddenly** it rains upwards and the sparrows all fly back into the cloud."],"允":["allow","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Dunes} hut when a camel slides in a *permit*. \"Please **allow** me to sit in your lap.\" The Yogi stamps it. Then more camels slide in permits. She has to **allow** a whole caravan onto her yoga mat."],"幅":["width","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} with a *towel* and a *full jar* of water. She stretches the towel across the pool to measure its **width**. Too short! She sews on another towel, and another. Finally she empties the jar and the pool shrinks to the towel's **width**."],"撒":["scatter","The {Sailor} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and a *helping hand* flings *scattered seeds* everywhere. They **scatter** into the jacuzzi, the sauna and the guests' ears. Flowers pop up from everyone's head. The Sailor joins in, **scattering** glitter, and the whole spa looks like a birthday cake."],"剩":["remain","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} camp where a *rider* on an elephant hacks at a giant cake with a *standing knife*. Slice after slice goes to the monkeys. Soon only one crumb is left to **remain** on the plate. The Sheriff guards it with her pistol so that something will **remain** for breakfast."],"凯":["triumph","The {King} parades into the {Basement} of the {Island} palace, blowing a *triumph horn*, after winning the coconut-throwing contest. He climbs on a *small table* and does a victory dance. \"**Triumph**!\" The crabs clap. He blows the horn so hard it shoots him through the roof in **triumph**."],"颗":["grain","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} counting every *page* of his diary, where each **grain** of rice is glued. One **grain**, two grains... A *fruit* falls from a tree and squashes them all. He has to start counting again, one tiny grain at a time."],"骂":["scold","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and lands on a *horse* that won't stop its angry *chatter*. \"Get off me! You're late! Your hat is silly!\" It **scolds** him all the way round the steam room. The Magician turns it into a duck, but the duck **scolds** him even louder."],"赏":["reward","The {Sheriff} lurks in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} when a pilot hands her a shiny *shell* as a **reward** for catching the plane thief. She's delighted. Then all the other pilots bring shells too, until she is buried in seashells: the biggest **reward** in history."],"液":["liquid","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} in the middle of the *night* and lands in a pool of *water drops* that glow green. Everything here is **liquid**: the chairs ripple, the table sloshes, the lamp drips. She tries to sit in lotus and sinks. Even her yoga mat turns to **liquid** and flows out the door."],"番":["foreign","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} and looks down at a *footprint field* full of strange tracks. Kangaroos? Penguins? Boots with curly toes? **Foreign** visitors have landed in the garden. They wave little flags and offer **foreign** sweets that fizz like fireworks, and she sprays them, by accident, with lemonade."],"箱":["box","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} next to a *lookout* tower made of *bamboo*, where a huge cardboard **box** sits on top. He opens it: sheep pour out, hundreds of them, onto the pitch. The match stops. He tries to stuff them back into the **box**, but now it's full of footballers."],"贴":["stick","The {Tailor} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} where a *fortune teller* is reading a pile of *shell* stickers. She licks each one and **sticks** it on a yeti's forehead. The yetis can't get them off. The Tailor laughs, so she **sticks** one on his nose that says \"Fool\"."],"漫":["overflow","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} wrapped in a *long veil* soaked in *water drops*. She wrings it out, and water keeps pouring, gallons and gallons. The bathtub begins to **overflow**, then the sink, then the ballroom. Guests float out of the front door as the whole mansion **overflows**."],"酸":["sour","The {Sailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion with a *handsome man* who pours from a *wine jug*. The Sailor takes a sip, and it's lemon juice: so **sour** his face folds in half. The swans taste it and their necks tie into knots. The handsome man smiles: \"Too **sour**? It's vinegar.\""],"郎":["young man","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} where a nervous *bridegroom* is waiting by a plane in a top hat. He's a **young man** of twenty with a bouquet of fish. The bride parachutes in. The **young man** faints, and the Lifeguard has to give him the kiss of life first."],"腰":["waist","The {Yogi} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} under the full *moon* and wraps a hula hoop around her **waist**. She spins it faster and faster, until the moon itself starts orbiting her **waist** like a silver belt. The owls clap with their wings."],"舒":["relax","The {Sheriff} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} building inside a tiny *hut*, where the locals leave her an *offering* of cushions, iced tea and a foot massage. She takes off her badge and starts to **relax**. Her boots slide off. Even her pistol takes a nap. The whole town learns to **relax** under her snoring."],"眉":["eyebrow","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house with one *raised brow*, which keeps going up, up, off his face, and floats away like a caterpillar. He chases the **eyebrow** across the lake. It lands on a duck, who suddenly looks very surprised. Now the duck wants his other **eyebrow** too."],"忧":["worry","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} with a *standing heart* that has a *wart* on its nose. It paces back and forth. \"What if it rains? What if the boats sink?\" It begins to **worry** so much that it turns grey. The Yogi tells it not to **worry** and a boat promptly sinks."],"浮":["float","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a little *hatchling* riding on *water drops* like a raft. It starts to **float** up, up, out of the pool and into the air. The Firefighter grabs its foot and **floats** too. Together they drift over the diving board, waving at the lifeguards."],"辛":["toil","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} and plants a red *chili* in a pot on the chimney. He has to **toil** all day: watering, weeding, chasing off pigeons. His sweat steams. The chili grows to the size of a car and he must **toil** all night to pick it."],"恋":["love","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and meets a *sweating man* holding out a giant red *heart*. He's in **love**, with her. He drips nervously. She blows her whistle: it's **love** at first sight. The bankers throw coins like confetti."],"餐":["meal","The {Tsar} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} at a long table while a *bone picker* serves every dish of *food* in the kingdom: soup, roasts, puddings, more soup. The **meal** goes on for three days. The Tsar's crown stops fitting. The bone picker tidies up and immediately starts the next **meal**."],"吓":["scare","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Piazza} and runs *downstairs* into the dark. A huge *mouth* yells \"BOO!\" He leaps three feet in the air. It's enough to **scare** the pigeons out of the square. Then the mouth tries to **scare** a statue, and the statue jumps too."],"挺":["straight","The {Tailor} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} and finds a *courtyard* where every tree is bent. A *helping hand* grabs each trunk and pulls it **straight**, like an ironing board. The Tailor stands up **straight** too. Then a boxer walks in slouching, and the hand straightens him with a twang."],"励":["encourage","The {Lifeguard} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where a *strong arm* sharpens a sword on a *whetstone*. She cheers: \"Go on! You can do it!\" She keeps shouting to **encourage** it. The arm sharpens faster, and the sword gleams. Then it turns to **encourage** her to swim to the horizon."],"辞":["resign","The {Tsar} storms up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} with a red *chili* on his *tongue*. He breathes fire and shouts, \"I **resign**!\" He throws down his crown. The queen bee picks it up and puts it on. Then all the worker bees **resign** too, and the honey has to make itself."],"艘":["counter for ships","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} counting every *boat* in the harbour for a white-bearded *elder*. \"One 艘, two 艘, three 艘!\" Every ship needs the **counter for ships**, 艘, and each one honks when counted. The elder falls asleep before the hundredth **counter for ships**."],"键":["key","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yen Exchange} where a *builder* has bricked up the vault. Inside are a billion *gold coins*. He hands the Juggler a **key** the size of an oar. The Juggler juggles it, drops it, and the **key** turns itself in the lock with a click."],"伍":["squad","The {Wizard} hides in the {Basement} of the {Pool} building with a *standing person* holding a *spool* of rope. They tie five swimmers into a **squad**. \"March!\" The squad dives in together, still tied, and spins like a propeller. The Wizard adds a sixth, and the **squad** sinks."],"峰":["peak","The {Firefighter} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple and finds a *mountain* sitting on it, its snowy *peak* poking the clouds. She climbs to the **peak** with her hose. From the top she sprays the whole jungle, and the monkeys build a smaller **peak** out of bananas to copy her."],"尺":["Chinese foot","The {Chef} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Beehive} with a wooden *ruler* marked in **Chinese foot** units, each a third of a metre. He measures the honeycomb: three feet. A bee stings him. He measures the swelling: one **Chinese foot**."],"昨":["yesterday","The {Zookeeper} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} and finds a *jack-in-the-box* popping up with a *sun* on its head. \"That was **yesterday**!\" it squeaks. She checks her calendar. It is! Every box in the warehouse pops open, all shouting about **yesterday**."],"黎":["multitude","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house and sees a **multitude** of people pouring onto the sand: farmers, sailors, grandmothers, babies, ice-cream sellers. Thousands, millions, too many to count. She blows her whistle and the whole **multitude** dives into the sea at once, and the tide goes out."],"辈":["generation","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house onto a wooden *cart* where a grandmother, mother and baby sit, each with *spread wings*. Each **generation** flaps in turn. The grandmother flies first, then the mother, then the baby. The Baker bakes three cakes, one for each **generation**, and the baby eats them all."],"贯":["pierce through","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swan Pond} and threads a *string of coins* onto a long spear. He thrusts it forward, and it **pierces through** a swan's floating hat, an apple, and the reeds. It keeps going and **pierces through** the pond, coming out the other side of the Earth."],"侦":["spy","The {Jockey} creeps across the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}'s helter-skelter as a *standing person* consults an *oracle* in a glass ball. \"Where's the stolen candyfloss?\" The **spy** pulls on a fake moustache and slides down the helter-skelter. The Jockey follows, now a **spy** too, both disguised as clowns."],"滑":["slippery","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Water Park} and treads on a *bone* covered in *water drops*. Whoosh! It's **slippery** as soap. He slides down every slide, through the lazy river and into the wave pool. Even his boots are **slippery** now."],"券":["ticket","The {Cheerleader} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint} where *rolling hands* are printing tickets and a *knife* chops them apart. One flutters to her: a golden **ticket**. \"Free cartwheels for life!\" She waves it around and a thousand cartwheeling strangers chase her for the **ticket**."],"崇":["lofty","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} temple, an *ancestral hall* perched on a *mountain* that keeps growing. The steps go up and up into the clouds. It's so **lofty** that eagles live in the kitchen. The Chef serves soup at the top, in this **lofty** spot where the stars stir the pot."],"扰":["disturb","The {Robot} hides in the {Basement} of the {Tower}, trying to recharge, but a *helping hand* keeps poking the *wart* on its metal nose. Beep! The robot jumps. Poke! Beep! It can't sleep. The hand loves to **disturb** it. In revenge, the robot plays loud music to **disturb** the whole tower."],"宪":["constitution","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and a *front runner* sprints in under the *roof*, waving a scroll. \"The **constitution**! The law of the land!\" He reads rule one: sheep may vote. The Shepherd cheers. Rule two: sheep must wear ties. The sheep protest the **constitution**."],"绕":["wind around","The {Robot} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and an *emperor* starts to **wind around** it with *silk thread*, round and round, like a spool. The Robot spins. The emperor keeps going, tower top to bottom, until the whole building is wound up. The threads **wind around** the flagpole, too."],"趋":["hurry","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} as a *runner* sprints past carrying a bale of *hay*. \"**Hurry**! The horses are hungry!\" She grabs some hay and races after him. The statues **hurry** behind them, clanking, and the dinosaur bones run fastest of all."],"慈":["kind","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} with a *magnet* on a string and a soft *heart* in his pocket. He drags the magnet past every lost bee and pulls them gently home. He is so **kind** that he knits tiny scarves for the drones. The queen calls him the most **kind** Tsar ever."],"乔":["tall","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} on a pair of *stilts*, and keeps climbing. She gets so **tall** that her head pokes out of the roof. The cats climb up her legs to sit on her shoulders. She's so **tall** now that pigeons try to nest in her ponytail."],"阅":["read","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} and lands by a *gate* where a *money changer* swaps coins for books. She skates round and round to **read** each page as she passes. The money changer charges per word. By the end of the night she has **read** a whole encyclopedia and is broke."],"汗":["sweat","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a boiling cellar, where clothes hang on a *drying rack*. He starts to **sweat**. *Water drops* pour off him, filling buckets, soaking the clothes again. The butler wrings out his shirt, and the **sweat** floods the hallway."],"枝":["branch","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive}, where a *tree* is growing out of the chimney. He grabs a *branch* to steady himself. The **branch** grows longer, carrying him over the garden, the river, and into the next town, where it drops him onto another **branch**."],"拖":["drag","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} as a *helping hand* grabs a *snake* by the tail and starts to **drag** it across the tiles. The snake hisses and **drags** the hand back. They tug-of-war over the chimney until the Tailor sews them both into a scarf."],"墨":["ink","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} into a pile of black *soot* mixed with wet *soil*. He stirs it with his wand into thick **ink**. He writes a spell on the wall, and the words climb off and start marching. The soldiers are now covered in **ink** footprints."],"胁":["threaten","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} under the *moon* and finds a yeti's *workshop* full of spiky tools. The yeti waves a hammer. \"Give me your sheep or else!\" It's trying to **threaten** him. The Shepherd waves a sheep back, and the yeti, scared of sheep, stops trying to **threaten** anyone."],"插":["insert","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} with a corn *husker* in a *helping hand*. He has to **insert** a corncob into every chimney. Pop! Pop! Smoke comes out as popcorn. He tries to **insert** one into a guest's ear, and the guest pops too."],"箭":["arrow","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} juggling *bamboo* sticks. One flies off the *front* of his hand, straight as an **arrow**, and pins a banker's tie to the wall. Another **arrow** knocks a coin out of a piggy bank. The Juggler bows and takes a bow and arrow on tour."],"腊":["cured meat","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} into the steam room, where strips of *sun-dried meat* hang drying under a fake *moon*. The steam turns them into **cured meat**, salty and smoky. Guests sniff hungrily. The Lifeguard hands out slices, and the sauna becomes a **cured meat** shop."],"粉":["powder","The {Firefighter} falls into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where someone has dropped a sack of *rice* into the cake mixer next to a *cut cake*. The mixer grinds everything into fine white **powder**. A puff of wind, and the whole funfair turns white. The Firefighter sneezes **powder** for a week."],"泥":["mud","The {Ninja} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} house, where a *nun* is making sandcastles with *water drops* poured onto the sand. It turns to sticky **mud**. The Ninja slips, slides, and becomes a sandcastle himself. The nun crowns him with a seashell and builds a **mud** moat round him."],"氏":["surname","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a huge *family tree* drawn on the honeycomb. Every bee's **surname** is written on it: Buzz, Buzz, Buzz. She adds her own name, Sheriff, and the bees argue about whether she can take their **surname**."],"彭":["Peng","The {Pirate} marches down the vine {Staircase} of the {Jungle} pounding a giant *drumbeat* on a barrel: PENG, PENG, PENG. Every monkey answers with its own *drumbeat* until the trees shake loose coconuts. A parrot screeches his family name back at him, \"**Peng**! **Peng**!\", and the whole jungle joins the **Peng** family band."],"拔":["pull out","The {Baker} slides down the steamy {Staircase} of the {Spa} and spots a *pulled weed* growing out of a mud bath. A giant *helping hand* rises from the mud, grabs it, and they **pull out** the weed together, roots and all, flinging mud on every guest. The roots keep coming, metres of them, until they **pull out** a rubber duck at the end."],"骗":["cheat","The {Pirate} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} riding a painted *horse* and props up a fake *nameboard* reading \"Honest Bank\". He swaps real coins for chocolate ones and tells every customer it's a great deal. When the chocolate melts in their pockets, they realise how badly he managed to **cheat** them, and the *horse* winks: a born **cheat** too."],"凤":["phoenix","The {Firefighter} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle} and finds a *small table* bursting into flames. A *right hand* reaches out of the fire and lifts a blazing bird: a **phoenix**! She sprays it with her hose, but the **phoenix** only sneezes sparks, shakes off the water, and rises from the ashes, singing."],"慧":["wise","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and finds an old owl sweeping it with a tiny *broom*. With every sweep, the owl brushes worries off each waiting patient's *heart*, and they become calm and **wise**. The hunter lowers his rifle and lets the owl sweep him too; he walks out so **wise** he forgets why he came."],"媒":["media","The {Magician} sweeps up the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house where a *woman* holds a giant *plum* like a microphone. She shouts the day's gossip into the *plum* and it booms across the water to every fish. Cameras pop out of the lake: the **media** has arrived, and the magician becomes front-page news for the **media** by morning."],"佩":["admire","The {Pirate} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Lake} pier and finds a *standing person* balancing on a single water lily. The pirate takes off his hat and stares in awe; every frog on the lake applauds. \"How do you do that?\" he asks, and he can't stop to **admire** the trick. He sits down to **admire** it all afternoon, forgetting to plunder anything."],"愤":["anger","The {Firefighter} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and finds a *standing heart* glowing red with **anger**, stomping beside a *fountain*. It kicks the fountain so hard that the *fountain* sprays boiling steam over the dodgems. She hoses the furious heart down, but its **anger** only fizzes louder, and the carousel horses flee in fright."],"扑":["pounce","The {Pirate} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} house and sees a *fortune stick* tumbling through the air. A giant *helping hand* swoops down; the pirate and the hand both **pounce** at the same time and miss, crashing into the deep end. The stick lands on a cat, which looks at them both and decides to **pounce** on the pirate instead."],"龄":["age","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} where a *herald* blows a trumpet and announces each boxer's **age**. A dentist counts the *teeth* of every fighter to check: \"This one has forty years of *teeth*!\" The lifeguard opens her mouth, the *herald* counts, and proudly bellows her **age** to the crowd."],"驱":["drive away","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} on a galloping *horse*, waving a *district map* like a pom-pom. She chants, kicks, and rides the horse in circles until every pigeon flees. She uses the map to **drive away** the burglars too, swatting them all the way into the next district: \"Go, go, **drive away**!\""],"惜":["cherish","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut beside her last strip of *sun-dried meat*, hugging it tight. Her *standing heart* thumps with love for it, guarding it from seagulls. When a gull swoops, she shields the snack with her body: she will **cherish** it forever. She names it, kisses it, and **cherish** wins over hunger."],"豪":["heroic","The {Hunter} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} chasing a tiny *pig*, but the *pig* turns around, puffs out its chest, and charges him like a knight. It rescues a princess, saves the guards, and poses on the battlements: so **heroic**! The hunter kneels and gives the **heroic** *pig* a medal instead of a cage."],"掩":["cover","The {Yogi} descends to the {Basement} of the {Mansion} to meditate, when a *sudden flash* of light blinds everyone. A *helping hand* shoots out and claps over her eyes to **cover** them. Then it grabs a bedsheet and tries to **cover** the whole mansion, chandeliers and all, until only the Yogi's toes stick out."],"兼":["both","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} juggling *two sheaves* of wheat at once, one in each hand. Then he swaps them for coins, still juggling **both** wheat and money together. A banker shouts \"Choose one!\", but the juggler refuses: he keeps **both**, plus the banker's hat."],"跃":["leap","The {Yogi} springs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} with a *kicking foot*, landing beside a twirling *dancer*. Together they **leap** across the ice, higher and higher, until their heads poke the ceiling lights. The *dancer* does a triple spin; the Yogi tries one giant **leap** and lands in a heap of snow."],"尸":["corpse","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} and finds a *lying man*, stiff as a plank, covered in honey. The bees think he's a **corpse** and start building wax walls around him. Suddenly the \"**corpse**\" sneezes, sits up, and asks for toast, and the Sheriff faints instead."],"肃":["solemn","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and every swimmer freezes. On the diving board stands a *stern face* glaring down, silent and **solemn**. Nobody splashes; even the inflatable flamingo stops bobbing. The sailor tries a joke, but the *stern face* stays so **solemn** that the water itself goes still."],"帕":["handkerchief","The {Pirate} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} wrapped in a fluffy *towel*. A *white dove* flies by carrying a tiny **handkerchief**, and the pirate sneezes so hard his towel flies off. The dove kindly offers the **handkerchief**, which the pirate uses to blow his nose with a foghorn honk."],"驶":["drive","The {Sheriff} rides a *horse* down into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where a *historian* sits with a steering wheel. \"Let me **drive**!\" says the historian, and he steers the horse through honey tunnels, narrating the history of every turn. They **drive** so fast the bees need speeding tickets."],"堡":["fortress","The {Baker} digs into the {Basement} of the {Tower}, piling up *soil* to build walls, while a *nanny* bosses him around. \"Thicker! Higher!\" she shouts, and the soil mounds become a mighty **fortress**. The nanny moves in with a cradle, and nobody gets past the **fortress** without a nap."],"届":["session","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} onto a *lying man* asleep beside a *sprouting field*. Every year the field sprouts a new crop of yetis who sit down for the annual **session** of the Yeti Parliament. The lying man yawns: he has slept through every **session** since 1890."],"欣":["happy","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} with a huge *grin* stretched ear to ear. The *grin* is so wide it lights up the night, and her sheep start dancing. Guests open their windows and catch it too: everyone in the inn is **happy**, and the **happy** grin floats off like a moon."],"惠":["favour","The {Hunter} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} into the {Waiting Room} and finds a giant *heart* handing out free cupcakes to everyone. \"Do me a **favour**,\" it says, and gives the Hunter its last cupcake. He feels so warm that he does every patient a **favour** too, carrying them in on his back."],"册":["booklet","The {Tsar} clambers out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} clutching a *bamboo book* tied with string. He unrolls it into a tiny **booklet** of royal decrees, and each slat clacks like castanets as he reads. The peasants applaud, so he publishes a **booklet** every hour until the hut is stuffed with them."],"储":["store","The {Chef} dives into the {Basement} of the {Pool} where a *standing person* counts jars by *headcount*: \"One, two, three hundred!\" They **store** pickles, jams, and soups under the water, stacked to the ceiling. The Chef adds a cake, and the counting person yells, \"Out of room to **store** it!\" as everything floats away."],"飘":["flutter","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} waving a *ticket*, when a gust of *wind* snatches it. The ticket and every cat's whisker **flutter** off into the sky like confetti. The pirate chases them, but his hat, beard and flag **flutter** off too, until he stands there bald and blinking."],"桑":["mulberry","The {Sailor} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, where a giant *mulberry* tree has burst through the roof. Silkworms ride its branches like pilots, munching **mulberry** leaves. The Sailor shakes the tree, and a purple rain of **mulberry** fruit splats over every aeroplane below."],"闲":["idle","The {Shepherd} lounges on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} beside a closed *gate*, where a *tree* grows right in the doorway. Nobody can get in, so everyone is **idle**: bankers nap, coins snore, and the tree yawns. The shepherd hangs a hammock in the branches and stays **idle** until next Tuesday."],"惨":["miserable","The {Tsar} stomps into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and finds his *standing heart* weeping into a bowl of bitter *ginseng*. It sobs that its crown is lost, its castle leaks, and its soup is cold: utterly **miserable**. The Tsar tastes the ginseng and becomes even more **miserable**; both weep until the basement floods."],"洁":["clean","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} carrying a *lucky charm* that sprays *water drops* everywhere. Every drop scrubs the hairy yetis until they sparkle white. The cave becomes so **clean** it squeaks, and the yetis refuse to get dirty again: **clean** fur only!"],"踪":["trace","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} hut following muddy prints from a *kicking foot*. They lead straight into an old *ancestral hall*, where she finds a faint **trace** of every escaped animal: a feather, a fin, a sock. She follows each **trace** until she has her whole zoo back."],"勃":["thriving","The {Baker} charges up the {Staircase} of the {Fort} when a blazing *comet* crashes into his flour sack. A *strong arm* grabs the comet and kneads it into the dough, and the bread grows, booming and bursting with life: **thriving**! Soon the fort is a **thriving** bakery with fiery loaves in every window."],"宾":["guest","The {Baker} rolls out a red carpet on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} for the *guest of honour*, a goat wearing a crown. Every chimney puffs confetti, and the Baker serves a cake taller than the chimneys. The **guest** eats it all, plus the tablecloth, and the innkeeper declares her **guest** of the year."],"频":["frequently","The {Pirate} hops up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} one *step* at a time, and at every *step* he flips a *page* of his treasure map. He stops **frequently** to check it, so frequently that the stairs start keeping score. By the top, he has stopped a thousand times; the innkeeper sighs that he visits **frequently**."],"仇":["hatred","The {Chef} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse}, where a *standing person* swings a *crowbar* at his canoes. They have been enemies for years, full of **hatred**, over a stolen soup recipe. The Chef throws a ladle, the crowbar clangs, and their **hatred** bubbles until the boats themselves start fighting."],"磨":["grind","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort}, where a round *stone* rolls over a pile of *hemp*. He waves his wand and the stone spins faster, faster, to **grind** the hemp into dust that clouds the fort. The soldiers sneeze in unison; the stones keep on to **grind** their swords into butter knives."],"递":["hand over","The {Dentist} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} road, where her *little brother* runs along the *road* with a toothbrush. He reaches her and must **hand over** the brush, but a crab grabs it first. Now the crab must **hand over** it, and a whole relay of crabs passes it down the beach."],"邪":["evil","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} carved into a *hillside*, where a giant *fang* glints in the dark. It belongs to an **evil** yeti cackling over stolen sheep. The Shepherd yanks out the *fang* with pliers, and the **evil** yeti lisps so badly nobody can take him seriously."],"撞":["bump into","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swamp} and lands on a skateboard. A *helping hand* shoves him straight at a *schoolkid* on a lily pad, and they **bump into** each other with a mighty SPLASH. Frogs fly everywhere; then the frogs **bump into** each other and the swamp becomes a bumper-car rink."],"拟":["draft","The {Ninja} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut, sketching a secret plan. A *helping hand* holds a *tool*, a quivering pencil, and scribbles the first **draft** of an attack on the sandcastle across the bay. The tide washes it away, so they write a new **draft** on a surfboard."],"滚":["roll","The {Gardener} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Casino} wearing a gold *royal robe* that trails behind her. *Water drops* pour from the ceiling, she slips, and she starts to **roll** across the floor like a dice. She knocks over the roulette wheel, and every chip, card and croupier begins to **roll** after her."],"奏":["play music","The {Zookeeper} springs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} holding a *spring planter* full of tulips that open like trumpets. She points them at the *sky* and they **play music**, a booming brass band. The clouds dance, the ducks sing, and the boats **play music** too by banging their oars."],"巡":["patrol","The {Shepherd} marches down the {Staircase} into the {Dunes}, following a long *road* beside a *wavy river* of sand. She and her sheep **patrol** the desert in a neat line, saluting every cactus. When a camel sneaks past, the whole flock spins around and goes back on **patrol**, baa-ing like sirens."],"颜":["colour","The {Yogi} poses on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} beside a dapper *gentleman* holding a blank *page*. She breathes out, and the page fills with every **colour** in the rainbow, splattering the gentleman's suit. He sneezes, and **colour** sprays across the whole mansion like fireworks."],"剂":["dose","The {Juggler} pops out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach}, where a *standing knife* trims a *trimmed hedge* into a perfect pill shape. The hedge pill is a giant **dose** of medicine for a sick whale. The juggler tosses the **dose** into the waves, and the whale burps, cured."],"绩":["achievement","The {Juggler} climbs through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where a *debt collector* waits with a list. To pay, he weaves a *silk thread* into a golden trophy, his greatest **achievement**. The collector weeps, frames it, and announces his **achievement** over a megaphone to every surfer."],"贡":["contribute","The {Gardener} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} onto a *workbench* covered in seashells. Each villager brings a *shell* to **contribute** to a giant shell statue of a whale. The gardener adds her watering can, and even the fish **contribute** bubbles until the statue begins to float."],"疯":["crazy","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse when a *wind* blows a *sickbed* up to her, wheels spinning. In it lies a monkey howling with laughter, completely **crazy**. The wind spins the bed in circles and the Firefighter starts laughing too, until the whole jungle goes **crazy**."],"坡":["slope","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} and spreads out an animal *hide* like a sled. He shovels *soil* off the roof until it tilts into a steep **slope**, then whooshes down it, cannonballs bouncing after him. He hits the moat and the whole fort slides down the **slope** behind him like a toboggan."],"瞧":["look","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} where a sizzling *barbecue* smells of grilled fish. One giant *eye* pops out of the grill and spins around: \"**Look**!\" Every cat stops licking and stares. The cheerleader shakes her pom-poms and chants, \"**Look**, look, look!\" until the eye winks and the fish fly onto every plate."],"截":["cut off","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} juggling a long *lance* when a *sparrow* lands on its tip. The sparrow chirps and the lance swings down to **cut off** a yeti's ponytail. Furious, the yeti tries to **cut off** the juggler's escape, but the sparrow carries the juggler away by his collar."],"燃":["ignite","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} carrying a tiny *campfire* in its chest. It sneezes sparks and *flames* leap onto the curtains, the piano, and the butler's wig. Everything begins to **ignite** in a dazzling chain, and the robot cheers, pressing a button to **ignite** the chandelier as a finale."],"焦":["burnt","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} juggling sausages over a smoking *barbecue*. He gets distracted by a cat and every sausage drops in, crackles, and turns black and **burnt**. The cats sniff, sneeze soot, and refuse to eat anything **burnt**, so the juggler wears the sausages as a necklace."],"殿":["palace hall","The {Dentist} rises through the {Trapdoor} into the grand **palace hall** of the {Yen Exchange}, gold columns glinting. On a golden *throne* sits the bank manager, swinging a *war club* at anyone with crooked teeth. The dentist ducks, polishes his teeth, and the whole **palace hall** echoes with a sparkling smile."],"伪":["fake","The {Wizard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Lake} house, where a *standing person* dresses up in a grey costume beside an *elephant handler*. The \"elephant\" is clearly **fake**: two people under a blanket with a hose for a trunk. The handler swears it's real, but the Wizard pulls the blanket and reveals a **fake** in tap shoes."],"柳":["willow","The {Lifeguard} slips into the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel} where a *tree* grows through a *mortise* hole in the floorboards. Its long branches droop like hair: a weeping **willow**, sobbing onto the bunk beds. The lifeguard hands it a tissue and the **willow** blows its nose so loudly the backpackers wake up."],"锁":["lock","The {Sailor} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} where a mountain of *gold coins* glitters. He reaches for one, and CLICK: every coin snaps shut like a giant **lock** around his wrist. He pulls and tugs, but each coin is a tiny **lock**, and he clanks out dragging a chain of gold."],"逼":["force","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut as a *full jar* of jam rolls down the *road* toward the sea. It squeezes every crab and tourist ahead of it into the water, a huge sticky wall. The jar shouts \"Move!\" to **force** them out of the way, and the baker uses a rolling pin to **force** the lid back on."],"颇":["quite","The {Pirate} sprawls on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} on a striped animal *hide*, reading a *page* of poetry aloud. The cannon crew nods: \"**Quite** good.\" He reads another page, and they nod harder: \"**Quite** excellent!\" Soon the whole fort is quite moved, quite weepy, and quite late for battle."],"昏":["faint","The {Hunter} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} as purple *twilight* swirls overhead like smoke from a slot machine. The sun sinks, the neon blinks, and he gets so dizzy he starts to **faint**. Every gambler beside him feels faint too, and one by one they **faint** in a pile of chips."],"劝":["urge","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint}, where a *right hand* and a *strong arm* push a stubborn coin toward the press. She chants, \"Go, coin, go!\" to **urge** it on, and the arm flexes and pushes harder. The coin finally rolls in, and every coin behind it begs her to **urge** them too."],"呈":["present","The {Chef} carries a silver tray up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple with a rolled *petition* on it like a fancy dish. At the top, a gorilla king waits. The chef bows and lifts the lid to **present** it with a drum roll, and the gorilla eats the *petition*, so the chef has to **present** dessert instead."],"搜":["search","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} while a wrinkly *elder* lost his false teeth. A giant *helping hand* rummages through every boat, net, and barrel to **search** for them. They **search** the gulls, the waves, and the sailor's beard, until the elder smiles: they were in his mouth all along."],"勤":["hardworking","The {Cheerleader} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} with a pot of *violet* flowers and a *strong arm* sticking out of her backpack. The arm sweeps, mops, and paints while she cheers: so **hardworking**! By dawn the inn is spotless, and the *violet* flowers are polishing the windows, equally **hardworking**."],"戒":["give up","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a *sentry* guards a jar of cookies. Every time a yeti reaches for one, the sentry bonks it with a spear and shouts, \"**Give up**!\" The yetis sob but finally **give up** sweets forever, and the juggler juggles carrots instead."],"驾":["drive","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Piazza} and lands on a *horse* with a big *plus sign* painted on its rump. Every time he pulls the reins, another horse is added: plus one, plus one. Soon he must **drive** a carriage pulled by forty horses, and they **drive** circles around the fountain."],"漂":["pretty","The {Pirate} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} holding a *ticket* to a beauty contest. He splashes *water drops* on his face, combs his beard with a fish, and paints his nails. The cats gasp: he's so **pretty**! He wins first prize and the cats crown him the most **pretty** pirate alive."],"饮":["drink","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Inn} beside a *side dish* of salty peanuts. Every peanut makes her *yawn* wider, until her mouth is big enough to **drink** the whole barrel of tea. She tips it in, gulp gulp, and the innkeeper serves her the next barrel to **drink** too."],"曹":["Cao","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} dragging a wooden *trough* full of soup. At the top waits a general wearing a name badge: **Cao**. The Tsar pours the soup over his head as tribute, and General **Cao** licks his moustache and declares it delicious."],"朵":["flower","The {Dentist} digs into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} and finds a single *flower* growing out of a crate of toothbrushes. She waters it with mouthwash, and the **flower** blooms bigger and bigger, filling the whole warehouse with petals. Now every customer gets a free **flower** with their filling."],"仔":["careful","The {Zookeeper} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Beehive} carrying a tiny lion *cub* wrapped in a blanket. She tiptoes past the sleeping bees, **careful** not to buzz or bump. The *cub* sneezes, the bees wake, and the Zookeeper whispers, \"Be **careful**!\" as she glides past them on tiptoe."],"柔":["soft","The {Robot} creaks up the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} holding a *springy twig* that bends and bounces. It touches the robot's metal chest, and suddenly the robot goes all **soft** and wobbly like jelly. It slumps onto a boat, hugs a pillow, and declares itself the most **soft** robot ever built."],"俩":["two","The {Lifeguard} slips into the {Basement} of the {Piazza} cafe, where a *standing person* weighs people on a *balance scale*. She steps on one side, her twin on the other, and the scale stays dead level: the **two** of them, perfectly matched. A third cousin hops on and the scale flips, so it stays just the **two**."],"孟":["Meng","The {Magician} shoots through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle} holding the *firstborn* baby of the **Meng** family, swaddled in leaves. He pulls a top hat off the baby and out pop a hundred monkeys chanting the family name. The jungle bows to young **Meng**, crowned eldest heir of all the trees."],"腐":["rotten","The {Firefighter} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Pool} house and finds a tiny *mansion* made entirely of *meat*. It's been there for months and is green, fuzzy and **rotten**, buzzing with flies. She sprays it with her hose, and the **rotten** mansion collapses in a stinky wave that empties the pool."],"幼":["young","The {Yogi} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} holding a silk *cocoon*. A tiny *strong arm* punches out of it, then a second, and out wriggles a baby caterpillar wearing a nappy: so **young**! It flexes, rows a boat, and the Yogi bows to the **young** champion."],"践":["carry out","The {Juggler} shoots up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} with a *kicking foot* and *twin blades* strapped to his shoes. He has a plan, and now he must **carry out** every step: he kicks open every vault and slices every coin into perfect halves. The bankers gape as he whistles and stops to **carry out** the last step in one breath."],"籍":["register","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} bar where a stalk of *bamboo* stands over a *ploughed field* of sand. Each bamboo stalk is a name in the town **register**, and he juggles them to sign up every crab. A crab who isn't on the **register** gets ploughed under the sand."],"牧":["herd","The {Magician} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} carrying a long *cane*, while a *cow* floats past on an inflatable ring. He taps the water with the cane and fifty more cows appear, splashing. He must **herd** them all into the shallow end, and the cows **herd** him back into the deep end."],"凉":["cool","The {Lifeguard} jogs down the {Staircase} of the {Stadium}, where *icicles* hang from a frozen *palace*. Every athlete breathes out clouds and shivers. She licks an icicle and the whole stadium becomes delightfully **cool**, so cool that the referee wears sunglasses and skates across the pitch, looking very **cool**."],"牲":["livestock","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} tower, watching a *cow* nibble a tiny *seedling*. Suddenly goats, pigs and chickens climb up after it until the roof is packed with **livestock**. The roof creaks, and the Sheriff lassoes all the **livestock** back down the vines, one moo at a time."],"佳":["fine","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} beside a *standing person* holding a polished *jade tablet*. The tablet reflects the sunset so beautifully that the pigeons applaud. \"**Fine** work,\" says the standing person, and the juggler toasts with a teacup of **fine** wine."],"娜":["female name","The {Ninja} sneaks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} where a *woman* in a mud mask reads name tags. A *pointing finger* glides down the list and stops at a long, graceful **female name**: Nana. The ninja insists that's his **female name** too, and nobody dares argue with a ninja in a robe."],"浓":["thick","The {Ninja} creeps down the {Staircase} into the {Lagoon} beside a *farm*, where *water drops* are boiling into soup. The soup grows so **thick** that the ninja's sword gets stuck upright in it. Cows wade in and become a **thick** stew, mooing, while ducks paddle around like croutons."],"芳":["fragrant","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} on a *square* patch of *grass* that smells of roses. She sprays it, and the scent explodes: every aeroplane smells **fragrant** as perfume. Pilots float out of cockpits sniffing, and the runway becomes **fragrant** enough to bottle."],"稿":["draft","The {Gardener} burrows into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and builds a tiny *tower* out of *grain stalk* bundles. On every stalk she writes a sentence, a rough **draft** of her novel. The tower topples, the sentences scramble, and she calls the new mess her second **draft**."],"竹":["bamboo","The {Jockey} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and casts a *fish hook* into the water. Instead of fish, she pulls up a stalk of green **bamboo**, then another and another. Soon the pool is a jungle of **bamboo**, and a panda floats by on a lilo, munching."],"腹":["belly","The {Firefighter} plunges through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} on a *return trip* to the *moon*, which hangs above the deep end. She belly-flops onto it with her round **belly**, and the moon bounces her back. She makes the trip again and again until her **belly** is shaped like a full moon."],"跌":["fall","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} as a *lost arrow* whizzes past and trips her *kicking foot*. She tumbles off the roof to **fall** onto a yeti's head. The yeti topples too, and the whole yeti family **fall** like dominoes down the mountain."],"逻":["patrol","The {Lifeguard} jogs down the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} along a *road* of conveyor belts, holding a *gauze net*. Her job is to **patrol** for runaway rubber ducks. She nets dozens, but more escape, so she has to **patrol** all night on roller skates."],"垂":["droop","The {Chef} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a *weeping willow* growing from the carpet. Its branches **droop** onto every patient, tickling their noses. The Chef props them up with spaghetti, but the spaghetti also starts to **droop**, and soon everyone wears noodle wigs."],"遵":["obey","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} raising a *toast* to the rules. Every animal lines up on the *road* below and promises to **obey**: no gambling, no biting, no stealing chips. A monkey refuses, so the zookeeper clinks her glass, and the monkey bows and starts to **obey**."],"脉":["pulse","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island}, where a *stream* glows under the *moon*. He presses his finger to it and feels a **pulse**: thump, thump, the island is alive! The stream throbs, the palm trees nod in rhythm, and the Magician's top hat bounces with every **pulse**."],"貌":["appearance","The {Magician} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a *badger* in his hat. The badger stands against a sheet, casting a *silhouette* of a dashing prince. Everyone admires its **appearance**, but when the sheet drops, the badger is just a badger, with a mustache drawn on to improve its **appearance**."],"柏":["cypress","The {Baker} digs into the {Basement} of the {Island} and finds a dark *tree* growing upside down. A *white dove* nests in its roots, cooing. The tree is an ancient **cypress**, and its scent is so strong that the bread smells of **cypress** for a hundred years."],"狱":["prison","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a dark cell, where a *prowling dog* guards the bars. She's in **prison** for stretching too close to the dinosaurs. The dog prowls, she stretches, and she slips between the bars like noodles, escaping the **prison** in a perfect downward dog."],"猜":["guess","The {Tsar} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut, where a *prowling dog* sniffs a patch of *moss*. \"What's under it?\" asks the Tsar. \"**Guess**!\" barks the dog. The Tsar guesses gold, a crown, a pie; the dog digs up a sock. \"Wrong **guess**,\" it says, and wears it as a hat."],"怜":["pity","The {Lifeguard} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} as a *herald* announces that a coin has lost its shine. Her *standing heart* swells with **pity** for the poor dull coin. She polishes it, sings it a lullaby, and soon every banker weeps with **pity** too."],"惑":["puzzled","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse}, where a *guard post* stands next to a beating *heart*. He asks the guard what the heart is guarding, and the guard scratches his helmet, completely **puzzled**. The heart beats out a riddle in Morse code, and all three stay **puzzled** till dawn."],"陶":["pottery","The {Tailor} spins up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} on a potter's wheel, carrying lumps of clay dug from a *hillside*. At every step she throws a new piece of *pottery*: vases, jugs, a teapot shaped like a goose. The tower fills with **pottery** to the roof, and she stitches tiny jackets for every piece of **pottery**."],"兽":["beast","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and meets a pair of enormous *horns* rising from the water. A hairy **beast** surfaces, wearing a lifejacket. It roars, the canoes flee, and the Sheriff pins his badge on its horns, deputising the **beast** to guard the docks."],"帐":["tent","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and pitches a **tent** made of one enormous *towel*. For guy-ropes she uses a horse's *long hair*, braided tight. Wind from a jet engine fills it like a balloon, and the **tent** floats off the runway with the jockey waving inside."],"饰":["decoration","The {Sheriff} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} carrying a *side dish* of jelly beans. The bees glue each bean to the honeycomb as **decoration**, sparkly and colourful. Soon the Sheriff's hat, boots and badge are covered too, and he jingles like a walking **decoration**."],"贷":["loan","The {Dentist} pops out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} and borrows a giant *shell* full of pearls from a crab. A *stand-in* dentist signs the papers so she doesn't have to. Now the crab chases the stand-in around the palm trees, waving the **loan** contract: pay back the **loan**, with interest in seaweed!"],"昌":["prosperous","The {Chef} grills on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} under a *double sun*, two blazing suns side by side. The heat makes everything grow: crops sprout, planes multiply, the business booms, all **prosperous**. The Chef sells sunny pancakes to every pilot and becomes the most **prosperous** cook in aviation."],"叙":["narrate","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} holding a plate of *leftovers*. A *right hand* points at each scrap, and she begins to **narrate**: this crust was a king's, this bone a dinosaur's. Visitors gather, the curator weeps, and she continues to **narrate** until the plate is a museum exhibit."],"躺":["lie down","The {Tailor} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} and finds an *attic* that fell through the ceiling. She stretches her *torso* across its dusty mattress and decides to **lie down** for a minute. A jet roars overhead; she doesn't care. The whole hangar staff joins her, all choosing to **lie down** in a row."],"钢":["steel","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} melting *gold coins* in a pot on the mountain *ridge*. She pours them into moulds, but out comes grey **steel** instead. She builds a **steel** watering can so heavy that the hangar roof bends under it."],"沟":["ditch","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} with a long *hook*, dragging it across the yard. It scrapes a deep **ditch**, and *water drops* rush in from the sky. Boats slide off their racks and float down the **ditch** like ducks heading for the sea."],"寄":["send","The {Juggler} climbs through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where an *oddball* sits under a *roof* made of envelopes. He folds himself into a box and asks the Juggler to **send** him to the moon. The Juggler stamps the box, kicks it into the waves, and they **send** him off, bobbing toward the horizon."],"扶":["help up","The {Firefighter} trips down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and a slippery *husband* goes splat beside her. A giant *helping hand* reaches out to **help up** the husband, then her, then a fallen inflatable shark. Soon the hand has to **help up** everyone in the building, one by one, like a crane."],"铺":["shop","The {Pirate} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and opens a **shop** on a floating *seedbed*. He sells seeds for *gold coins*, plus goggles and parrot snacks. Swimmers paddle up to buy, and soon the pirate's **shop** is the busiest one in the pool."],"邓":["Deng","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle}, where a *right hand* waves from the top of a *hillside*. It belongs to Mr **Deng**, who needs a filling. She climbs the hill, drills while monkeys hold the lamp, and Mr **Deng** smiles so wide the jungle echoes his name."],"寿":["long life","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and finds a *longevity peach* bobbing on the water. He takes one bite and grows a long white beard down to his boots: **long life**! The fish nibble it too and swim off whistling, a hundred years old and wishing everyone **long life**."],"惧":["fear","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Museum}, where a *toolbox* opens by itself and saws start to buzz. His *standing heart* jumps out of his chest, trembling with **fear**. The dinosaur skeletons shiver too, and everyone hides inside a mummy's coffin, chattering with **fear**."],"询":["inquire","The {Shepherd} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Dunes} with a *small speech bubble* floating above her, asking every camel: \"Where are my sheep?\" She must **inquire** for *ten days*, bubble after bubble, until the sky is full of question marks. Finally a cactus answers, and she stops to **inquire** no more."],"汤":["soup","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} stirring a cauldron of *soup* with a giant needle. The **soup** boils over and pours down the walls onto the planes. Pilots grab spoons, and the jets take off with their tanks full of **soup**."],"盗":["rob","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower}, where a long *queue* of thieves lines up at a golden *dish*. Each one grabs a gem and passes it down the line: they **rob** the dish in seconds. The dentist yanks a gold tooth from the leader, and they **rob** her of her drill in return."],"肥":["fat","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house, where a *python* curled up by the *moon* swallows a whole cake. The python swells round and **fat**, too big for the stairs. She tries pushing, pulling, hosing it, but the snake just gets more **fat**, and now it's eating the moon."],"尝":["taste","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} with a spoon for the *taste test*. He dips it into the jet fuel, a puddle, a pilot's soup, and makes faces. \"You must **taste** everything!\" he cries, and the planes line up to let him **taste** their engines."],"匆":["hurried","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} palace as a *flapping flag* whips in the wind, signalling: hurry! He grabs his crown, his slippers and his breakfast in one **hurried** grab. He sprints, trips, and does everything in such a **hurried** rush that he jumps into the lagoon still in pyjamas."],"辉":["shine","The {Hunter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} as an *army* marches below with polished shields. A beam of *light* hits them and they **shine** so bright that patients shield their eyes. The Hunter polishes his rifle until it can **shine** too, and the whole roof glows."],"奈":["how","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} beside a *big man* bowing at an *altar*. \"**How** do I win?\" he asks. The altar shrugs. The big man asks again, \"**How**?\", and the ninja throws a coconut at him: problem solved."],"扣":["button","The {King} sinks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and his robe bursts open. A *helping hand* rushes to sew a **button** back on, and a big *mouth* bites the thread. The **button** pops off again, ping, and lands in a fish's mouth, which swallows it and grins."],"廷":["court","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} into a grand *courtyard* where the emperor's **court** is in session. Two boxers fight beneath the throne while ministers take notes. The Tailor measures everyone for robes, and the whole **court** ends up in matching sequined gowns."],"澳":["Australia","The {Ghost} floats up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a *maze* filled with *water drops*. At the centre a kangaroo hops in a puddle, holding a sign: **Australia**. The Ghost follows it out of the maze and finds the tower has drifted all the way to **Australia**."],"嘛":["obviously","The {Magician} stands on the {Front Step} of the {Spa} with a rope of *hemp* hanging from his *mouth*. He pulls and pulls out a never-ending rope. \"**Obviously**,\" he shrugs, as if it's normal. The guests gasp, and he pulls out a towel too: \"**Obviously**!\""],"董":["director","The {Dentist} sinks into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hotel, where the *director* of the company sits in a bathtub. He bosses everyone with a rubber duck as a gavel, the board's **director**. The dentist checks his teeth, and the **director** pays her in seashells."],"迁":["move","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} as *thousand ants* march down the *road*, each carrying a coin. She waves her pom-poms to cheer them on as they **move** the whole bank across town. The building groans, lifts, and starts to **move** too, ants underneath like wheels."],"凝":["freeze","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} as *icicles* drip from the ropes. A boxer with a *puzzled face* tries to punch, but his fist starts to **freeze** mid-air. The whole crowd starts to **freeze** too, mouths open, until the arena is a museum of ice statues."],"慰":["comfort","The {Wizard} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake}, where an *officer* holds a broken *heart* that won't stop crying. The officer pats it, the Wizard sings, and they wrap it in a warm blanket to **comfort** it. The lake ripples, the ducks hum, and the heart purrs, full of **comfort**."],"厌":["fed up","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to the foot of a *cliff*, where a *dog* has fetched the same stick a thousand times. The *dog* finally drops it, rolls its eyes, and sighs: totally **fed up**. The Yogi is **fed up** too, so they both take a nap on the cliff."],"脏":["dirty","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} under the *moon* overlooking a *farmstead*, where pigs have rolled in oil. Everything is **dirty**: planes, pigs, the moon smeared with grease. She tries a bucket and sponge, but the pigs just get more **dirty**, and the moon wants a bath too.","zāng"],"腾":["soar","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple and sews wings onto the *moon*. The moon flaps, rises, and starts to **soar** over the treetops. Monkeys cling to its edges and **soar** with it, shrieking with joy, while the Tailor waves a needle."],"幽":["secluded","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse}, hidden behind a *mountain*, weaving a *silk pair* of slippers in perfect silence. No ducks, no boats, nobody: completely **secluded**. A fish peeks out, sees nobody, and sighs at how **secluded** it is."],"怨":["resent","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint}, where a *tossing sleeper* groans in bed, his *heart* full of grudges. Coins stamped with grumpy faces pile up around him. He tosses, he mutters, and he can't stop to **resent** his neighbour; every coin learns to **resent** him too."],"鞋":["shoe","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} with a sheet of *rawhide* and a *jade tablet* to cut on. She makes a giant **shoe** for a yeti with bunions. It fits! The yeti stomps happily, and now every yeti wants a **shoe** with jade buckles."],"丢":["lose","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} with a *shoulder pole* full of teeth on her *elbow*. She trips, and the teeth scatter down the roof. \"I **lose** everything!\" she wails. The backpackers below catch them, but she manages to **lose** her drill too."],"埋":["bury","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} lighthouse with a shovel to **bury** a treasure chest. He heaps *soil* over it, then a whole *village* moves in on top. Now the whole village wants to **bury** treasure, and the island is all lumps and grumbling pirates."],"泉":["spring","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} and discovers a *wellspring* bubbling up through the coin press. Out spurt sparkling coins in a spring, splashing everywhere. She cheers, does a cartwheel, and drinks from the **spring**, and her pom-poms turn to silver fountains of the **spring**."],"涌":["gush","The {Yogi} sits in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} villa when *water drops* begin to rush through a *tunnel* in the wall. The water starts to **gush** in torrents, sweeping chairs and fish around her. She keeps meditating while the waves **gush** around her, floating serenely on the flood."],"辖":["govern","The {Shepherd} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Piazza} town hall pulling a *cart*, chasing a *pest* that steals sheep. She is mayor now and must **govern** everything: the pigeons, the fountain, the pest. She locks the pest in the cart and decides to **govern** with a crook as her sceptre."],"躲":["hide","The {Dentist} chases a patient into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse}. He tries to **hide** his *torso* behind a giant *flower*, petals over his head. She tiptoes past, sees a pair of shoes poking out, and shouts \"Can't **hide** from flossing!\""],"晋":["advance","The {Juggler} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} wearing a *silver medal*, glinting like the *sun*. He juggles faster and faster, climbing up the stairs on the ball, to **advance** to gold. The innkeeper raises his flag, and the juggler continues to **advance** onto the roof."],"紫":["purple","The {Zookeeper} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Beehive} and points at *this spot* with a *silk skein*. She dyes every bee **purple**, then the honey, then the honeycomb. Soon the hive glows **purple** like a giant plum, and the bees buzz out grape-flavoured jam."],"艰":["hard","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} trying to juggle with only a *right hand* while a banker's *glare* burns into him. It's **hard**: the coins fall, the wind howls. Every glare makes it more **hard**, until the juggler juggles the banker too."],"魏":["Wei","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} castle, where a *ghost* clutches a *wilting stalk* labelled **Wei**. \"Restore the kingdom of **Wei**!\" it moans. The Wizard waves his wand, the stalk sprouts, and a tiny kingdom grows on the water."],"吾":["I","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and grabs a *speaker*. \"**I**, the Wizard, am the greatest!\" he booms, and the water ripples. Every swimmer shouts \"**I**!\" back, and the speaker squeals, unable to decide which loudmouth to believe."],"慌":["panic","The {Hunter} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Swamp} shack when his *standing heart* sees a *wasteland* where his lunch used to be. **Panic**! The heart runs in circles, bumps the chimney, and tumbles into the swamp. Frogs join the **panic**, croaking alarms."],"祝":["wish","The {Jockey} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} beside a *small altar* floating on a lilo. Her *big brother* kneels at it, blowing out birthday candles and making a **wish** so loud the lifeguards hear it: \"A pony!\" A pony rises dripping from the deep end, and every swimmer rushes to make a **wish** too."],"邮":["mail","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} carrying a sack of **mail** that a goose delivered from a *sprouting field* on the *hillside*. Letters sprout like lettuces, and each one she opens grows a new envelope. The boats fill with **mail** until they sink, and the fish read postcards underwater."],"吐":["spit","The {Tailor} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Pool} when a giant *mouth* in the wall starts to **spit** out *soil*: mud, worms, a whole flowerpot. She sews a bib for it, but it keeps going, determined to **spit** until the pool becomes a garden."],"狠":["ruthless","The {Hunter} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Funfair} where a *prowling dog* with a cold *glare* runs the ghost train. It shows no mercy: it pops every balloon, steals every candyfloss, and takes the Hunter's hat. \"**Ruthless**!\" he gasps, and the dog's glare grows even more **ruthless** as it eats his hat."],"鉴":["examine","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yen Exchange} where a bar of *gold* sits under a microscope. Bankers in goggles crowd around to **examine** it, sniffing, licking and tapping it. The Juggler tosses it in the air to **examine** it better, and it lands in a banker's soup."],"曰":["say","The {Yogi} balances on the {Rooftop} of the {Ice Rink} on a wobbly *plank*, a huge *mouth* painted on her belly. Every time she wobbles, the mouth opens to **say** something wise: \"Balance!\" The skaters below stop and wait for what she'll **say** next, and she slides off the roof."],"械":["tool","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave}, where a *sentry* stands under a *tree* hung with hammers, saws and wrenches. Each yeti must pick a **tool** before entering. She grabs a whisk, and the sentry laughs that it's the silliest **tool** ever, until she whips the yetis into fluffy shape."],"咬":["bite","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Tower} with *crossed legs* when a hungry *mouth* floats up beside her. It opens wide and tries to **bite** her toe. She uncrosses her legs, ties them in a knot, and the mouth gets so confused it tries to **bite** itself."],"邻":["neighbour","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} when a *herald* bursts out next door on the *hillside*, trumpeting: \"Your new **neighbour** has arrived!\" The new **neighbour** is a giant tortoise who borrows sugar, then her towel, then the entire swimming pool."],"赤":["red","The {Chef} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and the bees sting his face until he has huge *red cheeks*. He blushes so hard everything turns **red**: the honey, the hive, the bees. They now buzz around like cherries, angry and **red**, and the Chef serves them as tomato soup."],"挤":["squeeze","The {Juggler} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut, where a *trimmed hedge* fills almost the entire room. A *helping hand* pushes him from behind and he has to **squeeze** through the branches. Crabs, tourists and a seal follow, all trying to **squeeze** in, until the hut pops like a cork."],"弯":["bent","The {Wizard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a *bent bow*, pulling the string with all his might. Everything his arrow hits goes **bent**: chimneys, spoons, the weathervane. He shoots the moon by accident, and now there's a **bent** banana in the sky."],"椅":["chair","The {Yogi} sits in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut, where an *oddball* has carved a *tree* trunk into a giant **chair**. It has twelve legs and walks around on its own. The Yogi tries to sit, but the **chair** scuttles off like a crab toward the sea."],"陪":["accompany","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house, followed up the *hillside* by a *spitting mouth* that won't leave him alone. It insists on coming to **accompany** him everywhere, spitting cherry stones at the ducks. He tries to row away, but the mouth hops in the boat to **accompany** him across the lake."],"割":["cut","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} as a *pest*, a giant caterpillar, chews the thatch. She grabs a *standing knife* and starts to **cut** the grass on the roof, chasing the pest in circles. She accidentally **cut** the hut in two and the caterpillar falls asleep in the gap."],"揭":["uncover","The {Juggler} hops onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a giant *question mark* hides under a sheet. A *helping hand* pulls the sheet away to **uncover** it, and underneath sits a yeti in a bow tie. The yeti pulls another sheet to **uncover** a second yeti, then another, like nesting dolls."],"韦":["Wei","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house holding a long *leather strap* with the name **Wei** burned into it. He cracks it like a whip, and the lake splits open. Out rows Grandpa **Wei**, who had lost his strap and is very grateful."],"悟":["realise","The {Wizard} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, where a *standing heart* is listening to a *speaker* blare a riddle. Suddenly the heart stops, eyes wide, and the lightbulb above it flicks on: it finally starts to **realise** the answer! The Wizard is so jealous he jumps in the pool to **realise** something too."],"聪":["clever","The {Tsar} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} palace with a giant *ear* that hears everything. It keeps a *tally* of every secret: three fish, two frogs, one duck in love. The Tsar says, \"How **clever**!\" and the ear hears that too, and adds a tally mark for being **clever**."],"雾":["fog","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} to do one *chore*: mopping. But the *rain* falls, the steam rises, and the pool fills with **fog** so thick the swimmers swim into each other. The Wizard waves his mop, and the **fog** turns into sheep that bleat and drift away."],"锋":["sharp edge","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} lookout and sharpens *gold coins* on the *peak* of a mountain. Each coin gets a deadly **sharp edge**, glinting like a sword. She slices pineapples mid-air, and the monkeys use the coins' **sharp edge** to give each other haircuts."],"梯":["ladder","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut, where her *little brother* has turned a *tree* into a **ladder**. He climbs to the top rung and keeps going, sewing new rungs as he goes, into the clouds. The seagulls use the **ladder** to queue for the sky."],"猫":["cat","The {Magician} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower}, pulling a *prowling dog* out of his hat. It runs through a field of *young crop* and comes out the other side as a **cat**. The dog is furious, but the **cat** purrs, licks its paw, and steals the magician's hat."],"祥":["lucky","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Stadium}, where a woolly *sheep* sits on a *small altar* in the stands. Every fan rubs its fleece for luck, and the home team scores ten goals in a row. \"**Lucky** sheep!\" the crowd chants, and the *sheep* crowd-surfs, feeling very **lucky**."],"阔":["wide","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and flings open a giant *gate*. *Living water* rushes in, spreading out into a huge, **wide** lake. Boxes float like boats and the King sails off on a crate, his arms stretched as **wide** as the horizon."],"誉":["praise","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a surprise *party*, where every statue holds a *speech bubble* of **praise**. \"Wonderful flexibility!\" \"Superb stretching!\" The **praise** gets so loud that the Yogi blushes, ties herself into a knot, and the dinosaurs clap."],"筹":["raise funds","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} selling *longevity peach* tarts on sticks of *bamboo*. He needs to **raise funds** for a new kitchen, so he juggles them while singing. Rowers pay with their oars, and by evening the Chef has managed to **raise funds** for a floating restaurant."],"丛":["cluster","The {Tsar} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} palace with a *follower* behind him, then another, then hundreds more, all carrying a *plank*. They huddle together on each step, planks sprouting leaves, into a dense **cluster** of bushes. The Tsar can't get through the **cluster**, so he crowns it instead."],"牵":["lead","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} with a *big man* on a leash like a puppy. She chants \"This way!\" and he follows: she can **lead** him anywhere. She takes the **lead** and marches him through the bank, and he fetches coins."],"鸣":["chirp","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a little *bird* sits on the referee's bell. It opens its *mouth* to **chirp**, and the round begins. Every punch makes it **chirp** louder, until the boxers start chirping too and forget how to fight."],"沈":["Shen","The {Sheriff} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where *water drops* leak onto a soggy *pillow*. Asleep on it is old Mr **Shen**, snoring through the leak. The Sheriff tries to wake him, but Mr **Shen** just rolls over, sinking like a stone into the puddle."],"阁":["pavilion","The {Gardener} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} into a dusty *loft*, which unfolds like a flower into a grand **pavilion** with curved roofs. Lanterns sway, a pond appears, and the gardener sips tea in the **pavilion** while geese row by."],"穆":["solemn","The {Magician} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} holding a *grain stalk* that gives off a soft *shimmer*. Every swimmer stops splashing and stands still, quiet and **solemn**, as if at church. The Magician bows, the pool goes silver, and even the rubber duck looks **solemn**."],"屈":["bend","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} beside a *crouching man* stuck under a low chimney. She chants \"Lower!\" and he has to **bend** further and further until he's folded like a pretzel. The statues inside try to **bend** too, and the knight's armour squeaks."],"旨":["aim","The {Jockey} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where an *edict scroll* unrolls by itself, announcing the queen bee's **aim**: world honey domination. The bees cheer, and the jockey jumps on a bumblebee, takes **aim**, and gallops off to stop them."],"袖":["sleeve","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} wearing a *shirt* with one enormous **sleeve**. A *sprouting field* grows inside it: carrots, corn and sunflowers poke out the cuff. Backpackers reach into her **sleeve** for snacks, and a sheep is grazing at the elbow."],"猎":["hunt","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} with a *prowling dog* sniffing a trail of *sun-dried meat*. The dog leads them on a **hunt** deep into the cave. They find the yeti, who has been hiding the jerky all along, and the **hunt** becomes a picnic."],"臂":["arm","The {Baker} crashes through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} where a *pioneer* is flexing an enormous **arm** under the *moon*. He bets the Baker he can throw a loaf to the moon. With one swing of his **arm**, the bread flies off, and the moon catches it and takes a bite."],"蛇":["snake","The {Sheriff} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and finds a tiny *bug* riding a huge *serpent* like a horse. The **snake** hisses, the bug cracks a tiny whip, and they gallop around the hut. The Sheriff lassos the **snake**, and the bug asks him for a tiny badge."],"贺":["congratulate","The {Hunter} climbs through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hut}, and everyone throws a *shell* full of confetti at him with a *plus sign* on each. \"We **congratulate** you!\" they shout: he is the first hunter never to catch anything. He bows, they **congratulate** him again, and a rabbit hands him a trophy."],"柱":["pillar","The {Jockey} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and sees a *tree* growing straight up the middle, topped with a giant lit *candle*. It's a **pillar** holding up the whole building. She ties her horse to it, the horse pulls, and the **pillar** wobbles, sending wax onto the swimmers."],"抛":["throw","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} loading cannonballs into a *catapult*. A *helping hand* pulls the lever to **throw** them, but instead it throws the pirate. He soars over the sea, waving, and decides to **throw** his hat back home."],"鼠":["mouse","The {Sheriff} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a tiny **mouse** is grinding cheese in a *mortar*. It squeaks and points a pestle at him like a pistol. The Sheriff raises his hands, and the **mouse** steals his badge and his sandwich."],"瑟":["zither","The {Sailor} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} carrying a long **zither** with *twin jades* for tuning pegs. He plucks it, and a *pinned heart* on the wall starts to throb with sorrow. Every note makes the **zither** sigh like the sea, and the sailor weeps into his beard."],"戈":["halberd","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} waving a *halberd* to fight off a swarm of crows. She swings the **halberd** like a giant hoe, missing every crow but pruning every branch. The crows clap, and she uses the **halberd** to harvest all the apples."],"牢":["prison","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} and finds a *cow* locked under a tiny *roof* with bars. It's in **prison** for eating the king's flowers. The cow moos sadly, and the lifeguard throws it a rubber ring, which it uses to float out of the **prison** down the moat."],"逊":["modest","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Dunes}, where her *grandson* walks down the *road* wearing a crown of gold medals. Everyone praises him, but he blushes and says, \"It's nothing.\" He's so **modest** he hides the medals in the sand. The camels think he's too **modest** and dig them up."],"迈":["stride","The {Magician} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} and a *swarm* of bees chases him onto the *road*. He takes one giant **stride**, then another, crossing the whole island in three steps. The bees try to **stride** too, but they only have tiny legs."],"欺":["bully","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut, where a big bully stuffs smaller kids into a *winnowing basket*. \"Stop it!\" she chants, and she gives him such a huge *yawn* that he falls asleep. The kids climb out, and he never dares **bully** anyone again: who wants to **bully** with a cheerleader around?"],"吨":["ton","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} as a giant *mouth* opens over the army *camp* next door and swallows a whole tank. It weighs a **ton**, then another **ton**, and the roof groans. The dentist pulls out one molar and the whole mountain of metal clatters back onto the camp."],"琴":["zither","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} carrying a long **zither** with *twin jades* at one end and a ticking *clock* at the other. Every hour the clock strikes and the **zither** plays itself, twanging through the inn. Guests dance in their pyjamas, and she does high kicks to the beat."],"衰":["decline","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Wine Cellar} wearing a once-glorious *robe* that frays, fades and falls apart thread by thread. His badge rusts, his hat droops, and the weathervane wilts: everything is in **decline**. He tries to salute, but even his salute is in **decline**, flopping like a wet noodle."],"瓶":["bottle","The {Pirate} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} with a glass **bottle** that slides along *linked rails* and smashes on a *tile*. Out pops a tiny ship! The boxers stop fighting to stare, and the pirate pulls out another **bottle**, then another, until the ring is a fleet."],"恼":["annoyed","The {Ninja} sits in the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where his *standing heart* stomps around because someone stole its slippers. It's so **annoyed** it huffs steam from both ears. The ninja hands back the slippers, but the heart is still **annoyed** because they're on the wrong feet."],"燕":["swallow","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a fireplace full of glowing *embers*. A little **swallow** bursts out of the sparks, swoops around the chandelier, and dives into her hair. She meditates, and a whole flock of **swallow** chicks nests in her bun."],"仲":["middle","The {Jockey} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} and lands on a *standing person* holding a target. Her arrow hits the *bullseye*, exactly in the **middle**. The person cheers, then realises they're also standing in the **middle** of the lagoon and starts to sink."],"诱":["lure","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, where a *small speech bubble* whispers \"Come here...\" from behind a pink *blossom*. The sweet smell is a trap to **lure** her into a canoe. She floats away, and the blossom winks and moves on to **lure** the ducks."],"狼":["wolf","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} as a *prowling dog* sniffs a *good meal* on a pilot's tray. It howls, and its fur grows grey and shaggy: a **wolf**! The pilots flee, and the **wolf** climbs into the cockpit and takes off, howling at the moon."],"池":["pond","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} carrying a bucket of *water drops*, and pours it into a tiny **pond** for the bees. A *scorpion* rows a leaf boat across the **pond**, offering rides. The bees line up, and the chef serves honey lemonade from the shore."],"疼":["hurt","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} lodge to a *sickbed*, where a shivering monkey wears a *winter coat* four sizes too big. Its tummy is sore and it wails, \"It **hurts**!\" The Tailor stitches the coat smaller, and now nothing will **hurt** anymore; the monkey tries cartwheels."],"卢":["Lu","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a giant *black pot* bubbling at the top. Grandma **Lu** sits in it like a bathtub, scrubbing her back with a ladle. \"I'm **Lu**, and this is my pool now!\" she shouts, splashing everyone."],"仗":["battle","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} into a **battle** between a *standing person* armed with a *walking staff* and a squadron of paper aeroplanes. She charges on her horse, swinging the staff like a sword, and wins the **battle** as the planes surrender with tiny white flags."],"冠":["champion","The {Gardener} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond} with a *cloth cover* draped over her head. The swans whip it off for the *crowning*, placing a golden crown of flowers on her head. She is the **champion** gardener of the year, and every swan honks, \"**Champion**!\""],"粒":["grain","The {Lifeguard} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} and climbs a *podium* to award a prize to a single **grain** of *rice*. It won a race against the sand! Every other **grain** on the beach rises up and jealously chases the rice into the sea."],"遥":["distant","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} as a giant *claw* reaches down from somewhere far, far away. She stretches toward it, but it's so **distant** she has to grow her arms a mile long. When she finally touches it, the claw waves goodbye and flies off to a more **distant** star."],"吕":["Lü","The {Lifeguard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Museum} where a dinosaur *spine* lies on display. A label reads: discovered by Professor **Lü**. The spine starts dancing, and the professor's ghost, Mr **Lü**, appears with a whistle to blow on the clattering bones."],"玄":["mysterious","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} following a *dark thread* through the gloom. It leads to a coin that glows and has no face, deeply **mysterious**. She spins it, and it whispers riddles. The **mysterious** coin floats off, trailing the thread behind it."],"尘":["dust","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} with *crumbs* and *soil* blowing off his apron in a whirlwind of **dust**. The carousel coughs, the Ferris wheel sneezes, and every candyfloss turns grey. The chef bakes it all into a **dust** cake and sells it to vacuum cleaners."],"冯":["Feng","The {Firefighter} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} on a *horse* covered in *icicles*. The rider beside her introduces himself as Captain **Feng**, the coolest horseman in the jungle. Captain **Feng** cracks the icicles off and sells them as ice lollies to monkeys."],"抚":["comfort","The {Firefighter} descends to the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a *vanishing man* is crying because he keeps disappearing. A gentle *helping hand* pats his head to **comfort** him. Each pat makes him reappear a little more, and soon the hand can **comfort** him back to full visibility."],"浅":["shallow","The {Cheerleader} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} where *water drops* fill a tiny pool. *Twin blades* slice the water in half, then quarters, until it's so **shallow** the coins can't sink. She cartwheels across the **shallow** water without getting her ankles wet."],"敦":["honest","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino}, where a grandpa with a *cane* refuses to cheat at cards. Instead, he gives back everyone's chips and invites them to a *feast*. He's so **honest** that even the slot machines pay out. The dentist checks his teeth: perfectly **honest** gums."],"纠":["correct","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel}, where a *silk thread* is caught in a *twisted vine*. He tugs it straight, untangles it, and goes on to **correct** every crooked thing: the antenna, the chimney, a backpacker's hair. He even tries to **correct** the moon's lopsided face."],"钻":["drill","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} when a *fortune teller* rises up with an electric **drill** made of *gold coins*. She predicts treasure, then starts to **drill** a hole in the roof. Water gushes, and the swans dive in looking for jewels."],"晶":["crystal","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} juggling a *sun*, another *sun*, and a third *sun*. They melt together into one giant, glittering **crystal**. The boxers below are dazzled, and they spar using the **crystal** as a disco ball."],"岂":["how could","The {Cheerleader} sits in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut blowing a *triumph horn* in disbelief: \"**How could** we lose to the crabs?\" The crabs blow their own horn back. \"**How could** you lose?\" they jeer, and she leads a comeback chant until the sand trembles."],"峡":["gorge","The {Shepherd} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Piazza} clock tower, where a giant *mountain* splits in two, held apart by a pair of *tongs*. Between them opens a deep **gorge**. Her sheep leap across on a rope bridge, and one tumbles into the **gorge**, bouncing off a fountain."],"苍":["dark green","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, where *grass* grows so thick it buries a *barn*. Everything turns **dark green**: the planes, the runway, the Tsar's beard. He tries to stomp it flat, but the grass only grows more **dark green** and covers his crown too."],"喷":["spray","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} with a *mouth* full of soda, next to a giant *fountain*. He sneezes and starts to **spray** fizzy drink over every ride. The fountain joins in to **spray** back, and the carousel horses get a sticky shower."],"耗":["consume","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Tower} dragging a *plough* through a field of *fur*. A giant caterpillar munches the fur faster than he ploughs. It will **consume** everything: carpets, wigs, the hunter's eyebrows, and keeps on to **consume** his whole coat."],"凌":["soar","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} on a *hill climb* of *icicles*. At the top, she leaps off and begins to **soar**, arms out like wings, over the cheering crowd. The boxers try to **soar** too but only manage to wobble on the ropes."],"敲":["knock","The {Cheerleader} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} on a tiny *tower*, holding a *tall cane*. She leans over and starts to **knock** on every window: knock, knock, knock! The cats knock back with their paws, and soon the whole café is a drum circle of cats who **knock** in rhythm."],"菌":["bacteria","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} storehouse, where *grass* grows out of a mouldy *granary*. Tiny germs with top hats march out: **bacteria**! They multiply as he juggles them, and the **bacteria** form a conga line across the desert."],"赔":["compensate","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house after breaking a vase. A *spitting mouth* yells, \"You must **compensate** me!\" He pays with a *shell*, but the mouth spits it out and wants more. He must **compensate** with every shell he owns, then his parrot."],"涂":["smear","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} carrying a plate of *leftovers* and a bucket of *water drops*. She starts to **smear** the leftovers onto the walls like paint: spaghetti murals, jam sunsets. The lifeguard is horrified, but the swimmers love it and **smear** cake on the diving board."],"粹":["pure","The {Tsar} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a chess *pawn* sorts *rice* grain by grain. It throws out every dusty one until only **pure** white grains remain. The Tsar is impressed: such **pure** rice, it glows like snow."],"扁":["flat","The {Baker} rolls out dough in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} and accidentally squashes a *nameboard* under his rolling pin. Now it's completely **flat**, and so are the coins, the chairs and the banker's hat. Everything in the bank is **flat** as a pancake."],"亏":["lose money","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} holding a *leaky pot* full of gold coins. Every coin drips out the bottom and rolls down the drain, so he begins to **lose money** every second. He patches it with his crown, but still he continues to **lose money**, and now he's crownless."],"寂":["silent","The {Juggler} pops up through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where an *uncle* sits under a *roof* of palm leaves, totally **silent**. No waves, no gulls; even the sea holds its breath. The juggler drops a ball, and the clatter echoes for miles. The uncle glares, and the beach goes **silent** again."],"煤":["coal","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house to a *campfire* that's burning lumps of **coal** shaped like a *plum*. He pulls a plum from his hat, and it turns black too. Soon the whole lake is full of floating **coal** plums, puffing black smoke."],"熊":["bear","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Youth Club}, where a giant *bear* warms its paws by glowing *embers*. It's teaching the kids table tennis. The **bear** smashes the ball through the window, and the shepherd hides her sheep, but the **bear** just hugs them all."],"恭":["respectful","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} temple with *joined hands*, bowing to a *heart cushion* on a throne. She's so **respectful** she bows a hundred times. The fish bow too, ducks bow, everyone is **respectful**, until the cushion blushes and bows back."],"湿":["wet","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} to inspect a glass *showcase* of honey, when *water drops* pour down. He's soaked, his badge is **wet**, his moustache is **wet**, and the bees put on tiny raincoats and laugh at him."],"循":["follow","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Dunes} watchtower, holding a *shield* over her head against the sun. She spots a trail of *footsteps* in the sand and decides to **follow** them. They lead in a circle, back to her own feet. Her sheep **follow** her round and round."],"暖":["warm","The {Ninja} crouches in the cold {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} lodge, shivering. A *rescue rope* drops from the *sun*, and he climbs up into its golden glow. Everything becomes cosy and **warm**: his toes, his sword, his tea. He stays so long that he's now permanently **warm**."],"糖":["sugar","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and stitches a sack of *rice* together with a sack of *sugar*. The sack explodes over the runway in sweet white snow. Planes skid on the **sugar**, pilots lick the wings, and the tailor fills a jet with **sugar** to make cotton candy clouds."],"赋":["endow","The {Firefighter} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, where a *warrior* stands on a giant *shell*. He touches her hose and blesses it to **endow** it with magic: now it sprays rainbows. He goes on to **endow** her helmet, her boots and the pool float with superpowers."],"抑":["restrain","The {Yogi} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where a sunbather with an *upward gaze* desperately wants to sneeze. A *helping hand* covers his nose to **restrain** him. He twitches, he wiggles, he turns purple, and the hand strains to **restrain** him until the sneeze explodes and blows the beach away."],"秩":["order","The {Jockey} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive}, where bees line up in perfect **order** along a *grain stalk*. A *lost arrow* zips in and knocks them over. She blows a whistle, the bees buzz back into perfect **order**, and the queen salutes."],"帽":["hat","The {Magician} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} wearing a *towel* folded into a *brimmed hat*. He pulls a rabbit out of it, then a second **hat**, then another. Soon every guard wears a towel **hat**, and the tower looks like a spa."],"哀":["grief","The {Ghost} floats onto the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse wrapped in a tattered *robe*, its *mouth* open in an endless wail of **grief**. Its tears fall like rain, flooding the beach. The seagulls weep too, the crabs sniffle, and the whole island sinks under a tide of **grief** until someone offers the ghost a biscuit."],"宿":["stay overnight","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a floating *inn* made of lilos. The innkeeper hands him a snorkel and a key: he must **stay overnight** underwater. He sleeps on the bottom, bubbles snoring, and the fish ask to **stay overnight** too."],"踏":["tread","The {Tailor} slips through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and lands on a *stack of papers*. Her *kicking foot* starts to **tread** on them like grapes, squish, squish, and the papers turn into a paper-mache bathrobe. Every guest wants one, so they all **tread** papers in the mud bath."],"烂":["rotten","The {Lifeguard} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} where an *orchid* sits too close to a *campfire*. It wilts, browns, and goes completely **rotten**, oozing a smell like old socks. The butler faints. The lifeguard throws the **rotten** orchid out the window, and it lands on the gardener."],"袁":["Yuan","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint} in a *long robe* that trails fifty steps behind her. Every coin it touches gets stamped with the name **Yuan**. By the top, the whole mint is printing **Yuan** coins, and the robe is wearing a crown."],"侯":["marquis","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} and bows to a pompous *marquis* in a powdered wig. The **marquis** demands to be rowed across the lake in a golden canoe. The hunter rows, the **marquis** falls in, and his wig floats away like a fluffy duck."],"抖":["shake","The {Dentist} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} with a *dipper* full of fish. A *helping hand* starts to **shake** it, and fish fly everywhere. The dentist begins to **shake** too, then the boats, then the whole boathouse, as if it's dancing."],"夹":["clip","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} cafe juggling with giant *tongs*. He uses them to **clip** pigeons' feathers, then the waiters' ties, then the mayor's nose. The mayor sneezes so hard the tongs **clip** the juggler's pants instead."],"昆":["elder brother","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} next to a tiny *insect* in a tuxedo. \"This is my **elder brother**,\" he announces. The insect bows, places a bet, and wins the whole casino. The King hugs his **elder brother**, who is now the richest bug in the world."],"肝":["liver","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, hanging a giant **liver** on a *drying rack* under the *moon*. It wobbles like jelly in the night breeze. The cook climbs up with an onion, and the gardener guards her **liver** with a rake until dawn."],"擦":["wipe","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa}, where a *detective* searches for fingerprints. A *helping hand* follows behind to **wipe** them away with a fluffy towel. The detective finds nothing, so he decides to **wipe** the Tsar's moustache for evidence."],"猪":["pig","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} house riding a *prowling dog* in a race against a *busy man* on a **pig**. The **pig** wins by a snout, slides off the roof, and belly-flops into the pool. Everyone cheers, and the busy man misses his meeting."],"炼":["refine","The {Lifeguard} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a roaring *campfire* where bankers melt down old coins. They **refine** them until only shiny gold remains. The lifeguard throws in her whistle to **refine** it, and it comes out a golden trumpet."],"恒":["constant","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} lookout and finds a *standing heart* watching the *horizon*. Day and night it stands there, never blinking, never moving: **constant**. Monkeys throw bananas, storms blow, and the heart keeps on, **constant** as the sunrise."],"慎":["careful","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and finds a *standing heart* walking a tightrope with a *magnifying glass*. It checks every step, slow and **careful**, inspecting each wobble. The sheriff follows, equally **careful**, but sneezes and they both land on a trampoline."],"搬":["move","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a *boatman* and a giant *helping hand*. They need to **move** the whole house to the seaside. The hand lifts it, the boatman rows it like a raft, and they **move** it to the beach."],"纽":["button","The {Ninja} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel}, where a *clown* sews a giant **button** onto a jacket using *silk thread*. The clown honks, the **button** pops off and bounces around like a ball, and the ninja chases it down the corridors."],"纹":["pattern","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and spots a man with a *tattoo* of swirls weaving *silk thread* through it. The **pattern** starts to move, swirling over the carousel and the dodgems. Everything in the funfair is covered in the same **pattern**."],"玻":["glass","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} as a *king* wraps himself in a crocodile *hide* and dives through the skylight. Crash! **Glass** rains down, and the soldiers dodge. The baker sweeps up the **glass** and bakes it into sparkling sugar cookies."],"渔":["fishing","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} holding a fishing rod, casting it into a tank of *water drops*. A giant *fish* bites, pulling her up the stairs. She's **fishing** in the dinosaur hall, and the museum guards join, **fishing** from every balcony."],"磁":["magnetic","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} holding a *stone* that is actually a *magnet*. Every metal thing in the hive leaps toward it: helmets, hairpins, bee armour. The pull is so **magnetic** the bees stick to his crown, and he becomes a **magnetic** king."],"铜":["copper","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hotel holding a *matching cup* made of *gold coins*. When she pours water in, it turns orange-brown: pure **copper**. She sews **copper** buttons for every guest, and the fish swim around with shiny pennies."],"齿":["tooth","The {Chef} digs into the {Basement} of the {Beehive}, where a set of giant *teeth* chomps on honeycomb. Each **tooth** is as big as a door. The chef polishes them with a broom, but one **tooth** is loose, and it falls out, clanging like a bell."],"跨":["stride across","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Water Park}, where a *show-off* lifts his *kicking foot* to **stride across** the wave pool in one step. The King tries too, but his crown falls in. The show-off strides back, catches it, and they **stride across** every pool together."],"押":["pawn","The {Yogi} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} handing a suit of *armour* to a pawnbroker. A *helping hand* weighs it, and she leaves it to **pawn** for a bath ticket. Next day she wants it back, but the pawnbroker has turned the armour into a sauna. So she tries to **pawn** her yoga mat."],"怖":["terror","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, where a *standing heart* shivers beneath a floating sheet of *linen* that looks like a ghost. **Terror**! The heart screams, the swimmers scream, and the baker throws a baguette. The linen falls, revealing a duck, and the **terror** dissolves in giggles."],"漠":["desert","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort}, and all the *water drops* in the moat evaporate in the red *sunset*. The fort becomes a vast **desert**, sand everywhere. He pulls a camel from his hat, rides off into the **desert**, and the soldiers follow in flip-flops."],"疲":["weary","The {Pirate} trudges up the {Staircase} of the {Beach} hut dragging an animal *hide* and collapses onto a *sickbed*. He's so **weary** he can't lift his eyepatch. His parrot snores, his peg leg dozes, and even the waves feel **weary** and stop crashing."],"叛":["rebel","The {Pirate} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} with *half* his crew. The other *half* has turned **rebel**, waving flags and throwing jam. A *rebel* with an eyepatch climbs the chandelier and declares himself captain. The pirate swings on a curtain and joins the **rebel** side."],"遣":["dispatch","The {Cheerleader} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *dispatch rider* on a motorbike waits. She shouts, \"Go, go, go!\" to **dispatch** him with a sack of coins. He zooms off, and she must **dispatch** fifty more riders."],"兹":["this","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} holding a *magnet* toward a buzzing bee. \"**This** one!\" she says, and the bee flies onto it. Then she points again: \"**This** one!\" Soon the magnet is covered in bees wearing tiny metal helmets."],"祭":["offer sacrifice","The {Juggler} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where villagers prepare a *sacrifice* to the sea: a giant cake on a raft. They chant to **offer sacrifice** to the waves. The juggler adds a balloon, and the sea burps politely as they **offer sacrifice** again: a pineapple."],"醉":["drunk","The {Zookeeper} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *pawn* chess piece sips from a *wine jug*. It's totally **drunk**, hiccuping and wobbling across the chairs. The zookeeper tries to catch it, but now the patients are **drunk** too, singing loudly."],"拳":["fist","The {Cheerleader} bounds up the {Staircase} of the {Mint} with *rolling hands*, spinning her pom-poms. She clenches her *hand* into a giant **fist**, punches a coin press, and coins fly out like confetti. Every worker raises a **fist** in triumph."],"弥":["fill","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} villa, plucking a *bow* that rings a giant *wind chime*. The sound swells and starts to **fill** the air, the sea, the sand, until every shell rings too. The Magician tries to **fill** his hat, but it overflows with music."],"斜":["slanting","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a yeti eats *leftovers* from a tilted *dipper*. Everything in the cave is **slanting**: the stairs, the walls, the yeti's hat. The shepherd's sheep slide down the **slanting** floor like a slide."],"档":["files","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hangar}, where a *tree* grows through a *roadblock* of cabinets. Every branch holds **files** of patients' teeth. She grabs one, and a gust from a jet engine sends **files** flying like paper planes."],"稀":["rare","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut, holding a single *grain stalk* wrapped in *lace*. It's so **rare**, only one in the world grows here. Collectors crowd the beach, bidding millions, and the **rare** stalk sneezes and flies away."],"捷":["quick","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a *sprinter* in shorts races past. A *helping hand* tries to grab him, but he's too **quick**. The yetis try to catch him, but he's quicker still, zooming like a **quick** bunny."],"肤":["skin","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} house, where a *husband* sunbathes under the *moon* until his **skin** glows silver. She sprays him with sunscreen, but his **skin** keeps glowing, so she uses him as a night light for the pool."],"疫":["epidemic","The {Yogi} pops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach}, where every sandcastle is on a *sickbed* sneezing sand. An **epidemic** of sneezes! A crab doctor waves a *war club* at the germs. The Yogi breathes deeply, and the **epidemic** stops in one sigh."],"肿":["swell","The {Jockey} sits in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} villa when a bee stings her knee, right in the *bullseye*. It starts to **swell** up like a *moon*, bigger and rounder. Her horse laughs so hard its nose begins to **swell** too."],"豆":["bean","The {Dentist} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and finds a single *bean* that grows into a giant **bean** stalk. Rowers climb it, boats hang from it, and the dentist checks its teeth at the top: one magic **bean** tooth."],"削":["peel","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} with a *standing knife* in front of a *portrait*. She begins to **peel** the portrait like an apple, curls of paint falling on the cats. Under each layer is another face. She keeps going to **peel** until she reaches a cat.","xiāo"],"岗":["post","The {Gardener} sinks into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} and digs a *mountain* with a *ridge* on top. A guard climbs it to stand at his **post**, saluting planes. The gardener plants flowers around the **post**, and soon it is a guard tower of roses."],"晃":["sway","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swamp}, where the *sun* hangs on a string and swings, casting flickering *light*. Everything begins to **sway**: trees, frogs, the hunter's boots. He tries to stand still, but the swamp keeps him swinging, so he lets himself **sway** like a lily.","huàng"],"吞":["swallow","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} when a giant *mouth* opens in the *sky* and starts to **swallow** everything: dice, cards, the croupier's toupee. She stitches its lips together, but it bursts open to **swallow** the roulette wheel too."],"宏":["grand","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} palace, where a giant *roof* is held up by a single massive *upper arm*. Everything is huge and **grand**: chandeliers like moons, a bathtub like an ocean. The Hunter waves from a **grand** balcony."],"癌":["cancer","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Island} hospital to a *sickbed* weighed down with heavy *boulders*. The doctor explains it's a lump of **cancer**, like rocks pressing on the patient. The ghost helps the nurses roll the boulders away, one by one, until the **cancer** is gone and the patient sits up smiling."],"肚":["belly","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool}, where a swimmer with a big round **belly** floats like a *moon*. Kids pile *soil* on it to build a sandcastle. It grows taller, and the swimmer's **belly** laughs, shaking it all into the water."],"隶":["servant","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and finds a tiny *servant* polishing every seashell on the sand. She blows her whistle, and now the *servant* fans her, brings lemonade and carries her towel. By sunset the Lifeguard has six of them and is too lazy to swim: being the **servant** of your own **servant** is hard work."],"履":["fulfil","The {Lifeguard} tiptoes into the {Basement} of the {Museum}, where a *lying man* on a display plinth suddenly sits up. He swore to polish every exhibit tonight, so he slides *back and forth* on his socks, buffing dinosaur bones. At dawn he flops back down, promise **fulfilled**. The Lifeguard claps: a man who will **fulfil** his word even while lying down."],"涨":["to rise","The {Jockey} rides his horse down into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} as *water drops* plink from the ceiling. The puddle swells, the river **rises**, and he aims a *stretched bow* straight up and fires himself to safety. The flood keeps **rising** after him, lifting planes off the floor like rubber ducks."],"耀":["brilliant","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} when a *pheasant* lands on her head, swallowing a beam of *light*. It glows so **brilliant** that ships at sea steer by it and moths form a queue. The Yogi opens one eye, sighs, and puts on sunglasses: enlightenment was never meant to be this **brilliant**."],"扭":["to twist","The {Ninja} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel} and meets a *clown* blocking the stairs. A *helping hand* shoots out of the wall and **twists** the clown into a balloon animal, nose honking. Then it **twists** the Ninja too, so she leaves in a knot, still trying to look mysterious."],"坛":["altar","The {Tailor} stitches a tablecloth on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, but a heap of *soil* keeps piling up step by step. Out of the heap rises a raised **altar**, and a fluffy *cloud* settles on top to be worshipped. The Tailor drapes his cloth over the **altar** and kneels, a little confused, in front of the weather."],"拨":["dial","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} reaches for an old rotary telephone. A giant *helping hand* grabs the **dial** and spins it so fast that the whole *launch pad* beneath the fort ignites. Every time the Baker **dials** a number, a doughnut rockets into the sky."],"沃":["fertile","The {Wizard} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} into muddy *water drops* where a *dancer* is twirling barefoot. Wherever her toes splash, the soil turns **fertile**: tomatoes pop up, pumpkins swell, sunflowers smack the Wizard in the face. Soon the dungeon is the most **fertile** vegetable patch in the kingdom."],"绘":["to draw","The {Hunter} bursts up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *meeting* of bored patients is stuck. He hands each a strand of *silk thread*, and they start **drawing** pictures in the air with it: a horse, a rocket, the receptionist's angry face. Before the doctor calls anyone, the whole wall is covered in thread **drawings**."],"伐":["to cut down","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and finds a *lumberjack* in a bathrobe, swinging an axe at a potted palm. TIMBER! He **cuts down** the palm, the bamboo screens and the coat stand. The Firefighter sprays him with a hose, but he keeps on **cutting down** towels like trees."],"堪":["to endure","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} holding an *overflowing bowl* of hot soup that keeps spilling onto his crown. Courtiers shovel *soil* onto his feet so he cannot run. He must **endure** it: the heat, the drips, the itchy dirt. He grits his teeth and announces that a true king can **endure** anything, except perhaps more soup."],"仆":["servant","The {Pirate} stomps up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a *standing person* holding a *fortune stick* like a tray. 'Your fortune, sir, says I am your **servant**.' The Pirate hands over his parrot, his boots and his wet socks. The **servant** carries them all, bowing on every step, without dropping the fortune stick."],"郭":["Guo","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} building a *city wall* out of flowerpots. On each pot she paints the surname **Guo**, until the whole town reads like a family name tag. A passing pigeon is renamed Mr **Guo** and stamped with it too."],"牺":["sacrifice","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut faces a hungry storm god. To save his flock he offers up his *cow*, which walks forward wearing a *bird nest* as a crown. It is a great **sacrifice**. The god sniffs the cow, takes only the bird nest, and the Shepherd weeps anyway at his noble **sacrifice**."],"歼":["to annihilate","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} is attacked by a *skeleton* leading a *thousand ants*, all carrying coins. She juggles faster and faster, bowling pins flying, until every last ant is flicked into the sea and the skeleton falls apart. Enemies **annihilated**. She bows: total **annihilation**, and not a single coin dropped."],"墓":["tomb","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a dark *soil* pit under a red *sunset*. He waves his wand and up rises a stone **tomb** with his own name carved on it. Furious, he pulls a rabbit from the **tomb**, then a dove, then his own hat, insisting he is not dead yet."],"雇":["to hire","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands beside a *door* where a *sparrow* sits with a little CV in its beak. She **hires** it on the spot to guard the door. By noon she has **hired** forty sparrows, each with a tiny badge, all asking for lunch breaks."],"廉":["honest","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and finds a farmer in a *shed* who is offered a bribe for *two sheaves* of wheat. He pushes the bags of coins away and charges one coin, the fair price. Everyone gasps: an **honest** man in a money exchange! The Lifeguard hangs a medal on him that says **HONEST**."],"契":["contract","The {Cheerleader} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut, where a *big man* is *carving* words into a surfboard with a pocketknife. It is a **contract**: whoever sits on the board must cheer for him forever. She signs it with a pom-pom, and the **contract** grows legs and runs into the sea."],"拼":["to piece together","The {Pirate} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} finds his treasure map torn into a hundred bits. A *helping hand* lays down *linked rails*, and a toy train carries the scraps along while he **pieces** them **together**. The map is **pieced together** at last, but it only shows the way to the Inn's kitchen."],"惩":["to punish","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} catches a monkey stealing bananas. A drumbeat starts and a *march* of soldier ants parades up the steps, each holding a tiny *heart* sign. To **punish** the thief, they make him march with them all day. That is how the jungle **punishes**: with endless, cheerful parades."],"捉":["to grab","The {Jockey} sprints across the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} after a runaway sausage. A *helping hand* shoots out of a chimney and **grabs** his *foot* instead. He topples, reaches out wildly, and **grabs** the sausage just before it leaps off the edge."],"覆":["to cover","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, and the water is on fire. She drags a huge *cabinet* *back and forth* across the surface until its doors swing open and **cover** the flames like a lid. Steam hisses. The pool is **covered** so well that the ducks now walk on the cabinet."],"刷":["to brush","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} holds a *dustcloth* in one hand and a *standing knife* in the other. He **brushes** off the slides so hard they squeak, then **brushes** his moustache with the knife's bristly handle. Kids slide down shining like greased penguins."],"劫":["to rob","The {Juggler} on the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} spots a burglar with a *strong arm* sneaking toward the *exit* sign, stuffing yeti fur into a sack. 'Stop! You can't **rob** a yeti!' The yeti wakes, and the **robber** ends up juggled up and down the stairs along with her pins."],"嫌":["to dislike","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and offers a *woman* *two sheaves* of hay as payment. She holds her nose: she **dislikes** hay, **dislikes** sheep, and especially dislikes shepherds who smell of them. She flicks the hay back down the stairs one straw at a time."],"瓜":["melon","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} plants one seed, and a giant **melon** bursts out of the slide. It rolls down the tube, scattering swimmers, and splashes into the wave pool. Now everyone floats on slices of *melon*, and the lifeguards sell **melon** juice by the bucket."],"歇":["to rest","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} has walked the flock up the mountain all day. A huge *question mark* bends over him like a deckchair, and he lets out an enormous *yawn* that echoes off the ice. 'Time to **rest**?' He curls into the question mark and **rests**, while the sheep snore around him."],"雕":["to carve","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} uses her drill to **carve** a statue out of a block of cheese. A *sparrow* pecks the wires of an electric *circuit* to power the drill. Sparks fly, and she **carves** a perfect cat that immediately meows for milk."],"闷":["bored","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and is locked behind a giant *gate*. Nothing happens. No rides, no music, just his *heart* ticking slowly. He is so **bored** he pulls out one rabbit, then sends it back. Even the rabbit looks **bored**."],"乳":["milk","The {Robot} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} finds a fluffy *hatchling* zooming around on a tiny *ski*, crying for food. It opens a hatch in its chest and pours out a jet of warm **milk**. The hatchling skis through puddles of **milk** and burps happily."],"串":["string together","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond} holding a giant skewer. Splash! He **strings together** a fish, a lily pad, a frog and a confused swan into one long *kebab*. The swan honks to be let off, and the Chef **strings** on two more for balance."],"娃":["baby","The {Wizard} on the {Staircase} of the {Spa} hands a *woman* in a mud mask a glowing *jade tablet*. Poof! It turns into a gurgling **baby** wrapped in a fluffy spa towel. The **baby** grabs the Wizard's beard and won't let go, laughing every time he squeaks."],"缴":["to hand in","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} has to **hand in** her homework, but it is tangled in *silk thread* and full of *sparkle* glitter. She juggles it up the stairs and **hands** it **in** to the teacher, a fat tabby cat who sneezes glitter everywhere."],"唤":["to call","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond} with a huge *mouth* painted on his megaphone. He **calls** the swans for a *makeover*: lipstick, wigs, feather boas. Each time he **calls**, another swan glides in, fluffing itself up like a movie star."],"赢":["to win","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} in a headstand. The prize, a *winner's purse* stuffed with a golden *shell*, hangs from the ropes. Her opponent tires out just watching her balance. She **wins** without throwing a punch, and the crowd chants '**Win**! **Win**!' as she bows upside down."],"莲":["lotus","The {Lifeguard} on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} watches a *convoy* of tiny trucks drive up the steps, each loaded with pond *grass*. At the top they dump it all into a bucket, and a pink **lotus** blooms with a pop. Customers swap their coins for **lotus** petals instead."],"霸":["tyrant","The {Baker} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, slips on wet tiles, and lands on a *saddle* strapped to a bad-tempered **tyrant**. It is raining indoors, buckets of *rain* that the **tyrant** commands to fall on anyone who dares relax. The Baker rides him around the spa yelling until the clouds give up."],"桃":["peach","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} finds a *tree* growing straight out of the steps. Its fruit falls and lands on its *cracked shell*, splitting open to reveal a juicy **peach**. She sews every **peach** a tiny coat to stop them bruising."],"妥":["suitable","The {Tailor} in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} has a mountain of stock that won't fit anywhere. A *soothing hand* pats him on the head, then rearranges every box until they fit perfectly. 'There. Is that **suitable**?' It is perfectly **suitable**. The hand pats him again, and he purrs."],"瘦":["thin","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} onto a creaking *sickbed* where an *elder* lies. The old man is so **thin** he slips through the gaps in the slats and floats up like a kite. The Sheriff ties him to a fishing rod so the **thin** fellow doesn't blow away."],"搭":["to put up","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} wants shade for her patients. A *helping hand* ties bundles of *thatch* together and starts to **put up** a hut, while she holds the poles with dental floss. The hut is **put up** in seconds, and everyone opens wide for a check-up in the shade."],"赴":["to go to","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} as a *runner* sprints past waving a *fortune stick*. 'It says you must **go to** the party at once!' The Firefighter swims after him in full gear, sirens wailing, as they **go to** the far end of the pool where a cake waits."],"岳":["high mountain","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink}, and the ice cracks. Up shoots a *hillock*, then on top of it a *mountain*, then another, stacking into one **high mountain** that pokes the clouds. She does her poses on the summit while skaters spiral up the **high mountain** like a helter-skelter."],"嘉":["excellent","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} juggles books while a stern *scholar* grades her with a red pen. She throws seven, then nine, then the scholar's spectacles too. He writes '**Excellent**!' on her forehead and faints. The crowd agrees: **excellent**."],"舱":["cabin","The {Tsar} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} orders a *boat* hauled up for a voyage among the clouds. Inside its hull he builds a cosy *barn* full of hay as his royal **cabin**. Chickens peck around his throne. He insists it is the finest **cabin** in any airship."],"俊":["handsome","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes}, and every *standing person* in the sand turns into a *handsome man* with perfect hair. She juggles mirrors so they can admire how **handsome** they are. The sand gets in their teeth, but they stay **handsome** anyway."],"址":["site","The {Jockey} gallops into the {Basement} of the {Beehive} and piles up *soil* in a corner. He plants a red *stop sign* on top: 'This is the **site** of my new stable.' The bees buzz angrily at the building **site**, and the horse eats the stop sign."],"庞":["huge","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and finds an enormous *dragon* crammed into a garden *shed*. It is so **huge** that its tail pokes out of the window and its nose out of the chimney. The Pirate tries to steal its gold, but the **huge** beast sneezes him back down the stairs."],"耕":["to plough","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} tree house drags a *plough* round and round an old stone *well*. Clods of earth fly up as she **ploughs** a perfect circle, and parrots plant seeds behind her. Monkeys line up to **plough** too, pulling her along like a pony."],"锐":["sharp","The {Robot} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *money changer* sits filing *gold coins* on a whetstone. Each coin comes out razor **sharp**, and he flings them like throwing stars. One slices the Robot's antenna clean off. 'Too **sharp**!' it beeps, as magazines flutter to the floor in neat ribbons."],"缝":["seam","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} and has a *chance meeting* with a gorilla whose trousers have split. She pulls out a reel of *silk thread* and stitches the **seam** shut, right there on a branch. The gorilla checks the **seam**, nods, and swings away, perfectly decent again."],"悔":["to regret","The {Hunter} sits in the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room} next to a *busy mother* juggling five toddlers. He promised to help and didn't. Now his *standing heart* droops like a wilted flower and sighs loudly. He **regrets** it so much that he sobs into his hat. 'I **regret** everything,' he moans, as a toddler steals his boots."],"邀":["to invite","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} rolls out a long *road* of red carpet down the side of the building. *Sparkle* flies from her fingers, spelling out letters in the air: 'You are **invited**!' Pigeons, clouds and a passing balloon all accept. She **invites** the moon too, which arrives late."],"玲":["ting-a-ling","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a tiny *king* rings a bell before each round: **ting-a-ling**! A *herald* in tights shouts the name of each fighter. The king gets so excited that he rings and rings, **ting-a-ling**, until the boxers are dancing instead of punching."],"惟":["only","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house holding a *standing heart* in a jar. A single *sparrow* lands on it and sings. The Wizard has cast spells on thousands of birds, but this is the **only** one he loves. He feeds it his **only** biscuit and declares it the one and **only** queen of the lake."],"斥":["to blame","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} waving a *chipped axe*. 'Who broke my axe?' he roars, and starts to **blame** the bees one by one, pointing the jagged blade at each. The bees **blame** the queen, the queen **blames** the honey, and the honey just drips silently."],"宅":["residence","The {Jockey} rides up the {Staircase} of the {Island} lighthouse and finds a tiny *dwelling* tucked under each step. He knocks: crabs live in one, turtles in another, a grumpy seagull in a third. He hammers up a grand sign: 'Private **Residence**'. Now every step is someone's **residence**, and his horse needs permission to climb."],"添":["to add","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} is pouring *water drops* into a teapot when a *blushing* customer asks for more tea. She **adds** a drop. And another. She keeps **adding** until the teapot overflows, coins float away, and the blushing customer turns even redder."],"挖":["to dig","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} hears there is treasure below. A *helping hand* grabs a magic *shovel* and starts to **dig** straight through the roof tiles. It **digs** through the sauna, the massage room and the hot tub, until steam shoots up like a geyser and the treasure turns out to be a rubber duck."],"呵":["to breathe out","The {Hunter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} is freezing. He opens his *mouth* wide and **breathes out** a huge cloud of warm fog, and his *nodding head* bobs with every puff. Each time he **breathes out**, the snow on the roof melts into a little puddle."],"讼":["lawsuit","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} into a *town square* full of fish in wigs. A *small speech bubble* floats from his lips saying 'Not my fault!' He is being sued: a **lawsuit** for splashing. The crab judge bangs her claw, and the **lawsuit** drags on until high tide."],"氧":["oxygen","The {Yogi} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} holds her breath too long and turns blue. A fluffy *sheep* trots in, puffing *steam* out of its nose like a little kettle. It is pure **oxygen**. She breathes it in and floats up, while the sheep pumps out more **oxygen** for the airplanes."],"浩":["vast","The {Hunter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into *water drops* that keep spreading and spreading until they become a **vast** ocean. An *announcer* on a buoy shouts through a megaphone, 'Ladies and gentlemen, the most **vast** sea ever!' The Hunter paddles in circles, unable to see the shore."],"羽":["feather","The {Yogi} in the {Basement} of the {Museum} sneezes, and a pillow explodes. *Feathers* fill the room like snow, settling on the mummies and the dinosaur bones. She picks up a single **feather** and balances it on her nose, then floats upward on a cloud of **feathers**."],"斤":["catty","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggles a gleaming *axe* and a sack of rice. A market woman shouts, 'Is that a full **catty**?' The Juggler chops the rice into exact half-kilo bundles mid-air, each a perfect **catty**, and drops them neatly onto the scales below."],"酷":["cool","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} wearing sunglasses and holding a *wine jug* full of ice cubes. An *announcer* yells, 'Here comes the **coolest** King alive!' He slides across the water on the jug, so **cool** that the pool freezes behind him."],"掠":["to plunder","The {Lifeguard} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} into a *palace* made of ice. A greedy *helping hand* slides out, grabbing crowns, candlesticks and golden skates. It **plunders** the treasure room, then skates away. 'Come back!' cries the Lifeguard, but the hand has **plundered** her whistle too."],"妖":["witch","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} watches a *woman* in a pointy hat appear on a broomstick. She is a **witch**, and she makes a *dancer* spin and spin until he turns into a bat. The Yogi stays calm, but the **witch** turns her headstand into a teapot."],"祸":["disaster","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and lands on a *small altar* where a *wok* sits sizzling. He knocks it over. Oil spills, the warehouse catches fire, boxes of fireworks explode. A total **disaster**. The Hunter hides under the wok, wondering how one bump started such a **disaster**."],"侍":["to serve","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a tiny *temple* where a *standing person* holds a tray of honey cakes. 'I **serve** the queen bee,' he says, bowing. The Sheriff takes off his hat and starts to **serve** too, pouring nectar and polishing the throne."],"乙":["second in order","The {Yogi} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut holds a race for her pets. A *swan* comes **second** after a speedy crab, and it is furious. It curls into the shape of the number 2 and sulks. 'At least you are **second in order**,' the Yogi says, giving it a silver medal."],"妨":["to hinder","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} as a *woman* blocks her path with a giant concrete *square*. Every time the Firefighter steps left, the woman slides the square left too. She **hinders** every move, so the fire keeps blazing. Finally the Firefighter hoses the square away, still **hindered** by a pile of wet concrete."],"贪":["greedy","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} stares at a *clock* stuffed with golden *shells*. Every time it ticks, another shell drops out, and the Tailor grabs it greedily. He wants them all! He stuffs his pockets until his trousers split. Too **greedy**, he topples off the roof, still the most **greedy** man in town."],"挣":["earn","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} into a *tug of war* with a gorilla. A *helping hand* grabs the rope behind him, and he heaves and heaves. He wins! The gorilla pays him in bananas, and the Jockey proudly **earns** a whole bunch. Every rope he wins **earns** him more fruit.","zhèng"],"汪":["expanse of water","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} waves his wand and *water drops* pour out like a waterfall. A tiny *king* in a rubber ring floats past. The hangar fills to the brim with a glittering **expanse of water**. Planes bob like ducks, and the king rows across the whole **expanse of water** in his crown."],"尿":["urine","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} onto a *lying man* who has fallen asleep on a cushion. Then a cat lifts its leg, and *water* trickles all over him: **urine**! The man leaps up shrieking. The Ninja vanishes in a puff of smoke, holding her nose against the **urine**."],"莉":["jasmine","The {Lifeguard} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut into a field of tall *grass*. She swings a *sickle* like a scythe, and every swish releases a white flower: **jasmine**. The whole beach smells of perfume. Soon she wears a crown of **jasmine** and has forgotten all about the swimmers."],"悬":["to hang","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} of the {Mint} sees fresh coins drying on a line. He climbs a *stepladder* to **hang** his washing up too, but slips. Now the Shepherd **hangs** upside down from the line between the coins, swinging, while sheep look up and baa."],"唇":["lip","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Casino} holds a *clam* up to his *mouth* to slurp it. It snaps shut on his **lip**! He runs up the stairs shrieking, his **lip** stretched like a rubber band, and gamblers place bets on whether the clam will let go."],"翰":["writing brush","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} at *dawn* with a giant **writing brush** slung on his back. He dips it in the morning light and paints golden letters across the dark walls. By breakfast the whole mansion glows, and the butler wants his own **writing brush**."],"仓":["barn","The {Tsar} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} opens a wooden *barn* door and grain pours out like a waterfall. The planes below are buried in wheat. 'My royal **barn** is too small!' he shouts, and orders a second **barn** to be built on top of the first."],"轨":["track","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room} pushes a wobbly *cart* along the floor while a *crowbar* bends steel rods into a **track**. Patients climb in, and the cart rattles round and round the **track** past the reception desk, scattering magazines."],"枚":["piece","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lake} cottage, tapping his *cane* on a *tree* that grows coins. One **piece**, two **pieces**, three: each tap drops one coin. He collects them one **piece** at a time in his hat, and the hat sneezes them all back out."],"盐":["salt","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} carrying a *dish* scooped from a sparkling *salt flat*. She sprinkles **salt** on every step. The staircase becomes a slide of **salt**, and she rides down it on the dish into the soup pot."],"览":["to view","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} finds a *sightseer* with a gigantic camera, wandering among cobwebs. He wants to **view** the hidden treasure. The Lifeguard turns on the light, and he gasps: the basement is full of paintings! He **views** every one, flash, flash, flash, until his camera melts."],"傅":["instructor","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a swimming class. A *standing person* waves a *proclamation*: 'I am your **instructor**!' He teaches her to float, to splash, to rescue rubber ducks. She grins: her new **instructor** is very strict, but she passes with a gold star."],"帅":["handsome","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Wine Cellar}, wraps a *towel* around his shoulders like a cape, and poses among the barrels. 'How **handsome** am I?' The bottles all clink in agreement. He admires his reflection in every bottle, more **handsome** each time."],"庙":["temple","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} into a *shed* surrounded by a *sprouting field* of green shoots. He waves his wand, and the shed swells into a grand **temple** with golden roofs. Cats line up to pray, and the **temple** bells meow."],"芬":["fragrance","The {Firefighter} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}, where a field of *grass* surrounds a slice of *cut cake*. The **fragrance** is so sweet that the rollercoaster stops mid-air. Riders float toward the smell. The Firefighter sprays her hose, but the **fragrance** only grows stronger."],"屏":["screen","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a *lying man* is strapped to *linked rails* on a conveyor belt. He glides past a giant **screen** that shows his own face. The Pirate cuts him free, and the **screen** cheers."],"寺":["Buddhist temple","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a tiny golden *temple*. It is a **Buddhist temple**, and every bee wears a saffron robe and chants quietly. The Sailor bows, strikes the gong, and joins them, humming along in the **Buddhist temple**."],"胖":["fat","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and eats a full *moon* pie for breakfast. He grows **fat**. He cuts the next pie in *half*, but eats both halves. He grows so **fat** that he gets stuck in the hangar door, and the planes have to taxi around him."],"璃":["glass","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} hut, where a tiny *king* in a crown is chasing a *goblin*. The goblin crashes into a pane of **glass** and breaks it into a thousand shards. The king is furious and makes the goblin glue every piece of **glass** back."],"愚":["foolish","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} and finds a *monkey* trying to stuff a giant *heart* into a teapot. It squeezes, it pushes, it sits on it. How **foolish**! The Yogi shakes her head, but the monkey tries again with a bigger heart, even more **foolish**."],"滴":["to drip","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut is kept awake by a *dripping tap*. *Water drops* **drip**, **drip**, **drip** onto her head. She sticks a toothbrush in the tap to stop it, but it only **drips** faster, spraying toothpaste foam."],"疏":["to clear away","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} finds the drain clogged with rubber ducks and hair. He wrenches open an *unclogged drain* and all the rubbish is **cleared away** in a gurgling whirl. He **clears away** the ducks too, and swimmers cheer."],"萧":["Xiao","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} stares at a patch of *grass* with a *stern face*. A sign beside it reads '**Xiao** family lawn: keep off'. Mr **Xiao** himself appears and glares at the sheep, who back away very slowly."],"姿":["posture","The {Zookeeper} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} watches a *woman* waiting in a *queue* of bees for her photo. When it's her turn, she strikes a ridiculous **posture**: one leg in the air, arms like wings. The bees copy her **posture** and fly off in a wobbly line."],"颤":["to tremble","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a grain *silo* in the cellar. He reads a single *page* from an old recipe book, and he begins to **tremble**. The silo **trembles** too, and grain pours out in waves."],"丑":["ugly","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} hires a *clown* to cheer up the crew. He takes off his make-up and he is so **ugly** that the fish jump out of the water to escape. The Chef hides his face in a pot. Even the boats look away, ashamed to be near something so **ugly**."],"劣":["inferior","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} and holds an arm-wrestling contest. The yeti flexes a *strong arm* covered in fur. The Lifeguard's arm is a tiny *pinch* of a thing, thin as a noodle. Clearly **inferior**. The yeti wins in a second and hands her a trophy marked '**Inferior**'."],"柯":["branch","The {King} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} climbs a *tree* to fetch his crown. He sits on a thin **branch** with a *nodding head*, saying 'Yes, yes, it'll hold.' Crack! The **branch** snaps and he drops onto the roof, crown on his nose."],"寸":["inch","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} and bets his crown on roulette. He measures his winnings with his *thumb*: exactly one **inch** of gold. 'Only an **inch**?' he shouts. The croupier measures his crown with a thumb too: also one inch."],"扔":["to throw","The {Robot} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse has a long *ribbon* tied to its *helping hand*. It starts to **throw** coconuts, bananas, a sleeping sloth, all lassoed and flung into the river. It **throws** so hard that its own head flies off too, spinning on the ribbon."],"盯":["to stare at","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} hammers a *nail* into a beam and hangs up a giant *eye*. It **stares at** every boxer below without blinking. They freeze mid-punch. The Dentist checks their teeth while the eye keeps **staring at** them."],"辱":["disgrace","The {Robot} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} challenges a *clam* to a race. The clam snaps shut on the Robot's *thumb*, and everyone laughs as the Robot hops round squealing. What a **disgrace**! It hides under a towel, its circuits blushing red with **disgrace**."],"匹":["matching","The {Pirate} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut finds a *matching pair* of socks for the first time in his life. He holds them up: both striped, both smelly, perfectly **matching**. He weeps with joy and makes his parrot wear a **matching** eye patch."],"俱":["all","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} with a heavy *toolbox*. A *standing person*, the curator, opens it and gasps: **all** the tools are there. She juggles **all** of them at once: hammer, saw, spanner, drill, while statues applaud."],"辨":["to distinguish","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a loud *quarrel* between twins about which coin is fake. He bites both coins and can **distinguish** them at once: one is chocolate. Now he **distinguishes** every coin in the exchange by taste, and gets a stomach ache."],"饿":["hungry","The {Ghost} slips through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} wailing that it is **hungry**. A *spearman* on guard holds up a *side dish* of dumplings on the tip of his spear. The Ghost gulps them down, but they fall straight through its body. It stays **hungry** forever."],"蜂":["bee","The {Firefighter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} spots a *bug* on the highest *peak* of a tree, buzzing loudly. It is a **bee**, then two, then a thousand. She tries to hose them off, but every **bee** just takes a shower and buzzes happier."],"哦":["oh","The {Ghost} drifts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} and pops out in front of a *spearman*. His *mouth* drops into a perfect round O: '**Oh**!' The Ghost tries again. '**Oh**!' again. Soon the whole fort is a choir of round mouths going '**Oh**!'","ò"],"腔":["cavity","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} shouts into a hollow *moon* she has carried up there. Her voice echoes through its *empty room*, a huge **cavity** in the middle. Fans climb inside the **cavity** and cheer so loudly the moon bounces."],"郁":["gloomy","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} onto a grey *hillside* where a sad man stands *holding meat*. Rain drizzles on both of them. Everything is **gloomy**: the sky, the meat, his face. The Yogi tries to cheer him up with a headstand, but it only makes the **gloomy** hillside gloomier."],"溃":["to burst","The {King} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} as *water drops* pile up against the reception desk. A *price tag* hangs on the water: 'Very expensive flood'. The dam of chairs strains, groans, and **bursts**! Water rushes out, carrying patients on their magazines. 'It **burst**!' cries the King, surfing past."],"谨":["careful","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Inn} carries a fragile *violet* in a pot across a tightrope. A *small speech bubble* floats over her head: 'Be **careful**...' She inches forward, so **careful** that she doesn't breathe, and sets the flower down without losing a petal."],"糟":["messy","The {Zookeeper} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} pours *rice* into a *trough* for the elephants. They stampede, slurp and spray rice everywhere. Rice in his ears, on the clouds, on passing birds. Everything is **messy**, and the Zookeeper sighs at the **messy** roof."],"葛":["kudzu vine","The {Gardener} on the {Staircase} of the {Hut} pulls up some *grass* and finds a **kudzu vine** curling up like a *question mark*. It grows a step every second, wrapping around the railings, the door, the Gardener's ankles. By lunch the whole hut is a green question mark of **kudzu vine**."],"苗":["sprout","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} sprinkles magic dust on a pot of *young crop*. Up pops a green **sprout**, wiggling like a worm. A cat paws it, and it **sprouts** more leaves to tickle the cat's nose."],"肠":["intestines","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} tries to make sausages longer than a plane. He stretches the **intestines** from the *moon* down to the ground, drying them in hot *sun rays*. Pilots weave around the **intestines** like a slalom."],"忌":["avoid","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and lands next to a *coiled rope*. Her *heart* pounds: it might be a snake! She **avoids** it, tiptoeing in a huge circle around it. All day long she **avoids** every rope, hose and string on the beach."],"溜":["to slip away","The {Lifeguard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} slides down a gutter on *water drops*, clutching a stolen *keepsake*. Nobody sees her **slip away**, out the window, across the lawn, gone. The owner chases her, but she has **slipped away** into the night."],"鸿":["wild goose","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut and a **wild goose** splashes down, scattering *water drops* everywhere. It honks so loudly the Hunter drops his bow. The **wild goose** grabs his hat and flies away, honking with laughter."],"爵":["noble rank","The {Juggler} on the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} skates into a ballroom carrying a golden *wine goblet*. The queen taps her with a sword: 'I give you **noble rank**!' The Juggler bows, slips, and spins around on her new **noble rank** like a figure skater."],"鹏":["roc","The {Pirate} on the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} sees his two *buddies* waving from the back of a huge *bird*. It is a **roc**, with wings as wide as the sky. The **roc** swoops down and plucks the Pirate up too, and they all fly off to find treasure."],"鹰":["eagle","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} holds out an arm, and a *falconer* releases a giant *bird*. It is an **eagle**, and it lands on her head. The **eagle** shrieks, and the boxers below duck as if punched."],"笼":["cage","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} hut and finds a sulking *dragon* squashed inside a *bamboo* **cage** no bigger than a birdhouse. It breathes fire, but the bamboo only smokes and smells of toast. She blows her whistle, the bars spring open, and the dragon thanks her by locking her in the **cage** as a joke."],"丘":["mound","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} piles pillows into a little *hillock* and leaps on top, pom-poms high. 'Pyramid!' Her whole squad scrambles up after her, then the backpackers, then a confused goat. The **mound** swells and wobbles until it pokes the clouds, the tallest **mound** of pillows ever built."],"桂":["laurel","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} with a *tree* in a pot. She hangs a *jade tablet* from its branches, and it bursts into fragrant **laurel** leaves. She weaves a **laurel** crown for every patient and calls them all champions."],"滋":["to nourish","The {Zookeeper} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} waves a *magnet* above the hive, and *water drops* fly up and cling to it. The bees drink from it, plumping up and glowing. He **nourishes** the whole colony this way, and the honey **nourishes** him back."],"聊":["to chat","The {Lifeguard} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café}, an *ear* pressed to a *mortise* in the wooden wall. On the other side, the cats **chat** about tuna, naps and gossip. She joins in, and soon they **chat** for hours, purring through the hole."],"挡":["to block","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} sees a runaway plane rolling toward her. A *helping hand* drags a *roadblock* into its path to **block** it. The plane bounces off. She **blocks** three more planes this way, then goes back to drilling teeth."],"纲":["guiding principle","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} ties a *silk thread* from the top of a *ridge* down to every plane. This is her **guiding principle**: everything follows the thread. The planes taxi along it in single file, obeying the **guiding principle** without a word."],"肌":["muscle","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut lifts a *small table* with a giant glowing *moon* balanced on it. Her arm **muscle** bulges, pops and starts to sing. She flexes again, and the **muscle** takes over, juggling the moon by itself while she sips a coconut."],"茨":["caltrop","The {Tsar} on the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} trips over spiky seed pods hidden in the *grass*. Every **caltrop** pokes his feet. A *queue* of bees laughs. He orders each **caltrop** to be picked up, one by one, by the bees with tweezers."],"壳":["shell","The {King} on the {Staircase} of the {Hut} trips over a *scholar* buried in *clutter*: books, bottles, odd socks. In the scholar's hand is an empty snail **shell**. The King blows into the **shell** like a trumpet, and whoosh! All the clutter is sucked inside, scholar included, leaving the stairs spotless."],"痕":["scar","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and sees a man on a *sickbed* who gives him a terrible *glare*. Across his face runs a long **scar** from a bumper-car crash. The Hunter shows his own **scar**, and they compare scars until the ride closes."],"碗":["bowl","The {Wizard} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} taps a *stone* with his wand, and it hollows into a *rice bowl*. Hungry, he fills the **bowl** with soup, but it keeps growing until he can swim in it. The **bowl** becomes a pool, and he paddles around it with a spoon."],"穴":["cave","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} hears sheep bleating underground. He finds a dark *cave* in the ice. In the **cave**, his flock is skating in circles. He leads them out, and the **cave** closes with a crunch."],"膀":["upper arm","The {Baker} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} hears a rumble: a runaway *moon* is rolling down the *roadside* toward the planes. He braces his **upper arm**, flexes until his sleeve bursts, and catches it. He kneads the moon like dough against his huge **upper arm** and bakes it into a croissant."],"卓":["outstanding","The {Jockey} on the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} lights a blazing *beacon* on a pole and rides his horse straight up a tower of crates. They stand far above everyone, glowing gold. The workers drop their boxes and cheer: '**Outstanding**!' The horse takes a bow, and the Jockey hands out leaflets saying 'Officially **Outstanding**'."],"贤":["virtuous","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} finds a golden *shell* worth a fortune and climbs every step to hand it back to the old lady who dropped it. He refuses any reward. The money changers weep and bow: such a **virtuous** man! The shell glows with **virtuous** light, and his sheep get haloes."],"卧":["to lie down","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} and finds a *minister* yawning beside a *fortune stick*. The stick says '**Lie down**.' The minister **lies down** at once on the stone floor, and the Wizard lies down beside him and snores."],"膜":["membrane","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} stretches a thin, wobbly **membrane** between the *moon* and the *sunset*, like cling film over the sky. Birds bounce off it. He pokes it with his wand, it wobbles like jelly, and the **membrane** pings him back down the stairs."],"毅":["resolute","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut, and an *angry boar* charges at her. She plants her *war club* in the sand and doesn't move a muscle. **Resolute**. The boar skids to a halt, impressed by such a **resolute** stance."],"锦":["brocade","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Inn} juggles *gold coins* through flapping rolls of *silk cloth*. Each coin stitches itself in, and the silk turns into shimmering **brocade** covered in golden dragons. The innkeepers grab the **brocade**, wrap themselves up like emperors, and parade through the bar."],"欠":["to owe","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and lets out a gigantic *yawn*. Out tumble IOUs, hundreds of them. She **owes** money to everyone: the banker, the cat, the moon. The banker sends her a bill: she **owes** one yawn for every coin, so she yawns until morning."],"哩":["lively ending","The {Lifeguard} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Beach} hut, her *mouth* full of gossip about the *village*. Every sentence ends with a happy little 'li!', a **lively ending** that makes her words skip. The neighbours copy her, and soon the whole village chatters with a **lively ending**."],"函":["envelope","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} misses a step and tumbles into a deep *pit*. At the bottom waits a fat **envelope** with his name on it. Inside, a letter says: 'Please stop falling into pits.' He climbs out grumbling and posts the **envelope** back down the hole."],"茫":["boundless","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and opens the top door: outside is no airfield, only *grass* rolling into an *open sea* that never ends. It is **boundless**. He throws his hat as far as he can, and it just keeps flying. 'Where are the walls?' he squeaks, lost in the **boundless** green and blue."],"昂":["to raise","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} with an *upward gaze*, staring at the *sun* through the skylight. It wants to fly, so it starts to **raise** its sheet, then its arms, then a whole aeroplane. It **raises** the plane above its head like a trophy and drifts toward the sun, glowing with pride."],"薛":["Xue","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Ice Rink} grows a bitter herb called *wormwood* in a flowerpot. Skaters smell it, scrunch their noses, and twirl away. The pot is labelled '**Xue** family secret'. Old Grandma **Xue** skates up, snatches it, and pirouettes off, sprinkling wormwood on the ice like confetti."],"皱":["to wrinkle","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} into a pile of *hay*. Underneath is an old cow *hide* that has been soaking in the lake. As it dries, it **wrinkles** and **wrinkles** until it looks like a giant raisin, and the Jockey's own face crinkles up in sympathy."],"夸":["to boast","The {King} on the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} is a total *show-off*. He climbs the tallest slide and starts to **boast**: 'I'm the fastest! The bravest! The best swimmer in the world!' He leaps off, belly-flops with a SMACK, and floats up still **boasting** about his splash."],"豫":["carefree","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} onto the back of an *elephant* carrying an *offering* of bananas. Instead of guarding the exhibits, the elephant twirls, hums and lies in the fountain. Totally **carefree**! The Yogi joins in, and soon the mummies are dancing, **carefree** too."],"胃":["stomach","The {Wizard} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and lands in a giant pink *stomach*, gurgling like a whirlpool. It swallows boats, ducks and his wand. He casts a spell, and the **stomach** burps him out across the water, his beard full of seaweed and his own **stomach** rumbling."],"舌":["tongue","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and a huge pink *tongue* rolls down the steps like a carpet. It licks his boots, his badge and his moustache. He tries to lasso the **tongue**, but it curls round the rope and tastes it too. Every step is sticky with **tongue**."],"剥":["to peel","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} opens his *logbook*: 'Today: **peel** everything.' A *standing knife* hops up and begins **peeling** bananas, oranges, potatoes, then the fort's flag and the Baker's apron, all in long curling strips that float off the roof like streamers."],"傲":["proud","The {Ghost} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower}, where a *standing person* and a *wanderer* are arguing over who is grander. Both puff out their chests and refuse to bow. The Ghost tries to scare them, but they are too **proud** to notice. They stand nose to nose, the most **proud** pair in the tower."],"拾":["to pick up","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, where honey jars have tumbled everywhere. A *helping hand* follows him, **picking up** each jar and pressing on a *fitted lid* with a click. Click, click, click. It **picks up** the bees too, popping them into jars until the hive complains."],"窝":["nest","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} finds a dark *cave* where a dragon has built a **nest** inside a giant *wok*. The eggs sizzle gently. The Wizard sits in the **nest** to keep them warm, and three tiny dragons hatch and set fire to his beard."],"睁":["to open eyes","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse is fast asleep. Monkeys play *tug of war* with his eyelids, pulling them up and down, until his *eye* pops wide. He **opens his eyes** and screams: he is upside down above a crocodile. Every time he blinks, they make him **open his eyes** again."],"携":["to carry","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} with a *carried bird* on each shoulder and a *helping hand* holding his lantern. He must **carry** a lunchbox to the yeti at the top. The yeti grabs him and **carries** everything back down: shepherd, birds, lunch and hand."],"陵":["tomb","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, which suddenly turns into a steep *hillside*. A gruelling *hill climb* later she reaches the top, where an ancient emperor's **tomb** sits under the floodlights. The referee counts to ten, but nobody gets up from the **tomb**."],"哼":["to snort","The {Hunter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple opens his *mouth* to sing in the *shrine hall*, but a wild boar beats him to it. It **snorts** so loud the bells ring. The Hunter **snorts** back, and they keep snorting at each other until the monkeys cover their ears."],"棉":["cotton","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and taps a *tree* with his wand. Fluffy white **cotton** balls bloom on its branches. He spins them into *silk cloth* on the spot and pays the banker with fluffy **cotton** instead of coins. The banker sneezes."],"晴":["clear","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where it has rained for a week and *moss* grows on the ropes. She waves her pom-poms, chanting 'Sun, sun, sun!' The *sun* bursts through the roof, and the sky is perfectly **clear**. The moss dries up and the crowd cheers a **clear** blue sky."],"铃":["bell","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where a *herald* is shaking a bag of *gold coins* instead of ringing the **bell**. 'That's not a bell!' she shouts. He melts the coins into a gleaming golden **bell**, and DING! the fight begins."],"填":["to fill","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and spots a hole in the floor through her *magnifying glass*. She shovels *soil* in, but it vanishes. She **fills** it with buttons, thread, coins and a banker. It is finally **filled** when she sits on top of it."],"饲":["to rear","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive}, where the queen bee, the *boss*, orders him to **rear** her babies. He feeds them a *side dish* of pollen pancakes every hour. He **rears** a thousand fat, happy larvae, and they all call him Mum."],"渴":["thirsty","The {King} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Hut} gasping, tongue hanging out. He is **thirsty**. A few *water drops* fall from a leaky pipe, and each one bends into a *question mark*: 'More?' Yes! He slurps them all, but he is still so **thirsty** he licks the pipe."],"吻":["kiss","The {Wizard} in the {Basement} of the {Funfair} spots a *pennant* with a painted *mouth* fluttering above the ghost train. It swoops down and gives him a big wet **kiss** on the nose! He blushes so red his hat catches fire, and every pennant in the fair blows him a **kiss**."],"扮":["to dress up","The {Baker} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a costume party. A *helping hand* grabs a *cut cake* and smears it on him as make-up. Now he is **dressed up** as a giant cream bun. Everyone else has **dressed up** as bakers, so he wins the prize."],"逆":["contrary","The {Ninja} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and lands on a *road* where an *upside-down man* walks on his hands. Everyone else goes left; he goes right. The waves roll out instead of in. Everything here is **contrary**, so the Ninja sneaks backwards, the most **contrary** ninja ever."],"脆":["brittle","The {Tsar} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and lands beside a *teetering man* holding a *moon* made of sugar glass. It is so **brittle** that it shatters when the Tsar sneezes. Shards tinkle everywhere. Even the chairs are **brittle** and snap like biscuits."],"喘":["to pant","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} runs from an angry swan. His *mouth* hangs open and he **pants** like a dog. A *sprout tip* pokes up from the floor and trips him. He lies there **panting**, while the swan steals his apron."],"罩":["cover","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and throws a huge *fishing net* over the blinking *beacon* at the top. The light is **covered** and ships crash into the docks. He grins at his **cover**, then realises he's caught himself too."],"卜":["to divine","The {Baker} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} shakes a cup of *fortune stick* bundles. One leaps out and points at the water. He uses it to **divine** the future: 'Splash coming!' A whale bursts out of the pool. He **divines** more and more, getting wetter each time."],"炉":["stove","The {Lifeguard} on the {Staircase} of the {Pool} lights a *campfire* behind a little iron *door*. It turns into a roaring **stove**, and soon the pool is a bubbling hot tub. She cooks sausages on the **stove** and hands them to the dripping swimmers."],"柴":["firewood","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Island} lighthouse and marks *this spot* with a cross. He chops the nearest *tree* into a huge pile of **firewood**. Then he cooks a feast so big that the pile of **firewood** burns all night and sailors see it from the sea."],"愉":["pleased","The {Yogi} paddles a *dugout canoe* up the {Staircase} of the {Museum}, bumping over every step. Her *standing heart* bounces on the bow, beating with joy. She is so **pleased** that she waves at every painting she passes, and the paintings wave back, the stern portraits grinning, all equally **pleased**."],"绳":["rope","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} lookout and finds a busy *frog* weaving *silk thread* with its sticky tongue, braiding a long **rope**. Before he can draw his gun, it ties him up like a parcel, croaking. He wriggles free, grabs the **rope** and swings away through the trees, yodelling."],"胎":["fetus","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut builds a little *stage* under the *moon*. A shadowy **fetus** appears in a glowing bubble, curled up and sucking its thumb. She sews it a tiny blanket. The **fetus** kicks, and the moon wobbles."],"蓄":["to store up","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} with sacks of *grass* for his *livestock*. He starts to **store up** hay behind every statue, ready for winter. Soon the whole museum is **stored up** to the ceiling, and the cows are visitors."],"眠":["to sleep","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and waves his wand at a weary *commoner*. Her *eye* droops, then closes. She falls asleep standing up. He sends the whole bank to **sleep** too, and coins snore in their piles, deep in **sleep**."],"竭":["to exhaust","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} to a *podium* and juggles a hundred snowballs. She keeps going until every bit of energy is gone. A *question mark* forms over her head: 'Any left?' No. She is **exhausted**, and she has **exhausted** every snowball too."],"喂":["to feed","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house, and a hungry *spook* opens its *mouth* wide. He tries to **feed** it soup, but it passes straight through. So he **feeds** it ghost noodles instead, and the spook glows happily."],"傻":["silly","The {Sheriff} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} finds a *standing person* wearing cucumber slices as glasses and a towel as a cape. He insists he's a superhero. How **silly**! The Sheriff tries to arrest him, but he slips on a cucumber and looks even more **silly**."],"慕":["to admire","The {Magician} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a *heart cushion* floating under the *sunset*. A diver swims past doing perfect flips. The Magician sighs, eyes shining: he **admires** her so much. He hugs the cushion and **admires** every splash."],"浑":["muddy","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Casino} and finds an *army* of soldiers stomping through the fountain in muddy boots. The *water drops* turn brown and thick as soup. Soon the water is so **muddy** that the goldfish wear goggles, and every gambler leaves dripping and **muddy**."],"奸":["crafty","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} watches a *woman* hide coins inside socks on a *drying rack*. The socks look innocent, but they're stuffed with money. How **crafty**! The Juggler steals one, but the woman, even more **crafty**, has filled it with buttons."],"扇":["fan","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion}, and a swinging *door* covered in *feathers* swishes back and forth like a giant **fan**. The wind blows his hat off and his moustache sideways. He fans himself with the **fan**, and the whole mansion cools down."],"柜":["cupboard","The {Gardener} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and lands next to a *tree* growing in very straight lines. She checks it with a *set square*: perfect right angles. It has grown into a **cupboard**! She opens the **cupboard** doors, and a dozen patients tumble out like laundry, holding their appointment cards."],"悦":["delighted","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} and lands in the lap of a *money changer*, who hands her a sack of coins for no reason. Her *standing heart* skips and dances. She is **delighted**! She skates in loops, flinging coins, and every skater catching one is **delighted** too."],"拦":["to stop","The {Lifeguard} sprints up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} after a runaway vacuum cleaner gobbling the carpets. A *helping hand* leaps out and holds up an *orchid* in its path. She shouts '**Stop**!' The vacuum sniffs the flower, sighs, and **stops** dead, purring like a sleepy cat."],"诞":["birth","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and follows a *stretching road* of balloons to a room where a *small speech bubble* pops: 'It's a boy!' A new prince has been born. She checks his first tooth to mark his **birth**, and everyone celebrates the **birth** with cake."],"饱":["full","The {Baker} in the {Basement} of the {Tower} unwraps a *parcel* stuffed with every *side dish* in the world. He eats dumplings, noodles, buns, until he is so **full** he can't move. He rolls up the stairs, too **full** to walk."],"乾":["dry","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} finds a *beggar* waiting at *dawn* with an empty bucket. No rain for months, and everything is **dry**: the plants, the soil, even the clouds. The Gardener weeps, but her tears are **dry** too."],"泡":["bubble","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a soapy *parcel* in his arms. *Water drops* splash on it, and out comes a gigantic **bubble**. It swallows him whole, and he floats up past every window, waving his sword inside the **bubble**."],"贼":["thief","The {Zookeeper} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Lake} house and spots a **thief** in a stripy jumper stuffing a golden *shell* into his sack. A toy *soldier* marches out of the cupboard and blows a trumpet. The **thief** panics, falls in the lake, and the Zookeeper locks him in with the penguins."],"亭":["pavilion","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} and finds a little *pavilion* with a curly roof built right in the middle of the ring. The boxers have stopped fighting to sip tea inside it. She sews silk curtains for the **pavilion**, and the referee declares the **pavilion** the winner."],"夕":["evening","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut watches a pale *dusk moon* rise while the sun sinks into the sea. The sheep yawn. It is **evening**. The moon leans down and tucks each sheep in with a cloud, and the Shepherd counts them to sleep in the purple **evening** light."],"爹":["dad","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} meets a hairy *father* who has been waiting *many moons* for his son to visit. Out pops a little yeti: 'Dad!' It leaps into his arms. The **dad** is so happy his teeth chatter, and the Dentist checks them. Best **dad** on the mountain."],"酬":["to repay","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} owes the fishermen of many little *islands* for his fish. To **repay** them, he rolls a giant *wine jug* down the steps into each boat. Glug, glug. Every fisherman is **repaid** with wine, and they sail home singing."],"儒":["Confucian scholar","The {Robot} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a *standing person* *waiting in rain*, reading a scroll under a tiny umbrella. He is a **Confucian scholar**, calm and polite, bowing to every raindrop. The Robot bows too, and the **Confucian scholar** teaches it proper manners until its joints rust."],"姻":["marriage","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} watches a *woman* roll out a *sleeping mat* for two. The groom arrives on a tandem bicycle. They are married on the mat, sealing their **marriage** with a pillow fight. The whole inn throws rice, and the Yogi blesses the **marriage** in a headstand."],"卵":["egg","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Swan Pond} finds two *bamboo joints* rolling around like little logs. She taps one: it cracks open, and a fluffy cygnet tumbles out. Each *bamboo joint* is an **egg**! She puts the other **egg** under a swan, who looks very confused."],"氛":["atmosphere","The {Firefighter} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} where a giant *cut cake* puffs *steam* like a chimney. The scent spreads over the rides, and the whole **atmosphere** turns sweet and cosy. People start to hug strangers. The Firefighter sprays the cake, but the **atmosphere** only gets warmer."],"泄":["to leak out","The {Shepherd} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} clutching an inflatable *globe*. It springs a hole, and *water drops* begin to **leak out** of Africa, then Asia, then the oceans. The yeti tries to plug it with its thumb, but the secrets **leak out** too."],"杆":["pole","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} cuts down a tall *tree* and strips it into a long **pole**. She hangs a *drying rack* from it, loaded with socks. The **pole** wobbles in the wind, and socks rain down on the guests."],"挨":["next to","The {Ghost} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse wants a friend. A *helping hand* drags a deckchair **next to** it, and a *full stop* rolls up and sits down. They sit **next to** each other all night, watching ships, silent but cosy."],"僧":["monk","The {Sailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} temple finds a *standing person* in orange robes balancing a *steamer* of buns on his head. He is a **monk**, and he hums so deeply the trees vibrate. The Sailor shares a bun with the **monk**, and monkeys bow to them."],"蜜":["honey","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beach} hut and the *roof* starts to drip something golden. **Honey**! Bees have built a hive in the rafters. He pulls a rabbit from his hat, and it comes out covered in **honey**, buzzing."],"吟":["to chant","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} and opens her *mouth* to **chant** in rhythm with a ticking *clock*. Tick, ohm, tick, ohm. Guests come out of their rooms to **chant** along, and soon the whole inn hums like a beehive."],"猩":["ape","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} sees a *prowling dog* chase a falling *star* into the ring. A huge hairy **ape** catches the star and beats his chest. The dog runs, and the **ape** becomes champion of the ring."],"遂":["to succeed","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} onto a *road* where a *trotting pig* races to the doctor's door. The pig dodges chairs, leaps over toddlers and bursts in first. It **succeeds**! The Sailor cheers as the pig waves a certificate saying '**Succeeded**'."],"狭":["narrow","The {Shepherd} climbs a very **narrow** {Staircase} in the {Piazza}, so tight he has to turn sideways. A *prowling dog* squeezes behind him, and he pulls it through with a pair of *tongs*. The steps grow even more **narrow**, and they pop out at the top like toothpaste."],"肖":["to resemble","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and sees a *portrait* on the wall that looks just like him. Then a cat climbs into the frame and starts to **resemble** him too, beard and all. Soon every cat **resembles** the Shepherd and asks for a crook."],"甜":["sweet","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} licks a gigantic stick of *candy* with her *tongue*. It is so **sweet** that her teeth tingle and she floats up the steps like a balloon. The bankers lick their coins, and they taste **sweet** too."],"霞":["rosy clouds","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} of the {Piazza} watches *rain* fall and borrows a paint pot with a *borrowed tool*: a long brush. He paints the sky pink and orange, creating **rosy clouds** above the square. The tourists gasp at the **rosy clouds** and ask him to paint their faces too."],"驳":["refute","The {Baker} on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} argues with a talking *horse* stuck behind a wooden *lattice*. 'Bread is boring!' says the horse. The Baker **refutes** it with a warm croissant. The horse tastes it and cannot **refute** a thing."],"裕":["abundant","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a lush *valley* where *shirt* trees grow. Shirts in every colour hang from every branch, more than anyone could wear. Truly **abundant**! She dresses the mummies, the statues and the guards in **abundant** shirts."],"顽":["stubborn","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and finds a single *yuan coin* glued to a *page* of his spellbook. He tugs, he zaps, he blows. The coin will not move. It is **stubborn**. He gives up, and the **stubborn** coin winks at him."],"於":["in, at","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Museum} flies a *kite* inside a *square* glass case. Where is the kite? **In** the case. Where is the case? **At** the museum. The kite tugs, and the Yogi floats up **in** the air, **at** the very top of the stairs."],"摘":["to pick","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut reaches up into a coconut palm. A *helping hand* stretches out of a *dripping tap* to help him **pick** a coconut. Then another, and another, until he has **picked** the whole tree bare and the tap gurgles happily."],"矮":["short","The {Ghost} in the {Basement} of the {Island} hut tries to shoot an *arrow*, but it only reaches the top of a *wilting stalk*. Everything down here is **short**: short candles, short chairs, a short Ghost too. It stands on tiptoe but is still too **short** to reach the light switch."],"秒":["second","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} holds a *grain stalk* and plucks off a tiny *pinch* of husk every **second**. Tick, pluck, tick, pluck. Twelve cats sit in a circle, tails flicking like clock hands, counting along. If he is late by one **second**, they all hiss and knock his hat off."],"卿":["high official","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} peeks through a *mortise* in the wall and sees a **high official** in silk robes sitting on a throne. He waves a scroll and orders silence. She cheers anyway, and the **high official** joins the dance."],"畜":["livestock","The {Chef} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands on a pig floating on a lilo. Cows paddle, goats dive, chickens sunbathe. The *livestock* has taken over the pool! He waves his cleaver, but the **livestock** splash him so hard he gives up and serves the **livestock** ice cream instead."],"咽":["to swallow","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} onto a *sleeping mat* and opens her *mouth* wide. A giant dumpling falls from the ceiling. Gulp! She **swallows** it whole. Then she **swallows** the chandelier, the butler and the mat itself."],"披":["to drape","The {Pirate} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut is freezing. A *helping hand* grabs a bear *hide* and **drapes** it over his shoulders. He looks like a king. The hand **drapes** more over him until he is just a furry mountain with an eye patch."],"辅":["to assist","The {Firefighter} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} wants to plant tomatoes. A *cart* rolls up loaded with a *seedbed* and helps her dig. It **assists** her every step, wheeling soil and watering seeds. Soon there's a garden, and the cart **assists** with the harvest too."],"勾":["to attract","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} dangles a golden *hook* over the edge, baited with roses. It **attracts** bees, then butterflies, then a duck, then a dreamy sailor who climbs up the rope. Everything that sees the hook is **attracted**, and soon the roof is crowded with admirers holding hands."],"盆":["basin","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} and finds a *dish* with a *cut cake* that grows into a giant **basin**. Water fills it, and kids splash around in the **basin** while the Pirate floats on a slice of cake."],"疆":["border","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} draws a chalk line across the field: the *borderland*. On one side, home fans; on the other, away fans. She juggles across the **border**, and both sides chase her back and forth over the **border**."],"赌":["to gamble","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} meets a *busy man* in dark glasses shuffling cards on a lilo. He bets a golden *shell*. She **gambles** her drill and loses. She **gambles** her chair, her mask and finally her own false teeth, and swims home toothless and grinning."],"塑":["plastic","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} onto a pile of *soil* glowing under a *new moon*. He squeezes it, and it turns into shiny **plastic**: plastic boats, plastic ducks, a plastic whale. The pool fills with **plastic** toys."],"畏":["to dread","The {Wizard} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and comes face to face with a *spook*. His knees knock. He **dreads** ghosts more than anything. The spook says 'Boo!' and he **dreads** it so much his beard turns white."],"吵":["noisy","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Tower} opens his *mouth* to complain, and a *pinch* of pepper flies in. ACHOO! The sneezes echo, shaking pots and pans. It's so **noisy** that the tower bells ring. Even the mice cover their ears at the **noisy** kitchen."],"囊":["sack","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} dragging a gigantic **sack** behind her. Bump, bump, bump. Planes peek out curiously. She tips it over, and out pour smaller sacks, then even smaller ones, until the whole hangar is full of sacks. The last tiny **sack** holds a single peanut."],"嗯":["mm-hmm","The {Ghost} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Funfair} and gives every visitor a *warm hug*. Each time, its round *mouth* hums, '**Mm-hmm**.' The visitors hum back, '**Mm-hmm**,' nodding. Soon the carousel, the clowns and the candyfloss stall are all nodding and humming together like one huge, contented fridge."],"泊":["lake","The {Pirate} on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} catches falling *water drops* in his hat until they spill over into a calm, glassy **lake** right on the roof. A *white dove* lands on it and floats like a swan. He launches a rowing boat to catch it and paddles round and round the tiny **lake**, getting nowhere."],"肺":["lung","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} house and lands on a *moon* wearing an *apron*. She takes a deep breath, and her **lung** inflates like a balloon. She blows out the fire with one huge breath from her mighty **lung**."],"骤":["sudden","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, and his *horse* lands in a quiet *gathering* of ducks. **Sudden** chaos! Quacks, feathers and splashes explode everywhere. A **sudden** storm whips up from nowhere, the boats flip over, and the horse ends up rowing a canoe."],"缠":["to wind around","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with a spool of *silk thread* that **winds around** his legs. He trips into a *tangle*, and the thread **winds around** the banisters too, until the whole house looks like a spider's web."],"冈":["ridge","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} plants tulips along a long grassy *ridge* that runs like a dragon's back across the roof. Planes taxi underneath and scrape their tails on the **ridge**. Petals rain on the runway, and she plants a second **ridge** just to annoy the pilots."],"羞":["shy","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel} watches a *clown* try to kiss his *sheep*. The sheep blushes, hides its face in its wool and runs off. It is so **shy**! The clown is **shy** too and hides behind his red nose."],"瞪":["to glare","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} beside a *climber* stuck halfway up a tree. He **glares** at her with one huge angry *eye*, as if it were her fault. She **glares** back over her mask. They stare and stare until the monkeys get bored, and even the tree looks away."],"吊":["to hang up","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and **hangs up** a gigantic *hanging lamp* shaped like a fish. Cats leap and swing on it. She **hangs up** more, and soon the whole café is full of swinging cats."],"贾":["surname Jia","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Piazza} finds a dusty *cabinet* full of golden *shell* coins, each stamped with the **surname Jia**. She juggles them, and every coin that lands spells J-I-A on the floor. An old shopkeeper bursts in: 'Those belong to the **surname Jia** family!' and demands his shells back."],"漏":["to leak","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and gets hit by *water drops* from a *leaky roof*. Drip, drip, splosh. The boats start to **leak** too, then the buckets she uses to bail them. Everything **leaks**, even her whistle, which now only gurgles."],"斑":["spot","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} juggles *twin jades* while a parrot gives him a *tattoo*. Instead of a heart, it pecks a **spot**, then another, and another. Soon he is covered in **spots** like a leopard, and the jades are spotty too."],"涛":["big wave","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} drops a *longevity peach* into a bucket of *water drops*. The bucket boils, swells and launches a **big wave** that sweeps over the city. She surfs the **big wave** on her ironing board, stitching a sail as she goes."],"悠":["drawn out","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} goes for a *leisurely stroll* around the chimney, her *heart* beating slow as a drum. Each step takes an hour. Her yawn is long and **drawn out**, her 'hellooooo' to the boats even more **drawn out**. By the time she finishes, it's next week."],"鹿":["deer","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands on the antlers of a *deer* doing backstroke. The **deer** gives her a ride across the water, antlers dripping. Soon a whole herd of **deer** is racing lengths and she has to blow her whistle at them."],"俘":["to take prisoner","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and finds a *standing person* in armour guarding a tiny *hatchling* in a cage. 'This chick is our prisoner!' She grabs the guard instead, ties him up with a hose and **takes** him **prisoner**. The chick **takes** the guard's helmet **prisoner** too."],"锡":["tin","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut melts *gold coins* in a pan, but they turn dull grey: **tin**. A *lizard* scurries up and taps it with its tail. It clinks like a cheap can. The Shepherd makes **tin** bells for all his sheep."],"卑":["low","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house waves a huge *fan* at the king's barge. He bows so **low** that his nose touches the tiles, then lower, until he is lying flat. The king says, 'Even **lower**!' and the Baker slides into the gutter."],"葬":["to bury","The {Zookeeper} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} carrying a goldfish in a matchbox. He digs into the *grass* beside the runway to **bury** it gently. Pilots stand in a row with their caps off. A plane flies overhead in salute as he **buries** the little fish."],"铭":["to engrave","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring} with a hammer and chisel. He **engraves** the winner's name into a *name tag* made of *gold coins*, tap by tap. The champion lifts it, and the Magician **engraves** his own name on the back, just in case."],"滩":["beach","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} pours *water drops* everywhere, and suddenly the roof is a sandy **beach**. A *caught bird* wriggles in her sewing net. She lets it go, and it lies down on the **beach** in sunglasses."],"嫁":["to marry","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Piazza} into a wedding where a *woman* waits by a little *home* made of flowers. 'I'll **marry** you!' shouts the groom, juggling rings. She agrees to **marry** him if he catches all twelve, and he does, with his nose."],"催":["to urge","The {Tsar} on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} sees a *standing person* stuck halfway up a *lofty peak* of paperwork. He bellows through a megaphone to **urge** him on: 'Faster! Higher!' He **urges** so loudly that the papers blow away, and the man reaches the top by accident."],"璇":["jade","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, where a tiny *king* plays with a *spinning top* carved from green **jade**. It whirls so fast it hums. The Shepherd tries to catch it, but the **jade** top bounces off his head, leaving a perfect green bruise."],"翅":["wing","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and a *branch* breaks his fall. *Feathers* sprout from his back, then a **wing**, then another. He flaps up and down the hive, frying eggs mid-air, until one **wing** gets stuck in honey."],"盒":["box","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hut} with a *dish* of leftovers. He places a *fitted lid* on top, and it snaps into a perfect **box**. Then he puts that **box** into a bigger box, and that into another, until he can't find his lunch."],"蛮":["barbarian","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and meets a *sweating man* in furs, roaring and swinging a club at a *bug*. He's a **barbarian**, and he smashes the vase, the mirror and the piano chasing it. The Magician pulls a rabbit from his hat, and the **barbarian** cuddles it, calm at last."],"矣":["already","The {Yogi} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut is about to start the lesson when a *full stop* rolls in and sits on her mat. 'Too late. It's **already** over,' it says. She checks: everyone has **already** gone home. She meditates alone, grumbling."],"潘":["Pan","The {Pirate} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} kicks over a *slop bucket*. The slop slides down the walls and spells out the word **Pan**. Lady **Pan** storms out in her dressing gown: 'That's my family name, not your graffiti!'"],"歧":["diverge","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} hut, but halfway up the steps **diverge** like a tree *branch*. One goes left, one right. A *stop sign* stands in the middle. Her squad splits too, **diverging** into two teams cheering in opposite directions."],"赐":["to bestow","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and **bestows** a golden *shell* on the queen bee. In return she **bestows** a *lizard* on him, wearing a crown of honey. He doesn't know what to do with it, so he bestows it on his butler."],"鲍":["abalone","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower}, carrying a *parcel* that wriggles. He unwraps it: a slippery *fish* and a shiny **abalone**, clamped to the paper. He tries to prise off the **abalone**, but it suckers onto his nose instead."],"锅":["wok","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} grows vegetables in a giant *wok*. She stirs *gold coins* into the soup for luck. The **wok** sizzles so loudly that pigeons dive in for a bath, and the **wok** spits coins across the roof."],"廊":["corridor","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} into a long **corridor** made of a *shed* stretched like chewing gum. A nervous *bridegroom* runs down it, searching for his bride. The **corridor** keeps getting longer, and he arrives on his wedding anniversary."],"拆":["to tear down","The {Chef} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut wants a bigger kitchen. A *helping hand* grabs a *chipped axe* and starts to **tear down** the walls, the chimney, the door. Seagulls cheer. He **tears down** so much that he is left cooking on the bare sand."],"灌":["to pour","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Swan Pond}, where a *heron* holds a watering can in its beak. It **pours** *water drops* over her head, then the swans, then the lilies. It **pours** so much that the pond overflows and she floats away."],"勉":["to make an effort","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} tries to lift a safe, but a *dodger* keeps slipping out of work. The Magician flexes his *strong arm*, straining, sweating, and **makes an effort**. The safe rises an inch. The dodger, ashamed, finally **makes an effort** too."],"盲":["blind","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} with a blindfold over his *eye* and bumps into a *tombstone*. He's **blind** for a magic trick, but now he can't find the exit. Planes honk as he wanders the runway, **blind** and waving his wand."],"宰":["to slaughter","The {Zookeeper} in the {Basement} of the {Island} hut sees a tomato under the *roof* shaking with fear next to a red *chili*. The farmer has come to **slaughter** the vegetables for soup. The chili jumps on the knife and **slaughters** nothing; it just sets the soup on fire."],"佐":["assistant","The {Zookeeper} in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} hires an **assistant**: a *standing person* who only uses his *left* hand. He passes fish to the seals with his left, mops with his left, salutes with his left. His right hand just waves at nobody. Still, he is the best **assistant** the zoo has ever had."],"啥":["what","The {Sheriff} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} and peeks into a little *hut* where a giant *mouth* is sitting in a hot tub. '**What**?' he shouts. '**What**?' it shouts back, louder. They keep saying **what**, until the steam is so thick no one can see."],"胀":["to swell","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} as the *moon* starts **swelling**. A girl with *long hair* blows into it like a balloon, and it **swells** until it fills the entire hangar. Planes squeeze against the walls as the moon squeaks."],"扯":["to pull","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Hut} finds a *stop sign* blocking his kitchen. A *helping hand* **pulls** it, but it won't budge. He **pulls** too, and with a POP the sign comes loose, flinging him through the wall into the soup pot."],"禧":["joy","The {Shepherd} in the {Basement} of the {Beach} hut builds a *small altar* covered in seashells and candles. Bells jingle, lanterns glow, and the sheep dance a conga line. It is pure **joy**! Even the crabs clap their claws, overflowing with **joy**."],"辽":["distant","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} and spots a *swaddled baby* on a *road* far, far away. She runs, but it gets more and more **distant**. Cats wave from the window. Finally the baby waves back from the **distant** horizon."],"抹":["to smear","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Fort} has paint on his hands. A *helping hand* grabs a *treetop* like a brush and starts to **smear** the walls with green leaves. He **smears** the floor and the ceiling too, until the fort is a forest."],"筒":["tube","The {Tailor} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} saws a long *bamboo* stalk into a hollow **tube** and drops a *matching cup* inside. She takes a deep breath and blows. FWOOMP! The cup shoots out like a cannonball, skims across the water and knocks a fish's hat off. The fish demands a **tube** of its own."],"棋":["chess","The {Cheerleader} on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} hut plays **chess** with a talking *tree*. The pieces are stored in a *winnowing basket*. Every time she moves, she does a high kick. The tree moves with its branches. They play **chess** until the tide comes in."],"裤":["trousers","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} wearing only a *shirt* and his crown. Everyone giggles. Red-faced, he swims to a *warehouse* across the water and finds a mountain of **trousers**. He pulls on fifty pairs at once, waddles back to the edge, and sinks like a stone in all his **trousers**."],"唉":["sigh","The {Ghost} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse opens its *mouth* and lets out a long, sad **sigh**. A *full stop* falls out at the end. Then another **sigh**, and another full stop. The ships hear it and turn back."],"朴":["plain","The {Pirate} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} digs for treasure but finds only a *tree* and a *fortune stick* that reads: 'No gold for you.' Everything down here is **plain**: plain walls, plain rice, a plain wooden chest full of plain socks. He swaps his feathered hat for a **plain** cap and sulks."],"咐":["to instruct","The {Firefighter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and sees a *cashier* with a giant *mouth* shouting orders. 'Put out the fire!' She is **instructed** to splash the flames. The cashier **instructs** her to splash harder, until the whole pool is empty."],"孕":["pregnant","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes} and finds a camel tied with a pink *ribbon*. Its tummy is huge: it is **pregnant**. A tiny *child* camel kicks inside. The Yogi helps the **pregnant** camel do breathing exercises in the sand."],"誓":["vow","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive}, holds up a *snapped stick* like a sword and swears a solemn **vow**. A huge *speech bubble* floats from his lips: 'I will guard this honey forever!' Ten thousand bees stand to attention and take the **vow** too, saluting with their stingers."],"喉":["throat","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} and meets a *marquis* in a powdered wig gargling seawater. His *mouth* opens so wide that the Hunter can see right down his **throat**, where a little fish is swimming laps. The marquis gargles, the fish surfs, and the **throat** gurgles like a drain."],"妄":["absurd","The {Wizard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and sees a *woman* dancing on a *tombstone* with a plane on her head. It's **absurd**! She tells him she's the queen of the moon. Every **absurd** claim makes the plane spin faster."],"拘":["to restrain","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} is juggling marble statues when she reads a *quotation* carved on the wall: 'Hands off the art.' A giant *helping hand* shoots out of the plaque to **restrain** her, pinning her arms to her sides. It **restrains** her until every statue is safely back on its plinth."],"链":["chain","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, and a *convoy* of trucks drives past, each linked by a **chain** of *gold coins*. The **chain** clinks so loudly that the banker comes out and wraps it around himself."],"驰":["to speed","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} jumps on a *horse* as a *scorpion* waves its tail at him. They **speed** away so fast that the stairs blur and the bees can't catch them. They **speed** past the hive, the forest and the moon."],"栏":["railing","The {Lifeguard} slides down the banister of the {Staircase} in the {Mansion}, blowing her whistle, but there is no banister, only a living *tree* with an *orchid* blooming on every branch. She snaps the branches into a neat **railing**, ties the orchids on as decorations, and leans on her new **railing** to watch the guests tumble down the stairs."],"逝":["to pass by","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} onto a dusty *road* and sits on a *snapped stick* to wait. Bees, carriages and whole summers **pass by**, buzzing and rattling, and nobody stops. By sunset his beard reaches his boots, and he sighs that time just keeps **passing by**."],"窃":["to steal","The {Cheerleader} sneaks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} with her pom-poms muffled, scissors in hand. Deeper in the *cave* she *cuts* a hole in the sleeping yeti's sack and **steals** every snowball he owns. She cartwheels out chanting \"Give me an S, give me a T!\" while the yeti wakes to find someone **stole** his whole winter."],"艳":["glamorous","The {Yogi} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} in a gown of woven *wheat*, a *rainbow* draped over her shoulders like a feather boa. Spotlights swing, cameras flash, and the butler swoons at how **glamorous** she is. Even holding a perfect lotus pose she looks utterly **glamorous**."],"臭":["smelly","The {Chef} flings open the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and a green cloud of *stink* rolls out, wilting his tall hat. Inside, a week-old fish stew is bubbling by itself. Ducks paddle away, oars faint, and the whole lake turns **smelly**; even the Chef's moustache is **smelly** for a month."],"纤":["fine","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} unspools a *silk thread* so **fine** you can barely see it. A *thousand ants* march along it single file, carrying coins across the gap to the next building. The thread is so **fine** that bankers below think the ants are walking on thin air."],"玑":["irregular pearl","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} juggles pearls for a *king* who sits at a *small table*. One pearl is lumpy, bumpy, shaped like a potato, an **irregular pearl**, and it wobbles off course every throw. It bounces off the table and the king crowns it his favourite **irregular pearl**."],"棵":["counter for trees","The {King} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Hut}, where a *tree* is growing straight out of the chimney, heavy with *fruit*. He counts aloud: one *tree*, two *trees*, using the royal **counter for trees** at every trunk. Fruit rains onto his crown with each number, because the **counter for trees** only works if you shout it."],"趁":["to take advantage of","The {Chef} hides under the {Trapdoor} at the {Funfair} until the security guard dozes off, then takes **advantage of** the moment. A *runner* with *thick hair* bolts past, and the Chef grabs the long hair like a tow rope and waterskis behind him through the rides, **taking advantage** of a free trip to the candy floss stall."],"匠":["craftsman","The {Juggler} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} into a workshop where an *open crate* overflows with tools. A grizzled **craftsman** tosses him an *axe*, and the juggler, juggling three axes, carves a whole wooden grandstand in seconds. The crowd above roars; the old **craftsman** nods and hands him an apron."],"盈":["filled","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, balancing a *brimming cup* on a *dish* on her head. Every breath pours in more tea until the cup is **filled** past the brim and floods down the steps. The boxers paddle in the ring, now **filled** with tea to the ropes."],"翁":["old man","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse waves his wand and a *grandpa* appears in a rocking chair, beard down to his knees. The **old man** rocks so hard he launches into the canopy, swinging vine to vine and yelling \"In my day!\" Monkeys gather to applaud the fastest **old man** in the jungle."],"愁":["to worry","The {Chef} paces up and down the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse}, clutching his *heart* as *autumn* leaves pour in and bury his soufflé. He can only **worry**: will it rise, will it sink, will the boats float away? He **worries** so loudly that the leaves blow off the soufflé in a gust of sighs."],"瞬":["blink","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Casino}, and a giant *eye* on the roulette wheel stares back. In one *eyeblink*, the chips vanish, the dealer vanishes, and the Sheriff's hat vanishes. Everything happens in a **blink**, so the Sheriff keeps his eyes propped open with toothpicks, terrified to **blink** again."],"婴":["infant","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} cradles a tiny *baby* in red boxing gloves. The **infant** squirms out of her arms, hops into the ring below, and knocks out the heavyweight champion with one wobbly punch. The referee counts to ten while the **infant** naps on the champion's belly."],"孝":["filial piety","The {Shepherd} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and a *dutiful son* climbs out carrying his old father piggyback. He pours dad's tea, combs his beard, shoos cats off his lap, all with a deep bow. The cats are so moved by such **filial piety** they start carrying their own mothers around, purring with **filial piety**."],"颈":["neck","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} juggles a book until one *page* tears loose and wraps around his **neck** like a scarf. It keeps growing, printing more and more, until his **neck** is as long as a giraffe's and his head bonks the ring lights above."],"倘":["if","The {Tailor} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} looks up at a *standing person* balanced in the *attic* hatch. \"**If** you jump, I'll catch you; **if** you don't, I'll sew you a parachute.\" The person jumps, the Tailor stitches madly, and the parachute pops open one inch above the floor."],"浙":["Zhejiang","The {Jockey} gallops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} straight into a river, spraying *water drops*, and uses a *snapped stick* as an oar. He paddles his horse south along the coast until he reaches **Zhejiang**, where tea pickers wave from green hills. \"Welcome to **Zhejiang**!\" they cry, handing him a soggy towel."],"谅":["to excuse","The {Lifeguard} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} into a grand *palace*, landing on the queen's cake. A *small speech bubble* floats from the queen's lips: \"We **excuse** you.\" The Lifeguard bows, slips on frosting, flattens a second cake, and the bubble sighs: \"We **excuse** you again.\""],"蔽":["to shield","The {Baker} slams the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} as a sandstorm hits, then piles *grass* and old *rags* over his trays of bread to **shield** them. Sand pings off the heap like hail. When the storm passes, the loaves are perfect, and he wears the rags as a cape to **shield** himself from praise."],"畅":["smooth","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and slides down a giant *skewer* like a firepole, glowing in the *sun rays* pouring through the roof. Everything goes **smooth**: the kebabs glide off, the planes glide out, and the Chef's moustache is buttered perfectly **smooth**."],"赠":["to present","The {Zookeeper} pops out of the {Trapdoor} in the {Jungle} with a gift: a glittering *shell* balanced on a bamboo *steamer*. She bows and **presents** it to a gorilla. The gorilla opens the steamer, finds dumplings, and **presents** her with a banana in return, very formally."],"妮":["girl","The {Ninja} lands on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach}, where a *woman* and a *nun* are teaching a little **girl** to fly a kite. The ninja flips, the kite tangles in her sword, and the **girl** laughs so hard she floats up with the kite and waves goodbye."],"莎":["katydid","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} hears a chirp in a pot of *grass* growing out of warm *sand*. A green **katydid** pops up, sings \"katy-did, katy-didn't\" and sprays sand in his eye. He arrests the **katydid**, but it hops away into the steam room."],"尉":["officer","The {Wizard} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Lake} and surfaces in a uniform with brass buttons: a military *officer*. He salutes the fish, who line up in ranks. The **officer** inspects them, the frogs sound bugles, and the lake has never been so well drilled by an **officer**."],"冻":["to freeze","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} and *icicles* sprout from his drill. An arctic wind from the *east* howls, and the whole lagoon begins to **freeze** with a crackle. Flamingos stop mid-step, the waves **freeze** into glass curls, and the Dentist ice-skates out."],"跪":["to kneel","The {Gardener} trips through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *teetering man* wobbles in a queue. A *kicking foot* swings out of nowhere and taps his knee, and down he goes: everyone has to **kneel**. Patients, nurses and the receptionist all **kneel** in a row, waiting for their names."],"闯":["to charge","The {Chef} in the {Basement} by the {Swamp} rides a *horse* straight at a locked *gate*. He bellows, the horse snorts, and they **charge** through in an explosion of splinters and frogs. The swamp creatures cheer and **charge** after him, waving lily pads."],"葡":["grape, Portugal","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, where *grass* grows on every step and a slow *crawler* drags a bunch of **grapes**. The pirate swipes one, it bursts purple all over his beard, and the crawler squeaks \"Portugal!\" and waddles off with the rest of the **grapes**."],"後":["behind","The {Hunter} creeps through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, but he hears *footsteps* **behind** him. He spins: nothing. He tiptoes on: *footsteps*. Every time he looks, a duck in fluffy slippers is standing right **behind** him, whistling innocently and hiding a rowing oar behind its back."],"厨":["kitchen","The {Chef} tumbles down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} and lands under a *cliff* where his **kitchen** is carved into the rock face. Pots hang from stalactites, the oven is a cave, and the sink is the pool itself. Swimmers drift through his **kitchen** asking for lunch."],"鸭":["duck","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} meets a *bird* wearing shining *armour*: a **duck** knight. It quacks a battle cry and waddles off the edge, armour clanking, and belly-flops into the hot tub. The Yogi takes up arms beside the brave **duck**."],"颠":["top","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} does a *headstand* on the weathervane, the very **top** of the building. Coins tumble out of his pockets onto the traders below. From the **top**, upside down, he shouts \"Open wide!\" to the entire city."],"遮":["to cover up","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} sees a messy *kitchen* sliding down the *road* below and the inspector coming. He flings a tablecloth over the whole kitchen to **cover up** the mess. The inspector lifts a corner, a pot falls on his foot, and the Jockey **covers up** that too."],"谊":["friendship","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} into a *cozy room* made of driftwood. A *small speech bubble* floats over each guest saying \"friend!\" They hug, trade sandwiches, and knit a scarf a mile long out of **friendship**. The sea rolls in, but the **friendship** floats."],"圳":["ditch","The {Jockey} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into a **ditch** where the *soil* has been dug away and a little *river* rushes past. His horse uses the ditch as a water slide; children follow on inflatables. Soon the whole fair queues for the **ditch**."],"吁":["to implore","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} next to a *coat stand* with a giant *mouth*. \"Please, please!\" the mouth wails, \"Take off this hat!\" It **implores** every visitor until the Yogi lifts the hat, and the stand sighs in relief, and then **implores** her for a scarf."],"仑":["to arrange","The {Lifeguard} on the {Staircase} of the {Casino} blows her whistle at a chaotic pile of chips. She starts to **arrange** them into a *neat stack*, then another, then a tower that reaches the chandelier. Gamblers gasp; she **arranges** the cards, the dice and even the dealer's eyebrows."],"辟":["to open up","The {Pirate} crashes through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and meets a *pioneer* with a machete. Together they hack through the jungle to **open up** a new trail. The pioneer clears trees, the pirate clears coconuts, and the island is **opened up** for ice cream stands by lunch."],"瘤":["tumor","The {Lifeguard} lies on a *sickbed* on the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} with a lump on her arm. The doctor removes the **tumor** and hands it back as a *keepsake* in a jar. She names the **tumor** Gerald and puts it on the hostel shelf, where backpackers take photos with it."],"嫂":["sister-in-law","The {Sailor} in the {Basement} of the {Tower} hosts a family dinner. A *woman* and an *elder* argue over the dumplings: it's his **sister-in-law** and grandma. The **sister-in-law** wins, launches a dumpling across the room and it lands in the sailor's soup."],"陀":["slope","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} finds the steps have melted into a grassy *hillside*, and a *serpent* slithers down the **slope**. The tailor grabs its tail and they toboggan down the **slope**, crashing into stacks of fabric at the bottom."],"框":["frame","The {King} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swamp} and lands inside a huge *picture frame* nailed to a *tree*. Frogs line up to admire the royal portrait. The king, stuck in the **frame**, poses grandly, while the swamp hangs the **frame** in its gallery."],"谭":["surname Tan","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} pins a nametag onto every guest. A *small speech bubble* pops from each tag announcing \"Hello, my surname is Tan!\" Everyone in the **surname Tan** family hugs; the tailor soon realises he too has the **surname Tan**."],"亨":["prosperous","The {Hunter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} finds a golden *shrine hall*, where coins rain down from the roof. Every offering returns double, and the hunter's pockets overflow. He's so **prosperous** that monkeys open a bank, and the jungle has never been so **prosperous**."],"钦":["to respect","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} tosses *gold coins* in the air, but a sleepy *yawn* from a guest blows them back. She bows deeply to the guest to show she **respects** him. The guest yawns again; she **respects** that too, and does a quiet cheer."],"庸":["ordinary","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} boathouse sits in a plain wooden *shed* that is totally **ordinary**: one chair, one broom, one sock. Tourists come to see the famous yogi, and she does nothing special but drink tea. They leave thrilled by how **ordinary** it is."],"歉":["to apologize","The {Cheerleader} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} carrying *two sheaves* of wheat, then knocks over the banker. She does a giant *yawn* by accident, which looks rude, so she **apologizes** with a cheer: \"S-O-R-R-Y!\" The banker **apologizes** too, for some reason."],"芝":["zoysia grass","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} rides along a *winding path* through tall *grass*. He discovers a carpet of **zoysia grass** so soft that the horse lies down and bees nap on it too. The Jockey rolls a bale of **zoysia grass** home for his lawn."],"吼":["to roar","The {Hunter} in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} kneels by a dark *hole* in the floor and puts his *mouth* to it. He lets out a mighty **roar**, and from deep below comes an even bigger one back. Boats rattle, oars leap off the walls, and a walrus pokes its head up to **roar** that it is trying to sleep."],"甫":["just","The {Firefighter} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} waters a *seedbed* with her hose, and sprouts pop up instantly. \"I **just** planted those!\" she cries, as a beanstalk crashes through the ceiling into the deep end. Swimmers climb down it, saying they **just** came for a swim."],"衫":["garment","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} hangs his laundry, but his *shirt* has grown *bristles* like a hedgehog. Every **garment** on the line sprouts spikes and starts crawling toward the chimney. The Sheriff lassoes them, puts on the prickliest **garment**, and itches all the way to the saloon."],"摊":["to spread out","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} stretches out a *helping hand* and opens it, and a *caught bird* flutters free. Its wings **spread out** wide, then wider, until they cover the whole roof like a picnic blanket. The Tailor **spreads out** his sandwiches on the feathers and invites the pigeons to lunch."],"宴":["banquet","The {Yogi} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a **banquet** hall under a glass *roof*. A *sunbathing woman* lies stretched across the dining table between roast turkeys and jellies. Guests politely pass the gravy over her, and she declares it the sunniest **banquet** of the season."],"嘱":["instruct","The {Jockey} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} faces a huge *mouth* nailed to the wall that won't stop talking. It **instructs** all his *kinfolk* at once: \"Grandma, hold the reins! Uncle, mind the hurdles! Cousins, swim in a straight line!\" The kinfolk obey, and the mouth **instructs** the goldfish next."],"衷":["inner feelings","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} opens his silk *robe* to reveal a painted *bullseye* right over his heart. Arrows of emotion thud into it one after another: love, fear, homesickness. Each arrow plays a little tune that sings out his **inner feelings**, and the lagoon weeps at his **inner feelings**."],"娇":["pampered","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} carries a *woman* who refuses to touch the ground; she walks only on golden *stilts*. Cats fan her, waiters peel her grapes, and she sighs if the cushion is too soft. She is the most **pampered** guest ever, and the cats are jealous: they wanted to be **pampered**."],"陕":["Shaanxi","The {Sheriff} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} uses giant *tongs* to pick up a whole *hillside* of yellow loess and set it on the map. The hillside unfolds into terraces, cave homes and a terracotta army marching out of the soil. \"Welcome to **Shaanxi**,\" salutes a clay soldier, and the Sheriff stamps **Shaanxi** in his passport."],"矩":["rule","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Museum} juggles an *arrow* and a *set square*, measuring every statue as it flies past. Anyone crooked must obey the **rule**: straighten up! Statues snap upright, frames line up, and the juggler chalks the last **rule** on the wall at a perfect right angle."],"浦":["river bank","The {Pirate} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} finds a muddy **river bank** where the tiles should be, thick with swaying *cattail*. He pokes his cutlass into the reeds and a family of otters scolds him. He builds a hammock between two cattails and naps on the **river bank** till the tide comes in."],"讶":["astonished","The {Yogi} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} and a *small speech bubble* floats above a sleeping vampire's lips: \"Who's there?\" The vampire flashes a *fang*, the Yogi is **astonished**, and so is the vampire, who has never seen a person in a lotus pose before. Both stare, utterly **astonished**, in the steam."],"耸":["to raise up","The {Sailor} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} grabs a *follower* by the *ear* and starts to **raise up** the poor fellow toward the ceiling. The follower's ear stretches like rubber and pops through the floorboards above. Everyone in the lagoon **raises up** their own ears in alarm."],"裸":["naked","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} hears a crash: a stack of crates bursts and an army of *fruit* comes rolling out, every banana with its *shirt* torn off. Peeled, they run around totally **naked**, shrieking. She chases them with towels, but the oranges peel too, and soon the whole warehouse is **naked**."],"碧":["bluish green","The {Baker} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds an *amber* lump glowing beside a mossy *stone*. He tosses them into the sea, and the whole bay turns **bluish green**, like mint jelly. He dunks a croissant in it; now his croissants are **bluish green** and wildly popular."],"摧":["to destroy","The {Tsar} on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} raises a giant *helping hand* and karate-chops a *lofty peak* in the distance. The mountain crumbles, avalanches tumble, and he moves on to **destroy** the clock, the magazine rack and the 'please wait' sign. Patients cheer: he will **destroy** waiting forever."],"薪":["salary","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} gets paid in bundles of *firewood* tied with *grass*. Every month his **salary** grows taller, until his stack is higher than the chimney. The innkeeper burns half of it for heat, and the Shepherd demands his **salary** be paid in sheep instead."],"淋":["to sprinkle","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} swinging a watering can over a little indoor *grove* of lemon trees. She **sprinkles** *water drops* on everything: the trees, the guests, the cat, the wedding cake. The innkeeper opens an umbrella, so she crouches and **sprinkles** him from below until his slippers float."],"耻":["shame","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Beehive} has honey dripping from one *ear* after he licked the queen's private jar. A furious bee holds up a *stop sign* in his face. He blushes crimson with **shame**, and the bees hum a song of his **shame** for a week."],"胶":["glue","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} sits under the *moon* with *crossed legs*, but he has spilled **glue** all over himself. His legs stick together, his juggling balls stick to his hands, and a cat sticks to his head. The moon itself gets stuck to the chimney with **glue**."],"屠":["butcher","The {Tailor} on the {Staircase} of the {Pool} finds a *lying man* sprawled across the steps and a *busy man* sharpening knives above him. The busy man is the **butcher**, who mistakes everything for sausages. The tailor quickly stitches a sign reading \"not meat\" onto the lying man, and the **butcher** chops a pool noodle instead."],"鹅":["goose","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and finds a *spearman* guarding a white *bird*. With a honk, the **goose** grabs the spear, chases the spearman out the door and hisses at the Ghost. The ghost flees, terrified for the first time in his afterlife, while the **goose** takes over the hut."],"饥":["starving","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} sets a *small table* with a single *side dish*: one pea. He is so **starving** he juggles it to make it seem bigger. Seagulls swoop and grab it, and he chases them across the sand, still **starving**."],"盼":["to long for","The {Pirate} pops his head up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and his *eye* locks onto a *cut cake* on the dining table. He **longs for** that slice so hard that his eye pops out of its socket on a spring and floats toward it. Every pirate in the house **longs for** a slice too."],"脖":["neck","The {Baker} on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} looks up at the *moon* as a blazing *comet* swoops by. He stretches his **neck** to see it, longer, longer, until his **neck** is coiled up the staircase like a hose and his chin rests on the battlements."],"虹":["rainbow","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} sees a glowing *bug* hammering on a tiny *workbench*. It is painting stripes: red, orange, yellow, green, building a **rainbow** one plank at a time. When it's done, the bug slides down its **rainbow** into the lagoon with a splash."],"翠":["emerald green","The {Tsar} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} wearing a crown of *feathers*. He knights a chess *pawn*, which turns **emerald green** and glows. Every chair, magazine and patient turns **emerald green** too, and the receptionist asks if anyone has an appointment for envy."],"崩":["to collapse","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} canopy hears a rumble, and an *avalanche* of snow and dough comes thundering down the mountain. Trees, monkeys and bread rolls tumble as everything starts to **collapse**. The Baker surfs the avalanche on a baking tray, and the jungle **collapses** into a giant pile of bread."],"账":["account","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and opens a giant *shell* to find the bank clerk inside with *long hair* tangled in ribbons. She is counting every coin he owes on his **account**, with the long hair writing figures on the walls like a quill. \"Your **account** is overdrawn,\" she says, clicking the shell shut."],"萍":["duckweed","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, which is now flooded and covered with *grass* and green *pond weed*. Tiny round leaves of **duckweed** float everywhere and stick to his boots. He tries to box an opponent, but slips on the **duckweed** and floats away like a lily pad."],"逢":["to meet by chance","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} lodge and crashes into a stranger: a *chance meeting* with her long-lost twin. They both drop their hoses, stare, and laugh. What are the odds they **meet by chance** in a jungle? They plan to **meet by chance** again next week."],"赚":["to earn","The {Jockey} pops out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Swan Pond} and sells *two sheaves* of wheat to a swan for a gleaming *shell*. He sells more, and more, until he **earns** a whole sack of shells. The swans start a bank, and now the Jockey **earns** interest too."],"撑":["to prop up","The {Chef} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} treehouse watches the roof sag. He lifts a *palm* tree and a *helping hand* to **prop up** the ceiling. The tree groans, and monkeys hang from it, but it holds. The Chef **props up** his soufflé the same way."],"翔":["to soar","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} of the {Stadium} glues *feathers* onto every *sheep* in his flock. One by one they take a run-up and **soar** over the crowd, baa-ing like geese. The fans cheer as the sheep **soar** past the scoreboard into the clouds."],"倡":["to initiate","The {Chef} slams open the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and a *standing person* rises under a blazing *double sun*, shouting \"Let's begin!\" She **initiates** the first ever parade of flying saucepans, and the planes follow behind. Inspired, the Chef **initiates** a new tradition: pancakes tossed from every cockpit."],"绵":["continuous","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} pulls a *silk thread* out of his sleeve, then a sheet of *silk cloth*, then more and more, in a **continuous** stream. It wraps round the bankers, the vault and the stairs. The flow is **continuous**, without end."],"猴":["monkey","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} watches a *prowling dog* sniff around a velvet-robed *marquis*. The marquis pulls off his wig and reveals he's a **monkey**! He leaps onto the dog's back and they ride off, the **monkey** waving his crown."],"枯":["withered","The {King} on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} keeps an *antique* potted *tree*, but he forgot to water it for a century. It is **withered**, crackly and grey, its leaves falling like old paper. He hurls it into the pool; it gulps the whole pool dry, splutters, and stays exactly as **withered** as before."],"巫":["wizard","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} stands at a *workbench* with a *follower* mixing potions. One potion splashes on the follower and he becomes a **wizard** too, with a pointy hat. Now two **wizards** argue on the roof about who stole the wand."],"昭":["bright","The {Jockey} gallops onto the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} and swings a giant *spotlight* toward the night sky. The beam is so **bright** that owls put on sunglasses and the moon files a complaint. He aims it at his horse, who poses proudly, glowing **bright** enough to be seen from the next country."],"怔":["startled","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} lodge watches a *standing heart* jog toward the *goal line* on tiny legs, about to win the race. Just before the line it stops dead and stares at him. The Jockey is so **startled** he falls off his horse, and the horse, equally **startled**, sits on him."],"渊":["deep pool","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} lets *water drops* fall from her fingertips into the *abyss* below the building. The drops keep falling and falling and never splash, filling a **deep pool** that swallows coins, chairs and an entire printing press. She dives in; three days later she is still sinking through the **deep pool**."],"凑":["to gather together","The {Tsar} flings open the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and freezing air pours out, hanging *icicles* from every beam. All the shivering boatmen, ducks and fishermen **gather together** in a big furry huddle around his fur coat. The Tsar sighs, opens his coat, and they all **gather together** inside it."],"溪":["creek","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} watches a *page boy* carry a silver tray of *water drops* down the hill. The drops trickle off the tray and form a tiny babbling **creek** that winds between the sandcastles. The sheep line up to drink, and the page boy builds a toy bridge across the **creek**."],"蠢":["stupid","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Casino} bets everything on two *worms* racing through the *springtime* garden of a flower pot. He cheers, sweats, and then realises the worms are just napping. \"That was **stupid**,\" he whispers, and bets again; even the worms think he is **stupid**."],"禅":["Zen","The {Chef} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} before a *small altar*, holding a tennis *racket* in perfect silence. A ball flies at his head; he does not move, and it stops in mid-air. This is **Zen** tennis: no swing, no score, no worries. The butler bows to the master of **Zen**."],"阐":["to explain","The {Chef} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} stands before a locked *gate* and waves a tennis *racket* like a pointer. He **explains** to a class of potatoes exactly how a gate works: hinges, latch, push. The potatoes look blank, so he **explains** again, louder, then demonstrates by smashing through it."],"旺":["flourishing","The {Wizard} pops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} and a *king* stands under a blazing *sun*, scattering seeds. Plants burst up through the concrete, airplanes sprout leaves, and the place is **flourishing** like a jungle. Mechanics harvest pineapples from the propellers; business has never been so **flourishing**."],"寓":["to reside","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} and finds a *monkey* has moved in under the glass *roof* of the dinosaur hall. It hangs its laundry on the T. rex, sets up a bed in the ribs and **resides** there happily. The guard tries to evict it, but the monkey now **resides** in the guard's hat too."],"藤":["rattan","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple, through tall *grass*, and finds stems of *rattan* winding up the banister. He snips them and weaves a **rattan** chair, a **rattan** hat and a **rattan** handbag on the spot. The vines keep growing and weave the Tailor into the chair."],"匪":["bandit","The {Firefighter} in the {Basement} of the {Lake} house opens an *open crate* and out flies a **bandit** with *spread wings* made of stolen bedsheets. He swoops off with her helmet and her hose. She sprays him down, and the soggy **bandit** crash-lands in the lake."],"伞":["umbrella","The {Sailor} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} opens a black **umbrella** indoors and a tiny *person* drops out of it, then another, then twenty, all holding their own tiny umbrellas. They float around the cellar like dandelion seeds. The Sailor closes his **umbrella** and they all rain on his head."],"碑":["monument","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} by the {Lake} carves a huge *stone* into a **monument** of himself holding a baguette. He fans the dust away with a paper *fan*, and the statue sneezes. Fishermen row past to salute the **monument**, which keeps sneezing flour."],"挪":["to shift","The {Ninja} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} where a *pointing finger* on the wall orders \"That way!\" A huge *helping hand* reaches out to **shift** a crate, then a forklift, then the Ninja. Every time the finger points, the hand **shifts** the whole warehouse an inch to the left."],"琼":["fine jade","The {Cheerleader} on the {Staircase} of the {Youth Club} shakes pom-poms in front of a *king* who lives in a tiny *palace* carved from **fine jade**. He offers her a green cup that rings like a bell. She drops it; it bounces, unbroken, because it is the **fine jade** that never shatters."],"脂":["fat","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} reads an *edict scroll* by the *moon*: all horses must lose **fat**. His horse gasps, hides a doughnut, and starts jogging around the hive. The bees, also guilty of **fat**, buzz along behind with honey on their breath."],"谎":["lie","The {Hunter} in the {Basement} by the {Swamp} says he caught a crocodile with his bare hands, and a *small speech bubble* floats from his mouth. It drifts off into the *wasteland* and dissolves. It was a **lie**; every **lie** he tells drifts into the wasteland, now a gray field of bubbles."],"慨":["impassioned","The {King} in the {Basement} of the {Island} fort sits before a *finished meal*, and his *standing heart* leaps up on the table. It delivers an **impassioned** speech about pudding, pounding its chest. The king weeps, gives a standing ovation, and orders seconds; never was a lunch so **impassioned**."],"菩":["bodhisattva","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} through tall *grass* and meets a serene **bodhisattva** sitting cross-legged on the diving board. A *spitting mouth* hurls insults and peanuts at her, but she just smiles. The peanuts turn into lotuses mid-air; the Pirate kneels to the **bodhisattva** and surrenders his cutlass."],"萄":["grape","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, where *grass* sprouts from a *pottery* jar and vines spiral up. He picks one fat purple **grape**, then sews it a tiny waistcoat. The **grape** puts it on, bows, and rolls down every step to the bottom."],"狮":["lion","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} finds a *prowling dog* in a classroom with a strict *teacher*. The teacher shakes a mane onto the dog and it grows into a roaring **lion**. The bees flee, the Sheriff tips his hat, and the **lion** sits down obediently to learn arithmetic."],"掘":["to excavate","The {Juggler} on the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} finds a *crouching man* scraping the ice with an enormous *helping hand* like a digger bucket. Together they **excavate** a hole and find a frozen mammoth wearing skates. They **excavate** deeper still and pull out a penguin who complains they've woken him a thousand years early."],"抄":["to copy","The {Chef} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} watches a sneaky *helping hand* steal a *pinch* of salt from his neighbour's pot. He **copies** the move exactly, and the neighbour **copies** him back. Soon fifty chefs on the roof are pinching salt from each other in a perfect circle, and nobody's soup gets any saltier."],"岭":["mountain range","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} climbs a *mountain* that rises through the floor. A *herald* trumpets from the peak, and more mountains pop up in a row: a whole **mountain range**. She slides down the slopes, and the boxers hike the **mountain range** to the ring."],"晕":["dizzy","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} watches an *army* march round and round her in circles under the hot *sun*. She spins her head to follow them until she's utterly **dizzy**. She topples into the sand, and the army, also **dizzy**, falls on top of her."],"逮":["catch","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Island} lighthouse chases a *servant* who stole his drill down a winding *road*. He sprints, leaps over a crab, and finally **catches** him by the collar. The servant laughs and says \"**catch** me if you can\" again.","dǎi"],"砍":["to chop","The {King} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} swings his sword at a *stone* that won't stop yawning a huge *yawn*. He **chops** it in two, and both halves yawn. He **chops** again, and soon a dozen yawning pebbles fill the basement."],"掏":["to fish out","The {Tailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} sticks his *helping hand* into a tall *pottery* jar and starts to **fish out** treasures: a sock, a goldfish, a rubber chicken, a tuba. The jar keeps giving, so he **fishes out** a whole marching band."],"狄":["low official","The {Dentist} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} meets a *prowling dog* in an official hat warming its paws by a *campfire*. It is the **low official** of the beach, stamping forms for sandcastle permits. The dentist fixes its teeth, and the grateful **low official** stamps him a free pass."],"晰":["distinct","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} sees a *woodcutter* splitting logs under the blazing *sun*. Every chop is crisp, every splinter **distinct**, every shadow sharp as a knife. Even the sheep, normally fuzzy, become **distinct**, outlined in black like a cartoon."],"罕":["rare","The {Hunter} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} hangs a *torn net* on a *drying rack* and finds one strange fish stuck in it, glowing purple with three tails. It is so **rare** that scientists burst in with cameras and microphones. The fish winks; it knows it is **rare**."],"挽":["pull back","The {Wizard} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} grabs a fleeing *dodger* with a *helping hand* conjured out of smoke. \"**Pull back**!\" he yells, and the dodger is yanked off his feet like a rubber band. The dodger tries again; the Wizard **pulls back** harder."],"脾":["spleen","The {Pirate} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} feels a pain under his ribs. Under the *moon*, a doctor waves a *fan* over him and pulls out a **spleen** the size of a melon. The pirate looks at his **spleen**, salutes it, and puts it back in his treasure chest."],"舟":["boat","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} decides to ride a *boat* instead of a horse. He saddles it, cracks the whip, and gallops the **boat** down the roof tiles straight into the lake, splashing ducks. He wins the regatta by a nose, still riding his **boat** like a racehorse."],"痴":["infatuated","The {Chef} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} sees a wise *sage* lying on a *sickbed*, sighing, **infatuated** with the queen bee. He writes love poems in honey, hums bee songs and can't eat. The Chef brings soup, but the sage is too **infatuated** to notice."],"蔡":["surname Cai","The {Tsar} pops up through the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} and sees islanders making a *sacrifice* of *grass* bundles at a shrine. Each bundle has a name tag: **surname Cai**. The whole island shares the **surname Cai**, and they invite the Tsar to join the family."],"剪":["scissors","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} juggles a *knife* with two blades stuck together at the *front*, and they snap shut: a pair of **scissors**! He cuts banknotes into paper dolls, which dance across the floor. The bankers chase him, but he snips their ties with the **scissors**."],"脊":["spine","The {Juggler} in the {Basement} by the {Beach} hoists the full *moon* onto his back and staggers around, groaning and creaking. His **spine** bends like a xylophone, each vertebra ringing a different note. He plays a sea shanty on his own **spine** with two lobster claws, and the crabs dance a conga around him."],"弓":["bow","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} villa strings a giant *bow* with a garden hose. She shoots tulips like arrows, and they land in neat rows across the lagoon. Fish sit up to admire the champion of the **bow**, and she bows with her **bow**."],"懒":["lazy","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Mansion} finds a *freeloader* sprawled on a sofa, with a *standing heart* doing all his chores. He is so **lazy** that even his heart has to stand up to fetch the crisps. She blows her whistle; he is too **lazy** to hear it."],"叉":["fork","The {Chef} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} stabs a giant *fork* into the clouds and twirls them like spaghetti. He drops the clouds on the steam bath, where guests twirl their own. Every towel has a **fork** sticking out of it, and the Chef eats the sunset with a **fork**."],"拐":["to turn","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Wine Cellar} jams a *spare part* into a barrel with her *helping hand*, and the barrel starts rolling. She steers it, **turning** left and right between the wine racks, and it shoots up the ramp. At the top, she has to **turn** to avoid the butler."],"喃":["to mumble","The {Ninja} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} past a portrait whose *mouth* has turned to face *south*. It won't stop **mumbling**: shopping lists, grudges, soup recipes, the weather in Antarctica. The ninja clamps a hand over it, but it simply **mumbles** louder through his fingers, now giving away his hiding place."],"僚":["colleague","The {Lifeguard} on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} meets a *standing person* holding a *torch*: her new **colleague**. Together they patrol the café, rescuing cats from milk saucers. The **colleague** lights the way, she blows the whistle, and the cats elect them employees of the month."],"捐":["to donate","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} holds a *helping hand* out with a *silkworm* in its palm. The silkworm spins a gold coin and he decides to **donate** it. Coins pour out of the mint, and the juggler **donates** them to every passing pigeon."],"姊":["older sister","The {Zookeeper} in the {Basement} of the {Beehive} meets a tall *woman* in a beekeeper hat: her **older sister**, here to boss her around. \"Wrong honey, wrong hive, wrong hat,\" the **older sister** says, as bees swarm her and obey only her."],"骚":["to disturb","The {Sailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} tries to nap in his hammock, but a *flea* riding a tiny *horse* gallops up and down his nose. It leaps, bites and trumpets to **disturb** him all night long. He swats, misses, and swats again; by dawn the flea has recruited friends to **disturb** the whole town."],"拓":["to expand","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and uses a *helping hand* to push a *stone* wall outward. The warehouse **expands**, inch by inch, then mile by mile, and crates multiply. He keeps pushing, and the warehouse **expands** into the next town."],"歪":["askew","The {Wizard} on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} hut puts a *no sign* on the *goal line* of the beach football pitch. A ball hits it and it tilts **askew**. Then the palm trees, the hut and the Wizard's hat all go **askew**, and the whole island leans."],"粘":["to stick","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} visits a *fortune teller* who throws sticky *rice* at him. Every grain **sticks**: on his nose, on his saddle, on his horse. The fortune teller says \"You'll be together forever,\" as the horse **sticks** to the chimney."],"柄":["handle","The {Baker} in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} sets up a *tripod* over a fallen *tree* and carves it into a gigantic **handle** for his rolling pin. It is longer than the ring itself. When the bell rings he pole-vaults out of the basement on the **handle**, flattening the champion like a pancake."],"坑":["pit","The {King} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} canopy sees a man in a *high collar* digging *soil* furiously below. He has dug a **pit** so deep that monkeys use it as an elevator. The King jumps in to inspect it and the **pit** echoes \"your majesty\" all the way down."],"陌":["unfamiliar","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} and lands on a strange *hillside*, clutching a *banknote* covered in faces he has never seen. Every flag, coin and cow here is **unfamiliar**. He tries to make the banknote vanish; it comes back as a purple goat, equally **unfamiliar**, chewing his top hat."],"窄":["narrow","The {Jockey} in the {Basement} of the {Island} crawls into a *cave* where a *jack-in-the-box* springs up and blocks the way. The tunnel is so **narrow** he has to fold his horse in half. They squeeze through the **narrow** gap with a pop like a cork."],"湘":["Hunan","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} climbs a *lookout* tower and sees *water drops* falling into a long river. He follows it south to the land of chili peppers: **Hunan**! He eats one pepper and steams so much he could power the stadium; **Hunan** cheers."],"兆":["omen","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and finds a *cracked shell* glowing on the floor. The cracks spell a message: tomorrow it will rain carrots. It's an **omen**! Next morning carrots bounce off every roof, his horse gallops around catching them, and from then on believes every single **omen**, even fortune cookies."],"崖":["precipice","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Spa} climbs a *mountain* trail to the *cliff edge* and balances on one toe over a **precipice**. The steam swirls below like clouds. She does a headstand at the very lip of the **precipice**, and a goat applauds."],"骄":["arrogant","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} sees a *horse* strutting on golden *stilts*, nose in the air. It is so **arrogant** it refuses to talk to cats, then trips over a kitten. Still **arrogant**, it pretends it meant to fall."],"刹":["brake","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} chases an *assassin* on a runaway bathtub. At the last second he jams a *standing knife* into the roof to **brake**, sparks flying. The tub stops at the edge; the assassin, without a **brake**, flies into the pool.","shā"],"鞭":["whip","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} cracks a long **whip** of braided *rawhide* that takes a *shortcut* through the air, zigzagging between chimneys. Crack! It snatches coins from the bankers' fingers and stacks them in neat towers. Then he whirls the **whip** into a bowl and whisks cream so fast it turns to butter."],"芒":["awn","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} pulls a stalk of *prickly grass* from his hat, and its bristly **awn** shoots out like a spear, jabbing a pilot in the bottom. He pulls another, and another, until the stairs bristle with **awns** like a porcupine. The pilots climb up wearing oven gloves, yelping at every step."],"筋":["tendon","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggles a *bamboo* pole and a giant *rib* from last night's barbecue. The rib snaps back like a slingshot, held by a stretchy **tendon**, and fires a dumpling across the street. He plucks the **tendon** like a guitar string and serenades the innkeeper with a twangy ballad."],"聘":["to employ","The {Pirate} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} and whispers into a *knight*'s *ear*: \"I'll **employ** you as my cabin boy.\" The knight clanks, bows and starts swabbing the floor in full armour. By lunch the pirate has **employed** the cook, the cat and a goose, all on a salary of biscuits."],"钩":["hook","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} goes fishing with a golden *hook*, baiting it with *gold coins*. She casts it into the lake, and a whale bites, then a submarine, then the moon's reflection. Every catch dangles from the **hook**, and she reels in the whole lake on one gleaming **hook**."],"棍":["stick","The {Gardener} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Casino} holding a *tree* branch with an *insect* clinging to it. She strips the leaves and turns it into a **stick**, which the insect uses to pole-vault onto the roulette table. It wins every spin; the croupier confiscates the lucky **stick**."],"嚷":["to shout","The {Robot} in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} puts on an *embroidered robe* and opens a huge metal *mouth*. It starts to **shout** commands: \"TAKE OFF! LAND! MORE OIL!\" The planes taxi back and forth in panic. The mechanics plug their ears, but the robot only **shouts** louder, rattling every rivet."],"腺":["gland","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a cave where a *wellspring* bubbles under the *moon*. Every time a banker sweats, a tiny **gland** in his neck squirts like a water pistol. The Shepherd collects the drops in a bucket; every **gland** in the exchange is working overtime on market day."],"弦":["string","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and strings a *bow* with a *dark thread* pulled from his sock. He plucks the **string** and a deep note booms through the vault, making the coins jingle. Bankers dance, the gold bars hum, and he plucks the **string** again to stop the stock market."],"焰":["flame","The {Yogi} tumbles through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a *trap pit* where a roaring *campfire* sits at the bottom. She lands cross-legged right in the **flame**, perfectly calm, toasting marshmallows on her fingertips. The butler peers down; each breath she takes makes the **flame** dance higher."],"耍":["to play with","The {Sheriff} in the {Basement} of the {Water Park} meets a *woman* with a *beard* down to her knees. She lets him **play with** it: he braids it, swings on it, and slides down it like a water slide. The lifeguards join in, everyone wants to **play with** the beard."],"俯":["to look down","The {Firefighter} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} climbs onto the shoulders of a *standing person* who is so tall he pokes through the ceiling into a *mansion* above. She has to **look down** at the swimmers, tiny as ants. Everyone in the mansion **looks down** at her through the hole, waving teacups."],"厘":["one hundredth","The {Lifeguard} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} measures a tiny *village* tucked under a *cliff*. It is one **hundredth** the size of a normal village; the houses are thimbles and the mayor rides a snail. She blows her whistle and everyone in the village shrinks to one **hundredth** again."],"愣":["to stare blankly","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Jungle} and lands in front of a *standing heart* doing the cha-cha. She can only **stare blankly**, whistle half in her mouth. The monkeys **stare blankly** too, and a parrot forgets every word it ever knew."],"厦":["tall building","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} onto a *cliff* where the *summer* sun has grown a skyscraper out of the rock. The **tall building** keeps rising, floor after floor, until the spa guests in their robes take the elevator to sunbathe in the clouds. Swallows nest in the top of the **tall building**."],"恳":["earnest","The {King} in the {Basement} of the {Funfair} fixes everyone with a fierce *glare*, but his *heart* is full of hope. He kneels before the candy-floss seller and makes an **earnest** plea for the last pink cloud. His voice trembles, his crown wobbles; nobody has ever been so **earnest** about sugar."],"饶":["spare","The {Robot} on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} holds an *emperor* captive and threatens him with a *side dish* of cold broccoli. The emperor begs: \"**Spare** me!\" The robot beeps, considers, and decides to **spare** him, but only if he eats the carrots."],"钉":["nail","The {Dentist} on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} hammers a giant *nail* into the roof with a sack of *gold coins*. Each strike rings like a gong, and the boxers below duck. The **nail** sinks through the ring and the floor, all the way to China. The Dentist pulls it out with his pliers; the **nail** has a tooth on it."],"寡":["few","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Water Park} looks up at the *roof*, where only a **few** raindrops fall through a crack: drip, drip, drip. The giant slides are dry, the pools are empty, and the visitors are **few**: one duck, one tourist and one lonely inflatable flamingo."],"憾":["pity","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and the moose he chased escapes through the window. His *standing heart* sinks and he weeps big *tears* into his hat. \"What a **pity**,\" sighs the butler, and the moose, waving from the lawn, agrees: such a **pity**."],"摔":["to throw down","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Wine Cellar} hauls up a *dragnet* full of barrels with a *helping hand*. Then he **throws down** the whole net, and barrels bounce and roll down the hill, crashing into the vineyard. The farmer **throws down** his hat in fury."],"叠":["to pile up","The {Dentist} on the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} watches the *leaf pickers* bring in leaves and the yeti fold each one like a *folded blanket*. They **pile up** leaf after leaf, until the stack touches the cave roof. The yeti climbs to the top to sleep, and the dentist keeps **piling up** blankets."],"惹":["to provoke","The {Robot} in the {Basement} of the {Hut} meets a *lookalike*, another robot with an identical face, and its *heart* starts to buzz with jealousy. It pokes the lookalike, beeps rudely and steals its oil can to **provoke** it. The lookalike pokes back; they **provoke** each other until the hut explodes in sparks."],"喻":["analogy","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a *dugout canoe* where a giant *mouth* is teaching. \"Life is like a canoe,\" it booms, \"it floats till it sinks.\" That is an **analogy**. The Yogi paddles the canoe through the museum, and every exhibit offers its own **analogy**."],"谱":["chart","The {Pirate} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} unrolls a **chart** in *broad daylight* that streams through a crack. A *small speech bubble* rises from every note on the music **chart**, singing sea shanties. The pirate conducts with his cutlass, and the swimmers above join in."],"愧":["ashamed","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and a *ghost* floats out of the magazine rack and taps his *standing heart*. \"You jumped the queue,\" it moans. The King turns crimson, feeling deeply **ashamed**, and walks to the back of the line, still **ashamed**, apologizing to every patient."],"煌":["radiant","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Swamp} finds a *golden crown* glowing in a crackling *campfire*. It is so **radiant** that frogs turn gold and the mud shimmers. He puts it on, and he becomes **radiant** too, lighting the swamp like a lighthouse."],"徽":["badge","The {Hunter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} follows a trail of muddy *footsteps* across the tiles to a shiny **badge** glued to the chimney. He pins it on, and instantly every patient below salutes, the receptionist calls him Captain, and the doctor sees him first. The jealous dog follows the footsteps back, hoping to find its own **badge**."],"溶":["to dissolve","The {Robot} on the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} drops a sugar cube into a glass *container* of *water drops* and watches it **dissolve** with a fizz. Fascinated, it drops in a screwdriver, its antenna, then its whole left arm. Everything **dissolves** in a cloud of bubbles, and the robot beeps nervously as its foot slips toward the glass."],"坠":["to fall","The {Jockey} yanks the {Trapdoor} lever in the {Waiting Room}, and an entire football *team* in muddy kits drops through the floor. They **fall** in slow motion, cleats first, and land in a pile of fresh *soil* below, sprouting like turnips. Then the receptionist **falls**, then the potted fern, then the jockey's horse, still reading a magazine."],"煞":["to cut short","The {Sheriff} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} sits by glowing *embers*, telling a ghost story. Just as he reaches the scary part, a bucket of water hisses over the coals, and the story is **cut short**. Everyone groans, and he tries again, but the sauna timer rings and it's **cut short** again."],"巾":["towel","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} juggles wet *towels* in a thunderstorm. Each **towel** soaks up more rain, getting heavier and heavier, until one flops onto a pigeon. The pigeon dries itself off, bows, and hands him back a perfectly folded **towel**."],"滥":["overflowing","The {Lifeguard} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and *water drops* gush out, filling every room. An *inspector* in a raincoat arrives with a clipboard: the bathtubs are **overflowing**, the sinks are **overflowing**, even the teapots. He floats away on his clipboard, writing a report."],"洒":["to spray","The {Sailor} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} spots a *bird nest* above the hot pipes and cranks the valve. *Water drops* **spray** everywhere, soaking the birds, who **spray** back with their wings like sprinklers. The spa guests think it is a new treatment and pay double."],"堵":["to block up","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} watches a *busy man* shovel heaps of *soil* into the drain. Every pipe gets **blocked up** with mud and the pool overflows. The dentist grabs his drill and tries to unblock it, but the man keeps **blocking up** every hole."],"瓷":["porcelain","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} past a *queue* of bees carrying shiny white *tiles*. They are building a palace of fine **porcelain**, every cell gleaming. The Tsar taps one; it chimes like a bell. He orders a **porcelain** crown, and it immediately cracks."],"咒":["spell","The {Jockey} slams the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and a crowd of tiny mouths around a *small table* start to *chatter* in Latin. They are casting a **spell**: the oars turn to snakes, the boats to geese. The Jockey shouts \"Cancel!\" and the **spell** reverses, but now his horse is a canoe."],"姨":["aunt","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} meets a *woman* in a feathered hat and a *bowman*'s quiver: her **aunt**, the family's champion archer. She fires arrows that pop every beach ball and pins sandwiches to the lifeguard's chair. Then she hands everyone sweets and pinches their cheeks. Nobody dares refuse this **aunt**."],"棒":["club","The {Baker} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} carrying a *tree* trunk as a *tribute* for the pilot king. The trunk is carved into a huge wooden **club**, and the king swings it like a baseball bat, sending a helicopter flying. The Baker bows, and asks for his **club** back."],"郡":["county","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Dunes} onto a sandy *hillside* where a *lord* sits on a throne. He waves at the horizon: \"This whole **county** is mine.\" The juggler juggles sand to divide it into fields, and the lord names each one after himself, so the **county** is very confusing."],"浴":["bath","The {Yogi} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} into a misty *valley* filled with warm *water drops*. She takes a long **bath** among the dinosaur bones and the statues follow her lead. Soon the whole museum takes a **bath**, and the mummy unwraps to soak."],"媚":["charming","The {Magician} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} and meets a *woman* with one *raised brow*. She is so **charming** that fish leap to fetch her flowers and the swans curtsey. He tries to make her disappear, but she just smiles; he is the one who vanishes, it is that **charming**."],"稣":["to revive","The {Sailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} finds a dried-up *fish* lying by a *grain stalk*. He dips the stalk in water and sprinkles the fish, which flips, gasps, and starts to **revive**. It sits up, does a backflip into the pool, and **revives** the whole aquarium with a song."],"淮":["Huai River","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Wine Cellar} follows a trail of *water drops* and a chirping *sparrow* into a secret tunnel. It opens onto the wide **Huai River**, flowing between north and south China. He sails a wine barrel down the **Huai River**, and the sparrow steers."],"哎":["hey","The {Ghost} floats over the {Rooftop} of the {Island} and a huge *mouth* pops out of a bush of *mugwort* yelling \"**Hey**!\" The ghost jumps right out of its sheet. The mouth yells \"**Hey**!\" again, and now the whole island is shouting at each other."],"屁":["fart","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and lands beside a *lying man* sunbathing with *twins* on either side. Suddenly a thunderous **fart** shakes the sand. The twins point at each other; the lying man floats an inch in the air from the next **fart**, and the pirate holds his nose."],"漆":["lacquer","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} taps a *lacquer tree* and *water drops* of sticky red sap drip into her pom-poms. She paints everything with glossy **lacquer**: the chimney, the seagulls, her shoes. Then she slips on her own **lacquer** and skates off the roof."],"淫":["excessive","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Inn} watches a *greedy claw* poke through the ceiling, grabbing every *water drop* that leaks from the bathtub upstairs. It hoards bucket after bucket, then the soup, then the fish tank: wildly **excessive**. The buckets overflow and the stairs become a waterfall. The innkeeper paddles past in a pot, scolding such **excessive** greed."],"巢":["nest","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} finds a giant bird's **nest** built from spaghetti. A *nest* of eggs sits inside, and the mother bird glares at him. He cooks a tiny omelette as an apology and the bird lets him nap in the **nest**."],"吩":["to order","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} with a megaphone shaped like a giant *mouth*, slicing a *cut cake* with her axe. She bellows **orders**: \"You, ride the coaster! You, eat this slice! You, spin faster!\" Everyone obeys at once. The Ferris wheel whirls, crumbs fly, and the clowns salute and beg for more **orders**."],"撰":["to compose","The {Jockey} pops out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Swan Pond}, where a *kneeling pair* of swans holds up a quill like a sword. He takes it in a *helping hand* and begins to **compose** an epic: \"O swan, thy neck so long, thy honk so wrong.\" The swans, offended, snatch the quill back and **compose** a scathing review in honks."],"啸":["to whistle","The {Shepherd} climbs through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and a *stern face* on the wall puckers its *mouth*. It begins to **whistle**, one long piercing note that rises and rises. Cats fly off shelves, teacups crack, and the milk curdles. The Shepherd fights back: he puts two fingers in his mouth and **whistles** louder, and his sheep come running."],"滞":["stagnant","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} into a pool where *water drops* have stopped moving. A *belt* is tied round the pond to keep it still: totally **stagnant**. Bees grumble and the jockey's horse sniffs the **stagnant** water and refuses to drink."],"玫":["rose","The {Magician} on the {Staircase} of the {Lake} castle waves his *cane* at a *king*, and a red **rose** blooms from the tip. He pulls another, and another, until the king is buried in petals. Thorns poke the king, who sneezes; even his sneezes smell of **rose**."],"硕":["master's degree","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and lands on a huge *stone* tablet carved with a single *page* of tiny writing. It is his diploma: a **master's degree** in advanced lassoing. He lassos a forklift to celebrate, and the cows in the warehouse line up in caps and gowns to toast his **master's degree**."],"钓":["to fish","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} with a rod made from a soup *ladle* and a line baited with *gold coins*. He sets out to **fish** in the giant milk bowl and hooks a tabby, then a cupcake, then the barista. The cats, insulted, grab tiny rods and start to **fish** for his teeth."],"蝶":["butterfly","The {Dentist} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} and lifts a pile of *leaves* to find a shy *bug* curled up underneath. It stretches, unfolds, and keeps unfolding into a **butterfly** with wings as wide as a carpet. The yeti chases it with a net, but the **butterfly** lands on the yeti's nose and fans him to sleep."],"膝":["knee","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} trips on the root of a *lacquer tree* under the full *moon* and bangs his **knee**. It swells up like a red balloon and glows sticky and shiny. He sits down groaning, and his sheep queue up to bounce on his **knee** like a trampoline, baa-ing with delight."],"姚":["Yao","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, where a *woman* hands her a *cracked shell* with a name scratched on it: **Yao**. On every landing someone else waves the same shell. The plumber is Yao, the baby is Yao, even the parrot squawks its name. The Yogi gives up and writes **Yao** on her own forehead."],"茂":["luxuriant","The {Magician} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and tall *grass* bursts out, so thick a gardener must hack it with a *pole axe*. It grows back **luxuriant** and green faster than he can chop. Soon the tower is a jungle, the most **luxuriant** in town."],"躯":["body","The {Cheerleader} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Museum}, where an ancient marble *torso* is wrapped in a *district map*. She copies every street onto her own **body** in marker, from her ankles to her ears, and cartwheels across the roof. Lost tourists come up and read directions off her **body**: \"Café? Left elbow, then down the shin.\""],"吏":["minor official","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and nearly squashes a tiny *clerk* at a desk in the sand. He is the **minor official** in charge of waves, stamping a permit for each one before it may break. The sea waits impatiently. She bribes him with an ice cream, and the **minor official** stamps the whole ocean at once."],"猿":["ape","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Mint} meets a *prowling dog* in a *long robe* who turns out to be an **ape**. It swings from the coin presses, counts gold with its toes, and steals her yoga mat. The **ape** then does a perfect handstand."],"寨":["stockade","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} and lands beside a *bare tree*, sharpened to a point. Then he sees a hundred more, standing shoulder to shoulder in a ring: a wooden **stockade**. Pirates peer over the top with spyglasses. His horse takes a run-up and leaps clean over the **stockade** into the pirates' lunch."],"恕":["to forgive","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and hears an *echo* from deep below: his *heart* is begging. He decides to **forgive** the robber who stole his hat. The echo repeats \"**forgive**!\" so loudly that the robber cries and hands back the hat."],"渠":["canal","The {Cheerleader} on the {Staircase} of the {Museum} grabs a shovel and digs a **canal** right through the exhibits, past mummies and dinosaurs. A *tree* sprouts beside the *canal* and gondolas glide under its branches. She chants from the prow of each boat, and the **canal** finally pours into the café, flooding the cappuccinos."],"戚":["relatives","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} hosts a family reunion: a *pole axe* to cut the cake and a bowl of *soybean* snacks. **Relatives** arrive by boat, by plane, by cannon. She cheers for each, but the **relatives** keep arriving until the roof collapses."],"辰":["fifth Earthly Branch","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair}, and on the fifth step a giant *clam* yawns open with a dragon curled inside, holding a clock that points to dragon-hour. \"I am the **fifth Earthly Branch**,\" it booms, and breathes on the candy floss. The Chef serves it chowder, and the **fifth Earthly Branch** demands a seat on the dodgems."],"舶":["ship","The {Baker} on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} watches an enormous *boat* sail into the harbour, towed by a single *white dove* tugging a ribbon. It is an ocean-going **ship**, heavier than the fort, piled with flour sacks. The dove lands on his hat, exhausted. The Baker bakes the dove a loaf and the whole **ship** a cake."],"颁":["to issue","The {Baker} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} slices an enormous *cut cake* and slips a *page* of certificates into every slice. He **issues** them to every guest by catapult: best moustache, loudest sneeze, most polite pigeon. The butler, who is **issued** only a crumb and a blank page, sulks behind the chimney."],"惶":["anxiety","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Swamp} hut watches the swamp king's *golden crown* slip from his hand and sink into the mud. His *standing heart* pounds with **anxiety**, leaping out of his chest to pace up and down. Frogs croak with **anxiety** too. He dives in, and the crown bobs up, wearing a frog."],"狐":["fox","The {Hunter} on the {Staircase} of the {Pool} spots a *prowling dog* carrying a *melon*. It is actually a **fox** in disguise! It cracks the melon, eats it and winks. The **fox** dives into the pool and swims away with the hunter's hat."],"讽":["to satirize","The {Firefighter} in the {Basement} of the {Jungle} hut hears a *small speech bubble* blown in on the *wind*: \"Nice hose, hero, did it come with water?\" The parrots **satirize** her rescue, imitating her helmet. She sprays them, and they **satirize** that too."],"笨":["dumb","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} and plants *bamboo* upside down, *roots* waving in the air like hair. The crowd laughs: what a **dumb** idea. But the bamboo grows down, then sideways, then loops into a roller coaster. He rides it proudly, still looking **dumb**, waving a baguette at the screaming crowd."],"袍":["gown","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} with a mysterious *parcel*. Inside is one folded *shirt*, which he shakes out, and it keeps unrolling into a long silk **gown** that trails down twelve flights. He sweeps up the stairs like a queen, the hem dusting every step, and hides his cannonballs in the **gown**'s secret pockets."],"嘲":["to ridicule","The {Chef} on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} enters a *royal court* where a giant *mouth* hangs over the throne. It cackles and **ridicules** every dish he serves: \"Soggy! Bland! Is this soup or bathwater?\" So the Chef feeds it a ghost chili. The mouth turns tomato red, and now the whole court **ridicules** the mouth."],"啡":["coffee","The {Firefighter} on the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house unrolls her hose, but instead of water it gushes hot black *coffee*. She sprays the whole lake until it steams and smells of roasted beans. The fish start swimming at double speed, the ducks quack in fast-forward, and a frog orders a **coffee** with oat milk. Nobody in town sleeps that week: too much **coffee**."],"泼":["to splash","The {Pirate} on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} stands on a *launch pad* and fires a barrel of *water drops* into the sky. It bursts overhead and he **splashes** the enemy ship, the seagulls and his own captain. Delighted, he loads another barrel and **splashes** the fort's flag until it droops like a soggy sock."],"衔":["hold in mouth","The {Shepherd} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} to a busy *crossroads* of traders, where his sheepdog sits with *gold coins* stacked between its teeth. It refuses to drop them; it will only **hold in mouth**. The bankers hold coins in their mouths too, and every deal is mumbled. Even the Shepherd tries to **hold in mouth** his crook."],"倦":["weary","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint} and finds a *standing person* reading an endless *scroll* of coin numbers aloud. He has been reading for nine years, yawning between digits, utterly **weary**. The Juggler offers to help, reads two lines, and collapses snoring onto a pile of pennies, equally **weary**."],"涵":["to contain","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} holding a magic bottle that can **contain** anything. He uncorks it and *water drops* from the whole flooded hall rush in: the bathtub, the fountain, the goldfish, a rubber duck. Then he tries to **contain** the butler, who waves furiously from inside the glass."],"雀":["small bird","The {Cheerleader} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Ice Rink} and spots a *sparrow* skating in circles. She lifts it with a gentle *pinch*, the tiniest **small bird** in the world, no bigger than a thimble. It trills a cheer, does a triple axel, and the crowd tosses roses to the **small bird**, burying it completely."],"旬":["ten-day period","The {Shepherd} counts sheep on the {Staircase} of the {Dunes} lighthouse, one per step, and each step is *ten days* long. He marks off a **ten-day period** on the wall with chalk, then another. By the top of the stairs his beard has grown into the sand, and he has counted thirty **ten-day periods** and only four sheep."],"僵":["rigid","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} meets a *standing person* just back from a frozen *borderland*, stiff as a plank. He is completely **rigid**: arms out, legs locked, frost in his eyebrows. The Juggler tips him over and uses him as a bridge between two stands, and the fans walk across, the man still **rigid** as a board."],"撕":["to tear","The {Sailor} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} grabs a honeycomb with his *helping hand* and starts *tearing* it in half. Honey sprays everywhere. The bees **tear** his trousers in revenge, then his hat, then his map. He jumps into the river, his clothes **torn** to ribbons, buzzing all the way."],"肢":["limb","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} sees a *branch* glowing under the *moon*. It grows an elbow, then a wrist, then fingers: a new **limb**! It waves, grabs his reins, and steers the horse. By dawn the hive has sprouted a **limb** on every side, and it crawls away like a giant honey spider."],"垄":["crop row","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut hears a rumble, and a *dragon* bursts through the floor, ploughing the *soil* with its tail. It leaves a long raised **crop row**, then another, as neat as stripes on a shirt. She plants carrots along each **crop row**, and the dragon waters them with gentle steam."],"夷":["eastern tribes","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} watches a *bowman* paddle ashore in a canoe painted with rising suns. He is a warrior of the **eastern tribes**, and his arrows trail ribbons of sea mist. More canoes follow, drumming, and the **eastern tribes** set up camp on the stairs, offering the Yogi grilled fish."],"逸":["to escape","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and catches a *rabbit* digging a tunnel under her mat. It bolts down the coastal *road*, ears flapping, determined to **escape**. She chases it in lotus position, bouncing like a beach ball, but it **escapes** onto a passing surfboard and waves goodbye."],"茅":["reeds","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} and waves his wand over the *grass* in a window box. It shoots up into tall **reeds**, sharp as a *spear*, rustling and whistling. He weaves them into a thatched roof in seconds, and the tower now wears a hat of **reeds** that birds immediately move into."],"侨":["emigrant","The {Cheerleader} on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} meets a *standing person* tottering on enormous *stilts*, a suitcase in each hand. He is an **emigrant** who walked across the ocean on stilts to open a café abroad. She cheers his arrival, the cats help unpack, and the **emigrant** serves tea from the top of his stilts."],"舆":["the public","The {Yogi} on the {Staircase} of the {Museum} sets up a soapbox and asks a question about dinosaurs. Instantly **the public** floods in: tourists, schoolkids, grannies, a mime, all shouting opinions at once. They vote, argue, and carry her up the stairs on their shoulders. Whatever she says, **the public** answers louder."],"窑":["kiln","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Tower} to a hot *cave* at the top where a glowing **kiln** roars. She slides a *clay jar* inside, then meditates on the doorstep while it bakes. The jar pops out shiny and blue, then the **kiln** fires out a whole tea set, and finally her sandals, glazed."],"涅":["black dye","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} into a pit of *black mud* bubbling with *water drops*. He climbs out dyed jet black from head to toe; the perfect disguise. The yeti, jealous, jumps in too and comes out soaked in **black dye**. Now two black ninjas sneak around, and one of them is enormous and covered in **black dye**."],"蒲":["cattail","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} through tall *grass* and finds a fuzzy brown *cattail* growing out of the diving board. He snaps the **cattail** and uses it as a microphone, then a sword, then a torch. The swimmers find him sword-fighting the lifeguard with a **cattail** in each hand."],"谦":["modest","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} carries *two sheaves* of golden wheat, and a *small speech bubble* floats above her saying \"oh, it's nothing.\" She has just saved the economy, but she is so **modest** she hands the medals to a pigeon. The bankers cheer; she bows, too **modest** to look up."],"杭":["Hangzhou","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and finds a weeping willow *tree* wearing a scholar's *high collar*. It points him to a misty lake with pagodas and tea fields: he has landed in **Hangzhou**! He paddles across West Lake in a teacup, and the willow sighs poems about **Hangzhou** all night."],"噢":["oh, I see","The {Ghost} floats over the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} and gets lost in a hedge *maze*, wailing round and round. At last a giant *mouth* in the hedge explains: \"Turn left at the gargoyle.\" \"**Oh, I see**!\" says the ghost, and floats straight through the walls anyway. The mouth groans; the ghost waves: \"**Oh, I see**!\""],"弊":["drawback","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and bandages a leaking sandcastle with *rags* and *grass*. It holds, but the **drawback** is that every crab moves into it and pinches him. Another **drawback**: the grass sprouts and the whole castle walks away like a hairy turtle."],"勋":["merit","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Dunes} hotel watches an *employee* with a *strong arm* lift a falling camel off a tourist. The manager pins a giant gold star on him for **merit**. The camel, impressed, gives him its hump too. The employee flexes, and the **merit** star blinds three passing pilots."],"刮":["to scrape","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} grabs a *standing knife* and starts to **scrape** moss off the slides. The moss fights back, sticking out a long green *tongue*. She **scrapes** harder, sparks fly, and the slide becomes so slippery that swimmers shoot off the end into the sky."],"郊":["suburbs","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} sits with *crossed legs* and looks past the city to a green *hillside* in the **suburbs**. He juggles a cat, a cushion and a lawnmower, then hops a bus. In the **suburbs** everyone mows lawns in unison, and the cat moves into a garden gnome."],"凄":["mournful","The {Cheerleader} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} watches *icicles* grow on a fisherman's *wife* as she waits for his boat in the snow. Her song is so **mournful** that the seagulls weep and the waves stop to listen. The Cheerleader tries a chant, but it comes out **mournful** too, all minor keys."],"捧":["to cup","The {Pirate} in the {Basement} of the {Jungle} temple reaches a *helping hand* toward a glowing *tribute* of rubies laid before the stone idol. They are blazing hot, so he has to **cup** them in both palms, blowing and hopping like a man holding soup. The idol frowns; he gently **cups** the rubies back onto the altar and tiptoes out."],"浸":["to soak","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Inn} into a bathtub as big as a lake, full of warm *water drops*. He decides to **soak** for just a minute, still juggling. Hours pass. His fingers wrinkle into raisins, his juggling balls swell into watermelons, and the innkeeper tops up the tub so he can **soak** until breakfast."],"砖":["brick","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} pavilion watches a swan pedal a giant *spindle* that spins a lump of *stone* into a perfect red **brick**, then another, then a thousand. The swans honk orders and lay them in rows. Before he can whistle for his horse, the last **brick** clicks into place and he is walled in."],"鼎":["cauldron","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} finds a great bronze **cauldron** on three sturdy *cauldron legs*, a huge painted *eye* blinking on its belly. It bubbles with soup. He dips a spoon in, and the **cauldron** stands up, winks, and stomps upstairs into the ring to challenge the champion, spilling broth on every punch."],"篮":["basket","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} with a woven *bamboo* **basket**, and a fussy *inspector* blocks her way with a magnifying glass. He rummages through it: a kitten, a lobster, a trumpet, the duke's missing crown. The inspector faints from surprise, so she folds him up neatly and pops him into the **basket** as well."],"蒸":["to steam","The {Jockey} on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} lodge stuffs *grass* into a bamboo basket over a bonfire, and *rising steam* billows up into clouds. He means to **steam** a few dumplings, but the cloud swallows his horse. When it clears, the horse is pink, puffy and smells of pork buns. Monkeys queue to **steam** their bananas."],"饼":["flat cake","The {Baker} in the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} rolls out dough as wide as the ring and slaps it onto *linked rails* glowing like a grill. With a *side dish* of jam, it sizzles into a **flat cake** that the boxers practise their punches on, flattening it thinner and thinner. By the final bell the **flat cake** is so thin you can read through it."],"亩":["mu","The {Magician} in the {Basement} of the {Pool} lifts the *lid* off a shoebox and a tiny *rice field* unrolls across the floor, growing and growing until it covers exactly one **mu** of land. Farmers in straw hats wade in, planting seedlings between surprised swimmers. He measures it with his wand: one **mu**, not a grain more."],"肾":["kidney","The {Sheriff} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} clutching a prize from the ring toss: a squishy bean-shaped balloon, a giant **kidney**, glowing pink under the *moon*. It bounces off the carousel, the dodgems and the strongman. Children chase it shrieking, and the Sheriff lassoes his runaway **kidney** just before it floats over the Ferris wheel."],"陡":["steep","The {Dentist} in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} finds a *hillside* rising inside it so **steep** it goes straight up the wall. A *runner* in spiked shoes sprints up it, slides back down, and tries again. The Dentist drills toeholds for him, but every time he finishes, the hill gets even **steeper** and tips its hat."],"爪":["claw","The {Jockey} in the {Basement} of the {Tower} hears scratching, and a giant *talon* punches through the brick wall, groping for his cap. It is an eagle's **claw**, as big as a garden rake. He bravely offers it a sausage. The **claw** takes it delicately, then shakes his hand with great politeness and withdraws, crunching."],"兔":["rabbit","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and a *rabbit* in swimming goggles springs out of the deep end. It does a perfect lap of backstroke, then steals his measuring tape and sews itself a striped swimsuit. By evening every **rabbit** in town is queuing at his shop, and he measures each **rabbit**'s ears."],"殷":["plentiful","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} holds up a polished *mirror body* as a heavy *war club* swings at her. The club's reflection jumps out as a second club, then a fourth, then a hundred, and each one turns into a plate of food as it lands. The feast is **plentiful**: dumplings, mangoes, roast ducks, far more **plentiful** than the inn can hold."],"贞":["chaste","The {Jockey} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} to visit an *oracle* in a striped tent. She stares into a cracked bowl and declares he must remain **chaste** and pure until he wins the Derby. He blushes, refuses every candy apple and every kiss-me booth, and the clowns crown him the most **chaste** jockey ever."],"荐":["to recommend","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} onto a pile of *grass*, and a *piggy bank* in his lap squeaks: \"I **recommend** gold!\" He buys gold and gets rich. \"I **recommend** tulips!\" He buys tulips and gets richer. Now he follows the pig everywhere, and the bankers line up to ask its advice."],"哑":["mute","The {Yogi} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} wins a *silver medal* in the silence championship. She opens her *mouth* to give a speech, and nothing comes out: she has gone completely **mute**. She mimes her thanks, the judges mime applause, and the steam room becomes so **mute** that you can hear the bubbles in the hot tub."],"炭":["charcoal","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a cellar heaped with black *charcoal*, coughing in the dust. Inspired, he sews himself a whole suit of **charcoal**, buttons and all, and strides upstairs like a walking shadow. Guests faint, the curtains get smudged, and the cat now has **charcoal** whiskers."],"坟":["grave","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair}'s haunted house and finds a **grave** of fresh mounded *soil*, its headstone covered in a skull *tattoo*. The earth rumbles, and a rickety roller coaster rises out of the **grave**, screaming. She blasts it with her hose, and the soggy ride rattles off toward the dodgems."],"眨":["to blink","The {Jockey} in the {Basement} of the {Spa} kneels by his bike's *flat tyre* when a giant *eye* opens on the wall and begins to **blink**. Each **blink** puffs out a gust of steam like a bellows, and the tyre inflates, wheeze by wheeze. He thanks the eye; it winks, and the tyre bursts."],"搏":["to fight","The {Baker} on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} reads a *proclamation* nailed to the door: whoever wins the duel owns the bakery. He rolls up his sleeves, grabs a baguette in his *helping hand*, and starts to **fight** a knight in full armour. They **fight** step by step down the staircase, crumbs and sparks flying, until the knight surrenders for a croissant."],"咳":["to cough","The {King} on the {Staircase} of the {Hut} opens his *mouth* to make a royal speech, and a hairy *wild boar* charges out. He begins to **cough**, and with every **cough** another snorting boar tumbles out and thunders down the stairs. Soon the hut is full of pigs, and the court doctor hands him a cough drop the size of a turnip."],"拢":["to draw together","The {Lifeguard} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} finds the scales of a *dragon* scattered across the floor like sequins. With a giant *helping hand* she begins to **draw together** every scale, sweeping them into a shimmering heap. They click into place, and the reassembled dragon purrs, rolls over, and helps her **draw together** the floating pool noodles."],"舅":["maternal uncle","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} into a kitchen where a burly *man* is pounding chilies in a huge stone *mortar*. It's his **maternal uncle**, his mum's brother, cooking his famous curry for forty backpackers. Fire alarms wail, the hostel cat sneezes, and the **maternal uncle** ladles out bowls that make everyone cry."],"昧":["dark","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lake} cabin just as the *sun* sinks behind a skinny *sapling*. It gets **dark**, then darker, until he can't find his own hat. He conjures a lamp: it lights up black. He conjures fireflies: they glow black too. Everything he summons comes out **dark**."],"擅":["be good at","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and starts tossing hay bales into a tall *silo* with one *helping hand*. Every bale sails in perfectly, swish. He is so **good at** it that the butler applauds, so the Sheriff tosses the butler in too. Turns out he is also very **good at** apologizing."],"爽":["bright and clear","The {Sheriff} in the {Basement} of the {Swamp} hut meets a *big man* wrapped in *crisscross* bandages, groaning. The Sheriff unwinds him like a mummy, and with every loop the fog lifts, until the swamp is **bright and clear** and sparkling. The frogs blink in the sunlight, and the big man stretches, feeling **bright and clear** for the first time in years."],"咖":["café","The {King} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} opens a **café** with a door shaped like a giant *mouth* and a menu that is one big *plus sign*: every order comes doubled. Double espresso, double cake, double cream. Guests in fluffy robes queue round the roof, and the King, wearing an apron over his robes, steams milk for the busiest **café** in town."],"搁":["to put","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} reaches a long *helping hand* into the *loft* to **put** away her flowerpots. Then she **puts** in the cat, the dog, the chickens and a startled postman, stacking them neatly like jars. The loft creaks, groans and finally bursts, and everything rains down onto the vegetable patch."],"禄":["official salary","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and finds a *small altar* holding a dusty *logbook* that records her **official salary**: one sardine a day. She complains so loudly that the altar rumbles and the page rewrites itself. Now her **official salary** is two sardines and a free swim."],"雌":["female","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} and finds a fierce *sparrow* standing on *this spot*, guarding three speckled eggs. She is a **female** sparrow who bosses the bees around like a general. The queen bee, also **female**, flies over, and the two ladies shake wings and order the Tsar to fetch worms."],"哨":["whistle","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a gallery where an old *portrait* has puckered its painted *mouth*. Every time someone tiptoes past, it blows a shrill **whistle**: wheeeet! The guards come running. The Sheriff glares at it; the portrait winks and blows the **whistle** again just to annoy him."],"巩":["to secure","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} hut sees a crack running up the wall and hammers in a wooden *brace* to **secure** it. Then she braces the wobbly table, the leaky boat and the dog, who keeps trying to walk off. When the storm hits, everything she **secured** stands firm while the roof sails away."],"绢":["thin silk","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint} and a fat *silkworm* spins a glimmering *silk thread* round and round until it forms a sheet of **thin silk**. It is so light he juggles it like a cloud. The mint starts printing money on it, and banknotes of **thin silk** float out of the windows like kites."],"螺":["snail","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} and spots a *bug* tucked in a *yarn pile*, wound up in spirals: a **snail**. It inches up the steps leaving a glittering trail. She cheers it on with her whistle, but three days later the **snail** has only reached step four and asks for a lift."],"裹":["to wrap","The {Gardener} in the {Basement} of the {Warehouse} takes off her *robe* to **wrap** a giant *fruit* as a birthday present: a melon the size of a sofa. Then she **wraps** a pineapple, a bicycle and finally herself, rolling around in tape and ribbon until only her nose pokes out."],"昔":["the past","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} by the {Beach} hangs strips of *sun-dried meat* on a line. One sniff of the salty smell whisks him back into **the past**: he is a boy again, chasing lambs, losing his sandals in the waves. He bites a strip and the whole beach turns sepia, every gull flying through **the past**."],"轩":["high pavilion","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} hauls a creaking *cart* loaded with a *drying rack* up to a **high pavilion** perched on stilts above the city. He pegs freshly printed banknotes on the rack to dry in the wind. They flap like flags, and the pigeons start a bank in the **high pavilion**."],"谬":["erroneous","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} and a *small speech bubble* flaps past on *soaring wings*, squawking \"The moon is made of cheese!\" Totally **erroneous**. He catches it in his hat, but another flies out: \"Fish can knit!\" The common room fills with flapping, **erroneous** bubbles."],"谍":["spy","The {Dentist} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} hidden under a costume of *leaves*, whispering a *small speech bubble* into his tooth microphone. He is a **spy**, here to steal the yeti's toothbrush. Then he discovers the yeti, also under leaves, is a **spy** too, spying on him."],"龟":["turtle","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} finds a **turtle** using a *bent knife* to scratch a *lightning bolt* onto its shell. It revs up and zooms across the tiles like a race car, leaving skid marks. The patients below hear thunder; the **turtle** wins every race and still waits politely for its appointment."],"媳":["daughter-in-law","The {Shepherd} on the {Staircase} by the {Beach} meets a *woman* gasping for *breath*, dragging eleven suitcases up the steps: his new **daughter-in-law**, moving in with the family. She drops the bags and blows one huge breath that inflates every beach ball on the shore. The **daughter-in-law** has arrived, and so has her tuba."],"姜":["ginger","The {Juggler} on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} juggles a *sheep* and a knobby root, while a *woman* shouts that it is **ginger**. She grates it into the sheep's mouth mid-air. The sheep turns red, sneezes fire and rockets over the stadium like a woolly firework. The crowd chants for more **ginger**."],"瞎":["blindly","The {Shepherd} on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} gets a buzzing *pest* in his *eye* and staggers **blindly** about, flapping his crook. He walks **blindly** off the edge, bounces off a café awning, lands in the fountain, and the tourists, thinking it is a show, throw coins."],"冤":["injustice","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} finds a *rabbit* trapped under a *cloth cover* accused of stealing carrots, but the real thief is a goat chewing nearby. Such **injustice**! She whips off the cloth, the rabbit protests with a placard, and the two march round the roof chanting against the **injustice**."],"鸦":["crow","The {Yogi} on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} meets a big black *bird* with a gleaming vampire *fang*: a **crow** with attitude. It caws, snatches her fluffy towel and flies off cackling. The **crow** perches on the chimney wearing it like a cape, and the spa guests applaud the new mascot."],"蓬":["disheveled","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Jungle} temple and has a *chance meeting* with a lion lounging in tall *grass*. Both scream. The pirate's hair shoots up in every direction, utterly **disheveled**, his beard knotted like seaweed. The lion's mane is **disheveled** too; they borrow a comb from a passing monkey."],"巷":["lane","The {Shepherd} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} into a narrow *alley*, a **lane** so tight his sheep have to walk in single file. Behind him the whole flock squeezes in, bleating, wool scraping both walls. The **lane** fills from end to end with fluff like toothpaste, and the stadium cheers when they pop out the other end."],"琳":["gem","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Inn} into a tiny indoor *grove* where a *king* sits polishing a **gem** the size of an egg. It flashes so brightly the trees grow sunglasses. She blows her whistle; the king, startled, drops the **gem**, and it bounces down every step, lighting up the inn like a disco."],"栽":["to plant","The {Zookeeper} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Island} lighthouse with a *lance* and a baby *tree* under one arm. He stabs the lance into a flowerpot, drops the sapling into the hole and yells \"**Plant**!\" Seagulls bring him seeds, and he keeps going until the whole roof is **planted** like a jungle."],"沾":["to moisten","The {Jockey} gallops across the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} where a *fortune teller* sits reading the clouds. Suddenly *water drops* patter on her crystal ball, and she licks her thumb to **moisten** each page of her prophecy book. Soon the jockey, the horse and the whole future are **moistened** and dripping."],"诈":["to cheat","The {Jockey} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} like a *jack-in-the-box*, springs wobbling. A *small speech bubble* over his head says \"Free massage!\", but when guests lie down he steals their towels and slippers. Everyone shouts that he **cheats**, and the spa bans him for **cheating** at bingo too."],"斋":["to fast","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of a hut on the {Island} beside a monk with a long *beard* and a *tattoo* of an empty bowl. Coconuts fall and fish leap into the monk's lap, but he won't eat a bite: he has sworn to **fast**. By day ten the jockey's stomach growls so loudly that he joins the **fast** just to annoy it."],"瞒":["to conceal","The {Magician} tiptoes down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} carrying a stolen cake. A giant painted *eye* on the wall follows him, so he drapes his cape over it to **conceal** what he is doing. He hides the cake inside his top hat, but forgets to **conceal** the crumbs in his moustache."],"彪":["tiger stripes","The {Baker} is painting the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} when a *crouching tiger* leaps out of a cardboard box. He swats it with a brush of black *bristles*, and every swipe leaves a dark band on its orange fur. The tiger admires its brand-new **tiger stripes**, and the café cats queue up for **tiger stripes** of their own."],"厄":["distress","The {Ghost} drifts up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and finds a *trapped man* wedged under a fallen bookshelf, waving a tiny white flag of **distress**. The ghost tries to lift the shelf, but its hands pass straight through. So it wails at the top of its lungs, and the whole village hears the call of **distress**."],"咨":["to consult","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} with a *queue* of bees stretching round the chimney. Each bee buzzes into his *mouth*, asking whether honey can be spicy. He has no idea, so he opens a fat encyclopedia to **consult** an expert, and the queen bee flies up to **consult** him about her crown."],"纺":["to spin","The {Firefighter} slides down the pole into the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, where a spinning wheel sits inside a chalk *square*. She feeds it a fluffy cloud, the wheel whirs, and out comes *silk thread* by the mile. She can't stop it: it **spins** and **spins** until every plane upstairs is wrapped like a parcel."],"罐":["jar","The {Gardener} lifts the {Trapdoor} beside the {Swan Pond} and finds a *heron* stuck head-first in a *clay jar*. He tugs its legs, it honks, and the swans cheer him on. With a loud pop the bird flies free, still wearing the **jar** like a helmet, and now every swan wants a **jar** hat too."],"桶":["bucket","The {Tailor} digs a *tunnel* out of the {Basement} of her shack by the {Lagoon}, and seawater gushes in. She chops down a *tree*, stitches the planks together with her needle and makes a **bucket**. All night she bails, **bucket** after bucket, while curious fish swim through the tunnel to watch."],"壤":["soil","The {Robot} clanks into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} wearing an *embroidered robe* and dragging a sack of *soil*. It tips the dark earth across the floor, plants potatoes in the fresh **soil** and waters them with motor oil. By morning the basement is a farm, and the robe is caked in **soil** up to the collar."],"糕":["cake","The {Gardener} hauls a sack of *rice* up to the {Rooftop} of the {Tower}, followed by a hungry *lamb*. She grinds the rice, bakes a giant **cake** inside the chimney and sticks candles on top. Before she can sing, the lamb leaps in face-first and eats the whole **cake**, frosting and all."],"颂":["ode","The {Sailor} bursts out of a {Trapdoor} on the jetty of the {Lagoon}, right in the middle of the *town square*. He unrolls a *page* as long as a sail and bellows an **ode** to his little rowing boat. Pigeons gather, fishermen weep, and the mayor orders the **ode** carved into the fountain."],"膨":["swollen","The {Pirate} stomps up a vine {Staircase} in the {Jungle} under a full *moon*. With every *drumbeat* from the village below, his belly puffs up a little more, until he is **swollen** like a beach ball. He floats off the steps and bobs over the treetops, his **swollen** belly booming like a drum."],"谐":["harmonious","The {Shepherd} leads his flock up the icy {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave}, and every sheep has a *small speech bubble* singing a different note. The yeti roars, then joins in, and suddenly they sing *all together*. The cave fills with such **harmonious** baaing that even the icicles chime along, perfectly **harmonious**."],"垒":["rampart","The {Lifeguard} spots a flood wave and dives into the {Basement} of the boathouse on the {Lake}. She grabs a *brick pile* and shovels *soil* against it with her flippers, building a **rampart** across the doorway. The waves crash, the ducks cheer, and her muddy **rampart** holds."],"咕":["gurgle","The {Gardener} on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} house finds an *antique* drinking fountain shaped like a giant *mouth*. She turns the brass tap and it doesn't spray: it just goes **gurgle**, **gurgle**, gurgle. Bubbles float out, and every swimmer below starts to gurgle along like a choir of frogs."],"隙":["crack","The {Shepherd} chases a lamb down a *hillside* onto the {Beach} and steps on a {Trapdoor} hidden in the sand. It splits with a loud **crack**, and he gets wedged in sideways. Through the narrow **crack** he spots crabs having a tea party, and the lamb squeezes in to join them."],"辣":["spicy","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} hugging a *bundle* of red *chili* peppers. She tosses them into the hot tub, and the water turns **spicy** at once. Guests leap out with steam whistling from their ears, and even the rubber duck breathes fire: far too **spicy**!"],"绑":["to tie","The {Baker} chases a map of his whole *country* that keeps blowing around the {Basement} of the {Hangar}. He catches it and winds *silk thread* round and round to **tie** it to a propeller. Then, overexcited, he **ties** up the flour sacks, his own shoes and his sleepy assistant, until nothing in the basement can move."],"宠":["to pamper","The {Chef} keeps a baby *dragon* in the {Basement} of his hut by the {Lagoon}, under a *roof* lined with silk pillows. He **pampers** it shamelessly: fresh fish on silver plates, bubble baths, foot rubs. The dragon burps a little flame of joy and demands to be **pampered** again at midnight."],"嘿":["hey","The {Hunter} climbs out of a chimney onto the {Rooftop} of a cabin by the {Lake}, face black with *soot*. Only his *mouth* shows, and he shouts \"**Hey**!\" at a passing boat. The fishermen think a talking chimney is calling them, so they yell \"**Hey**!\" back and paddle away fast."],"兑":["to exchange","The {Dentist} opens a {Trapdoor} in the floor of the {Waiting Room}, and up pops a *money changer* behind a cash drawer. Patients line up to **exchange** their pulled teeth for shiny coins. One grandpa **exchanges** all his false teeth at once and walks out rich, grinning a toothless grin."],"霉":["mold","The {Magician} sits on the soggy {Staircase} down to the {Lake} after a week of *rain*. His top hat has sprouted green fuzz. A *busy mother* rushes past with a mop, scrubbing furiously, but the **mold** grows faster than she cleans, and soon even the rabbit in the hat wears a little coat of **mold**."],"挫":["setback","The {Tsar} marches proudly across the {Warehouse} and falls straight through a {Trapdoor}. He lands on a *sitting pair* of guards eating soup, and his crown rolls away: a royal **setback**. A *helping hand* lowers a rope, he climbs halfway, then the rope snaps: another **setback**."],"稽":["to check","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut, tossing a *grain stalk* in one hand and a magnifying glass in the other. Farmers pass up whole sheaves, and he must **check** every kernel for beetles. He gets so fussy that he **checks** the seagulls' feathers too, and drops everything onto the sand."],"辐":["spoke","The {Firefighter} rolls a *cart* down the {Staircase} into the {Pool}, and its wheel collapses. She pulls chopsticks from a *full jar* and jams them between hub and rim as new **spokes**. The cart squeaks back up the steps on twenty wobbly **spokes**, dripping water everywhere."],"乞":["to beg","The {Cheerleader} finds a *beggar* living in the {Basement} of a {Beach} café. He holds out a seashell and **begs** for a single chip. She waves her pompoms and starts a chant, and soon the whole beach is **begging** on his behalf, until the seagulls drop him a mountain of chips."],"纱":["yarn","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} rolling a *pinch* of cotton between his fingers. It stretches into *silk thread*, then into thick **yarn**, then just keeps growing. By sunset he has lassoed every bathrobe on the washing line with one endless strand of **yarn**."],"裙":["skirt","The {Cheerleader} climbs a sandy {Staircase} up the {Dunes} and meets a grumpy *lord* whose *shirt* is so long it reaches his ankles. The wind catches it and he spins like a top. She cheers, and he realises his shirt has become a swirling **skirt**. Now every camel wants a **skirt** too."],"嘻":["giggle","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut, beating a *joy drum* for his sheep. Each beat tickles them, and they **giggle**. He covers his own *mouth* to stay serious, but the drum keeps thumping, and soon he is rolling across the roof, **giggling** until he falls off into the sand."],"哇":["wow","The {Wizard} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and lifts a glowing *jade tablet* to the sky. Fireworks burst out of it in the shape of bathtubs. Every guest in the hot pool below opens their *mouth* and shouts \"**Wow**!\", and the rubber ducks quack \"**Wow**!\" too.","wā"],"绣":["to embroider","The {Shepherd} lifts the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} and finds a sheep holding a needle in its hoof. It is **embroidering** a pink *blossom* onto every pillow with *silk thread*. The backpackers wake with flowers stitched onto their socks, and the sheep starts to **embroider** the shepherd's beard."],"杖":["staff","The {Jockey} falls through a {Trapdoor} in the {Hangar} and twists his ankle. A *tree* growing down there bends politely and snaps off a branch, handing him a *walking staff*. He hobbles out leaning on the **staff**, then uses the **staff** to whack the trapdoor shut behind him."],"塘":["pond","The {Tailor} sweeps the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} and spills a sack of *sugar* into a hole in the *soil* outside. It rains, the hole fills, and a sweet **pond** appears. Frogs leap in, ducks sip it like syrup, and by noon the **pond** is so sticky the frogs can't jump out."],"衍":["to spread out","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, right where four tunnels meet like a *crossroads*. A pipe bursts, *water drops* splash on his head, and the puddle starts to **spread out** down every tunnel. Calmly he lets his arms and legs **spread out** too, and floats away on his back."],"轴":["axle","The {Jockey} drives a *cart* down the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse}, bumping every step, until the **axle** snaps in two. The wheels roll away into a *sprouting field* and plant themselves. Next spring a forest of wheels grows there, each one spinning on its own little **axle**."],"攀":["to climb","The {Pirate} wants the treasure on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, so he bolts a giant *climbing frame* to the wall. He starts to **climb**, parrot on his head, cutlass in his teeth. Halfway up the frame wobbles, but he keeps **climbing**, reaches the top and finds only a pigeon's egg."],"膊":["upper arm","The {Baker} kneads dough on the {Staircase} of the {Fort} under the *moon*, so hard that his **upper arm** swells like a loaf. A herald reads a *proclamation*: whoever has the biggest **upper arm** becomes captain. The baker flexes, his sleeve bursts, and every soldier salutes."],"譬":["example","The {Pirate} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and meets a *pioneer* with a map. \"Show me how to find treasure,\" he growls. The pioneer's *speech bubble* fills with drawings: \"For **example**, dig here.\" He digs and finds a boot. \"Another **example**, here!\" Boot number two."],"斌":["refined","The {Baker} serves tea on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} to a huge *warrior* with a poem *tattoo* across his chest. The warrior lifts his cup with his little finger out, recites verse and bows: so **refined**! The baker, dusted in flour, tries to look **refined** too and pours the tea into his own shoe."],"祈":["to pray","The {Cheerleader} runs down the wooden {Staircase} to the {Beach} and drops her *axe* in front of a *small altar* built of shells. She kneels to **pray** for sunshine on the day of the big game. The clouds only rumble, so she **prays** louder, shaking her pompoms, until the sun pops out and sneezes."],"踢":["to kick","The {Tailor} naps on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut until a *lizard* crawls up her trouser leg. Her *kicking foot* goes wild: one **kick** sends the lizard flying over the sea. It lands on a surfboard, rides a wave back and dares her to **kick** it again."],"肆":["unrestrained","The {Sailor} bursts out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Beehive}, his *flowing locks* full of honey, waving a huge *writing brush*. He paints wild poems across every wall, splashing ink on the bees, totally **unrestrained**. The queen bee joins in, and soon the whole hive dances, **unrestrained**, until bedtime."],"坎":["pit","The {King} wanders into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and lets out an enormous *yawn*. The *soil* under his feet yawns back, opening into a deep **pit**, and down he tumbles, crown first. From the bottom of the **pit** he yawns again, and it gets even deeper."],"轿":["sedan chair","The {Juggler} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} on a *cart* with no wheels, carried by four cats on *stilts*. He waves from his **sedan chair** like an emperor while juggling teacups. The cats wobble, the **sedan chair** tips, and he lands face-first in a bowl of cream."],"棚":["shed","The {Pirate} and his *buddies* march up a vine {Staircase} in the {Jungle}, chop down one *tree* and hammer it into a **shed**. It has three walls and a leaky roof. When the rain comes they all squash inside the tiny **shed** with a parrot, a monkey and a very annoyed toucan."],"泣":["to sob","The {Cheerleader} stands on a *podium* on the {Beach} when a {Trapdoor} opens beneath it and drops her into the sand. She lands in second place and starts to **sob**. Her tears fall as *water drops* that fill a bucket, then a paddling pool, and a crab sits in the puddle and **sobs** along with her."],"屡":["repeatedly","The {Lifeguard} patrols the {Basement} of the {Museum}, where a *lying man* keeps sliding off a bench. A woman with a *tall bun* catches him again and again, **repeatedly**. The lifeguard blows her whistle **repeatedly**, the man slides off **repeatedly**, and the bun grows taller with every rescue."],"躁":["impatient","The {Zookeeper} waits by the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} for the morning *birdsong* to finish so he can feed the parrots. But the birds sing on and on. His *kicking foot* taps, stamps, then bangs the trapdoor: he is so **impatient**. The parrots copy him, stamping their claws, the most **impatient** choir in the world."],"邱":["surname Qiu","The {Cheerleader} leads a cheer on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Hostel}, which sits on a tiny *hillock* at the foot of a huge *hillside*. Her whole family joins in, shouting \"Q-I-U!\" because that is their name, **surname Qiu**. Sheep on the hillside bleat it back, and the mailman delivers every letter marked **surname Qiu** to the hostel."],"凰":["phoenix","The {Hunter} creeps up the {Staircase} of a hut in the {Swamp} and finds a *golden crown* resting on a *small table*. It bursts into flame, and out of the fire rises a **phoenix**, shaking ash off its wings. The hunter drops his net in awe, and the **phoenix** puts the crown on its own head and flies away."],"溢":["to overflow","The {Yogi} pops up through a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} carrying a *spilling dish* that never stops filling with *water drops*. He tries to hold it still, but it **overflows** onto his toes, then the sand, then the sea. Soon the whole ocean **overflows**, and surfers ride waves straight out of his little dish."],"椎":["vertebra","The {Jockey} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *tree* grows with a trunk made of knobbly bones. A *sparrow* hops up it, bone by bone, tapping each **vertebra** like a xylophone. The jockey's own spine starts to sing along, every **vertebra** clicking in tune."],"砸":["to smash","The {Zookeeper} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Spa}, a sweaty *headband* round his forehead and a *stone* in each hand. A nut that no monkey can open sits on the top step. He lifts the stone high and **smashes** it: crack! The monkeys cheer and start to **smash** coconuts, flowerpots and the spa's fancy mirrors."],"趟":["trip","The {Tailor} is a *runner* carrying clothes from the *attic* to the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar}, one shirt at a time. Up, down, up, down: each **trip** takes ten minutes. By dinner she has made three hundred trips, and the pilots beg her to take just one last **trip** with all their uniforms."],"帘":["curtain","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} into a dark *cave* where the money is counted. Customers keep peeking, so she hangs a beach *towel* across the opening as a **curtain**. A gust blows the **curtain** open, and a bat is sitting there counting coins."],"帆":["sail","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, which has floated out to sea in a flood. The *sail* on the chimney is ripped, so she ties a giant bath *towel* to the flagpole as a new **sail**. The wind fills it and the whole mansion races across the waves, its fluffy **sail** puffed out proudly."],"栖":["to perch","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels across the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut, where a *tree* sprouts from the chimney. At sunset a hundred parrots fly home to the *bird nest* at the top and **perch** in a row. There's no room left, so the cheerleader climbs up and **perches** too, squawking along."],"窜":["to flee","The {Tsar} lifts the {Trapdoor} by the {Swan Pond} and peers into a smoky *cave* where a mouse is roasting a *kebab*. Startled, the mouse **flees** with the kebab, and the tsar chases it round and round the pond. Then the swans see the tsar's crown flapping and they **flee** too, honking."],"丸":["ball","The {Wizard} stumbles down the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, juggling a tiny magic *pill*. He drops it, and it grows into a huge bouncing **ball** that thunders down every step. The butler dives aside, the chandelier swings, and the **ball** rolls out the front door and down the hill."],"斩":["to chop","The {Jockey} drags a carrot as tall as a horse down into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} and slaps it on a *chopping block*. Whack! He **chops** it in two with a cleaver. Then he gets carried away and **chops** the wardrobe, a broom and his own riding boots into neat slices."],"堤":["dike","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} café as the tide rises. She shovels *soil* into a long wall along the sand and marks its height with a *tick mark* on a stick. The sea crashes against the **dike**, the café stays dry, and she fills the cracks in the **dike** like cavities."],"塌":["to collapse","The {Tailor} lands a hot-air balloon on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa}, which is made of nothing but dried *soil*. A pigeon with *drooping wings* lands next to her. The roof sags, groans and **collapses**, and they drop straight into the hot tub. Then the walls **collapse** too, and everyone is bathing in mud."],"贩":["to deal in","The {Firefighter} slides down through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and finds a *rebel* selling *shells* from a suitcase. \"I **deal in** shells,\" he whispers, \"rare ones.\" The firefighter buys a shell that sings, and soon the whole mansion is crawling with people who **deal in** seashells."],"厢":["side room","The {Shepherd} climbs a *cliff* to the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} and finds a *lookout* tower with a little door. Behind it is a cosy **side room** with a sofa, tea and a sleeping sheep. He takes the best seat in the **side room** and watches the whole match through the window."],"掀":["to lift","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} beside a manhole cover. A *helping hand* reaches up and **lifts** it, and a sheep pops out with a wide *grin*. Then another hand **lifts** the whole roof like a lid, and the bankers below look up, blinking at the sky."],"喀":["coughing sound","The {King} relaxes in a steam bath on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} when a *guest* climbs in beside him. The steam goes up the guest's nose, and out of his *mouth* comes a dry **coughing sound**. The king copies it, the bath bubbles copy it, and the roof echoes with a royal **coughing sound**."],"乖":["well-behaved","The {Gardener} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Wine Cellar}, where a *thousand ants* sit in neat rows facing *north*. Not one wiggles. She drops a sugar cube, and still they sit, so **well-behaved**. She hands each ant a tiny gold star, and the snails nearby pretend to be **well-behaved** too, hoping for one."],"谜":["riddle","The {Magician} sits on the {Staircase} down to the {Beach} when a *lost traveller* stumbles up asking the way. The magician only answers with a *small speech bubble*: \"What has sand but never tells the time?\" The traveller scratches his head over the **riddle** for hours, while crabs queue up to hear the next **riddle**."],"捏":["to pinch","The {Ninja} sneaks onto the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} and scoops up a lump of *black mud*. With a *helping hand* from the yeti, she **pinches** it into a tiny snowman, then **pinches** its nose into a sharp point. The yeti laughs so hard that she pinches his furry cheek too."],"阎":["Yan","The {Yogi} meditates at the foot of the {Staircase} of the {Mansion}, beside an iron *gate* with the name **Yan** carved on it. A visitor creeps through and drops straight into a *trap pit*. From the bottom a voice booms: \"Who dares enter the house of **Yan**?\" The yogi does not even open one eye."],"滨":["shore","The {Baker} rows his boat to the {Rooftop} of the {Inn}, which now stands at the very edge of the sea. Waves splash *water drops* over the tiles. A *guest of honour* in a shiny sash steps out, and the baker serves him buns on the wet **shore**. A seal wants a bun too and flops up onto the **shore**."],"虏":["to capture","The {Lifeguard} hears splashing in the {Basement} of the {Pool} and finds a *tiger* doing backstroke. She flexes her *strong arm*, flings a rubber ring and **captures** it in one throw. The tiger sulks, wearing the ring like a necklace, while the swimmers cheer the great **capture**."],"匙":["key","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Beehive}, locked out. He has no **key**, only a honey *spoon*. He bends it, twists it, scratches a *tick mark* on the handle and jams it into the lock. Click! The spoon has become a **key**, and the bees invite him in for tea."],"芦":["reed","The {Lifeguard} walks down the {Staircase} into the {Pool} and finds it full of tall *grass* growing from the water. She pushes through the **reeds** to a hidden *door*. Behind it a frog plays a tune on a hollow **reed**, and the lifeguard blows her whistle along."],"苹":["apple","The {Pirate} climbs the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring}, where the floor is covered in *grass*. His opponent is a giant red **apple** wearing boxing gloves. One punch, and the pirate is *flat* on his back. The **apple** takes a bow, and the hungry crowd cheers and starts to eat it."],"卸":["to unload","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave} on the back of a tired *porter* loaded with sacks of wool. The porter groans and starts to **unload**: wool, two sheep, a sofa and finally the shepherd. The yeti helps **unload** the rest and builds itself a fluffy bed."],"沼":["pond","The {Jockey} rides into the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where *water drops* drip from the ceiling into a muddy **pond**. A *town crier* stands knee-deep, ringing his bell: \"Hear ye! Frogs wanted!\" Frogs arrive by the hundred, and the jockey's horse wades into the **pond** to join them."],"钥":["key","The {Yogi} skates in circles over a locked {Trapdoor} in the {Ice Rink}. He tries to bribe it with *gold coins*, but it won't budge. Then the *moon* drops a thin silver **key** through the skylight. He turns the **key**, the trapdoor swings open, and a line of penguins skates out."],"株":["tree trunk","The {Jockey} parks his horse on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, where a *tree* grows out of the diving board. He paints *red lacquer* round and round the **tree trunk** until it shines like a fire engine. The horse scratches its back on the wet **tree trunk** and comes away bright red."],"祷":["prayer","The {Dentist} kneels in the {Basement} of the {Tower} before a *small altar*. She sets down a *longevity peach* and whispers a **prayer** for healthy teeth across the land. The peach glows, rises into the air and starts brushing its own stone. Her **prayer** has worked."],"剖":["to cut open","The {Pirate} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} holding a fish with a *spitting mouth* that squirts seawater in his eye. He grabs a *standing knife* and **cuts open** the fish to find a treasure map inside. He **cuts open** a second fish and finds a second map, pointing back at the first."],"熙":["bright","The {Shepherd} lights a bonfire on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut, and the *embers* fly up into the night. Their *glow* spreads until the whole sky turns **bright** as noon. The sheep put on sunglasses, the owls complain, and the moon squints down at the **bright** little roof."],"哗":["clang","The {Hunter} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Water Park} with a crate of *fireworks*. He lights them, and instead of whooshing they rocket into the metal slides: **clang**! **Clang**! Every swimmer's *mouth* drops open, and a lifeguard bangs a saucepan to join the clanging."],"劈":["to hack","The {Pirate} and a bearded *pioneer* stand on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} hut, arguing over a coconut. The pioneer pulls out a huge *knife* and **hacks** it in two. The pirate wants a turn, so he **hacks** at the roof, the door and the palm tree until the whole hut is firewood."],"怯":["timid","The {Cheerleader} peeks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave}, her *standing heart* thumping like a drum. She is far too **timid** to shout a single cheer. When the yeti waves hello, she squeaks and dives for the *exit*, and the yeti, just as **timid**, hides behind an icicle."],"棠":["crab apple","The {Tailor} sews a *lampshade* on the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} when a small red **crab apple** drops into her lap from a pilot's pocket. She bites it, and it is so sour her face freezes in a *blank stare*. The pilot laughs, and she pelts him with **crab apples** all the way down the steps."],"胳":["arm","The {Gardener} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} under the *moon* when a *visitor* climbs up a wobbly ladder. He offers his **arm** to steady her, and she grips it so hard that his **arm** stretches like toffee. It stretches all the way up to the moon, and he waves at it."],"桩":["stake","The {Jockey} lands on the {Rooftop} of a sinking *farmstead* in the {Swamp}. Thinking fast, he cuts down a *tree* and hammers it into a sharp **stake** beside the chimney to prop the house up. It still sinks, so he hammers **stake** after stake, until the roof looks like a hedgehog."],"瑰":["precious stone","The {Gardener} weeds a flowerbed on the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} and digs up a glowing **precious stone**. At once a *ghost* swirls up and moans that it belongs to the *king*. The king himself arrives by ladder, and the three of them squabble over the **precious stone** until it rolls down the drainpipe."],"娱":["to amuse","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Museum} beside a *woman* who is a real *loudmouth*. She tells jokes to the statues, and the yogi tries hard not to be **amused**. Then she juggles a mummy's bandages, and even the dinosaur skeleton is **amused**, rattling with laughter."],"娶":["to marry","The {Cheerleader} hears music in the {Basement} of the {Museum}: a knight in armour wants to **marry** a *woman* in a painting. A *grabbing hand* pulls her out of the frame, he kneels, and the cheerleader throws confetti. The mummies weep with joy, and soon everyone wants to **marry** someone by midnight."],"沫":["foam","The {Magician} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort}, and *water drops* spurt up as high as a *treetop*. He waves his wand to stop them, but they turn to **foam**. White **foam** pours from every window, and the soldiers slide down the walls as if it were a bubble bath."],"嗓":["throat","The {Sailor} sings sea shanties in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} until his **throat** is raw. A friend pops a *mulberry* into his *mouth*, and it slides down cool and sweet. Now his **throat** is so smooth that his next high note shatters a plane's windscreen."],"蹲":["to squat","The {Dentist} sneaks onto the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} for a snack. She tucks in her *kicking foot* and **squats** low behind the chimney, nibbling *toast*. A row of pigeons **squats** beside her, begging for crumbs, and the security guard mistakes them all for gargoyles."],"焚":["to burn","The {Firefighter} rushes up the {Staircase} of the helter-skelter at the {Funfair} as a *campfire* below sets a *grove* of candyfloss trees alight. The sugar starts to **burn**, smelling of caramel. She sprays her hose, but it is full of lemonade, and the grove **burns** on in a fizzy pink glow."],"淘":["to wash","The {Tailor} stands on the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, swirling *pottery* bowls in a bucket of *water drops*. She means to **wash** away the mud, but gold sparkles appear at the bottom. Delighted, she **washes** every pot in the tower, then the stairs, then the bewildered mayor."],"嫩":["tender","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into a hot-dog stand. A *woman* there is cooking for a shouting *drill sergeant*. He bites a sausage so **tender** it melts, and his face goes soft too. He stops shouting, hugs everyone and says his heart is **tender** as well."],"韵":["rhyme","The {Yogi} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Dunes} playing *music* on a sand-filled flute. Every line he sings must **rhyme**, so he hands the camels *even shares* of words: \"sun\", \"fun\", \"run\". One camel tries \"banana\" and the whole song falls apart. The yogi glares until it finds a proper **rhyme**: \"bun\"."],"衬":["lining","The {Chef} climbs out of a {Trapdoor} at the {Funfair}, his *shirt* lined with candyfloss to keep him warm. He sticks his *thumb* inside to show off the fluffy pink **lining**. Then the rollercoaster whooshes past, the wind tears it out, and children chase his **lining** across the fairground, eating it."],"匈":["Hungary","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Club} and puffs out his *chest* to sing the anthem of **Hungary**. His chest swells bigger and bigger, until it is shaped like a map of **Hungary**, with a river down the middle. The teenagers below salute and ask for goulash."],"钧":["great","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of a palace in the {Dunes}, juggling *gold coins* while the sultan shares them out in *even shares*. Each coin weighs as much as a camel: truly **great**. He catches the last one, the roof cracks, and he sinks into the sand with a **great** thud."],"竖":["vertical","The {Sheriff} stands on a *podium* in the {Pool} when the {Trapdoor} under it springs open. Instead of falling, he shoots straight up, stiff as a flagpole, perfectly **vertical**. Swimmers stare as he hovers above them, and he refuses to come down until every diving board is **vertical** too."],"峻":["steep","The {Juggler} pops up through a {Trapdoor} at the top of the {Dunes} and sees a *mountain* so **steep** it leans backwards. A *handsome man* in climbing boots grins and starts up it. Halfway, the slope gets even more **steep**, and he slides down on his bottom, still grinning, still handsome."],"豹":["leopard","The {Baker} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and a *badger* jumps out, wanting to be fierce. The baker dips a *ladle* in chocolate and dabs spots all over its fur. Now it's a **leopard**! It prowls proudly around the bakery, roaring, until it licks itself and turns back into a badger, a very sticky **leopard**."],"捞":["to fish up","The {Lifeguard} leans off the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a giant net, because a *labourer* has dropped his lunchbox into the moat. A *helping hand* holds her ankles as she dips in to **fish up** the box. She also **fishes up** a boot, a bicycle and an angry eel."],"菊":["chrysanthemum","The {Juggler} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Museum} carrying a *handful of rice*. He throws it onto a patch of *grass*, and every grain bursts into a golden **chrysanthemum**. The curators gasp, the paintings sneeze, and the statues wear a **chrysanthemum** behind each ear."],"鄙":["despise","The {Baker} hides in the {Basement} of a {Beach} villa, where a snooty lord studies a *village plan*. He points at the farmers on the *hillside* and sniffs: \"I **despise** them, and their muddy boots.\" The baker throws a cream pie at him, and now the lord **despises** pastry too."],"魄":["soul","The {Pirate} falls through a {Trapdoor} in the {Fort} and lands on a sleeping *ghost*. With a yelp, his **soul** pops out of his chest as a *white dove* and flutters around the room. The ghost catches the bird in its hat and politely hands the pirate back his **soul**."],"兜":["pocket","The {Dentist} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Boathouse} and stretches her *legs*. Her trousers have a magic **pocket** on the knee. She pulls out a toothbrush, then a canoe, then a whole lighthouse, and finally a tiny fisherman who asks to go back into the **pocket**."],"哄":["coax","The {Hunter} kneels in the {Basement} of a hut by the {Lagoon}, where a baby crocodile is sulking. He puts his *joined hands* together, opens his *mouth* and sings a soft song to **coax** it out from under the bed. It works, so he **coaxes** the whole crocodile family out with marshmallows.","hǒng"],"颖":["clever","The {Yogi} sits in the {Basement} beneath the {Boxing Ring}, reading a single *page* of puzzles upside down. While the boxers above punch each other, he solves every one in a second: so **clever**. He folds the page into a paper boxer that wins the championship. Even the referee admits it is **clever**."],"镑":["pound","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar}, landing on a *roadside* stall that sells *gold coins*. Each coin is stamped with a crown and worth one **pound**. He buys a loaf with one, and the change is another **pound**, and another, until coins pour out like flour."],"屑":["bits","The {Shepherd} trips through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave} and smashes a framed *portrait* into tiny **bits**. A *lying man* on the sofa sweeps them up, but the yeti sneezes and blows the **bits** everywhere, gluing them into a new picture of a sheep."],"蚁":["ant","The {Yogi} lies in the {Basement} of a {Beach} hut when a *bug* marches in wearing a wig like a *judge*. It bangs a crumb and sentences the yogi to share his sandwich. It is a tiny **ant**, and a thousand more **ant** jurors carry the sandwich away."],"壶":["pot","The {Hunter} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, beside an old *scholar* holding a round teapot. The scholar tips the **pot**, and tea pours out without stopping, filling the pool. The swimmers float on their backs sipping, and the scholar says the **pot** is only half empty."],"怡":["pleased","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} to a wooden *stage* on the {Beach}, where a band plays only for him. His *standing heart* dances, his toes wriggle in the sand, and he grins: he is so **pleased**. The crabs clap their claws, also very **pleased**, and the band plays an encore."],"渗":["to seep","The {Sheriff} hides some *ginseng* roots under the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} ghost train. But it rains, and *water drops* begin to **seep** through the wooden boards. The ginseng tea **seeps** into the ghost train, and every skeleton suddenly feels young and dances out of the tunnel."],"秃":["bald","The {Tailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, trying to sew a wig for a man with a *bald head* that shines like a mirror. The sun bounces off it and blinds the swimmers. She plonks the wig on top, but a seagull steals it, and he is **bald** again, gloriously **bald**."],"迦":["Buddhist sound","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of a temple in the {Piazza}, where a monk walks a long *road* chanting. Each chant makes a *plus sign* of light in the sky, and the bells ring a deep **Buddhist sound**. The juggler hums along, and the pigeons coo the same **Buddhist sound**."],"旱":["drought","The {Hunter} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to find the cellar lake bone-dry. Up above, the *sun* has shone for a year, and the laundry on the *drying rack* is crisp as crackers. It is a terrible **drought**: the goldfish are sunbathing on rocks, and the hunter prays for rain to end the **drought**."],"哟":["oh","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort}, tying a *promise knot* in a rope. It slips, tightens round his toe, and his *mouth* pops open: \"**Oh**!\" He tugs harder, and the knot tightens on his other toe. \"**Oh**, oh, oh!\" The soldiers below think it's a song and join in."],"咸":["salty","The {Shepherd} trips down the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} with a sack of *salt* that bursts open. Salt pours over the counters and coins. The banker licks his finger, winces and says the money tastes **salty**. Now even the cash machine spits out **salty** notes."],"焉":["how","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} when a strange bird lands on the *goal line* painted across the roof. It asks: \"**How** do I get to the sky?\" The yogi points up. The bird blinks and asks, \"Yes, but **how**?\" and they sit there puzzling until dark."],"谴":["to reprimand","The {Cheerleader} hides in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} when a *dispatch rider* gallops in carrying a letter from the boss. A *small speech bubble* bursts out of it shouting, \"You dropped the gold!\" The boss arrives to **reprimand** her in person, and then **reprimands** the horse for muddy hooves."],"宛":["as if","The {Wizard} sits in the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, stirring a *rice bowl* with his wand. The rice floats up and swirls around the room, **as if** it were snow. Then he blows, and it drifts back down softly into the bowl **as if** nothing happened."],"稻":["paddy rice","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} straight into a flooded field of **paddy rice**. She pulls a *grain stalk* from the mud and scoops the kernels with a *rice scoop*. The ducks join in, planting rows of **paddy rice** with their beaks until the tower floor is a farm."],"铸":["to cast","The {Jockey} drops a pile of *gold coins* through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} into a bubbling furnace. He pours the melted gold into a mould shaped like a *longevity peach* and **casts** a golden fruit. It is so pretty that he **casts** a golden horse to match."],"锻":["to forge","The {Dentist} opens the {Trapdoor} by the {Swan Pond} and finds a sweaty *blacksmith* hammering *gold coins* on an anvil. Clang, clang: he **forges** them into a swan-shaped crown. The swans queue up, and he **forges** a crown for each one, plus golden braces for the dentist."],"伽":["phonetic ga","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} clock tower. A *standing person* below holds up a sign with a big *plus sign* on it, and every time it flashes the crowd yells the syllable **ga**. The juggler tosses balls in time: **ga**, ga, ga, until the pigeons shout it too."],"詹":["verbose","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, trapped under the *eaves* by a talkative bat. The bat explains his whole family tree, every cousin, in detail, for six hours: so **verbose**. The jockey falls asleep, wakes, and the bat is still going, even more **verbose** than before."],"毙":["to die","The {Baker} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach}, and the *twins* find a deep *grave* where an old pirate is said to **die** each night and come back at dawn. Sure enough, the pirate climbs out yawning, eats a bun, then lies down and pretends to **die** again with a dramatic groan."],"恍":["hazy","The {Hunter} wakes in the {Basement} of a hut in the {Swamp}, where a strange *light* drifts through the fog. His *standing heart* flutters, and everything looks **hazy**: the frogs wear hats, the mosquitoes play cards. He rubs his eyes, but the room stays **hazy** and the frogs wave."],"贬":["to demote","The {Baker} is called down to the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, where the boss swaps his golden *shell* badge for a bicycle with a *flat tyre*. He has been **demoted** from head baker to crumb sweeper. Then the boss accidentally eats a burnt bun and **demotes** himself."],"烛":["candle","The {Jockey} creeps down the {Staircase} of the {Pool} at night with a tiny *campfire* stuck on top of a wax stick: a **candle**. A *bug* flutters round and round the flame, dizzy. The jockey sneezes, the **candle** goes out, and the bug glows on its own to light the way."],"骇":["to startle","The {Hunter} rides a *horse* across the {Island} when a *wild boar* bursts out of a {Trapdoor} in the ground. The horse rears and neighs, completely **startled**, and the hunter lands in a palm tree. The boar, equally **startled**, dives back through the trapdoor and slams it shut."],"芯":["core","The {Shepherd} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} peeling an onion the size of a sheep. Layer after layer of *grass* comes off, and at the very centre he finds a beating *heart*: the onion's **core**. It whispers that it is shy, so he wraps the **core** back up in leaves."],"汁":["juice","The {Jockey} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} and squeezes an orange on a *cross*-shaped press. Sticky *water drops* dribble out as sweet **juice**. The bees swarm in, dunk their heads, and soon they are buzzing in zigzags, dizzy on **juice**."],"桓":["soapberry","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} beside the {Swan Pond} and sees a *tree* so wide it fills the *horizon*. Its berries are **soapberry** fruit, and when the swans peck them, bubbles foam everywhere. The hunter rubs a **soapberry** on his muddy boots and they come out sparkling."],"坊":["lane","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, looking down at a narrow **lane** of *soil* between rows of *square* houses. A fire engine is stuck in it, too wide to move. She lifts the houses one by one like boxes until the **lane** is wide enough to drive through."],"驴":["donkey","The {Lifeguard} leads a small grey *horse* up the {Staircase} of the {Museum}, but at the *door* it plants its hooves and won't budge. It is a stubborn **donkey**. She tries carrots, music and pleading, then gives up and buys the **donkey** its own museum ticket."],"朽":["rotten","The {Shepherd} hides in the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel}, leaning on an old *tree* trunk holding up the ceiling. He blows a *puff of breath* on it, and it crumbles like biscuit, completely **rotten**. The backpackers' beds drop down beside him, and the floorboards turn out to be **rotten** too."],"靖":["peaceful","The {Juggler} climbs out of a {Trapdoor} in the middle of the {Boxing Ring}, ready for a fight. But *moss* covers the ropes and the old *podium*, and the boxers are napping in their corners. Everything is so **peaceful** that he juggles feathers instead, and the crowd hums a **peaceful** lullaby."],"佣":["to hire","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of a hut by the {Lagoon}, leaking water everywhere. He decides to **hire** help, and a *standing person* climbs up with a *bucket*. Each time she bails, the yogi pays her one coconut, and soon he has to **hire** her whole family."],"汝":["thou","The {Robot} clanks into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a *woman* sits beside a fountain of *water drops*. It bows and speaks in old poetic style: \"**Thou** art fair.\" She giggles and replies, \"And **thou** art rusty.\" The robot blushes and squirts oil."],"碌":["busy","The {Lifeguard} rushes past the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, so **busy** she cannot stop: hauling *stone* blocks, filling in her *logbook*, blowing her whistle, rescuing a duck. She runs in circles until the trapdoor opens and swallows her. Even underground she stays **busy**, scribbling notes."],"迄":["until","The {Cheerleader} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} onto a long dusty *road* where a *beggar* is walking. She cheers him on, step after step, **until** he reaches the sea. Then he keeps walking **until** the waves reach his nose, and she hands him a snorkel."],"冀":["Hebei","The {Juggler} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} wearing a *strange mask* and pointing *north*. \"To **Hebei**!\" he shouts, and he juggles his way up the coast past Beijing. When he arrives, everyone in **Hebei** wears the same mask and juggles back."],"荆":["chaste tree","The {Juggler} bounces on the {Rooftop} above the {Boxing Ring}, juggling sprigs of purple **chaste tree** blossom. He loses his balance and lands in the town *stocks*, wedged among tall *grass*. The boxers below wave branches of **chaste tree** at him like fans, and bees buzz round his trapped head."],"崔":["Cui","The {Tsar} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room}, which sits on a *lofty peak* above the clouds. He plants a flag that reads **Cui**, the family name of everyone who lives up here. Snow falls, the flag freezes, and goats from the whole mountain come to bleat \"**Cui**!\" at the top of their voices."],"雁":["wild goose","The {Yogi} sits by the {Trapdoor} at the edge of the {Mansion}'s *cliff* when a *wild goose* waddles out of it, honking. Behind it come a hundred more, in a perfect V. The yogi joins the end of the line, flapping his arms, and the leading **wild goose** carries him south with the other **wild goose** travellers."],"绅":["gentry","The {Sheriff} rides the Ferris wheel up to the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair}, where the **gentry** are having a picnic in top hats. Their sashes are made of *silk thread* and pinned with a golden *skewer*. They serve him a single grape on a silver tray, and he decides he would make fine **gentry** himself."],"珊":["coral","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion}, which has sunk to the bottom of the sea. The sea *king* swims up holding a *bamboo book* whose pages have turned to pink **coral**. Fish nibble the words, and the sheriff arrests a crab for stealing a chapter of **coral**."],"榜":["list of names","The {Baker} rushes into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} where a *list of names* hangs on a *tree* growing beside the *roadside* door. He scans the **list of names** for the winners of the cake contest. His name is last, so he bakes a giant cake, nails it to the tree and adds himself to the top of the **list of names**."],"诵":["to recite","The {Sailor} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Lagoon} jetty and stands at the mouth of a *tunnel*. He **recites** a sea poem, and each line floats out as a *small speech bubble* that echoes down the tunnel. The fish learn every word and **recite** it back to him, bubbling."],"傍":["near","The {Baker} hides by the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar}, standing very **near** a *standing person* who is selling buns at the *roadside*. He creeps closer and closer, until he is so **near** that their noses touch. Then he whispers: \"Your buns are too small,\" and drops through the trapdoor."],"彦":["accomplished","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} to greet a *gentleman* who can paint, sing, fence and bake, all at once. He is so **accomplished** that he juggles the yogi's teapots while reciting a sonnet. The yogi tries to look **accomplished** too and stands on his head, then falls over."],"醇":["alcohol","The {Chef} wobbles down the {Staircase} of the {Casino} hugging a *wine jug* for the *feast*. A drop of strong **alcohol** splashes on the roulette wheel, and it spins faster and faster. The gamblers sniff the air, giggle, and the whole casino sways, dizzy with **alcohol** fumes."],"笛":["flute","The {Dentist} sits on the wooden {Staircase} down to the {Beach}, carving a stick of *bamboo* into a **flute**. She blows a note, and a *sprouting field* of seaweed pops up from the sand to dance. She plays faster, and crabs line up to have their claws drilled into tiny **flutes** too."],"禽":["fowl","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} with her pompoms, and a flock of *fowl* follows her, flapping and clucking. Hens, ducks and one confused goose form a pyramid on the landing. The guests cheer the dancing **fowl**, and the innkeeper serves breakfast to every **fowl** in the building."],"勿":["do not","The {Wizard} stands over the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool}, waving a red *pennant* that says **do not**. **Do not** dive, it says; do not splash, do not open the trapdoor. Then he trips, the trapdoor bursts open, and a whale leaps out."],"娟":["graceful","The {Juggler} tiptoes across the {Rooftop} of the {Mint}, where a *woman* dances among glittering coins. She spins on one toe, light as a *silkworm*'s thread, so **graceful** that the coins pause mid-air to watch. The juggler tries to copy her and falls into a bucket, the least **graceful** moment in history."],"瞄":["to take aim","The {Magician} crouches on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café}, closing one *eye* to **take aim** at a mouse hiding in a pot of *young crop*. He flicks his wand, but the cats leap first. All twenty of them **take aim** at the mouse, and the mouse takes aim at the cheese."],"幢":["building counter","The {Jockey} rides through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swamp} and counts the houses on stilts: one **building counter**, two, three. Each **building counter** is marked by a *towel* hung from its roof. A *schoolkid* paddles past, laughing, and swaps the towels around so he has to count all over again.","zhuàng"],"寇":["to plunder","The {King} rows into the {Boathouse} and finds bandits dropping through the {Trapdoor} to **plunder** his treasure. They tear off the *roof*, grab golden oars and crowns and **plunder** even his rubber duck. The king splashes after them shouting, but they sail away laughing."],"睹":["to observe","The {Dentist} hides in the {Basement} of the {Pool}, pressing one *eye* to a peephole to **observe** a *busy man* who is polishing every tile with a toothbrush. She takes notes, then **observes** him brushing a duck's teeth too. She hires him on the spot."],"贿":["bribery","The {Hunter} sits in the {Waiting Room} as a sly man pops up from the {Trapdoor} *holding meat* in one hand and a pearly *shell* in the other. He slides them to the receptionist: pure **bribery**, to jump the queue. She takes the meat but throws the shell, and everyone boos the **bribery**."],"踩":["to step on","The {Tsar} stomps into the {Basement} of a hut on the {Island}, where a *fruit picker* has left mangoes all over the floor. The tsar's *kicking foot* comes down and **steps on** one: splat! Juice flies. He slips, slides and **steps on** every mango in the room."],"霆":["clap of thunder","The {Tailor} sews on the {Staircase} beside the {Boxing Ring} as *rain* pours into the open *courtyard*. Suddenly a **clap of thunder** booms so loud her needle flies into the ring and knocks out the champion. The crowd roars like a second **clap of thunder**."],"呜":["whimper","The {Wizard} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, where a soggy *crow* opens its *mouth* and lets out a sad **whimper**. Its feathers are wet. The wizard dries it with a hot spell, but singes its tail, and the crow gives an even longer **whimper**."],"拱":["to cup hands","The {Gardener} kneels in the {Basement} of a hut by the {Lagoon} and puts his *joined hands* together to **cup hands** under a dripping pipe. A *helping hand* from his neighbour **cups hands** below his, and soon they have a tower of cupped hands holding a goldfish."],"妃":["imperial consort","The {Firefighter} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of a palace on the {Lake} to rescue the **imperial consort**. The *woman* has tied her silk sashes into a *coiled rope* and swings down past the firefighter. She saves herself, the emperor and a cat, the most daring **imperial consort** ever."],"蔑":["to belittle","The {Magician} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} to perform his best trick. The yeti yawns, picks a blade of *grass* from its teeth and says, \"Is that all?\" It loves to **belittle** everything. The magician turns it into a snowman, which goes on to **belittle** the snow."],"谕":["decree","The {Yogi} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} in a *dugout canoe*. A *small speech bubble* floats out of the emperor's statue: a royal **decree**. \"Everyone must paddle!\" So the visitors climb into canoes and row across the marble floor, obeying the **decree**."],"缚":["to bind","The {Firefighter} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and lands on a royal *proclamation* floating in the water. A spider swims up and **binds** her ankles with *silk thread*. She wriggles free and uses the thread to **bind** the spider to a lilo."],"诡":["sly","The {Gardener} sneaks down to the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *teetering man* is whispering a *small speech bubble* into the ear of a potted plant. He is a **sly** fox in a suit. He swaps all the waiting tickets so he goes first. The plant winks: just as **sly**."],"篷":["sail","The {Pirate} climbs a vine {Staircase} in the {Jungle} and has a *chance meeting* with a panda weaving *bamboo* into a giant **sail**. Together they lash it to a hollow log, and the wind fills the **sail**. Off they rush through the trees, steering past monkeys."],"淹":["to flood","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} when a *sudden flash* of lightning splits the sky. *Water drops* pour down until the lawn, the gardens and the ground floor **flood**. The rising water lifts him, still cross-legged, and he floats on as the whole valley **floods**."],"腕":["wrist","The {Wizard} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} clutching a *rice bowl* in the light of the *moon*. He lands and twists his **wrist**. He waves his wand to heal it, but his **wrist** now spins like a propeller and stirs the rice into soup."],"煮":["to boil","The {Jockey} lights *embers* in the {Basement} of the {Pool} and sets a giant pot on top. A *busy man* tosses in noodles, eggs and a rubber duck to **boil**. The water bubbles so hard that the whole swimming pool starts to **boil** too, and the swimmers come out as dumplings."],"倩":["pretty","The {Cheerleader} slides down through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} and lands beside a *standing person* in a dress made of *moss*. She is so **pretty** that the bank clerks forget to count. The cheerleader paints herself green to look **pretty** too, and a frog proposes to her."],"卒":["soldier","The {Zookeeper} climbs the {Staircase} out of the {Pool} and finds a *pawn* from a giant chessboard in a tiny helmet. It salutes: a brave **soldier**. It marches into the deep end, gurgles, and twenty more **soldier** pawns follow it in."],"勘":["to survey","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a telescope to **survey** his land. His *strong arm* holds an *overflowing bowl* of soup in the other hand. He **surveys** the hills, the river, then spills soup on the gardener, who surveys him back angrily."],"馨":["fragrant","The {Shepherd} lights *incense* on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} and taps a *chime stone*: ding! The smoke spreads, so **fragrant** that the guests float up in their pyjamas, sniffing. The sheep in the yard below start to smell **fragrant** too, like roses, and bees follow them home in a buzzing cloud."],"逗":["to tease","The {Dentist} drops a *bean* down the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} to **tease** a hungry duck. It quacks, she pulls the bean away on a string, it waddles after it down the *road*. She **teases** it all the way to the bakery, then gives it a whole loaf."],"甸":["outskirts","The {Dentist} pops out of a {Trapdoor} in the {Yen Exchange} and finds herself far out in the **outskirts** of town, among *rice field* after rice field. Farmers wrapped in a *blanket* swap pennies for rice. Even the money changers moved to the **outskirts**, where the rent is lower."],"贱":["cheap","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a *bargain bin* full of gold watches. Everything is so **cheap** that he buys a crown for one coin and a castle for two. Then the bin sells him for a penny, and he finds out he is **cheap** too."],"炒":["to stir-fry","The {Chef} lights a *campfire* in the {Basement} of the {Tower} and tosses noodles in a wok to **stir-fry** them. He adds a *pinch* of chilli, and the noodles leap out and **stir-fry** themselves, swirling round the room like a tornado of dinner."],"灿":["glorious","The {Tsar} pops up through a {Trapdoor} in the {Mansion} lawn and lights a *campfire* on a *mountain* of firewood. It blazes so high the night turns gold: **glorious**! He sings, the fireworks join in, and the sunrise arrives early just to see the **glorious** blaze."],"敞":["spacious","The {Chef} goes down into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} with a *cane* and knocks out every wall, then climbs into the *attic* and knocks out the ceiling. Now the basement is so **spacious** he can cook for an army. Planes taxi in for lunch, it is that **spacious**."],"蜡":["wax","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, where a *bug* coats a slab of *sun-dried meat* in yellow **wax**. The steam melts it, and the guests get slathered in hot **wax** instead. They come out shiny, smooth and smelling of honey."],"囚":["prisoner","The {Cheerleader} bounces down the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} and finds a *person* locked inside a *fence* in the hallway: a **prisoner** of the laundry rules. She cheers him up with a dance and passes him a spoon. He digs out, and now she is the **prisoner**."],"栗":["chestnut","The {Lifeguard} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds a *cabinet* hidden under a *tree*. It's crammed with spiky **chestnuts**. A squirrel pops out and pelts her with them. She roasts a **chestnut** on the sand and offers it back as a peace gift."],"辜":["crime","The {Gardener} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} and finds an *antique* vase stuffed with *chili* peppers. Someone has committed a **crime**: the vase was stolen from the museum. A detective arrives, sniffs, sneezes, and arrests the chili for the **crime**."],"垫":["cushion","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange}, landing on a giant **cushion** of soft *soil*. A guard snaps *handcuffs* on her for breaking in, but she is so comfy she refuses to get up. The guard sits down on the **cushion** too and falls asleep."],"妒":["to envy","The {Dentist} peeks up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} and sees a *woman* behind a glass *door* in a golden swimsuit. The dentist turns green with **envy**. She steals the suit, but now the lifeguard **envies** her, then the ducks, then the trapdoor."],"魁":["chief","The {King} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room}, where a crowd of ghosts argue about who is boss. The biggest *ghost* grabs the *dipper* of soup and serves himself first: he is the **chief**. The king tries to take it, but the ghosts vote and the soup ladle stays with the **chief**."],"谣":["rumor","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Tower} when a *small speech bubble* floats up the steps whispering a **rumor**: \"The tower is made of cheese.\" Every floor passes it on, the **rumor** gets bigger, and by the top a mouse is nibbling the walls."],"寞":["lonesome","The {Magician} sits alone by the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} under a leaky *roof*, watching the *sunset*. Nobody came to his magic show. He pulls a rabbit from his hat for company, but it hops away too, and he feels even more **lonesome**. The fort's cannon sighs, just as **lonesome**, and puffs a little smoke ring for him."],"蜀":["Sichuan","The {Sheriff} wades into the {Basement} of the {Pool} with a *fishing net* and scoops up a *curled worm* wearing a tiny map of **Sichuan**. The worm uncurls and points to the mountains of **Sichuan**, then breathes out chilli fire. The sheriff's moustache sizzles and the pool water starts to taste of hot pot."],"甩":["to fling","The {Sheriff} swings a *bucket* round his head in the {Basement} of the {Wine Cellar} and **flings** it across the room. It lands on a *ski* that zooms off down the barrels. Excited, he starts to **fling** everything: bottles, corks, his hat, and finally himself onto the ski."],"涯":["horizon","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} to a *cliff edge* where *water drops* spray up from the sea far below. He stares out to the **horizon**, where the sky meets the water. He stretches his arms so far that his fingertips touch the **horizon**, and the sun sits in his palm like a peach."],"枕":["pillow","The {Jockey} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Funfair} and finds a *tree* stump carved into a *pillow*. He lays his head on it, but it is hard as rock. So he stuffs it with candyfloss, and now the **pillow** is pink and sticky. The ghost-train skeletons queue up to borrow the **pillow** for a nap."],"丐":["beggar","The {Gardener} rows to the {Island} and opens a {Trapdoor} in the sand, where a *begging bowl* sits on the bottom step. A **beggar** pops up and holds it out to her. She drops in a seed, it sprouts into a coconut tree, and the **beggar** becomes the richest man on the island."],"泳":["to swim","The {Yogi} jumps into the {Basement} of a hut by the {Lagoon}, where a *stream* runs straight across the floor. He kicks *water drops* everywhere and starts to **swim**, cross-legged, in circles. Fish join him, then a crab, then the furniture, until even the armchair can **swim**."],"奎":["crotch","The {King} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room}, where a *big man* stands with his legs wide apart, blocking the way. The king ducks to crawl through the gap at his **crotch**, holding a *jade tablet* over his head like a shield. The big man giggles, his **crotch** is ticklish, and he topples down the stairs."],"泌":["to secrete","The {Magician} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach}, and inside a giant *pinned heart* is slowly oozing *water drops*. It **secretes** them like sweat on a hot day. The magician catches the drops in a bottle, and they turn to perfume. Now the crabs **secrete** perfume too."],"逾":["to exceed","The {Yogi} paddles a *dugout canoe* up the {Staircase} of the {Museum}, along a *road* painted on the floor. The sign says \"Speed limit: slow\", but he **exceeds** it, whooshing past dinosaurs. The guards chase him, and they **exceed** the limit too."],"叮":["to sting","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} when a mosquito with a *mouth* sharp as a *nail* buzzes in. It **stings** her right on the nose. She swats, misses, and it **stings** the champion below, who punches the referee by mistake."],"黛":["eyebrow paint","The {Dentist} hides beneath the {Trapdoor} of a hut on the {Island} while her *stand-in* goes out on stage. Before the show, she mixes *soot* with oil into **eyebrow paint** and draws two thick black arches on the stand-in's face. The crowd gasps, and every parrot wants **eyebrow paint** too."],"燥":["dry","The {Zookeeper} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower}, and a hot wind from the *campfire* below blasts out. The air is so **dry** that the morning *birdsong* cracks into croaks. The parrots' feathers crackle, the lizards cough, and the zookeeper's sandwiches turn **dry** as toast."],"掷":["to throw","The {Jockey} pops up from the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and **throws** a *pitcher* of honey at the angry bees. A *helping hand* grabs a second pitcher and **throws** it too. The bees catch the honey mid-air, lick it, and decide they love the jockey after all."],"藉":["to tread on","The {Juggler} skips down the {Staircase} to the {Beach}, where *grass* grows in a *ploughed field* by the sea. He tries not to **tread on** the seedlings, but with every hop he juggles and loses track. He **treads on** a tomato, a melon and finally a sleeping crab."],"枢":["hinge","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, where a *tree* holds up a giant gate. He checks the *district map*, then oils the squeaky **hinge**. The gate swings so fast the whole roof spins like a door on its **hinge**."],"憎":["to detest","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of a hut in the {Jungle} beside a bamboo *steamer*. His *standing heart* burns: he **detests** dumplings, and the monkeys keep stealing his bananas to fill them. He **detests** the monkeys too, until they offer him one, and then it is delicious."],"鲸":["whale","The {Juggler} balances on the {Rooftop} above the {Boxing Ring} when a **whale** crashes up through the floor. It's a *fish* so big it carries a *palace* on its back. The boxers bounce on the **whale** like a trampoline, and it sprays water from its blowhole to cheer them on."],"弘":["great","The {Hunter} climbs the {Staircase} beside the {Lagoon} with a *bow* taller than a house. He draws it back past his *elbow*, and the arrow flies so far it circles the world: a **great** shot. The fish jump to applaud, and the arrow returns to hit the same tree, a **great** bullseye."],"倚":["to lean on","The {Yogi} relaxes in the {Basement} of a {Beach} hut and starts to **lean on** a *standing person* who's an *oddball*: he never moves. When the yogi falls asleep, the oddball **leans on** him too, and they hold each other up like two playing cards."],"侮":["to insult","The {Wizard} splashes in the {Basement} of the {Pool} when a *standing person* comes down to **insult** him: \"Your beard looks like seaweed!\" The *busy mother* who runs the pool hears this, marches over and **insults** the insulter's goggles, and everyone goes quiet."],"藩":["hedge","The {Firefighter} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} and sees the garden ringed by a **hedge** made of *grass* and twigs. A goat knocks over a *slop bucket*, and the **hedge** eats the slops, growing fat. Soon the hedge is taller than the mansion, and the firefighter sprays it back."],"拂":["to brush off","The {Firefighter} sweeps the {Staircase} of the {Pool} when a *dollar sign* floats up and sticks to her sleeve. A *helping hand* flicks out to **brush off** the money. More dollars stick, she **brushes off** each one, and the pool fills with swimmers diving for the cash."],"鹤":["crane","The {Hunter} pokes his head through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and finds a tall white *crane* standing on one leg. A smaller *bird* tries to copy it and falls over. The hunter tries too, and soon he, the bird and the **crane** stand in a wobbly row until the **crane** lifts off and leaves them."],"蚀":["to eat into","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Beehive} with a *side dish* of honey cakes. A greedy *bug* starts to **eat into** them, crumb by crumb. Then it starts to **eat into** the staircase, the hive and the sheriff's boots."],"浆":["thick liquid","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} stirring flour into a barrel of *water*. It turns into a gloopy **thick liquid** that he tosses at the crowd. Everyone gets sticky, and the football players slide around the pitch on the **thick liquid**, scoring by accident."],"芙":["lotus","The {Firefighter} slides down the {Staircase} into the {Pool} where *grass* grows round a pink **lotus**. A *husband* in swim trunks sits on the lotus, refusing to come out. She sprays him with her hose, and he bobs away on the **lotus** like a little boat."],"垃":["garbage","The {Lifeguard} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} and finds a mountain of **garbage**: banana skins, old towels, *soil* from potted plants. A *podium* sits on top. She stands on it and delivers a speech about recycling, and the **garbage** cheers and sorts itself."],"烤":["to roast","The {King} lights a *campfire* in the {Basement} of the {Tower} to **roast** marshmallows while studying for an *exam*. He gets distracted reading, and the marshmallows **roast** black. He eats them anyway and fails, but the examiner gives him extra points for crispy marshmallows."],"晒":["to bask","The {Sheriff} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} on the {Island} to **bask** in the hot *sun*. He lies so still that a bird builds a *bird nest* on his chest. The chicks hatch, and they **bask** too, lined up like little sunbathers."],"霜":["frost","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of a hut in the {Swamp} after a night of freezing *rain*. Everything sparkles white with **frost**. From his *lookout* he sees frogs skating on the frozen water, and the alligators have **frost** on their eyelashes."],"剿":["to wipe out","The {Juggler} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} with a *standing knife* to **wipe out** a *nest* of mice. But the mice are juggling too, better than him. Instead of fighting he joins them, and together they **wipe out** every cheese in the kitchen."],"蕴":["to store up","The {Yogi} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Dunes} and starts to **store up** for winter: bales of dry *grass*, blankets of *cotton padding*, jars of honey. He **stores up** so much that the trapdoor won't shut, and the camels move in for the season."],"圾":["rubbish","The {Juggler} lands on the {Rooftop} of a {Beach} café piled with **rubbish**, where a *chaser* sprints across the *soil* after plastic bags. The juggler grabs the **rubbish** and juggles it into the bin, and the seagulls clap their wings."],"绸":["silk","The {Chef} skips down the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} wrapped in shining **silk**. A spider weaves *silk thread* round and round in a *circuit*, making more and more cloth. Soon the boats are wrapped in **silk** too and slip into the water like smooth fish."],"屿":["islet","The {Yogi} meditates in the {Basement} of the {Museum} when the floor splits and a tiny *mountain* pops up, wrapped like a *gift*. Water fills the room, and the mountain becomes an **islet**. A crab moves in, a palm tree sprouts, and the curators argue over who owns the **islet**."],"氢":["hydrogen","The {Cheerleader} pumps *steam* into a balloon on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring}. It's **hydrogen**, the lightest gas, and the balloon rises, taking her with it. She cheers in a squeaky voice, filled with **hydrogen**, as the boxers watch her float away."],"驼":["camel","The {Tailor} leads a *horse* up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} and notices it now has a hump. A *serpent* has curled up under its blanket! The tailor sews a saddle round the hump, and it becomes a **camel**. The **camel** spits at the serpent, which slithers off."],"妆":["makeup","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of a hut in the {Swamp} beside a *woman* perched on a *split log*. She paints her face with mud and petals: swamp **makeup**. The frogs line up for **makeup** too and hop away with pink cheeks."],"捆":["bundle","The {King} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Casino} and finds a *trapped tree* tied with rope. A *helping hand* passes him a **bundle** of banknotes. He ties them to the branches, and soon the tree is a **bundle** of money, blooming with cash."],"铅":["lead","The {Cheerleader} jumps on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}, waving *gold coins* that are really grey **lead** painted yellow. They are so heavy that the roof cracks. She falls through into the vault, and the bankers find the **lead** coins sinking in their coffee."],"逛":["to stroll","The {Gardener} pops out of the {Trapdoor} in the {Swamp} and starts to **stroll** along a muddy *road*. A *mad dog* barks and races after him, so he breaks into a sprint, then remembers to **stroll** and walks backwards, slowly, while the dog laughs."],"淑":["gentle","The {Sheriff} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} beside his *uncle*, who is so **gentle** he catches *water drops* in a teacup so they won't hit the swimmers. He pats a wasp on the head and sings to the ducks: the most **gentle** man in town."],"榴":["pomegranate","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} where a *tree* grows a single **pomegranate**. She keeps it as a *keepsake*, but it bursts open and red seeds rain on every bed. The backpackers eat them, and the **pomegranate** tree grows another."],"丙":["third","The {Baker} hides in the {Basement} beneath the {Boxing Ring} and props up a cake on a *tripod*. The cake comes **third** in the contest: not first, not second, but **third**. He sulks, then eats it, and the tripod wobbles away in protest."],"痒":["to itch","The {Yogi} lies on a *sickbed* in the {Basement} of the {Hangar} when a *sheep* wanders in and rubs its wool on his feet. His toes start to **itch**. He scratches, giggles and falls off the bed, and now the whole hangar's planes **itch** too, scratching their wings."],"钞":["paper money","The {Chef} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a pot of *gold coins*. He melts them, adds a *pinch* of salt, and rolls them flat into **paper money**. He hangs the **paper money** out to dry, and pigeons fly off with banknotes in their beaks."],"蹄":["hoof","The {Tailor} kneels on the {Staircase} to the {Beach} fitting a *kicking foot* with a golden shoe. It belongs to a horse sent by the *sky god*, and the **hoof** glows. When it kicks, sand flies, and the tailor sews a second shoe for its other **hoof**."],"犬":["dog","The {Cheerleader} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Mint}, where a *dog* is guarding a mountain of coins. She cheers, and the **dog** wags its tail so hard coins fly everywhere. The bankers chase them, the **dog** chases the bankers."],"躬":["to bow","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of a hut by the {Lagoon} and bends his *torso* low like a *bow*: he **bows** to the sunrise. He bows so deep that his nose touches his toes and he tips into the water. The fish **bow** back politely."],"昼":["daytime","The {Jockey} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} at *sunrise* and lays a giant *ruler* across the river to measure the light. Inch by inch the sun climbs until it is full **daytime**. He gallops off to race, but the ruler says the **daytime** has only nine inches left, so he hurries."],"藻":["aquatic grass","The {Zookeeper} fills a *bath* in the {Basement} of the {Tower} for the penguins, but green *grass* sprouts from the plughole. It's **aquatic grass**, waving like hair underwater. The penguins dive in and wear the **aquatic grass** as wigs, and the zookeeper has to comb them all one by one."],"蛛":["spider","The {Jockey} rides onto the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} and finds a huge **spider** painted in shiny *red lacquer*, spinning a web between the chimneys. A little *bug* is stuck in it, waving. The jockey cuts it free, and the **spider** knits him a racing jersey as a thank-you."],"褐":["brown","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} into a muddy cellar. His white *shirt* turns a deep chocolate **brown**, and a *question mark* pops above his head: where did the white go? He shakes himself like a dog, and now the walls, the cat and the ceiling are **brown** too."],"颊":["cheek","The {Juggler} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Piazza}, drawing a face on a *page*. A pigeon lands on his head, and he pinches its beak with *tongs* by mistake. It pecks his **cheek**, which swells pink and round. The crowd laughs, and a child paints a pigeon on her own **cheek**."],"奠":["to settle","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a vault where a *chieftain* and a *big man* argue over a heap of gold. She slams a giant tooth down between them to **settle** the fight once and for all. The gold coins **settle** into two neat piles, and everyone shakes hands."],"募":["to raise funds","The {Magician} stands by the {Trapdoor} of the {Pool} at *sunset*, waving a bucket with his *strong arm* to **raise funds** for a new diving board. Every coin dropped in turns into a fish. Soon the pool is overflowing with fish, and he has to **raise funds** all over again to buy a net."],"耽":["to delay","The {Dentist} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with one *ear* buried in a fluffy *pillow*. Patients wait below, but she snoozes and **delays** the appointments. \"Five more minutes,\" she mumbles. The patients' teeth fall asleep too, and the whole mansion **delays** lunch until sunset."],"蹈":["to tread","The {Dentist} dances in the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where her *kicking foot* starts to **tread** on piles of rice. She scoops the rice up with a *rice scoop* and throws it in the air like confetti. Stamping and twirling, she **treads** the whole harvest into flour."],"陋":["humble","The {Lifeguard} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} and finds a tiny shack on a bare *hillside* inside. It's **humble**: one stool, one candle, one sock. A happy old man lives there, and when she offers him a palace, he says his **humble** sock is all he needs."],"侣":["companion","The {Lifeguard} patrols the {Basement} of the {Museum}, where a *standing person* is made of only a *spine*: a skeleton on display. Every night it wakes up lonely, so she becomes its **companion**, and they play chess with bones. The dinosaur skeleton gets jealous and wants a **companion** too."],"魅":["charm","The {Magician} pops out of the {Trapdoor} by the {Lake} and finds a *ghost* hiding inside a *sapling*. The ghost has such **charm** that the ducks swoon and the frogs propose. The magician tries to steal the ghost's **charm**, but only manages to make the sapling blush."],"岚":["mountain mist","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} to the top of the {Mansion}, which sits on a *mountain*. The *wind* blows, and thick grey **mountain mist** swirls round her ankles. She blows her whistle, and the **mountain mist** curls up into the shape of a fluffy lifeguard and whistles back."],"侄":["nephew","The {Jockey} gallops up the {Staircase} of the {Beehive}, where a *standing person* waits at the *arrow landing*, holding a bow. It's his **nephew**, a tiny boy dressed as a bee. The **nephew** fires a candy arrow, and the bees chase the jockey for the sugar."],"虐":["brutal","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Ice Rink}, where a *tiger* on skates is bullying the penguins. It is **brutal**: it steals their fish and knocks over their snowmen. The ninja ties its skates together, and the tiger slides into a snowbank, a **brutal** ending for a bully."],"堕":["to fall","The {Dentist} steps onto a {Trapdoor} in the {Warehouse}, and it gives way in a *landslide* of *soil* and boxes. She starts to **fall**, past shelves, past pipes, past a surprised mole. She keeps **falling** until she lands on a mattress delivery, safe and dusty."],"陛":["throne steps","The {Baker} opens a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds *throne steps* carved into a sandy *hillside*. He climbs the **throne steps** carrying a loaf for the sand king. The king is a crab, who bows and invites him to sit on the top of the **throne steps**."],"莹":["lustrous","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, where morning dew lies on the *grass* growing in the corners. Each drop glows so **lustrous** that it lights the room. The boxers stop fighting to polish their gloves until they shine, **lustrous** as pearls."],"荫":["shade","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn}, under a tree with *grass* growing round its roots. Its leaves make a cool **shade**, and he never moves. The sun gets jealous and tries to sneak in, but the *shade* grows bigger and swallows it. Now the whole inn sits in **shade**."],"狡":["cunning","The {Juggler} sits with *crossed legs* in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} when a *prowling dog* sneaks in. It is **cunning**: it pretends to be a cat, meows, and steals the cats' milk. The cats look at each other, then trick it back, and the dog runs off, beaten at its own **cunning** game."],"阀":["clique","The {Firefighter} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Spa} to a *gate* guarded by a *lumberjack*. Behind it, a **clique** of rich guests sips tea and refuses to let anyone in. She hoses the gate down, and the members of the **clique** are dripping wet, just like everyone else."],"绞":["to twist","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} with *crossed legs*, playing with *silk thread*. The cats **twist** the thread round chair legs, the lamp and the juggler. He **twists** his body to escape, but now he is tied like a pretzel."],"膏":["ointment","The {Gardener} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a jar of thick white **ointment** for her sunburnt nose. She rubs it on, then the pigeons beg for some, then the chimney. Soon everything on the roof is coated in shining **ointment** and nothing will ever sunburn again."],"垮":["to collapse","The {King} wanders into the {Basement} of the {Water Park}, where a *show-off* is stacking *soil* into a huge sandcastle to impress him. The king sneezes, the castle starts to wobble and **collapses**. Then the show-off **collapses** too, sobbing, onto the soggy heap."],"茎":["stem","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} holding a flower by its long green **stem**. The *grass* at his feet grows taller to see. He juggles flowers, and every **stem** grows longer until they twine round the ring ropes like vines."],"缅":["remote","The {Magician} sits in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} winding *silk thread* round a portrait of a smiling *face*. The face belongs to a friend on a **remote** island, so far that letters take a year. The magician tugs the thread, and the face winks back, smiling from far, far **remote** waters."],"喇":["phonetic la","The {Lifeguard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Spa} and blows a *trumpet* with her *mouth*: \"**La**!\" The steam rooms echo back \"**La**!\", and every guest wrapped in a towel starts to sing scales. The sauna door bangs in time, the hot tub bubbles along, and soon the whole spa is one giant choir singing nothing but \"la, la, la\"."],"绒":["velvet","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} beside the {Lagoon} wearing a suit of soft **velvet** woven from *silk thread*. A *soldier* tries to salute, but strokes the robot's arm instead and purrs: so smooth. The robot blushes, and the soldier orders a **velvet** uniform for the whole army."],"搅":["to disturb","The {Juggler} hides in the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} trying to nap, but a *helping hand* shakes an *alarm clock* by his ear. It rings and rings to **disturb** him. The cats wake up and **disturb** the customers, and soon the café is full of yowls."],"凳":["stool","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle}, where she plops down on a little **stool** with *spread feet*. A monkey steals it, then a tiger, then an elephant who flattens the **stool** into a pancake. The dentist sits on the pancake."],"梭":["shuttle","The {Sailor} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} at a loom carved from a *tree*. A *handsome man* passes the wooden **shuttle** back and forth, weaving sails at top speed. The **shuttle** flies so fast that it shoots off the roof and lands on a passing ship."],"丫":["fork","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} holding a *pole* with two *horns* on top: a **fork**. He uses it to scoop clouds into his mouth. A pigeon lands between the horns, and now the **fork** is a nest."],"姬":["lady","The {Juggler} skips across the {Rooftop} of a palace on the {Beach}, where a noble **lady** sits with her *chin* held high. She is a *woman* so elegant that the seagulls bow. She juggles sandwiches with him, then the **lady** catches him and politely puts him on the tea table."],"诏":["imperial edict","The {Jockey} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} with a scroll: an **imperial edict**. A *town crier* reads it aloud, and a *small speech bubble* floats over the crowd: \"Everyone must ride backwards on Tuesdays!\" The horses neigh, and the **imperial edict** blows away in the wind."],"钮":["button","The {Ninja} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Youth Hostel} and meets a *clown* sewing *gold coins* onto his coat as **buttons**. One pops off and bounces up the stairs, ringing like a bell. The ninja catches the **button** and sews it back on, perfectly silent."],"棺":["coffin","The {Gardener} trims a *tree* on the {Rooftop} by the {Swan Pond} when an *official* in black arrives with a measuring tape. He measures the gardener for a **coffin**. Shocked, the gardener jumps into the pond, and the swans use the empty **coffin** as a boat."],"耿":["honest","The {Gardener} sits in the {Basement} of a hut in the {Jungle}, his *ear* glowing red beside a *campfire*. A monkey asks who ate the bananas, and he's so **honest** that he admits it at once. The monkeys clap and give him more bananas for being **honest**."],"缔":["to form a union","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and finds two crabs who want to **form a union**. She ties their claws with *silk thread*, and the *sky god* thunders his blessing. The crabs dance, and the starfish line up to **form a union** too."],"懈":["lax","The {Shepherd} sneaks down through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave}, where the guard yeti has gone **lax**. Its *standing heart* snores, and its belt hangs in an *untied knot*. The shepherd tiptoes past with his sheep, and even the sheep get **lax** and start napping."],"嫉":["jealous","The {Juggler} skips down the {Staircase} to the {Beach}, where a *woman* lies sunbathing with a *fever* of anger. She is **jealous** of the juggler's three golden balls. She grabs them, juggles them better, and now he is **jealous** of her."],"灶":["stove","The {Zookeeper} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} and finds a **stove** made from a ring of baked *soil* with a *campfire* inside. He cooks soup for the lions on it. The lions want the **stove** too, so they carry it off and cook a zookeeper-shaped cake."],"匀":["even","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of a palace in the {Dunes}, sharing out sand into *even shares*. Every camel gets the same pile, perfectly **even**. One camel complains, so the yogi weighs every grain, and the piles are even more **even**."],"嗣":["to inherit","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive}, where the old queen bee, the *boss*, is retiring. Her crown passes to her son, the sailor's pet bee, who will **inherit** the whole hive. The sailor helps the bee **inherit** a honey throne."],"鸽":["pigeon","The {Gardener} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} when a **pigeon** lands on a jar with a *fitted lid*. It pecks and pecks until the lid pops off. The *bird* finds seeds inside and calls a hundred friends, and every **pigeon** in town lands on the roof."],"澡":["bath","The {Zookeeper} fills a giant *bath* in the {Basement} of the {Tower} for the elephants. One climbs in, and water floods out the windows. They splash, spray and blow bubbles: the best **bath** ever. Then the zookeeper gets in too, and now everyone needs another **bath**."],"凿":["chisel","The {Zookeeper} stands on a *scaffold* on the {Staircase} of the {Tower}, tapping a **chisel** into the stone. Chips fly, and out comes a giraffe statue that sneezes. He keeps working, and the **chisel** carves a zoo full of stone animals that walk off."],"纬":["latitude","The {Wizard} sits in the {Basement} of a cabin by the {Lake}, winding *silk thread* round a globe and fixing it with a *leather strap*. Each thread marks a line of **latitude**. He pulls one, and the whole world spins, sliding along its **latitude** lines."],"沸":["to boil","The {Firefighter} lifts the {Trapdoor} by the {Lake}, and *water drops* fly out of a giant kettle. The water has started to **boil**, bubbling so hard that it spits a *dollar sign* of steam. She tries to cool it, but her hose water **boils** too, and the lake becomes soup."],"畴":["arable field","The {Chef} skips down the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} into an **arable field**, where every *rice field* is lined with peach trees. He picks a *longevity peach*, takes a bite and becomes a farmer, ploughing the **arable field** with a ladle."],"刃":["blade edge","The {Robot} pops out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Funfair} and polishes its arm into a gleaming *blade edge*. The **blade edge** is so sharp that it slices candyfloss into perfect squares. The robot ends up the champion of sushi, cutting with its **blade edge**."],"遏":["to restrain","The {Ghost} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and sprints for the *road*, wailing. A giant glowing *question mark* swings down like a shepherd's crook, hooks him by the collar and yanks him back. \"Why?\" the Ghost moans. The *question mark* only tightens its grip: its job is **to restrain** him, and it **restrains** him all night long."],"烁":["luminous","The {Sheriff} kicks open the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} and finds a *campfire* someone lit among the crates. Every spark that pops out rings like tiny *joy bells* and hangs in the air, glowing. Soon the whole dark warehouse twinkles, **luminous** as a Christmas tree, and the Sheriff's badge shines so **luminous** he has to wear sunglasses indoors."],"嗅":["to sniff","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Youth Hostel} with his nose twitching. A terrible *stink* drifts from the bunk room. He opens his *mouth* wide and goes **sniff**, **sniff**, sniffing every sock and sleeping bag like a bloodhound, until all the backpackers line up so he can **sniff** them one by one."],"叭":["bang","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} behind a pair of red *curtains*. The curtains whip open, and an enormous *mouth* pokes out and shouts \"BANG!\" so loudly that every bather leaps out of the hot tub. Towels fly, cucumbers fly. **Bang**, says the mouth again, and the *curtains* swish shut. **Bang!**"],"熬":["to simmer","The {Ghost} drifts down the {Staircase} of the {Tower} carrying a cauldron. A weary *wanderer* sits on every step, blowing on a pile of *embers* to keep it barely glowing. The cauldron is passed down step by step, and the soup inside starts **to simmer**, slowly, for a hundred years. The Ghost tastes it and sighs: let it **simmer** a little longer."],"瞥":["glance","The {Pirate} lounges on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave}, wrapped in filthy *rags*. A Yeti stomps past below. The pirate lifts one corner of his rags and a single *eye* peeks out for a split-second **glance**, then the rags drop again. Snap. Another quick **glance**. The Yeti never catches him looking."],"骸":["skeleton","The {Hunter} tiptoes up the rickety {Staircase} on the {Island} and finds a *wild boar* made entirely of *bone*, clattering up the steps behind him. It snorts dust. The hunter screams and the whole **skeleton** falls apart into a heap, then reassembles itself, wrong way round. Now the **skeleton** walks backwards, chasing him in reverse."],"奢":["extravagant","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} and finds a *big man* lounging on a golden sofa, eating diamonds on toast. A *busy man* rushes around him, gluing gold leaf to the chimney and pouring champagne into the rain gutter. \"Too **extravagant**!\" yells the Sheriff. \"Not **extravagant** enough,\" says the big man, ordering a solid-gold weathervane."],"拙":["clumsy","The {Jockey} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse} to stack a *double mountain* of boxes. A huge *helping hand* reaches in to help, but it is so **clumsy** that it knocks both mountains over, slaps the jockey off his feet, and drops the last box on its own thumb. Boxes rain down the fire escape. What a **clumsy** hand."],"栋":["building","The {Dentist} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Lagoon} and lands beside a *tree* growing straight up out of the water toward the *east*. Every time the sun rises in the east, the tree sprouts another floor, windows and all. By breakfast it is a ten-storey **building**, and the Dentist opens a surgery on the top floor of the **building**."],"毯":["rug","The {Tailor} stomps down into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} with a bundle of *fur*. A *blaze* roars in the furnace, so he lays the fur in front of it, sews it flat, and rolls out a giant fluffy **rug**. The butler trips over the **rug**, the rug trips the cat, and the cat ends up asleep on the warm fur by the blaze."],"桐":["paulownia","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} with a *matching cup* in each hand. At the top grows a broad-leaved *tree* with huge purple flowers, a **paulownia**, shaped exactly like teacups. The tailor holds up his cups and they match perfectly. He drinks purple flower tea under the **paulownia** until his whole suit turns violet."],"砂":["sand","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} holding a huge *stone*. He crushes it in his fist, then takes a *pinch* of what is left and sprinkles it on the bathers below. More pinches, more pinches: soon the hot tub is full of **sand**, the guests are buried to their necks, and someone builds a **sand** castle on the massage table."],"莽":["reckless","The {Magician} crashes down into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} on a motorbike, straight through a wall of tall *grass* that grows there for no reason. He doesn't look, he doesn't brake, he just revs and smashes through every stalk, scattering bats and aeroplane parts. \"That was **reckless**!\" shouts a pilot. The Magician grins, being even more **reckless**, and drives up the wall."],"泻":["to pour out","The {Shepherd} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave} and lands on a *writing desk*. *Water drops* start dripping on it, then gushing, until the desk drawers spring open and the water **pours out** of them in waterfalls. The Yeti, soaked, keeps trying to write a letter while ink **pours out** of the pen as well."],"坪":["plain","The {Pirate} stomps down the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring} carrying sacks of *soil*. He dumps them in the ring and rolls them perfectly *flat* with a steamroller, until the ring is a wide open **plain** with grass and grazing cows. The boxers have to jog for an hour across the **plain** just to reach each other."],"梳":["comb","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} combing a *tumbling baby*'s wild hair. The baby keeps rolling away, so the Sheriff snaps a branch from a *tree*, and the branch's twigs line up into a wooden **comb**. Every time the baby tumbles past, the Sheriff gives it one neat stroke with the **comb**, until its hair is a perfect quiff."],"杉":["fir","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} where a tall *tree* has sprouted through the slates. It is covered in stiff green *bristles* instead of leaves. He brushes his moustache on it, and the bristles prickle like a hedgehog. \"It's a **fir**,\" the gardener calls. The Sheriff hangs his hat on the **fir** and it smells of Christmas."],"晤":["to meet","The {Wizard} pops up through the {Trapdoor} beside the {Pool}. The *sun* and a big black *speaker* are sitting at a table by the water. They have never been introduced. The Wizard waves his wand: \"Sun, **meet** Speaker!\" The speaker booms \"PLEASED TO MEET YOU\" and the sun blushes orange. They agree **to meet** every afternoon for a swim."],"稚":["young","The {Jockey} rides through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} on a tiny *sparrow*. The sparrow is so **young** it still has fluff on its head, and it keeps pecking at a *grain stalk* instead of flying. Baby bees crowd round, also very **young**, and they all chew the grain together, squeaking, while the jockey tries to look serious."],"蔬":["vegetables","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} and pulls the plug on an *unclogged drain*. Instead of water, *grass* shoots up, then carrots, cabbages, leeks and peas, a geyser of **vegetables** raining down on the swimmers. Everyone at the pool is pelted with sprouts and has to eat their **vegetables** before they can get out."],"蝇":["fly","The {Yogi} floats down the {Staircase} of the {Boxing Ring}, meditating, but a buzzing *bug* keeps landing on his nose. A big green *frog* hops into the ring, shoots out its tongue, and misses the **fly** every time, slapping the Yogi instead. The **fly** buzzes off laughing, and the Yogi gives up meditating to go fly-swatting."],"捣":["to pound","The {Dentist} goes down into the {Basement} of the {Tower} where a tiny *island* floats in a puddle. A giant *helping hand* with a pestle starts **to pound** the island, thump, thump, thump, grinding palm trees and sand into paste. The Dentist covers his ears; the whole tower shakes as the hand keeps **pounding** until the island is powder."],"顷":["unit of area","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} and finds a giant *tilted head* lying on its side. She measures it with a tape: it covers exactly one **unit of area**, a whole field. \"Give me an A! Give me an R! Give me an E-A!\" she chants, and the head grumbles that it is one **unit of area** and no more."],"麽":["tiny","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Fort} holding a bundle of *hemp*. He pulls out a *tiny thread*, then cuts it in half, and in half again, until it is so **tiny** no one can see it. He bows. The audience squints at an empty hand. \"**Tiny**,\" he whispers, and threads a needle with nothing."],"尴":["awkward","The {Gardener} hobbles onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} on a *crutch*, and the crutch snaps right in front of the *inspector*. The gardener falls into the chimney and comes out sooty, holding the inspector's toupee. Silence. Nobody knows where to look. It is horribly **awkward**, and it gets more **awkward** when the toupee starts to sneeze."],"镖":["dart","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} throwing a **dart** made of *gold coins* stacked into a spike. It flies across the street and pins a *ticket* to the wall: a free lifetime of cream cakes. Below, a hundred cats leap after the ticket, so the Baker throws another **dart** to win them all a saucer of milk."],"诧":["astonished","The {Chef} pokes his head up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}. A *small speech bubble* floats out of an empty *dwelling* in the steam room and says, \"Hello, I live here.\" The Chef is so **astonished** his hat flies off and his eyebrows shoot up into the steam. The bathers, equally **astonished**, all drop their cucumbers at once."],"尬":["embarrassing","The {Gardener} crashes through the {Trapdoor} into the {Spa}, still leaning on her *crutch*, right between two strangers on a blind date. The *go-between* who arranged it freezes. Everyone stares at the gardener, dripping and covered in mud. It is very **embarrassing**. Then her crutch sinks into the hot tub with a loud gurgle, which is even more **embarrassing**."],"硫":["sulfur","The {Lifeguard} drags a smoking yellow *stone* up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel}. It smells of rotten eggs. A *tumbling baby* rolls down the steps past him, gets a whiff and turns green. \"It's **sulfur**!\" screams the warden. Every backpacker grabs a pillow to cover their nose as the **sulfur** fumes chase the baby back upstairs."],"嚼":["to chew","The {Juggler} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Cat Café} juggling a *wine goblet* above his open *mouth*. Each time it falls he catches it in his teeth and starts **to chew**: crunch, crunch, crunch. He chews the goblet, the saucer and a cat's toy mouse. The cats watch, then begin **to chew** his shoelaces in sympathy."],"羡":["to envy","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} with one scruffy *sheep*. Ahead is a long *queue* of fluffy, shampooed sheep, each carrying a bag of yen. His sheep stares at their glossy wool and turns green: it starts **to envy** them all. The Shepherd looks at their money bags and starts **to envy** too."],"沦":["to sink","The {Lifeguard} stands on the {Staircase} of the {Casino} as *water drops* trickle down from above, then pour. A *neat stack* of gambling chips sits on each step, and one by one the stacks begin **to sink**, glug, glug, glug, under the rising flood. The Lifeguard blows his whistle at the chips, but they keep **sinking** to the bottom."],"沪":["Shanghai","The {Hunter} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} and finds a *door* standing on its own in the water, *water drops* streaming from it. He opens it and sees skyscrapers, river boats and neon: **Shanghai**. He steps through, dripping, buys a soup dumpling on the Bund, then comes back through the door with the whole of **Shanghai** in his pockets."],"旷":["to skip class","The {King} sneaks down through the {Trapdoor} into the {Swamp} and hides in a muddy *shed* when he should be at school. Through a hole in the roof the *sun* shines on him like a spotlight. \"Aha! You decided **to skip class**!\" bellows his teacher, a frog. The King argues that kings are allowed **to skip class**, then sinks into the mud."],"彬":["well-bred","The {Baker} steps out onto the {Rooftop} of the {Inn}, where a little *grove* of trees grows in pots. Each tree has neatly combed *bristles* instead of leaves, parted down the middle. They bow politely to him and offer him tea. \"Such **well-bred** trees,\" he says, and bows back. A **well-bred** pigeon curtseys too and nibbles his croissant very daintily."],"芽":["sprout","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Spa} in a perfect lotus position. A green *fang* pokes up through the *grass* between his toes and keeps growing, uncurling two tiny leaves: a **sprout**. He breathes in, it grows. He breathes out, it grows more. By sunset every step of the spa is green with **sprouts**, and the bathers are wading through a salad."],"狸":["wild cat","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} at the {Beach} and meets a *prowling dog* with stripes, a bushy tail and tufted ears. It is not a dog at all: it is a **wild cat**, sneaking back from raiding the fishing *village*. It hisses, steals the Lifeguard's sandwich and vanishes into the dunes. \"Another **wild cat**,\" sigh the villagers."],"冥":["dark","The {Magician} trots down the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring} with a huge *cloth cover*. He throws it over the *dim sun* that lights the ring, and everything goes **dark**: pitch-black, boxers punching the air. \"Ta-da!\" he says. Nobody can see him bow. In the **dark** a boxer punches the referee, who punches the Magician."],"碳":["carbon","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into the cellar, onto a heap of black *charcoal* and one white *stone*. He tries to sew the charcoal into a suit, but everything he touches turns sooty black. \"Pure **carbon**,\" says a passing chemist. The tailor's tape measure, scissors and teeth are now all **carbon** too, and he grins like a chimney."],"咧":["to grin","The {Lifeguard} stomps into the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a *lineup* of yetis stands for a photo. \"Say cheese!\" he shouts. Every *mouth* stretches wider and wider, ear to ear, until the yetis **grin** so broadly their heads almost split. The flash goes off. In the photo even the Lifeguard can't help **grinning**."],"惕":["wary","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} and sees a *lizard* sunbathing on a red *standing heart*. The lizard opens one eye. The heart beats faster. The Tailor takes one step, the lizard tenses; another step, the heart freezes. Both are **wary**, watching each other for hours, and the Tailor stays very **wary** of lizards ever after."],"暑":["heat","The {Sheriff} stomps down into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a *busy man* is shovelling the *sun* into a furnace. The basement glows red. Sweat pours off the sheriff's moustache, the pool boils above them, and the swimmers come out pink. \"Turn down the **heat**!\" he yells. The busy man shovels faster, and the **heat** melts the Sheriff's badge."],"咯":["cackle","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} when a *visitor* climbs up the chimney. The visitor opens a huge *mouth* and lets out a **cackle**: \"Ka-ka-ka-ka!\" Hens all over the farm answer, cackling back. The gardener tries to shoo the visitor off, but each push makes it **cackle** louder, until the roof is covered in chickens."],"萝":["radish","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} dragging a *gauze net* full of *grass*. He tips it out and pulls on a leaf, and up comes a giant white **radish**, as big as a sofa. He pulls another: a pink one. Soon the warehouse stairs are blocked with rolling **radishes**, and he has to surf down on one."],"汹":["torrential","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Youth Club} when someone triggers a *booby trap*. A few *water drops* spit out, then a **torrential** flood bursts from every window, sweeping ping-pong tables, guitars and teenagers into the street. The Shepherd clings to the chimney as his sheep surf past on the **torrential** wave."],"腥":["fishy","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} at night, staring at the *moon*. A *star* falls out of the sky and lands at his feet, flapping. It's a starfish, and it smells terribly **fishy**. The moon wrinkles its nose. Soon the whole sky reeks: every star is **fishy**, and seagulls circle the ring."],"窥":["to peep","The {King} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a tiny *cave* in the slates. He crouches and puts his eye to it to **peep** inside, holding a *compass* to guide him. Below, the patients are all playing cards. The compass needle points at the best hand, so the King keeps **peeping** and calling out bets."],"俺":["I","The {Ghost} pops up in the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, where a *standing person* is fumbling with a torch. A *sudden flash* lights the room. \"Who's there?\" the person shrieks. \"Me! **I**!\" says the Ghost, pointing proudly at himself with both hands. \"**I** live here,\" he adds, and flashes the torch under his chin for effect."],"潭":["deep pool","The {Tailor} slips on the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and tumbles down, step after step, followed by a waterfall of *water drops*. At the bottom the water collects into a **deep pool**, so deep the Tailor sinks out of sight with only his top hat floating. Goldfish move in. The butler starts selling tickets for a dip in the **deep pool**."],"崎":["mountainous","The {Cheerleader} bounces up the {Staircase} at the {Beach}, but the stairs keep sprouting into a *mountain*, then another, then a jagged range. An *oddball* in a snorkel sits on each peak, waving. The whole beach becomes **mountainous**, all cliffs and ridges, and the Cheerleader has to pom-pom her way over the **mountainous** sand to reach the sea."],"麟":["qilin","The {Lifeguard} hears hooves on the {Staircase} of the {Inn}. A *deer* with dragon scales clatters up the steps, a *will-o'-the-wisp* glowing on its single horn like a lantern. It is a **qilin**! Guests faint into their porridge. The **qilin** blesses the innkeeper's baby, eats the doormat and trots off over the rooftops."],"捡":["to pick up","The {Juggler} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} where a whole *assembly* of coins has spilled across the floor. A giant *helping hand* swoops down **to pick up** every coin, one by one, and flicks them into his juggling act. Ten coins, fifty coins, a thousand. The manager screams, and bends **to pick up** his false teeth."],"拯":["to rescue","The {Jockey} plunges into the {Basement} of the {Jungle}, where his *assistant* is sinking in quicksand, still taking notes. A huge *helping hand* bursts out of a tree and grabs the assistant by the ponytail, swinging him free. \"We must **rescue** the notes too!\" the assistant cries, so the hand dives back **to rescue** the clipboard."],"厥":["to faint","The {Juggler} wobbles up the icy {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} to the edge of a *cliff*. He gets a *hiccup*, hic!, and drops all ten balls over the edge. Another hiccup: he goes pale, rolls his eyes and starts **to faint**, toppling backwards onto the ice. Every skater who sees it hiccups too, and they **faint** in a heap."],"澄":["clear","The {Chef} climbs the mossy {Staircase} in the {Jungle} behind a *climber* hauling a muddy bucket of *water drops*. At the top the climber shakes the bucket and the mud falls away: the water turns **clear**, clear as glass. The Chef can see straight through it to a goldfish winking at him. Even the air grows **clear**."],"萎":["to wither","The {Wizard} goes down into the {Basement} of the {Lake} where a lawn of *grass* grows by a lamp. He casts a gloomy spell. Every blade droops into a *wilting stalk*, brown and floppy, and his roses begin **to wither** too. The Wizard's own beard goes limp. The lake frogs sigh as even the water lilies **wither** into crisps."],"哉":["exclamation","The {Zookeeper} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Island} holding a long *lance*. On its tip is skewered a huge *mouth* that cannot stop shouting, \"Alas! Ah! Oh!\" in dramatic poetry. Every gasp is an **exclamation**. The parrots copy it. Soon the whole island rings with **exclamations** and the Zookeeper puts earplugs in the mouth."],"涡":["whirlpool","The {Wizard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Fort} stirring a gigantic *wok*. *Water drops* rain into it and he stirs faster and faster until the water spins into a roaring **whirlpool**. Cannonballs, soldiers and a goat get sucked in, going round and round. The **whirlpool** spits them out over the walls, dizzy."],"滔":["torrent","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a *rice scoop*, ladling *water drops* from a bucket over the edge. But the scoop never empties: water surges out of it in a raging **torrent**, roaring down the tower, flooding the streets. The tailor tries to stop it with his thumb, and the **torrent** blasts him into the clouds."],"暇":["leisure","The {Shepherd} lounges on the {Staircase} of the {Piazza} in the *sun*. He has a *borrowed tool* for mending fences but has no intention of using it: it is his day of **leisure**. He uses the tool as a back-scratcher, a straw and a pillow. Pigeons join him, sunbathing. **Leisure**, he sighs, and orders an ice cream."],"溯":["to go upstream","The {Sailor} plunges through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool}, where *water drops* are flowing in a strong current. A silver *new moon* rises from the water like a canoe. The Sailor jumps in and paddles **upstream**, against the current, all the way to the filter pipe. The swimmers cheer as he **goes upstream** into the plumbing."],"鳞":["scales","The {Lifeguard} drags a huge *fish* up the {Staircase} of the {Inn}. A *will-o'-the-wisp* floats beside it and lights it up, and every **scale** on the fish glitters like a coin. The fish shakes, and **scales** fly everywhere, sticking to guests' faces until everyone in the inn shimmers like a mermaid."],"酿":["to brew","The {Ninja} springs out of the {Trapdoor} in the {Stadium} carrying a *wine jug*. He tips in the leftovers of a *good meal*, rice, plums, a whole cake, and seals it. The jug bubbles and burps through the match. By half time he has managed **to brew** a strong wine, and the fans line up to taste what he **brewed**."],"茵":["mattress","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} lying on a *sleeping mat*. *Grass* grows up through the mat, thick and springy, until it puffs into the softest **mattress** in the world. Guests climb out of their beds and onto the roof. The Yogi floats gently on his grass **mattress** while forty tourists snore around him."],"愕":["startled","The {Ghost} rises silently from the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut}. Inside sits a *standing heart*, knitting. The Ghost shouts \"BOO!\" as a *jump scare*. The heart leaps three feet and flips upside down, **startled**. Then the heart shouts back \"BOO!\", and now the Ghost is so **startled** that he turns solid for a moment and drops his chains."],"瞅":["to look at","The {Chef} squats in the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, where a single giant *eye* peers out of a pile of *autumn* leaves. The eye swivels to **look at** the Chef. The Chef **looks at** the eye. Each time a leaf falls, the eye blinks, and the Chef blinks too, until they're having a staring contest that lasts till winter."],"暮":["evening","The {Magician} pops out of the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} just as the sun sinks into the tall *grass* around it. He waves his wand and the sky turns orange, then purple. \"Behold, **evening**!\" Swimmers yawn and put on pyjamas. He waves again, the evening deepens, and bats swoop over the water in the **evening** gloom."],"衙":["government office","The {Yogi} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} into a *crossroads* where four corridors meet. In the middle stands a big *speaker* shouting new rules: \"No splashing! Fill in form 27B!\" This is the **government office**. Bathers queue in towels for permits. The Yogi needs a stamp from the **government office** just to breathe."],"诫":["commandment","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Yeti Cave}, and a *sentry* with a spear blocks his way. A *small speech bubble* pops out of the sentry's mouth: \"Thou shalt not juggle!\" It's a **commandment**. The bubble carves itself into the cave wall in stone letters. The Juggler secretly juggles snowballs behind the **commandment**."],"斧":["hatchet","The {Firefighter} kicks down the door of the {Basement} at the {Pool}. A *father* in a swimsuit stands there holding an enormous *axe*. \"Too big for chopping kindling,\" he says, and shrinks it by blowing on it, into a neat little **hatchet**. The Firefighter borrows the **hatchet** and chops the pool's inflatable crocodile into kindling."],"兮":["poetic ah","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut, between two velvet *curtains*. He opens his mouth and a *puff of breath* rolls out as a long poetic sigh: \"**Ah**…\". The waves stop to listen. He sighs again, \"Oh sea, **ah**,\" and seagulls weep into their chips. It is the **poetic ah**."],"焕":["shining","The {Hunter} crawls out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Swan Pond}, all muddy. A *campfire* flares and a swan gives him a *makeover*: soap, comb, a silk jacket. He steps into the firelight **shining** like a new coin. The swans gasp. His boots, his teeth, his hat are all **shining**, and fish leap out to see their reflection in him."],"棕":["brown","The {Zookeeper} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} boathouse where a *tree* grows out of an *ancestral hall*. Every leaf, branch and ancestor's portrait inside is **brown**. He touches the tree and his white uniform turns **brown**, then his parrot, then the lagoon itself, like a giant mug of tea."],"佑":["to bless","The {Yogi} rises through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse}, where a *standing person* is about to sail into a storm. The Yogi stretches out a *feeding hand* full of rice and sprinkles it over them, humming, **to bless** the boat. Lightning bends politely around the mast. The sailor goes home safe, **blessed**, and her boat is blessed too."],"嘶":["neigh","The {Sailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} when a horse gallops past below. Its *mouth* opens in a wild **neigh** so loud there's a *tearing* sound, like ripping cloth. The beehive rips in half. Bees pour out. The horse **neighs** again, and the Sailor's trousers tear clean in two."],"妓":["prostitute","The {Juggler} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} in front of a painted *woman* holding a cherry-blossom *branch*. She is a **prostitute** in an old story, a courtesan who sings at banquets. She tosses him the branch, he juggles it with three melons, and the **prostitute** in the story finally gets a better job, as his assistant."],"喧":["clamor","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Mint} where coins are being stamped. Every coin is a little *mouth* shouting. He grabs a *megaphone* to shout \"Quiet!\" but the megaphone just amplifies the **clamor**: clanking, yelling, sheep bleating. The mint workers can't hear themselves think, and the **clamor** shakes coins off the roof."],"蓉":["paste","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} holding a *container* of lotus seeds and *grass*. It crushes them in its metal claws, squish, squish, into a sweet **paste**. The paste is so sticky that the Robot's feet glue to every step. It spends all night trapped on the stairs, coated in lotus **paste**."],"删":["to delete","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a *bamboo book* listing every outlaw. A *standing knife* slices along each line, scraping the names away one by one **to delete** them. \"Now there's no crime!\" declares the Sheriff. Then the knife **deletes** his own name, and he vanishes from the roof."],"樱":["cherry","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} under a *tree* full of pink blossoms. A *baby* climbs up the branches and shakes them. Down tumble ripe **cherry** after **cherry**, bouncing off the Yogi's bald head, ping, ping, ping. He keeps meditating, now covered in red juice, while the baby eats the cherries."],"伺":["to wait on","The {Tsar} sits in the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} like a throne. A *standing person* runs back and forth to **wait on** him, bringing honey and slippers, fanning him with a leaf. The *boss* bee buzzes in and makes them **wait on** her too, so the poor servant juggles honey for the Tsar and the bee at once."],"嗡":["buzz","The {Wizard} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} canopy, where *grandpa* is fast asleep in a hammock. Grandpa's *mouth* opens and out comes not a snore but a **buzz**: bzzzzz. The jungle bees think he's their queen and swarm around him. The Wizard waves his wand to stop it, and his wand starts to **buzz** too."],"娥":["beautiful","The {Ghost} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Hut} and finds a *woman* so **beautiful** the stairs light up under her feet. A *spearman* guards her, pointing his spear at the Ghost. The Ghost bows and offers her a rose. She smiles, and even the Ghost turns **beautiful** for a moment, glowing pink."],"梢":["branch tip","The {Sheriff} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} and keeps climbing, up a *tree* that grows out of the chimney. At the very top, on the thinnest **branch tip**, hangs a *portrait* of the Sheriff himself, swaying. He reaches for it, the **branch tip** bends like a fishing rod, and he swings over the town."],"坝":["dam","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa} carrying sacks of *soil* and a giant *shell*. A flood of bath water is gushing down the corridor. He piles the soil, wedges the shell in the middle and builds a **dam**. The water stops. Bathers float behind the **dam** like ducks in a pond, and the Baker sells them buns."],"蚕":["silkworm","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and finds a fat white *bug* munching mulberry leaves under the open *sky*. It spins and spins until it wraps the Tsar in silk from his crown to his boots. \"A **silkworm**!\" he roars from his cocoon. The **silkworm** bows, and makes him a pair of silk pyjamas as an apology."],"敷":["to spread","The {Firefighter} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} with a bucket of sticky *ointment* and a *cane*. Sunburned swimmers line up. She dips the cane in the ointment and starts **to spread** it on them, slap, slap, slap. Then she **spreads** it on the chimney, the gutter and a seagull, which slides off the roof."],"澜":["big waves","The {Lifeguard} runs up the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} just as *water drops* splash over the *railing*. Then **big waves** crash through the windows, rolling up the stairs, one after another. The Lifeguard grabs the railing and surfs on a tea tray. The butler sails past in a bathtub, riding the **big waves** like a pro."],"杏":["apricot","The {Shepherd} pops up through the {Trapdoor} into the {Boxing Ring}, where a *tree* is growing. A huge *mouth* has opened in its trunk and spits out round orange **apricots** like a pitching machine: pow, pow, pow. The boxers dodge and catch them. The Shepherd eats one, juice everywhere: the sweetest **apricot** he has ever tasted."],"绥":["to pacify","The {Sailor} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room}, where an angry crowd is shouting about delays. A *soothing hand* ties each angry person with soft *silk thread* and pats them on the head **to pacify** them. They calm down one by one and fall asleep, snoring. The Sailor is **pacified** too, and drools on the doctor."],"冶":["to smelt","The {Yogi} climbs down into the {Basement} of the {Hut}, which is a furnace room. Sharp *icicles* hang from the ceiling, but he puts them on a *stage* in front of the furnace and they melt and glow. He pours in iron ore and begins **to smelt** it, red-hot metal dripping. The Yogi **smelts** a perfect copper teapot."],"庇":["to protect","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} as a storm hits. Two *twins* are being pelted by rain. He builds a little *shed* over them out of baguettes **to protect** them. Hail bounces off the bread roof. The twins nibble the walls. \"I'll **protect** you,\" says the Baker, and adds a croissant chimney."],"挠":["to scratch","The {Ninja} sneaks up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} to the *emperor*'s chamber. A huge *helping hand* creeps out of his sleeve and starts **to scratch** the emperor's back. The emperor purrs. Then it **scratches** his nose, his chin, his crown, until the emperor giggles and makes the Ninja his royal back-scratcher."],"搂":["to hug","The {Lifeguard} squeezes into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, where a woman with a *tall bun* is crying. A *helping hand* the size of a canoe reaches out and wraps around them both **to hug** them. The tall bun squashes flat. The hand **hugs** harder, and the Lifeguard's whistle squeaks."],"倏":["sudden","The {Sheriff} is drinking tea on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} when, **sudden**ly, without warning, a swimmer shoots up out of the water and lands in his cup. Then, equally **sudden**, the swimmer is gone, and so is the tea. The Sheriff blinks. The whole roof was a blur. Things around this pool happen fast."],"聂":["Nie","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} and finds an *eavesdropper* with three huge ears pressed to the wall. Each ear has a name tag reading **Nie**. \"My name is **Nie**,\" says the eavesdropper, \"and I hear everything.\" The Yeti whispers a secret. All three ears blush."],"婉":["tactful","The {Wizard} hurries down to the {Basement} of the {Mansion}. A *woman* holds out a *rice bowl* of burnt porridge. Instead of saying \"this is awful\", the Wizard says, very **tactful**ly, \"How brave and smoky!\" The woman beams. He is **tactful** again with the burnt toast, then secretly feeds both to the cat."],"噪":["noise","The {Zookeeper} plummets through the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} into a room where a thousand birds sit on wires. Their *birdsong* rolls into one giant *mouth* in the middle that blasts it out: shrieking, chirping, honking. The **noise** cracks the windows. The Zookeeper's earmuffs explode. Even the tower bell covers its ears from the **noise**."],"稼":["crops","The {Juggler} bursts out of a {Trapdoor} in the middle of the {Piazza} juggling a *grain stalk*. Each time he throws it, it lands and plants itself, until the piazza is a golden field of **crops** around a little farm *home*. The café tables vanish under wheat. The waiters, grumbling, become farmers and harvest the **crops** with butter knives."],"鳍":["fin","The {Cheerleader} jogs up the {Staircase} at the {Beach} and meets a *fish* with a long white beard: *great-grandpa* fish, a hundred years old. He waves one **fin** at her. She cheers, he flaps the other **fin** in time, and soon the old fish is doing perfect pom-pom routines with his fins on the steps."],"菱":["water caltrop","The {Lifeguard} jogs down the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring}, which has flooded into a pond full of floating *grass*. Each boxer must do a *hill climb* over a spiky black nut with two horns: a **water caltrop**. The Lifeguard steps on one. \"OUCH!\" He hops round the ring while the referee boils a **water caltrop** for lunch."],"盏":["small cup","The {Jockey} rides down into the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, where two *twin blades* are slicing a big *dish* into smaller and smaller pieces. Finally it is shaved down into one dainty **small cup**, perfect for tea. The jockey sips from it, gasps, and the blades start making another **small cup** for his horse."],"匿":["to hide","The {Ninja} slips through a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} and jumps into an *open crate* full of sand. A *lookalike*, another ninja exactly like him, jumps into the crate too. They both pull the lid closed **to hide**. The police open the crate and find only sand and two pairs of eyes. The ninjas are **hiding** perfectly, apart from the giggling."],"吱":["creak","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Beehive} on a thin *branch*. The branch opens a tiny *mouth* and lets out a long **creak**: \"eeeeek.\" The bees freeze. He shifts his weight. **Creak**! The branch creaks louder and louder until it snaps, and the jockey lands in the honey."],"寝":["bedroom","The {Cheerleader} tiptoes down into the {Basement} of the {Inn} carrying a pillow. She crawls under a low *roof* propped over a mattress: a secret **bedroom**. She tries to sleep but keeps doing star jumps in her dreams, bumping the roof. Soon every guest in the inn sneaks down to her **bedroom** to join the sleepover."],"揽":["to seize","The {Lifeguard} dives into the {Basement} of the {Mansion} where a *sightseer* is taking photos. A giant *helping hand* swoops out of a portrait **to seize** the camera, the hat, then the sightseer himself. It seizes the Lifeguard too and squeezes them together for a selfie. \"Stop **seizing** things!\" shouts the butler."],"髓":["marrow","The {Sailor} sits in the {Basement} of the {Waiting Room}, gnawing on a huge *bone*. A little *tagalong* dog follows him everywhere, drooling. The Sailor cracks the bone open and slurps out the soft **marrow**. The tagalong begs. He shares, and the two of them sit slurping **marrow** while the nurse calls their names."],"秉":["to grasp","The {Baker} clambers down into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} with a *grain stalk*. His hand closes round it and a *long comb* in his other hand teases it straight. He holds it up like a torch **to grasp** it firmly. No one can pull it away; the boxers try. He keeps it **grasped** through ten rounds, and bakes it into a loaf."],"哺":["to feed","The {Baker} tumbles into the {Basement} of the {Pool}, where a *seedbed* is full of baby birds, each with a wide open *mouth*. He breaks bread into crumbs and drops it in, beak by beak, **to feed** them. They chirp for more. He empties the bakery into the basement **feeding** them, and the chicks grow as big as swans."],"矢":["arrow","The {Sheriff} lurks in the {Basement} of the {Beehive} with a bow and one long *arrow*. He fires it at a wasp. The **arrow** misses, ricochets off a honey jar, flies round the basement and comes back to pin his hat to the wall. He fires another **arrow** and this one comes back carrying a honey sandwich."],"啪":["pop","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} with a huge *mouth* painted on his belly. He gives one thunderous *clap*: **pop**! A bubble in the hot tub pops. Clap: **pop**! The bathers' shower caps pop off one by one. On the final clap, the pirate's belly button pops off too."],"帜":["flag","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Beehive} and ties his sweaty *towel* to a stick. A *lone bird* lands on top and spreads its wings across it. Now it flaps like a proud **flag**. The bees all salute. The Jockey marches round the hive waving the towel **flag**, and the bird crows the national anthem."],"邵":["surname Shao","The {Sheriff} opens a {Trapdoor} in the {Tower} and finds a *town crier* standing on a *hillside* that is somehow inside the tower. The crier rings his bell and bellows, \"Oyez! Everyone here is now named **Shao**!\" The Sheriff checks his badge: it says **surname Shao**. The tower's pigeons all get name tags too."],"嗽":["to cough","The {Sailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} drinking lemonade through a *sipping straw*. It goes down the wrong way. His *mouth* opens: \"HACK! HACK!\" He starts **to cough** so hard the straw shoots out like a dart and pops a lifeboat. Every **cough** blows another boat across the harbour."],"挟":["to clasp","The {Shepherd} slips on the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} and a giant *helping hand* holding iron *tongs* grabs him by the belt. The tongs **clasp** him tight under the hand's arm like a parcel. The Yeti strolls past and gets **clasped** too. The hand carries both of them down the stairs."],"缸":["vat","The {Gardener} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} and finds a *clay jar* on a *workbench*. It keeps growing every time he pours water in, until it is a huge **vat** taller than a plane. He climbs in to clean it and his voice booms like a gong. Pilots come up to swim in the **vat**."],"揉":["to knead","The {Robot} clanks up the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} with a lump of dough. A *springy twig* boings out of its chest and a *helping hand* grabs the dough **to knead** it: push, fold, push, fold. The robot copies, **kneading** everything it touches, including the captain's hat, which rises into a loaf."],"腻":["greasy","The {Ninja} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} and finds the *moon* sunbathing, covered in suntan oil. It is so **greasy** that a *second coin* tossed onto it just slides off. The Ninja tries to climb on and slips. Even his sword gets **greasy**, and he spends the night skidding along the sand."],"驯":["to tame","The {Shepherd} bursts through the {Trapdoor} into the {Dunes}, where a wild *horse* gallops across the sand. He tosses a rope and splashes it into a *river* to cool it. The horse calms down, drinks and lets him ride. He starts **to tame** it, and the horse is **tamed** so well it carries his sheep home one by one."],"缆":["cable","The {Lifeguard} slides into the {Basement} of the {Mansion}, where a *sightseer* is tied up in *silk thread*. He twists the thread round and round until it becomes a thick **cable**, and the sightseer is lifted up the stairs on a cable car. Other tourists cheer and book tickets for the **cable** ride."],"晌":["midday","The {Sheriff} crawls down into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} and finds the *sun* trapped there. A rusty *weathervane* spins and points straight up. \"It's **midday**!\" he cries, and the sun shoots out through the roof to the top of the sky. Exactly at **midday** every pilot stops for a sandwich."],"瘫":["paralyzed","The {Tailor} climbs to the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} with a *sickbed*. He lies down on it and a *caught bird* in a net flutters onto his chest. He tries to get up but can't move a finger: he's **paralyzed** with laziness. The bird can't move either. The butler finds them both **paralyzed**, snoring in the sun."],"贮":["to store","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} into a *storeroom* stuffed with seashells. Each *shell* holds a coin. The jockey stacks them on shelves **to store** them, but they keep rolling out. He stuffs them in his boots, hat and pockets. Soon the pool has no room left **to store** anything, even the swimmers."],"觅":["to seek","The {Magician} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto the {Beach} and a giant *claw* lifts him up. A *watcher* with binoculars sits on the claw scanning the sand. \"We **seek** buried treasure,\" the watcher says. The claw digs everywhere, tossing up sandcastles. They **seek** all day and find only the Magician's lost rabbit."],"朦":["dim","The {Magician} creeps up the vine-covered {Staircase} in the {Jungle}. The *moon* is wearing a *blindfold*, so the night is **dim**, just a blur of grey shapes. He trips over a snoozing tiger. \"Turn up the moon!\" he shouts. The moon peeks out under its blindfold, but everything stays **dim**."],"僻":["remote","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} onto a **remote** {Beach} at the end of the world. A *standing person* is there already, a *pioneer* in a fur hat with a flag. \"Nobody comes here, it's too **remote**,\" says the pioneer. The pirate buries his treasure, and the pioneer charges him rent for the sand."],"隋":["Sui dynasty","The {Sailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room}, which leads to a grassy *hillside*. An emperor in yellow robes is digging a canal there with a tiny spoon. \"I am from the **Sui dynasty**!\" he declares. The patients help him dig, and the canal reaches the doctor's office: built by the **Sui dynasty** in one afternoon."],"蔓":["creeper","The {Magician} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} and a *long veil* of *grass* creeps out, stretching tendrils across the floor. It's a **creeper**! It winds up the piano, the chandelier and the butler's legs. The Magician pulls a rabbit out of his hat, and the **creeper** grabs that too."],"咋":["how","The {Zookeeper} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Spa} and opens a box. A *jack-in-the-box* springs out with a wide *mouth* yelling \"**How**? **How**?\" How did it get here? How do you shut it? The Zookeeper pushes it down; it pops up again: \"How?\"","zǎ"],"嵌":["to inlay","The {Cheerleader} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} onto a *mountain* of coins. A kid with a *sweet tooth* presses gumdrops into the coins **to inlay** them like jewels. The Cheerleader starts **inlaying** too, sticking candy into her pom-poms. The bank manager weeps at the sticky treasure."],"虔":["reverent","The {Cheerleader} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Yen Exchange} and meets a *tiger* with a *tattoo* of a temple on its back. It kneels at every step, very **reverent**, bowing to the cash machines. She stops cheering and bows too. Bankers, silent and **reverent**, light incense beside the tills."],"畔":["side","The {Pirate} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into a muddy *rice field* in the cellar. He walks only along one **side** of it, exactly *half* the path. The butler, on the other **side**, shouts \"This side is mine!\" They argue across the field until the ducks take both sides."],"琐":["trifling","The {Sailor} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Warehouse}, where a *king* sits on an upturned bucket worrying about **trifling** things: a bent paper clip, a sock with a hole, a crumb. He sends the Sailor to fetch each one. The king spends all day on **trifling** jobs while the warehouse burns down behind him."],"碟":["plate","The {Dentist} wobbles up the {Staircase} of the {Yeti Cave} carrying a flat *stone*. He sweeps the *leaves* off it, polishes it, and it becomes a perfect **plate**. The Yeti eats dinner from it, then smashes it like at a wedding. The Dentist carves another **plate** from the next stone."],"涩":["astringent","The {Sailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hut}, where *water drops* drip from a green persimmon on the ceiling. He licks one. His mouth puckers up so tight he can't speak. It is **astringent**, dry as sandpaper. The cat licks a drop too and its whiskers curl. Everything in the hut tastes **astringent**."],"胧":["hazy","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon} at night. A *dragon* swims across the *moon* puffing smoke, and everything turns **hazy**, blurred and soft. The lifeguard can't find the lagoon. He blows his whistle into the **hazy** fog, and the dragon sneezes the moon clean again."],"嘟":["toot","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool}, where a giant *mouth* blows a trumpet over the *capital city*. **Toot**! Every car in the city stops. **Toot** toot! All the buses honk back. The Dentist checks the mouth's teeth while it toots the national anthem."],"蹦":["to hop","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Jungle} just as an *avalanche* of coconuts rolls down a hill. His *kicking foot* starts **to hop**, boing, boing, over every coconut. Monkeys join in. The whole jungle **hops** like popcorn, and the Baker hops all the way home with a coconut stuck on his head."],"冢":["burial mound","The {Jockey} rides into the {Basement} of the {Lagoon} and sees a mound of earth under a *cloth cover*. A *shackled pig* pokes its head out of the soil. It is a **burial mound**, but the pig refuses to stay buried. It sings sea shanties from the **burial mound** until the jockey sets it free."],"浏":["browse","The {Lifeguard} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} as *water drops* stream down a phone screen. A *tattooed blade* scrolls through it, flicking past pictures like flipping pages. \"I'm only going to **browse**,\" he says. Six hours later the whole hostel is still **browsing** with him."],"裔":["descendants","The {Yogi} pops out of a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} wearing a long *robe*. A *skylight* opens in the sand, and up climb his **descendants**: children, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, all in tiny robes. More and more **descendants** keep coming until the beach is packed with Yogis meditating."],"襟":["lapel","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Inn} in a fancy *shirt*. On the **lapel** grows a little *forbidden grove* of tiny trees nobody may touch. A squirrel sneaks up his sleeve to steal an acorn. \"Off my **lapel**!\" he cries, and juggles the squirrel instead."],"叨":["garrulous","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} with a talking *mouth* that won't stop: \"and another thing, and another thing…\". It's so **garrulous** that he waves a *knife* to cut a word off. The mouth just talks faster. Birds fall asleep. Even the knife gets **garrulous** and starts chatting about cutlery."],"诀":["knack","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Ice Rink} where a *small speech bubble* whispers a secret: wear the *archer's ring*. He slips it on and suddenly he has the **knack**: he juggles ten skates while spinning on one toe. Every skater wants the **knack**, and the bubble starts charging for lessons."],"旭":["rising sun","The {Shepherd} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum} at dawn holding a *crowbar*. He wedges it under the *sun*, which is stuck behind a dinosaur skeleton, and levers it up. The **rising sun** glows over the exhibits. The dinosaurs yawn and stretch. Every morning he levers up the **rising sun** again."],"虾":["shrimp","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Piazza} clock tower. A pink *bug* with a curled tail crawls *downstairs* towards the fountain, then another, then a thousand. **Shrimp**! They pile into the fountain, which boils, and the whole piazza smells of garlic and **shrimp**."],"簿":["register","The {Baker} plunges through the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} carrying *bamboo* slips. A *floodplain* of water pours in, and every slip floats into place, stitching itself into a soggy **register**. The Baker calls the roll of swimmers. Every name in the **register** splashes \"Here!\""],"啤":["beer","The {Pirate} sits on the {Staircase} at the {Beach} with a huge *mouth* gulping foaming **beer**. A palm-leaf *fan* waves the foam into the air in bubbles that drift off over the waves. Seagulls catch them and burp. The pirate orders another **beer** from a crab with a tray."],"擒":["to capture","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} after a runaway *fowl*. A giant *helping hand* swoops down **to capture** it. Feathers explode. The hand grabs the fowl, then the innkeeper, then the Cheerleader. \"We are **captured**!\" she cheers, waving her pom-poms from inside its fist."],"枣":["Chinese date","The {Zookeeper} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Tower}, where a spiky bush grows in the dark. Every *thorn* on it shoots out *two sparks*, and in the flash he sees fat red fruit hanging there: a **Chinese date**. He picks one, gets pricked, yelps, and eats it anyway. It's so sweet he fills his hat with every **Chinese date** on the bush."],"嘎":["squawk","The {Gardener} is fixing the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} when a crow lands on her watering can. It opens its *mouth* and lets out a **squawk** so loud there's a *clank* as every gutter falls off. Squawk, clank! Squawk, clank! Bathers below are buried in drainpipes. The crow takes a bow and gives one final **squawk**."],"苑":["garden","The {Yogi} pops out of the {Trapdoor} at the {Mint}, right into a lush lawn where *grass* grows between the coin presses. A *tossing sleeper* rolls about on the lawn, flattening flowers and snoring. The Yogi waters him. Coins sprout like tulips. The mint has become a royal **garden**, and the guards prune the money trees in the **garden**."],"牟":["to moo","The {Magician} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Boathouse} with a *cow* under one arm. He jabs it with his *elbow* and it starts **to moo**: \"MOOOO!\" The boats rock. He jabs again, and it **moos** a whole opera. Ducks join in the chorus, and the Magician pulls a carton of milk out of his hat for an encore."],"呕":["to vomit","The {Ghost} sinks into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse} and finds a sailor seasick on a rocking floor, studying a *district map*. The map spins. The sailor's *mouth* opens, and he starts **to vomit**, gallons of green soup splashing out. The Ghost turns green too and has **to vomit** ectoplasm, and the map gets soggy."],"骆":["camel","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} onto a *horse* with two humps. A *visitor* in a turban rides the second hump, sipping water from a hose. \"That's no horse, it's a **camel**!\" he shouts. The **camel** spits on him and walks off with a crate of dates."],"凸":["protruding","The {Tailor} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} sewing a swimsuit. Suddenly a knob shoots up from the middle of the roof, then another: everything is **protruding**, sticking out like a big bump. His belly sticks out too. The tailor tries to iron the bumps flat, but each one pops up again, **protruding** further than before."],"熄":["to put out","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut to light a *campfire* for his sheep. A gust of wind blows; he takes a huge *breath* and goes \"FOOO!\" **to put out** the flames. They just flare up. He blows again, and the fire finally goes out, along with the lighthouse, the moon and the barbecue next door, all **put out**."],"兀":["towering","The {Wizard} rises up out of the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} on a *tall stool*. It keeps growing, legs stretching up past the diving board, past the clouds. Soon the stool is **towering** over the whole town. The Wizard waves from the top. Pigeons nest on his hat, and the **towering** stool casts a shadow over three swimming pools."],"喔":["oh","The {Ghost} sits on the {Front Step} of the {Fort} beside a tiny *cottage*. A huge *mouth* pops out of its chimney and says, \"**Oh**!\" The Ghost jumps. \"**Oh**! **Oh**!\" says the mouth, surprised at everything: the sun, a soldier, a pigeon. The Ghost hides behind the cottage and the mouth says, \"Oh?\""],"裳":["clothes","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Front Step} of the {Hangar} with a long silk *robe*. He shakes it, and out falls a mountain of **clothes**: shirts, socks, ball gowns, pilot jackets. They fill the hangar. The pilots dress up in the **clothes** and fly off in tutus, and the Sheriff puts on all of them at once."],"凹":["concave","The {Ghost} floats onto the {Rooftop} of the {Tower} and sits down. With a groan the roof sinks in the middle, curving into a deep dip shaped like a bowl, **concave** as a satellite dish. Rain collects in it. The Ghost floats in the puddle. The whole tower is now **concave**, and birds use it as a bath."],"赎":["to ransom","The {Sheriff} storms up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} to a *market stall* where a pirate has kidnapped the lifeguard's whistle. He slams down a giant *shell* full of coins **to ransom** it. The pirate counts the money, takes it, and gives the whistle back. Then the Sheriff has **to ransom** his own hat, too."],"屯":["to station","The {Tailor} marches up the {Staircase} of the {Casino} with an army of thread soldiers. He orders them **to station** a *camp* on every step: tents, flags, little campfires. Gamblers must step over sleeping soldiers. \"We are **stationed** here till the jackpot pays out,\" the Tailor declares, and pitches a tent on the roulette table."],"膛":["hollow space","The {Tailor} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} into an empty *main hall*. The *moon* drifts in through the roof and floats in the middle of a vast **hollow space**. The tailor shouts and his voice echoes for ten minutes. He measures the **hollow space** with his tape, but it's always bigger than his tape."],"浇":["to pour","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} with a watering can. An *emperor* below demands rain on his flowers, so the Juggler starts **to pour** *water drops* on him, then buckets, then a whole lake. The cats run. The emperor shouts \"Not on me!\" but the juggler keeps **pouring** until the emperor sprouts petunias."],"灼":["to scorch","The {Jockey} rides up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} with a *ladle* full of glowing coals scooped from a *campfire*. The coals spill on each step and start **to scorch** the wood, black hoof-shaped marks smoking behind him. His horse's tail gets **scorched**, and the warehouse smells like burnt toast."],"裘":["fur coat","The {Cheerleader} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} wrapped in a silk *robe*. It's freezing. She pulls on a huge *fur coat*, then another, then another, until she is a walking haystack. \"Who owns this **fur coat**?\" asks a backpacker. She gives him the **fur coat** and he looks like a bear."],"砰":["thump","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} canopy throwing *stone* after stone. Each one lands *flat* on the ground below with a heavy **thump**. Monkeys look up. **Thump**! A gorilla thumps its chest back. Soon the whole jungle is thumping, and the pirate's wooden leg thumps along in time."],"棘":["thorns","The {Juggler} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Beach} with bare feet, and every step is covered in **thorns**. One *thorn* jabs him, then another *thorn*, ouch, ouch! He starts juggling to distract himself. The **thorns** grow into a prickly hedge, and the juggler ends up juggling cacti."],"橡":["oak","The {Shepherd} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Stadium} and finds a huge *tree* growing on the pitch. An *elephant* is shaking it with its trunk, and acorns rain down like hail. \"It's an **oak**!\" he cries. The crowd catches acorns in their hats. The elephant curls up to sleep in the shade of the **oak**."],"碱":["alkali","The {Juggler} goes down to the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} juggling a *stone*, a jar of *salt* and a lemon. He drops them all in a bucket. The stone fizzes, the salt hisses and the bucket bubbles: it's **alkali**! The lemon sizzles. All the coins turn slippery. The banker washes his hands in **alkali** and they squeak."],"聋":["deaf","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Lagoon}, where a *dragon* roars into a giant *ear*. The roar is so loud the ear goes **deaf**, ringing like a bell. The Lifeguard blows his whistle. Nothing. Now he's **deaf** too, and the two of them talk in sign language while the dragon apologises."],"姥":["grandma","The {Lifeguard} jogs down into the {Basement} of the {Tower} and meets a little *woman* knitting beside an *old man* in a rocking chair. She's **grandma**, and she stuffs everyone she meets with dumplings. The Lifeguard eats twenty. The old man eats thirty. **Grandma** knits him a woollen whistle."],"瑜":["excellence","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} past a *king* paddling a *dugout canoe* up the steps, perfectly balanced, in a perfect yoga pose. Every exhibit applauds. A plaque appears: \"Prize for **Excellence**.\" The Yogi tries to copy him and falls off. The king polishes his prize for **excellence** with his crown."],"毋":["don't","The {Wizard} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Pool}, about to cannonball off the top step. A huge *left hand* rises from the water, palm out, like a crossing guard: \"**Don't**!\" He tries again. \"**Don't**!\" The hand even blocks the diving board. The Wizard sulks and paddles in the kiddie pool."],"娅":["for foreign names","The {Yogi} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, where a *woman* wearing a *silver medal* is reading a name card: \"Ya.\" It's the end of her foreign name, Maria, Sonia, Olivia, written in Chinese. The character is only **for foreign names**. Every guest wants a Ya on their badge, so the Yogi stamps them all **for foreign names**."],"沮":["dejected","The {Juggler} slumps in the {Basement} of the {Museum} on a broken *stepladder*. *Water drops* drip on his head from a leaky pipe: plip, plip. Every ball he throws lands in a puddle. He sighs. He's **dejected**. The museum's stuffed animals look **dejected** too, droopy ears and all, and a mammoth hands him a hanky."],"萌":["to sprout","The {Magician} creeps up the {Staircase} in the {Jungle} and taps a patch of *grass* with his wand. The *sun and moon* both shine on it at once, and it starts **to sprout**, shoots popping up everywhere: beans, flowers, a baby palm tree. Even his wand begins **to sprout** leaves, and a rabbit in his hat grows antlers."],"俏":["charming","The {Cheerleader} cartwheels out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and lands beside a *standing person* painting a *portrait*. She strikes a pose. The portrait winks, waves and blows kisses: it's so **charming** that cats fall off their cushions. The painter faints. Even the coffee machine finds her **charming** and makes heart-shaped froth."],"黯":["dim","The {Ghost} sinks through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into the ballroom, coughing up *soot*. As the band plays sad *music*, the soot drifts over the chandeliers and the room grows **dim**, grey, gloomy. Couples dance by touch. The Ghost turns up the music, and it only gets more **dim**."],"撇":["to cast away","The {Pirate} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yeti Cave} wearing smelly *rags*. A giant *helping hand* grabs the rags, rips them off and flings them **to cast away** into the snow. The Yeti puts them on. The hand flings the pirate's hat, his boots and finally the parrot: all **cast away** across the mountain."],"粟":["millet","The {Sailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} into a *cabinet* full of tiny yellow grains, smaller than *rice*. It's **millet**. He opens a drawer and **millet** pours out like sand, filling the pool. Swimmers float on grain. Chickens arrive from three towns away."],"粪":["manure","The {Firefighter} crashes through the {Trapdoor} of the {Funfair} into a giant pile of **manure**. Two *joined hands* pop up and toss *rice* over her as if it were a wedding. The cows nearby cheer. She uses her fire hose on the **manure**, and the whole funfair gets sprayed brown."],"尹":["Yin","The {Yogi} sinks into the {Basement} of the {Inn}, where a stern *magistrate* sits at a desk, stamping papers with a giant stamp: **Yin**, **Yin**, **Yin**. \"That is my name,\" he says. Every guest leaves with Yin stamped on their forehead, and the Yogi meditates to the rhythm."],"苟":["careless","The {Gardener} stomps into the {Basement} of the {Boathouse}, where a *scruffy dog* is supposed to tidy up. It's very **careless**: it knocks over paint, sinks a canoe and chews the oars. It wags its tail. The Gardener sighs and steps in the paint too, equally **careless**."],"癫":["crazy","The {Dentist} drags a *sickbed* to the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange}. The patient on it does a *headstand* and shouts \"Coins taste like music!\" He's gone completely **crazy**. He throws money to the pigeons. The Dentist tries to calm him, but soon he's doing headstands too, also **crazy**."],"蚂":["ant","The {Magician} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Spa} and finds a tiny *bug* saddled like a *horse*. It's an **ant**, galloping with a crumb of soap on its back. He waves his wand: the **ant** grows to the size of a pony, and he rides it round the steam room."],"禹":["Yu the Great","The {Yogi} sinks into the {Basement} of the {Museum}, which is flooding. A bearded *flood hero* in straw sandals marches in with a shovel and digs channels until the water runs away. \"I am **Yu the Great**!\" he booms. The exhibits cheer. The Yogi bows to **Yu the Great**, who goes on to drain the café."],"廖":["surname Liao","The {Lifeguard} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} into a garden *shed*. A pair of *soaring wings* bursts out of the roof carrying a sign: **surname Liao**. \"Liao is my name,\" says a cat with a nametag. Every cat flies off on wings, all with the **surname Liao**."],"俭":["frugal","The {Juggler} goes down into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange}, where a *standing person* is holding an *assembly* of coins. She counts each one, refuses to spend any and patches her socks with old banknotes. She's so **frugal** she juggles with peas. The Juggler is impressed and becomes **frugal** too, washing his tea bag."],"帖":["notice","The {Tailor} slips into the {Basement} of the {Yeti Cave}, where a *fortune teller* is pinning a *towel* to the wall. On the towel is a **notice**: \"TOMORROW: SNOW.\" The Yeti reads it and groans. The Tailor pins up his own **notice** on another towel: \"FREE PANTS FITTING.\"","tiě"],"煎":["to pan-fry","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Yen Exchange} over glowing *embers*, juggling eggs. He catches one in a frying pan held out in *front*. Sizzle! He starts **to pan-fry** everything that falls: eggs, dumplings, coins. The bankers line up with plates. He **pan-fries** a gold coin."],"缕":["strand","The {Lifeguard} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Museum} where a statue with a *tall bun* is slowly unravelling. A loose *silk thread* dangles from it. The lifeguard pulls one **strand**: the bun unwinds, the statue spins, and soon a single **strand** of hair stretches across the whole museum."],"窦":["cavity","The {Dentist} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} into a dark *cave* hiding a *market stall* that sells teeth. He peers into a giant fish's mouth: a huge **cavity**. He drills it and fills it with gold. The fish smiles. The stall sells him another fish with an even bigger **cavity**."],"簇":["cluster","The {Tsar} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Pool} where a whole *clan* of frogs huddle on *bamboo* rafts. They crowd closer and closer into one tight **cluster** like a bunch of grapes. The Tsar tries to swim through. The **cluster** wraps around him, croaking."],"棱":["edge","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} in the {Jungle} and the steps turn into a *hill climb*. At the top, a *tree* has been cut into a perfect square. He walks along its sharp **edge**, arms wide. A monkey dares him to skate along the **edge** on one foot."],"叩":["to kowtow","The {King} kneels on a {Trapdoor} in the {Boathouse} and knocks his forehead on it, bonk, bonk, bonk, to **kowtow** to the river god. A brass *door knocker* on the trapdoor knocks back. The King keeps bowing; the knocker keeps answering. They **kowtow** to each other until dawn."],"呐":["battle cry","The {Ninja} bursts out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, from an *inner room* full of steam, opening his *mouth* in a huge **battle cry**: \"AAAARGH!\" Bathers leap out of their seaweed wraps. Cucumbers fly. Every hot tub erupts. The masseur answers with his own **battle cry**."],"瑶":["jade","The {Yogi} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} to a *king* sitting on a throne of green stones. Each stone glows. \"My **jade**,\" whispers the king. He gives the Yogi one smooth piece to hold. The Yogi meditates with the **jade** on his head and floats up to the moon."],"墅":["villa","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} by the {Pool} into an empty *wilderness* of weeds. He pats the *soil*, and up springs a white **villa** with shutters, a swimming pool and a hammock. He moves in at once. Coyotes knock on the door asking to rent rooms in his **villa** for the summer."],"莺":["oriole","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} in long *grass* that has grown there. A bright yellow bird hops out and sings like a flute: an **oriole**. Its song knocks out a boxer below. The referee counts to ten while the **oriole** sings on the Yogi's head."],"烫":["to scald","The {Tailor} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hangar}, carrying a pot of *soup* off a roaring *campfire*. He sips it, too soon. \"OWWW!\" The soup is hot enough **to scald** his tongue. He drops it on his foot, which is also **scalded**, and hops round the hangar blowing on his toes."],"蛙":["frog","The {Wizard} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} holding a green *jade tablet*. A *bug* lands on it, and a big **frog** leaps up and swallows it with a slurp. Then the **frog** swallows the tablet, the Wizard's hat and his wand, and sits in the hot tub looking very pleased."],"歹":["bad","The {Dentist} stumbles into the {Basement} of the {Island} and meets a *skeleton* with a moustache, twirling it like a villain. It steals his drill and stomps on his toe. It's a **bad** skeleton, very **bad**. It laughs, teeth clacking, and runs off with the pirates' treasure map."],"伶":["actor","The {Lifeguard} jogs down the {Staircase} into the {Boxing Ring}, where a *standing person* in face paint is reciting Shakespeare. A *herald* with a trumpet announces: \"Presenting the great **actor**!\" The boxers take off their gloves and weep at the tragedy. The Lifeguard throws roses, and the **actor** bows six times."],"葱":["scallion","The {Tsar} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} boathouse as long green *grass* shoots up through the tiles. \"*Hurry*!\" he orders his cook, who pulls it up. It smells of onion: **scallion**! The cook chops it at top speed into a soup. The Tsar sneezes, and a **scallion** flies out of his nose."],"哮":["roar","The {Shepherd} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} and finds a *dutiful son* trying to wake his cat. The cat opens its *mouth* and lets out a lion's **roar** that blows off his glasses. Every cat in the café joins in: **roar**, roar, ROAR. The Shepherd's sheep run all the way to the next town."],"眩":["dizzy","The {Shepherd} falls through the {Trapdoor} into the {Mint}, where coins are spinning round and round. A *dark thread* ties itself round his *eye* and twirls him like a top. He staggers about, the room whirling, **dizzy**. He grabs a coin press for balance. The guards try to help but get **dizzy** too and fall over."],"坤":["earth","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Casino} spinning a roulette wheel. He spears a lump of *soil* on a *skewer* and holds it up like a kebab: \"I bet the whole **earth**!\" The ball lands on his number. The casino owner hands him the planet. The King roasts the **earth** on its skewer like a marshmallow."],"廓":["outline","The {King} bursts through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into a dusty *shed*. He draws a *city wall* in chalk, just the **outline** of a city, around every crate. The workers step inside the chalk lines and live there. Soon the King has drawn the **outline** of a country around the whole warehouse."],"讳":["taboo","The {Hunter} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} and opens his mouth to speak. A *small speech bubble* appears, but a *leather strap* wraps round it and pulls tight. The word is **taboo**: never say it here! The patients gasp. He tries again; the strap snaps around the next bubble too. Everything he says is **taboo**."],"啼":["to cry","The {Tailor} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Beach} when a huge *mouth* starts **to cry**, howling into the wind. Up above, the *sky god* is upset because his kite blew away. His tears rain down. The waves **cry** too, seagulls sob, and the Tailor sews a giant hanky to wipe the sky's face."],"乍":["suddenly","The {Jockey} rides over a {Trapdoor} in the {Spa} when, **suddenly**, a *jack-in-the-box* springs out with a boing! His horse leaps into the hot tub. Bathers scream. **Suddenly** another jack-in-the-box pops out of the sauna, then one from a cucumber, and the Jockey never knows where the next will spring."],"瓣":["segment","The {Baker} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion} into the middle of a *quarrel*. Two cooks are tugging a *melon* between them, shouting. The Baker whips out his knife and slices it into neat **segments**, one for everyone. The quarrel stops. Each guest gets a **segment**, and the melon seeds are shared out too."],"矫":["to correct","The {Juggler} wobbles into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café} on *stilts*. He fires an *arrow* at the target, but it bends like a banana. He grabs it and bends it straight **to correct** it. Then he **corrects** the crooked stilts, the tilted paintings, and the cat's lopsided whiskers."],"跋":["to trek","The {Baker} sets off up the {Staircase} of the {Spa} as if climbing a mountain, with a backpack and a map. His *kicking foot* stumbles over a *pulled weed* on every step. Days pass. He camps on step forty. He keeps going **to trek** up the stairs, and when he finally reaches the top, he has **trekked** all the way to the sauna."],"枉":["crooked","The {Wizard} climbs down to the {Basement} of the {Hangar}, where a *king* is trying to stand a *tree* up straight. Each time he lets go, it bends sideways, **crooked**. The king himself leans **crooked** in sympathy. The Wizard waves his wand, and now the planes in the hangar are crooked too."],"梗":["stalk","The {Gardener} creeps into the {Basement} of the {Jungle} temple and sees a tiny *tree* growing out of a *gong*. Its single leafy **stalk** bends towards the light. She taps the gong and the **stalk** wiggles, dancing. She bangs harder and the stalk does the cha-cha."],"厕":["toilet","The {Tsar} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and lands on the edge of a *cliff*, where a **toilet** sits all alone. A *rulebook* on a chain says: \"Wash your hands. No singing.\" He sits on the throne anyway and sings. The **toilet** flushes in disapproval and splashes him."],"琢":["carve","The {Jockey} rides up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} where a *king* is trying **to carve** a jade statue. A *shackled pig* holds the chisel in its mouth and taps away. Chips fly everywhere. They **carve** the king's face, then the pig's, then a portrait of the Jockey's horse.","zhuó"],"讥":["to ridicule","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut juggling. A cocky gull lands on a *small table* and a *small speech bubble* pops out of its beak: \"Rubbish! My granny juggles better!\" It starts **to ridicule** his every catch. The other gulls **ridicule** him too, so he juggles the gulls."],"釉":["glaze","The {Yogi} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Boathouse} with a wet clay pot. He sets it down in a *sprouting field*, and wild *animal tracks* stamp around it: a fox, a hen, a deer. The footprints glitter. He paints the whole pot with shining **glaze**, and the animals line up so he can **glaze** their paws."],"窟":["grotto","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Pool} and finds a hole leading into a *cave*. A *crouching man* waves him in. Inside, it opens into a huge glittering **grotto** full of stalactites and glowing fish. The King declares the **grotto** his new throne room and hangs his crown on a stalactite."],"敛":["to gather","The {Lifeguard} sweeps into the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} where coins are everywhere. He calls an *assembly*, then taps his *cane* on the floor: every coin rolls into one pile. He wants **to gather** them all. He **gathers** the coins, the notes, the bankers and their lunches into one heap."],"轼":["carriage handrail","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} onto a wooden *cart*. He grabs the bar in front of the seat, the **carriage handrail**, as the cart hurtles down a hill. Bees paint a *stencil* of flowers on it as it flies. He clings to the **carriage handrail** and waves to the queen bee."],"庐":["hut","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} to a tiny *shed* with a round *door*. He knocks. Inside is the coziest little **hut** in the world, with a thatched roof and a teapot. He moves in. Swimmers queue to visit the **hut**, which can only fit one at a time."],"胚":["embryo","The {Pirate} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Lake} house and finds the *moon* resting on a stone *plinth* like an egg. It cracks. Inside floats a tiny curled-up creature, an **embryo**, with a pirate hat. \"Arr,\" it squeaks. The pirate keeps the **embryo** warm under his coat until it hatches."],"呻":["groan","The {Sheriff} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Funfair} with a *skewer* of candy floss stuck to his back. His *mouth* opens in a long **groan**: \"Ohhhhh.\" The roller coaster groans too. Every ride starts to **groan**, creak and sigh, until the funfair sounds like a sickroom."],"绰":["ample","The {Chef} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse}, where a *beacon* glows over a mountain of *silk thread*. He uses it to tie up roasts, and there is always more: miles and miles, more than **ample**. He ties up the warehouse, the trucks, the moon. There is still **ample** thread left."],"扼":["to grip","The {Ghost} drifts up out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} and a huge *helping hand* reaches out **to grip** him. A *trapped man* is already dangling from its fingers. The hand **grips** them both so tight that the ghost can't float through walls. They hang there arguing about whose fault it is."],"懿":["virtuous","The {Yogi} pops up through a {Trapdoor} on the {Beach} with *one jug* of water. A *runaway heart* races past, panting. He gives it his only drink, then his sandals. The heart is amazed. \"How **virtuous**!\" The seagulls nominate him for a halo. He floats away, **virtuous** and barefoot."],"炯":["bright","The {Juggler} crouches in the {Basement} of the {Youth Club} by a single *window*. He lights a *campfire* and the flames bounce off the glass. The whole basement glows **bright**, then brighter, then the teenagers need sunglasses. The juggler's eyes shine **bright** too."],"竿":["pole","The {Gardener} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} beside a *drying rack*. She grabs a long *bamboo* stick, hangs the laundry on it and hoists it up like a flag. The **pole** sways in the wind, socks flapping. She uses the **pole** to knock pears off the tree next door."],"慷":["generous","The {King} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar}, throwing away handfuls of *rice husk* and gold. His *standing heart* beams. He gives each pilot a plane and gives the pigeons a castle. \"So **generous**!\" they cry. He gives away his crown, his boots, his socks, still **generous**."],"虞":["to expect","The {Yogi} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Museum} beside a *tiger* reading tea leaves. A *loudmouth* shouts predictions: \"I **expect** rain! I expect lunch!\" The tiger growls. The Yogi **expects** quiet, but the loudmouth keeps on shouting about what tomorrow will bring."],"锤":["hammer","The {Chef} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room} and finds a *weeping willow* growing through the floor. He shakes it and *gold coins* fall, which he melts into a **hammer**. Bang, bang! He hammers the stairs flat. The patients wake up. He gives the **hammer** to the doctor for reflex tests."],"栓":["stopper","The {Sheriff} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Swan Pond} boathouse holding a *treasure chest*. A *tree* sprouts from its keyhole. He pulls the tree out like a cork, and water gushes out. He jams it back in: a perfect **stopper**. The swans cheer. He uses the **stopper** to cork the pond."],"桨":["oar","The {Juggler} wades into the flooded {Basement} of the {Stadium}. He grabs a *tree*, snaps it in half and carves a long wooden **oar**. He paddles round the stadium in a bathtub. The football team grabs another **oar** and rows with him, racing the goal posts."],"蚊":["mosquito","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair}, where a *bug* with a *tattoo* buzzes in his ear: a **mosquito**. It bites him, and the bite glows like a light bulb. He waves his wand and the **mosquito** grows huge, rideable, and tourists queue for rides."],"磅":["scale","The {Baker} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} onto a giant *stone* by the *roadside*. It's a weighing **scale**, and the dial spins wildly. He puts a loaf on it, then a plane, then the pilot. The **scale** squeaks, the needle snaps, and the loaf weighs the most."],"孽":["disaster","The {Ninja} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yeti Cave} into a pile of *wormwood*. A naughty *child* is waving a match at it. Whoosh! Smoke, sneezing, the Yeti runs. One thing after another breaks. It's a **disaster**. The child giggles, the ninja sighs, and the **disaster** spreads to the snowmen."],"惭":["ashamed","The {Tsar} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Mansion} and sees his *standing heart* sitting on a *chopping block*, blushing scarlet. Last night he ate all the guests' cake. The heart hides its face. The Tsar hangs his head, deeply **ashamed**, and bakes a new cake. Even his crown looks **ashamed**."],"戳":["to poke","The {Chef} perches on the {Rooftop} of the {Warehouse}, where a *pheasant* is pecking at the shingles. He grabs a *halberd* and starts **to poke** it gently. Poke! It squawks and pokes back with its beak. They **poke** each other across the roof until the pheasant lands in his soup pot."],"禀":["to report","The {Baker} sneaks down into the {Basement} of the {Boxing Ring} and lifts a *lid* off a barrel. A tiny officer salutes from inside. \"Sir, I must **report**: the bread is stale!\" The Baker salutes back. Every time he opens the lid, another officer pops up **to report** another disaster."],"鄂":["Hubei","The {Ghost} rises out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Hut} on a green *hillside* in central China. He gives a hiker a *jump scare*: \"BOO!\" The hiker lands in a lake, then another; this province, **Hubei**, has a thousand lakes. The ghost tours **Hubei** scaring tourists into each one."],"馈":["to present","The {King} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Waiting Room} carrying a *side dish* with a big *price tag* on it. He crosses out the price and bows deeply **to present** it to a patient. Then he **presents** a bowl of noodles to the nurse, a cake to the doctor, and a gift to everyone."],"垣":["wall","The {Yogi} floats up the {Staircase} of the {Mint}, carrying *soil*. He piles it higher and higher until it stretches to the *horizon*: one long **wall** around the mint. Robbers come to climb it. He stands on top meditating, and the **wall** grows taller with every breath."],"溅":["to splash","The {Juggler} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Yen Exchange} into a *bargain bin* full of *water drops*. SPLASH! Coins, receipts and bankers fly. He starts **to splash** everyone, kicking and paddling. They **splash** back with umbrellas, until the whole bank is wet."],"咚":["boom","The {Dentist} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Lagoon} boathouse, where a huge *mouth* wearing a *winter coat* is beating a drum. **Boom**! The lagoon ripples. **Boom**! Fish leap out. The Dentist tries to check its teeth, but every time it opens wide, another boom blasts his hat into the water."],"钙":["calcium","The {Gardener} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} holding a *begging bowl*. Instead of *gold coins*, people drop in milk, cheese and chalk. She drinks it all, and her bones grow so strong she can kick down palm trees. \"Pure **calcium**!\" she roars. The island goats demand **calcium** too."],"礁":["reef","The {Juggler} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café} grilling fish on a *barbecue* made of *stone*. The grill sinks into the sea and becomes a jagged coral **reef**. Fish move in and swim between the sausages. Cats dive in after them. The juggler snorkels round the **reef**, juggling crabs."],"彰":["conspicuous","The {Jockey} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Hangar} wearing a *badge* the size of a dinner plate, glittering with tinsel. *Bristles* stick out of it in every direction like fireworks. Pilots can see it from the clouds. He's so **conspicuous** that birds crash into him. He adds flashing lights, even more **conspicuous**."],"豁":["open","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Warehouse} into a narrow *valley* between towering crates. A *pest* scurries along, gnawing at the crates until they topple and the valley breaks wide **open**. Sunlight floods in. The Hunter stretches his arms: everything is **open**, wide and free, and the pest waves from the top."],"眯":["to squint","The {Magician} lies on the {Rooftop} of the {Beach} hut in blazing sun. A grain of *rice* flies into his *eye*. He starts **to squint**, scrunching his face, and now he can't tell a seagull from a sandwich. He bites the gull. The seagull **squints** back, equally confused."],"磷":["phosphorus","The {Lifeguard} jogs up the {Staircase} of the {Inn} at night and trips on a *stone* that glows green. A *will-o'-the-wisp* floats out of it. \"It's **phosphorus**!\" a guest shouts. The Lifeguard's whistle glows, then his shorts. Every step is coated in **phosphorus**, and guests find their rooms without candles."],"雯":["colorful clouds","The {Wizard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Funfair} as *rain* falls on a cloud with a *tattoo* of a rainbow. He paints the clouds pink, gold and lilac, and the sky fills with **colorful clouds** like cotton candy. Kids eat them. The Wizard rides the Ferris wheel up through the **colorful clouds**."],"墟":["ruins","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum}, shovelling *soil* onto the floor below. An ancient city slowly appears, then collapses, crumbling, into **ruins**. The shepherd's sheep graze on toppled columns. A tour guide sells tickets to the *ruins* and the shepherd gets a cut of the **ruins** money."],"迂":["pedantic","The {Yogi} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} beside a *road*, where a *coat stand* with spectacles lectures every passer-by on comma rules. It refuses to let a car pass until the driver spells \"museum\" correctly. The coat stand is so **pedantic** it corrects the clouds. The Yogi sighs: too **pedantic**."],"瞻":["to gaze","The {Jockey} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Mansion} under the *eaves*, chin in his hands. A huge *eye* peers out beside him. Together they **gaze** at the stars for hours, not blinking. The moon gets shy and hides. They keep **gazing**, and the jockey's horse falls asleep."],"颅":["skull","The {Lifeguard} climbs the {Staircase} of the {Pool} carrying a *black pot*. He lifts the lid and finds a grinning **skull** reading a *page* of a book. It clacks its jaw: \"Shh!\" The lifeguard puts on his reading glasses and the **skull** reads him a bedtime story."],"琉":["precious stone","The {Lifeguard} sits on the {Staircase} of the {Youth Hostel} when a *king* rolls in, a *tumbling baby* on his back. The baby drops a sparkling **precious stone** that bounces down the stairs. Backpackers chase it. The **precious stone** lands in a teacup and the tea turns blue."],"悼":["to mourn","The {Dentist} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Tower} holding a lit *beacon*. His *standing heart* is weeping because his favourite tooth fell out. He lays it in a little coffin and the whole tower comes **to mourn**. Bells toll. Everyone **mourns** the tooth."],"蝴":["butterfly","The {Hunter} tiptoes up the {Staircase} of the {Pool} with a net. A *bug* with long *whiskers* flutters past, wings as big as umbrellas: a **butterfly**. He swings and misses. The **butterfly** lands on his nose, and he goes cross-eyed while the swimmers cheer."],"拣":["to pick","The {Juggler} squats in the {Basement} of the {Yen Exchange} in front of a mountain of coins. A giant *helping hand* swoops down **to pick** only the shiny ones. Plink, plink. It ignores the bent ones. The juggler tries **to pick** too, but he picks only chocolate coins, and eats them."],"渺":["vast","The {Magician} wanders into the {Basement} of the {Cat Café}, and it's flooded with *water drops* stretching away forever. A tiny cat stares out with *one eye* across the **vast** sea. The Magician rows and rows but never reaches a wall. The basement is so **vast** that whales swim past."],"眷":["family","The {Juggler} opens the {Trapdoor} of the {Mint} and out climbs his whole **family**: grandma, uncles, cousins. *Rolling hands* pass round biscuits, and every *eye* sparkles. They hug him. The guards ask for passports. The **family** moves into the mint and sets up a picnic among the coins."],"悯":["to pity","The {Magician} slides into the {Basement} of the {Inn} and finds a *mourner* weeping into a hanky. His *standing heart* melts. He starts **to pity** her and pulls a rabbit out of his hat to cheer her up. She cries harder, the rabbit cries too, and he **pities** them both."],"汰":["to eliminate","The {Tailor} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Island} into a pool of *water drops*. A *giant* is panning for gold, throwing away everything that isn't shiny. Old boots, fish and finally the Tailor get flicked away. \"I must **eliminate** the junk!\" says the giant. The Tailor is **eliminated**."],"慑":["to frighten","The {Sheriff} drops through the {Trapdoor} into the {Hut}, where an *eavesdropper* has his ear glued to the wall. The Sheriff's *standing heart* roars \"BOO!\" **to frighten** him. The eavesdropper jumps out of his shoes. It **frightens** the cat, the kettle and a ghost hiding under the bed."],"婶":["aunt","The {Sheriff} sneaks into the {Basement} of the {Funfair}, where a *woman* holds court in a tiny *courtroom* made of candy floss. It's his **aunt**, banging a toffee-apple gavel and judging the bumper cars for reckless driving. She spots him hiding behind a teddy bear and sentences him to seven goes on the teacups. \"Yes, **Aunt**,\" he mumbles, already dizzy."],"斐":["phonetic fei","The {Firefighter} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Lake} house and finds a parrot with *spread wings* and a *tattoo* on its chest saying FEI. It squawks \"Fei! Fei!\" It only makes sounds, **phonetic fei**, in names like Fiona. She hoses it down, but it keeps squawking the **phonetic fei**."],"嘘":["to hiss","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Museum} among crumbling *ruins*. A huge *mouth* pokes out of a fallen column and starts **to hiss**: \"SSSSSS!\" The tourists below freeze. The shepherd's sheep **hiss** back. Soon the whole museum hisses like a punctured tyre."],"镶":["to embed","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium} with an *embroidered robe* and a sack of *gold coins*. He pushes each coin into the cloth **to embed** it, until the robe is a glittering suit of armour. Fans gasp. He **embeds** coins in the scoreboard as well."],"炕":["kang bed","The {King} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Hangar} onto a big brick **kang bed** with a *campfire* burning inside it. He rolls about in his *high collar*, toasty warm. Pilots climb on to nap. The whole air force snores on the **kang bed**, warmed from below."],"宦":["official","The {Hunter} drops through the {Trapdoor} at the {Swan Pond} into a palace under a golden *roof*. A *minister* in silk robes is stamping orders. Swans in hats stand to attention. Every one of them is an **official**. The Hunter gets a hat and is made an **official** too."],"趴":["lie face down","The {Pirate} crawls out onto the {Rooftop} of the {Spa} under a pair of *curtains*. A *kicking foot* trips him, and he flops flat to **lie face down** on the tiles. The masseur thinks he's a client and massages his back. Soon every bather wants to **lie face down** on the roof."],"绷":["to stretch taut","The {Baker} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Jungle} lodge with his *buddies*. They grab a *silk thread* at each end and pull, pull, pull, **to stretch taut** a tightrope across the jungle. It twangs like a guitar. The baker walks along it. The monkeys pull it even more **taut**, and he bounces into the clouds."],"窘":["embarrassed","The {Juggler} trips into the {Basement} of the {Youth Club}, into a dark *cave* where a *lord* is reciting poetry. The juggler drops all his balls into the lord's soup. Silence. The lord stares. The juggler is very **embarrassed**, turns tomato red, and gets more **embarrassed** when his trousers fall down."],"襄":["to assist","The {Shepherd} climbs onto the {Rooftop} of the {Stadium}, where a player in an *embroidered robe* is stuck on the scoreboard. The shepherd reaches up **to assist**, and his sheep form a fluffy ladder. The fans cheer. Then he has **to assist** the referee, the mascot and a pigeon."],"珀":["amber","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Fort} holding a golden lump of *amber*. Trapped inside is a mosquito waving a tiny flag. He polishes the **amber** and it glows like honey. The soldiers trade cannonballs for it. The pirate keeps the **amber** under his eye patch."],"嚣":["noisy","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of the {Cat Café}, where a *chorus* of cats sings from a *page* of music. Each sings a different song at full volume. It's so **noisy** the windows rattle. Customers stuff croissants in their ears. The shepherd's sheep join in, even more **noisy**."],"拚":["to strive","The {Pirate} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion}, and a *helping hand* plonks an *officer's cap* on his head. Suddenly he wants to be the best at everything. He sets out **to strive**: scrubbing every floor twice, racing the butler up the chimney, arm-wrestling the grandfather clock. He **strives** so hard his wooden leg starts smoking, and the cap gives him a medal."],"酌":["to pour wine","The {Jockey} rides up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} holding a *wine jug* and a *ladle*. On each step he stops **to pour wine** for a thirsty worker, one ladleful at a time. The workers sing. By the top step he's **pouring wine** into his horse's bucket too."],"浊":["murky","The {Jockey} rides up the {Staircase} of the {Warehouse} as *water drops* trickle down from a leaky tank. A *bug* paddles in the puddles, stirring up mud until the water is **murky** and brown. The Jockey can't see his boots. Everything turns **murky**, even his horse."],"毓":["to nurture","The {Yogi} pops out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Museum}, where a *busy mother* rocks a *tumbling baby* while feeding seedlings. She waters them all **to nurture** them. The baby grows, the plants grow, the museum's dinosaur grows a new tooth. The Yogi helps **nurture** them."],"撼":["to shake","The {Hunter} stomps through the {Trapdoor} of the {Mansion}. A giant *helping hand* grabs the house and begins **to shake** it like a snow globe. *Tears* stream down the butler's face. Paintings fall. The hand **shakes** harder and the chandelier swings like a pendulum."],"嗜":["to crave","The {Sheriff} climbs out of the {Trapdoor} of the {Beehive} and meets *great-grandpa*, who has a sticky *mouth* and a jar of honey. \"I **crave** sweets!\" he cries, licking the honeycomb. The bees protest. Great-grandpa **craves** more, and the Sheriff has to lock up the honey."],"扛":["to shoulder","The {King} staggers up the {Staircase} of the {Hangar} carrying a heavy *workbench* on his crown. A giant *helping hand* lifts it off and swings it up **to shoulder** it like a sack of potatoes. Then the hand shoulders a propeller, a fuel tank and a whole aeroplane. The pilots line up, and the King proudly **shoulders** them two at a time."],"峭":["precipitous","The {Cheerleader} falls through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} onto the side of a *mountain* so **precipitous** it's vertical. A *portrait* hangs on the cliff. She dangles from it, pom-poms flapping. Cats cling to her ankles. The cliff is **precipitous** all the way to the cake shelf."],"磕":["to knock","The {King} sits on the {Rooftop} of the {Hut} with a *lidded dish* of dumplings, but the lid is stuck. He grabs a *stone* and starts **to knock** on it: knock, knock, KNOCK! The lid won't budge. He **knocks** harder, and the chimney falls off, the hens fly away and the whole hut shakes. Finally the lid pops open and a dumpling says, \"Who's there?\""],"翘":["to stick up","The {Cheerleader} pops up through the {Trapdoor} of the {Cat Café} beside an *emperor* with *feathers* in his hair. At her first cheer, every feather springs up to **stick up** straight at the ceiling like a firework. She tries to comb them flat; they boing back. The cats are so startled their tails **stick up** too, and the emperor's moustache joins in."],"槽":["trough","The {Tsar} puffs up the {Staircase} of the {Tower} dragging a hollowed-out *tree* as long as a canoe. He sets it on the top step as a *trough* for his thirsty horses, and they slurp so loudly the bells ring. Then he pours borscht into the **trough**, and the dinner guests kneel down beside the horses and slurp from the **trough** too."],"淌":["to trickle","The {Tailor} crawls into the {Basement} of the {Hangar} as *water drops* leak from the *attic* far above, through every floor. They begin **to trickle** down the walls in thin silver lines, then along the floor, then into the Tailor's shoes. He tries to catch them in a thimble. They **trickle** round it, under the planes and out of the door."],"栅":["fence","The {Jockey} drops through the {Trapdoor} of the {Spa}, chops down a *tree* and saws it into stakes, following a plan in a *bamboo book*. Bang, bang, bang! He hammers them in a ring around the hot tub to build a **fence**. The bathers are trapped inside, steaming like dumplings. The **fence** keeps growing, and soon a goat is peering in through the gaps."],"颓":["to crumble","The {Tailor} creeps up the {Staircase} of the {Waiting Room} carrying a marble statue with a *bald head*, reading a *page* of instructions. The stone steps start **to crumble** under him like stale biscuits. The statue's nose crumbles off, then its ears. Patients cling to the bannister as the whole staircase **crumbles** into dust, leaving the Tailor hovering, very surprised."],"熏":["fragrance","The {Shepherd} stands on the {Rooftop} of a hut in the {Dunes}, blowing on smoking *embers* in a brass bowl. A sweet **fragrance** of sandalwood curls out and drifts over the desert. Camels lift their noses and wander towards it in a long dreamy line. By sunset the whole desert is soaked in **fragrance**, and even the sand smells like a temple."],"瑛":["jade-like stone","The {Yogi} meditates on the {Rooftop} of the {Boxing Ring} as a *king* climbs up and hands a *hero* a shining green **jade-like stone**. The hero thinks it's a sweet and bites it. CRACK! His tooth breaks; the stone is fine. The crowd below roars. The king polishes the **jade-like stone** on his robe and the Yogi floats over to admire it."],"颐":["chin","The {Yogi} sits on the {Staircase} at the {Beach}, stroking his long beard and reading a *page* of philosophy. His *chin* begins to grow, longer and longer, rolling down the steps like a red carpet. Crabs stroll along it. Kids slide down it into the sea. \"My **chin**!\" he cries, and his **chin** now reaches the lighthouse."],"忖":["to ponder","The {Tsar} slumps in the {Basement} of the {Casino} with his *thumb* on his lip and his *standing heart* thumping. He has one chip left. Red or black? He starts **to ponder**. He ponders for an hour, then a day. Dust gathers on his crown. The croupier falls asleep. Still the Tsar **ponders**, thumb twiddling, as the roulette wheel rusts."]};
